2 CONT Norman Armour (October 14, 1887– September 27, 1982) was a career United States diplomat who The New York Times once called "the perfect diplomat". In his long career spanning both World Wars, he served as Chief of Mission in eigh
2 CONC t countries, as Assistant Secretary of State for Political Affairs, and married into Russian nobility.
