1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tabitha is the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Parnell Wilkenson. She married Stephen Bishop, May 4, 1654, Guilford, CT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had nine known children all born in Guilford: Stephen Jr., Tabitha, Caleb, Daniel, Mehitable, Hannah, Josiah, Ebenezer, and James.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Bishop, son of John and Anne Bishop, b. prior to arrival of his parents in this country. Neither the place nor date of his birth has been found, m. in Guilford, May 4, 1659, Tabitha Wilkenson, dau. of "Widow Parnell Wilken
2 CONC son," formerly of Bermuda Islands. Bebecame a planter in 1649 and a "freeman" ten years later. His name appears as one of the patentees to the Charter for the land at Guilford, by action of the General Court, Dec. 7, 1685, and whi
2 CONC ch was signed by Robt. Treat, Governor, and by John Allyn, as secretary. He appears to have been prominent in all good deeds, d. Guilford, June, 1690 and his widow d. Dec. 21, 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=160629139
