1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Deliverance Smith BIRTH	1667, Dartmouth, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA DEATH	30 Jun 1729 (aged 61–62), Dartmouth, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	Smith Family Cemetery, Dartmouth, Bristol County, Mas
2 CONC sachusetts, USA, MEMORIAL ID 49445985
2 CONT
2 CONT Deliverance Smith, eldest s. and child of John Smith and his 2nd wife Ruhamah Kirby, b. before Mar. 4, 1667/8 at Dartmouth, Mass. He d. at Dartmouth June 30, 1729. As a known Quaker, Deliverance is assumed to have been interred, w
2 CONC ithout gravestone, at the private Smith Family Burying Ground at South Dartmouth, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT By circa 1692, Deliverance m. Mary Tripp, dau. of Peleg Tripp and Anne Sisson, b. circa 1671 at Portsmouth, Rhode Island. She d. at Dartmouth, Mass. after Nov. 12, 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT An extended bio will be added later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deliverance and wife Mary had ten children b. of record at Dartmouth, Mass., their second child being:
2 CONT
2 CONT • ii. Deborah Smith, b. July 13, 1695, d. after Mar. 13, 1738/9; m. Sept. 20, 1716 under auspice of the Dartmouth meeting of the Society of Friends, Eleazer Slocum, Jr., s. of Eleazer Slocum and Eliphal Fitzgerald, b. Jan. 20, 169
2 CONC 3/4 at Dartmouth, Mass. where d. testate betw. Jan. 18 and Mar. 13, 1738/9. Eight children of the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents John Smith 1618–1692 Ruhamah Kirby Smith 1645 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Mary Tripp Smith 1670–1729 (m. 1692)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Hannah Smith Shearman 1681–1744
2 CONT
2 CONT Half Siblings Eleazer Smith 1654–1733
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Deborah Smith Slocum 1695 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49445985/deliverance-smith
