1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John King son of Captain Philip and Judith Whitman King was born in Taunton Massachusetts in 1681 and died according to his graveyard inscription in 1741 in his 60th year. Like his father he was friendly with the I
2 CONC ndians doing humanitarian work among them and educating two Campbell and Occeun at his own expense to become missionaries among their people. He married about 1700 Alice Dean of a well known Taunton family and they had thirteen ch
2 CONC ildren one of them Benjamin...
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=gxEwAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22John%20King%22%20Weymouth%20children%20Philip%20%22Judith%20Whitman%22&pg=PA182#v=onepage&q=%22John%20King%22%20Weymouth%20children%20Philip%20%22Judith%20Whitman%22&f=false  
2 CONC American Biography: A New Cyclopedia, Volume 6 edited by William Richard , Cutter, page 162]
