2 CONT From "Genealogical record of the Hodges Family in New England":
2 CONT
2 CONT Elkakah Leonard, senior, grandson of James Leonard who built  the first iron works in Massachusetts, was a stirring, energetic man.  His father built a forge on Trout Brook, Middleboro, and Elkanah  was placed in charge of it, alt
2 CONC hough only 23 or 24 years old. He  held town offices while still young, being selectman, as early as 1709.  He was agent of the town in various affairs, lieutenant of the military  company, etc Meanwhile he carried on his own priv
2 CONC ate business of  farming and dealing in real estate. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elkanah Leondard was born May 15, 1677 at Raynham. He died Dec. 14 or Dec 29, 1714 at Middleboro, Mass. He married March 25, 1703 Charity HODGES, the daughter of Elder Henry and Esther (Gallup) Hodges. She was born April 5, 1682 a
2 CONC t Taunton and died Feb.29,1739. She married 2nd Jabez Perkins of Norwich ,Conn. On his death she returned to Middleboro.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Leonard-343 Profile last modified 27 Feb 2020 | Created 21 Feb 2011 | Last significant change: 27 Feb 2020
2 CONT
2 CONT Elkanah Leonard
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 15 May 1677 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Leonard and Mary (Watson) Leonard
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Mary (Leonard) Tisdale, Thomas Leonard, John Leonard, George Leonard, Samuel Leonard, James Leonard, Unknown Leonard, Seth Leonard, Phoebe Leonard and Elizabeth (Leonard) Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Charity (Hodges) Perkins — married 25 Mar 1703 in Taunton, Bristol Co, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Elkanah Leonard, Joseph Leonard, Rebecca (Leonard) Perkins, Abiah (Leonard) Haskell, Simeon Leonard and Jemima (Leonard) Perkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 29 Dec 1714 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 27 Feb 2020 | Created 21 Feb 2011 | Last significant change: 27 Feb 2020
