1 OCCU a Hetman of Zaporizhian Host from 1727 to 1734. 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Апостол,_Даниил_Павлович Russian Wikipedia] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Danylo Pavlovich Apostol''' (Ukrainian: Данило Апостол; Russian: Данила Апостол; Romanian: Dănilă Apostol) (1654–1734), was a Hetman of Zaporizhian Host from 1727 to 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT The founder of the Russian noble house of the Apostles, after the suppression of continuity in the male line, who received permission to bear a double surname - Muravyov-Apostol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Danila the Apostle's father Pavel Efremovich (died in 1678[5]). Pavel Efremovich was originally from Moldova, he moved to the Cossacks of the Zaporozhye Army and during the Khmelnitsky uprising in 1653 married Cossack Maria Lesnit
2 CONC skaya, daughter of Mirgorod Colonel Grigory Lesnitsky. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife - Ulyana, daughter of Chimera Colonel Vasily Iskritsky, grandniece of Hetman Pavel Teteri. Ovdovev, Ulyana Vasilyevna was approved inherited and granted a pension of 3,000 rubles. She died in 1742. Seven daughters and four so
2 CONC ns were born in the marriage, including:
2 CONT # Ivan.
2 CONT # Pavel was elected a Mirgorod colonel on the day his father was elected to the hetman; there were no children.
2 CONT # Peter has been a Luboonian colonel since 1728.
2 CONT # Vasily (died young, left his son Jacob).
2 CONT # Martha; her husband is Poltava Colonel Vasily Kochubey.
2 CONT # Anna; her husband is Nezhynsky, Colonel Lukyan Zhurakovsky.
2 CONT # Praskovya; first husband - Mikhail Dunin-Borkovsky, the second - general Podskorbiy Mikhail Skoropadsky.
2 CONT # Tatiana; her husband is Bunchuk comrade Ivan Lomikovsky.
2 CONT # Maria; her husband is Prilutsk Colonel Andrei Gorlenko. Bishop Joasaph of Belgorod was born in this marriage.
2 CONT # Anna; her husband is military comrade Pyotr Kulyabko.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Apostles family died out with the death of the great-grandson of the hetman, after which the surname "Apostle" was taken by a descendant of Daniil Pavlovich in the female line - Ivan Muravyov.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Apostol's grandson Joachim A. Gorlenko (1705–1754), the son of his daughter Maria, entered the priesthood of the Russian Orthodox Church and became Ioasaph of Belgorod, who was glorified as a saint in 1911.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT On the postage stamp of Ukraine, 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000190088410854&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT konekäännös:
2 CONT
