2 CONT !According to Edward Warren Day's "One Thousand Years of Hubbard History, 866 to 1895 (New York: Harlan Page Hubbard, 1895) MARY HUBBARD  was descended from immigrant GEORGE HUBBARD [2,600], who is first recorded in Watertown, Mas
2 CONC s. in 1633.  GEORGE's wife MARY BISHOP [2,601], dau of JOHN and ANNE BISHOP [5,202; 5203], who d. in Guilford ct. 14 Sept. 1675.  JOHN and ANNE were in Wetherfield, and then removed to Guilford in 1639, where JOHN was one of the s
2 CONC even proprietors of the town.  He d. there in Feb. 1661 leaving as follows family:
2 CONT 5,202.1  John      m. Susannah Goldhom.
2 CONT 5,202.2  Stephen   m. Tabitha Wilkinson.
2 CONT 5,202.3  Betsey    m. James Steele.
2 CONT 5,202.4  MARY      [=2,601] m. GEORGE HUBBARD.
