2 CONT Nathaniel arrived in Wethersfield CT inin 1634. He died after August 1, 1644, but before Nov 20, 1644 when his inventory was presented at Hartford.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Robert Foote Jr and Joan (Brooke) Foote of Shalford, Co.Essex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Elizabeth Deming. She was a sister of John Deming of Wethersfield. After Nathaniel Foote's death, she married Thomas Welles (Governor of Connecticut 1655-1658).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Elizabeth Foote Churchill, Nathaniel Foote Jr, Mary Foote Stoddard Goodrich Tracy, Robert Foote, Frances Foote Dickinson Barnard(whose second husband was Francis Barnard), Sarah Foote Judson, and Rebecca Foote Smith Cook
2 CONC . 
