2 CONT The following was taken from the Hatfield Town Records:
2 CONT ''Elizabeth, wife to Daniel Beldenye head of the family, together
2 CONT with Daniel Belden, John Belden and Thankful Belden, their chidren, were all of
2 CONT them slaine by the enemie September 16, 1696."
2 CONT "Sept. 16, 1696. The Indians came along from up Green River to the town,
2 CONT and assaulted Mr. Daniel Belden 's house; took Mr. Belden, his son Nathaniel and
2 CONT daughter Esther captive, killed his wife and three children, and wounded Samuel
2 CONT and Abigail, but they recovered, altho' Samuel had a hatchet stuck in his head,
2 CONT and some of his brains came out at his wound. Samuel was born Apr. 10, 1687. From Mather's Magnalia:
2 CONT "The Indians making an Assault upon Deerfield, in this Present War, they
2 CONT struck a Hatchet some Inches into the Skull of a Boy there, even so deep that
2 CONT the Boy felt the force of a Wrench used by 'em to get it out. There he lay a
2 CONT long while Weltering in his Blood; they found him, they Dress 'd him; consider-
2 CONT able Quantities of his Brain came out from time to time when they opened the
2 CONT Wound; yet the Lad recovered, and is now a Living Monument of the Power
2 CONT and Goodness of God."
