1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not a known child of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Robert-Childe/6000000003858505101?through=6000000003937379502
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Potter married by 1635, Frances ____. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had six Children: Joseph, Mary Mansfield, Sarah Foote Blachley, Hope Robinson, Rebecca Adams, & Nathaniel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Anderson'd Great Migration Study Project
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, pg. 1137, 1459
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrived in America in 1635 on "Abigail" with her husband and 4 month old son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT #  William Potter (1608-1662)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William and Frances Potter:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph, b in England c. Feb,1635; m. Phebe Ives
2 CONT # Mary, b say 1637, bpt in New Haven, 22 Aug 1641; m abt 1657 Joseph Mansfield
2 CONT # Sarah, b say 1639, bpt in New Haven, 22 Aug 1641 (but not a twin); she m1 Lieut. Robert Foote of Branford; she m2 Aaron Blachley/Blakesley. Not named in her father's will but living 23 Aug 1706 when she obtained some piece of he
2 CONC r father's estate.
2 CONT # Hope, bpt 3 Oct 1641; m 3 Feb 1663 Daniel Robinson; (removed to NJ[citation needed])
2 CONT # Rebecca, bpt 1643[/4?]; m 27 Nov 1667 Thomas Adams; (removed to Crosswicks, NJ[citation needed])
2 CONT # Nathaniel, bpt 12 Nov 1644; m 1 Apr 1675 Elizabeth Howes
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT October 2020:
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no record to my knowledge that William and Frances Potter had a son Thomas or a daughter Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, Hope, Rebecca and Nathaniel are named in the 19 May 1662 Will of their father William Potter. Daughters Mary and Sarah are not named in William Potter's Will. However, they are named in other documents as the daughters of 
2 CONC William Potter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-104136
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Robert C. Anderson, the wife of William Potter was Frances Unknown.[1] Her surname and parents are unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that Frances's [2] maiden name was Child, and that she was the daughter of Thomas Child of Bedfordshire. However, Frances's origin remains unknown. This is according to Robert C, Anderson in his Great Migrati
2 CONC on series.[1]. In the case of Puritan Great Migration project profiles, we defer to Anderson, unless there is new evidence discovered.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth c. 1609 at Lewes, Suffolk, England is a guess, based on the ship's passenger list which reported her age as 26 in 1635.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT An article by Patricia Law Hatcher, published in 2004, identifies the parish records for the Potter and Beecher families at Lewes.[3]. William was baptized on 28 August 1608 at St. Thomas as in the Cliffe, Lewes, Sussex, England, 
2 CONC son of William Potter and possibly his 2nd wife, Ann/Hannah Langford.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
