1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Hazard
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Thomas Hazard and Martha (Potter) Hazard
2 CONT * Born 10 Jul 1637 in Portsmouth, Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT * Sister of Elizabeth (Hazard) Lawton, Robert Hazard, Martha (Hazard) Mowry, Thomas Hazard and George Hazard
2 CONT * Died 30 Jan 1685 in Portsmouth, Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Married
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Stephen Wilcox,''' on 30 Jan 1657-1658 in Portsmouth, Newport Co. Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Children
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''EDWARD WILCOX,''' b.1661/2; married Mary Hazard, daughter of Robert  
2 CONT *'''THOMAS WILCOX,''' died 1728; married Martha, daughter of Robert and Mary Hazard. 26. 
2 CONT *'''DANIEL WILCOX,''' married 1697, Mary Wodell.
2 CONT *'''WILLIAM WILCOX,''' married Jan. 25, 1698, Dorothy Palmer. 
2 CONT *'''STEPHEN WILCOX,''' married 1704, Elizabeth Crandall. 
2 CONT *'''HANNAH WILCOX,''' married Samuel Clarke, son of Jeremiah and Ann (Audley) Clarke, 
2 CONT *'''JEREMIAH WILCOX,''' married Mary Mallett, daughter of Thomas Mallett.
2 CONT
2 CONT >====[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003468372529&photo_id=6000000152415412822&position=0 The Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island, page 320] 
2 CONT >Stephen Wilcox & Hannah Hazard: dated 30 Jan 1658, as her father Thomas gives and bequeathed "in dowry with his daughter Hannah Hazard unto Stephen Wilcoke of Portsmouth thirty-four acres of land." in Portsmouth.
2 CONT >''The Early Records of the Town of Portsmouth''; by Portsmouth (R.I.); Perry, Amos, 1812-1899, ed; Brigham, Clarence S. (Clarence Saunders), 1877-1963, ed (Providence, R.I., E. L. Freeman & Sons, state printers, 1901) pp. 383, 38
2 CONC 4 #314. This date is used as their wedding date.
2 CONT
2 CONT >====Hannah Hazard's Dowry
2 CONT >This present writteinge Bareinge the Thirith day of January in the y[] of our Lord one thowsand Six hundred fifty eight witnesseth that Thomas Hazard of portsmouth on Rhoad Island: hath by these presents give and bequeathed in do
2 CONC wrie with his daughter Hannah Hazard, vnto Stphen wilcoke of portsmouth Thirty fower acres of land more or less Situate with in the bounds of limites of ye Towne of portsmouth afore-said and lyinge in the farme of the aforesaid Th
2 CONC omas Hazard and adjoyneinge vnto the wadeing or mill river, Eight acres wherof being butted and bownded by the land of Samuel Gine one the south and north and on the East End by the Comon and Highway to the mill, the other twenty 
2 CONC Sixe acres being butted and bownded by the fence as now it stands one the south and Southwest and on the west and northwest by the land of the Afore said Thomas Hazard and on the north by the land of mr porter and on the East and 
2 CONC South-East by the abouse sayd eight acres and the land of Samuel Geinne afore said Twenty acres.
2 CONT >>(NOTE: Good thing Hannah got this upon her marriage since her step-mother Martha Sheriff came in and alienated Thomas from his children! See the two wills of Thomas Hazard.)
2 CONT
