1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Stephen Wilcox=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Edward Wilcox and Susanna Thompson
2 CONT * Born:  6 FEB 1633 in Crofts, Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT * '''Baptism Record:''' [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000004382506593?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000081492264841 '''Baptized on 26 Dec 1634 in Croft, Lincoln, ENGland''']
2 CONT * Death:  died: 6 Feb 1689-90, Westerly, Washington Co., RI, United States
2 CONT * He was of Portsmouth, Rhode Island, in 1655. He had a grant of sixteen acres December 10, 1657, and in 1658, from his father-in-law a dower of thirty acres. He was freeman, May 18, 1658. In May 1669, he was among the free inhabi
2 CONC tants of Westerly in Rhode Island
2 CONT * In 1670 he was complained of, with his partakers, by John Richards, Treasurer of Harvard College, for unjustly possessing five hundred acres in the Pequot country, on the east side of Pawcatuck River, within the bounds of Stonin
2 CONC gton. This controversy, which resolved itself into a question of boundary and jurisdiction between Massachusetts and Rhode Island, continued for several years, and was ﬁnally settled in favor of the latter state. In 1670 and 1672 
2 CONC he was deputy, one of the ﬁrst from Westerly.
2 CONT * Brother of Daniel Wilcox [half], Daniel Wilcox, John Wilcox and Mary (Wilcox) Sherman
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/details/hazardfamilyofrh00byurobi?view=theater#page/12/mode/2up '''The Hazard Family of Rhoad Island''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Stephen married [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000004382506593?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000173104280857 '''Hannah Hazard,'''] daughter of Thomas Hazard and Martha Potter, on 30 Jan 1658 or 1659 in Boston, New E
2 CONC nglad. (Hannah Hazard was born on 10 Jul 1637 in Boston, Suffolk Co., MA 9 and died in 1685. https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000004382506593?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000102692310872
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Hannah Hazard=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Edward Wilcox;''' was born 5 Nov 1662 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., RI and died on 5 Nov 1715 in Westerly, Washington Co., RI. Married Mary Hazard, daughter of Robert Hazard, married (2) Thomasin Stevens, daughter of Richard St
2 CONC evens of Taunton Massachusetts.
2 CONT * '''Thomas Wilcox;''' was born on 18 Feb 1664 in North Kingston, RI and died in 1728 in Exeter, Washington Co., RI. Married Matha Hazard, daughter of Robert & Mary Hazard
2 CONT * '''Daniel Wilcox;''' was born about 1666 in Westerly, Washington Co., RI and died after 1717 in Stonington, New London, CT.  Married in 1697 Mary Wodell
2 CONT * '''William Wilcox;''' was born about 1668 in Westerly, Washington Co., RI and died on 27 Dec 1757 in North Stonington, New London Co., CT. Married Dorothy Palmer on January 25, 1698
2 CONT * '''Stephen Wilcox;''' was born about 1670 in Westerly, Washington Co., RI. Married in 1704 Elizabeth Crandall
2 CONT * '''Hannah Wilcox;''' was born about 1672 in Westerly, Washington Co., RI and died in Newport, Newport Co., RI. Married Samuel Clarke, son of Jeremiah & Ann Audley
2 CONT * '''Jeremiah Wilcox;''' was born between 1675-1680 in Westerly, Washington Co., RI. Married Mary Mallett, daughter of Thomas Mallett.
2 CONT * '''Bethiah (Wilcox) Cottrell,''' born circa 1678
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003468372529&photo_id=6000000152415412822&position=0 The Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island, page 320] Stephen Wilcox & Hannah Hazard: dated 30 Jan 1658, as
2 CONC  her father Thomas gives and bequeathed "in dowry with his daughter Hannah Hazard unto Stephen Wilcoke of Portsmouth thirty-four acres of land." in Portsmouth.The early records of the town of Portsmouth; by Portsmouth (R.I.); Perr
2 CONC y, Amos, 1812-1899, ed; Brigham, Clarence S. (Clarence Saunders), 1877-1963, ed (Providence, R.I., E. L. Freeman & Sons, state printers, 1901) pp. 383, 384 #314. This date is used as their wedding date.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Hannah Hazard's Dowry=
2 CONT
2 CONT This present writteinge Bareinge the Thirith day of January in the y[] of our Lord one thowsand Six hundred fifty eight witnesseth that Thomas Hazard of portsmouth on Rhoad Island: hath by these presents give and bequeathed in dow
2 CONC rie with his daughter Hannah Hazard, vnto Stphen wilcoke of portsmouth Thirty fower acres of land more or less Situate with in the bounds of limites of ye Towne of portsmouth afore-said and lyinge in the farme of the aforesaid Tho
2 CONC mas Hazard and adjoyneinge vnto the wadeing or mill river, Eight acres wherof being butted and bownded by the land of Samuel Gine one the south and north and on the East End by the Comon and Highway to the mill, the other twenty S
2 CONC ixe acres being butted and bownded by the fence as now it stands one the south and Southwest and on the west and northwest by the land of the Afore said Thomas Hazard and on the north by the land of mr porter and on the East and S
2 CONC outh-East by the abouse sayd eight acres and the land of Samuel Geinne afore said Twenty acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT (NOTE: Good thing Hannah got this upon her marriage since her step-mother Martha Sheriff came in and alienated Thomas from his children! See the two wills of Thomas Hazard.)
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah mentioned in her father’s will and received a legacy of 1 shilling likely due to her objections to his marriage to Martha Sheriff.  Named as Hannah Wilcox.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized on St. Stephen's Day
2 CONT
2 CONT He is not in the list of Rhode Island Freemen made in 1655 (R.I.. Col. Rec. 1:299), but was admitted an inhabitant of Portsmouth on 13 Dec, 1656 (Portsmouth Records, P. 75). On 10 Dec, 1657, he was granted land with Thomas Kent. H
2 CONC e is listed as freemen there in 1658, and of the colony at Weslerly on the organization of that town, 1669. His farm at Watch Hill, Westerly, passed out of the Wilcox family in 1880. He was deputy to the general assembly in 1670 a
2 CONC nd 1672.On 30 Jan, 1657/8  Thomas Hazard gave him 34 acres in Portsmouth in dowry with his daughter, Hannah (Portsmouth Rec., printed, p. 383). He removed to Westerly, RI, upon the settlement of that town and was an inhabitant the
2 CONC re on 18 May 1669. He is the ancestor of the Wilcox family of Washington Co., RI, and Stonington, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieutenant-Governor Edward Wilcox, of Charlestown, RI, was great-great-grandson of this Stephen (through Edward his son). He was a prominent merchant; served many terms in the legislature between 1794 and 1823; and was presidentia
2 CONC l elector, 1816 [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Another of his great-grandsons was Isaiah Wilcox (through Edward his son) who entered the Baptist ministry; was baptized in February, 1766, and ordained February 14, 1771; was first pastor of the "Wilcox Church" of Westerly, and i
2 CONC n 1785, under his ministry, more than two hundred members were added to the church [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen was either arrested or sued June 21, 1670, for unjustly possessing, with others, five hundred acres of land in Stou (t) ington (Stonington?).This controversy which resolved itself into a question of boundary and jurisdicti
2 CONC on between Massachusetts and Rhode Island continued for several years and was finally settled in favor of the latter state [2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of Stephen's descendants other than those of his son, William, seem to have remained in Rhode Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Stephen Wilcox, son of Edward Wilcox, was born in 1633 and died in 1690.He had a grant of 16 acres, Dec 10, 1657, and in 1657 from his father-in-law, Thomas Hazard, a deed of 30 acres as a dowery with the daughter. He was a free 
2 CONC man May 18, 1658.In May 1669, he was among the free inhabitants of Westerly, RI.He was  (obliterated) June 21, 1670 for unjustly possessing, with others, five hundred acres of land in Stovington. This controversy, which resolved i
2 CONC tself into a question of boundary and jurisdiction between Mass. and RI, continued for several years and was finally settled in favor of the latter state. In 167? and 167? he was of the first from Westerly. In a paper dated Feb. 6
2 CONC , 1690 he is mentioned as 'lately deceased.'In 1648, he married Hannah, daughter of Thomas and Martha Hazard of Portsmouth. Thom Hazard was a ship carpenter by trade and came from Wales to Boston about 1635.In the Hutchinson, he w
2 CONC as driven from Mass. and settled upon Aquideeck."
2 CONT
2 CONT This was transcribed from notes recopied by Kate Wilcox Thorsen, 4/26/1980.Researched and copied by Agnes Wilcox Limas 9 May 1958 for Jeffrey Wilcox. Also see NEHGR Vol. 147, pp 188-191.
2 CONT
2 CONT Received a grant of land with Thomas Kent at 2s per acre [4]
2 CONT Received a deed for 34 acres from Thomas Hazard as dower for the latter's daughter Hannah. Listed among the inhabitants of the town. He was complained of, with his partakers, by John Richards, Treasurer of Harvard College, for unj
2 CONC ustly possessing 500 acres in Pequot County, east of the Pawcatuck River, within the bounds of Stonington. Served as Deputy Mentioned as of 6 Feb 1690 as lately deceased. [4]
