2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nathaniel, son of Edward and Katherine Reynolds starbuck, through whom almost all Starbucks in the United StatesTrace their ancestry. Nathaniel became an influential man on the Island and one of the wealthiest if not individually 
2 CONC the wealthyest man on the Island. He inherited much of his wealth from his father, but undoubtedly expanded it through the store owned and operated by he and his wife. He married Mary Coffin (b.20 Feb, 1644/5 d. 13 Sep, 1717 at Na
2 CONC ntucket, Ma) in 1662 at Nantucket, Ma He was buried in the Friends' First Burial Ground, Nantucket, Ma. For children --see spouse-Mary Coffin Starbuck. The first Quaker or Friends, Burial Ground occupied one acre near the south en
2 CONC d of Maxcey's Pond and was used for internments from about 1711 untill 1760. A second burial site. located at Quaker and Madaket Roads, was added in 1730. There are very few markers to account for thousands of Quakers buried in th
2 CONC e two cemeteries. Quakers disapproved of the use of headstones, considering them idolatrous(graves were most likely set off by unmarked fieldstones, although nineteenth-century sects did use gravestones.
2 CONT --------------------
