1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She is the direct descendant of Mayflower Pilgrims Francis Cooke and Richard Warren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John Cooke, "Mayflower" Passenger and Sarah Cooke 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Cooke, daughter of John Cooke and Sarah Warren, was born about 1632/1635 in Plymouth, Massachusetts.[1] Arthur Hathaway married Sarah Cooke on November 20, 1652, in Duxbury, Plymouth, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Hathaway,[3][4]
2 CONT John Hathaway,[5][6]
2 CONT Sarah Hathaway,
2 CONT Mary Hathaway,[7][8][9]
2 CONT Lydia Hathaway,[10][11]
2 CONT Thomas Hathaway,[12][13]
2 CONT Jonathan Hathaway,[14][15]
2 CONT Father's Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Before John Cooke's death, he deeded most of his lands to his children, and there are several conveyances "to my loving sonne in law Arthur Hathaway." [16]
2 CONT In John Cooke's will he gives to Arthur Hathaway "and Sarah my daughter" "all the land in the point at or near the burying place in Dartmouth which I bought of John Russell." This point was to the north of Arthur Hathaway's farm, 
2 CONC and is probably where John Cooke was buried. [17]
2 CONT Husband's Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur's will, dated 9 Dec., 1709, proved 6 Feb., 1711, names wife Sarah and children John, Thomas, Jonathan, Mary Hammond, Lydia Sisson and Hannah Cadman.[18] In his will, Arthur describes himself as "very weak of body, but of pe
2 CONC rfect mind and memory." His wife, Sarah, who was probably some ten years his junior, was living when the will was drawn. To his daughter, Mary who had married Samuel Hammond, he left a legacy of five shillings. [19]
2 CONT
2 CONT Unsourced
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 20 Nov 1635
2 CONT Death: 26 Feb 1712
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cooke-21
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah (Cooke) Hathaway (abt. 1635 - aft. 1709)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sarah Hathaway formerly Cooke===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1635 in Plymouth, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Jean Cooke and Sarah (Warren) Cooke
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Elizabeth (Cooke) Wilcox, Hester (Cooke) Taber, Mary (Cooke) Taber and Mercy (Cooke) West
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Arthur Hathaway Jr. — married 20 Nov 1652 in Plymouth, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of John Hathaway, Arthur Hathaway, Sarah Hathaway, Hannah (Hathaway) Cadman, Lydia (Hathaway) Sisson, Mary (Hathaway) Hammond, Thomas Hathaway and Jonathan Hathaway
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 9 Dec 1709 at about age 74 in Dartmouth, Bristol, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 22 Sep 2021 | Created 11 Jun 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah (Cooke) Hathaway was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
