1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Photo ref.: Document dated "May Seventh 1728,"  Receipt of Capt. John Akin ... for money received for the Town of Dartmouth, signed by "Stephen West" as one among two other "Trustees for the Town of Dartmouth".
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo ref.:  1728/9 Bristol Massachusetts court document, on hand laid paper with county seal. This document has John Akin, Samuel Cornel, & STEPHEN WEST, yeomen, all of Dartmouth, in a plea of debt and forfeiture of a bond of 8 p
2 CONC ounds current money of Massachusetts Bay, Henry Gidley defendant of Dartmouth, husbandman, for forfeiture of the bond amount owed to the claimants.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Akin and STEPHEN WEST are related by the marriage of John's son, Benjamin to Stephen's granddaughter, Eunice Taber.                                                                                                              
2 CONC                                                    https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LCM8-HVW                                                                                     https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/1
