1 OCCU Ensign
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The below seem to be the only children verified.  Josiah and Elijah are not authentic. Esther, Joanna, and Abigail are also in doubt.   Many sources agree that he had seven children.  And many sources agree that he
2 CONC  had only one son. [Hatte Blejer June 6, 2016]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary, — married John Leonard
2 CONT # Elizabeth, — married John Hall and/or Samuel Richmond  (Thomas Rogers Society only lists Samuel Richmond)
2 CONT # Experience, — married Nicholas White
2 CONT # Lydia, — married Nathaniel Williams and John Macomber  (this seems to be incorrect since her niece Abigail Paddelford married a John Macomber born 1719)
2 CONT # Hannah, — married Jonathan Paddelford 
2 CONT # Judith, -- married (1) Ebenezer Williams and (2) Ebenezer Robinson
2 CONT # John -- married Alice Dean
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  http://gatewayfirstfouryears.com/files/Barnes-King-Families-of-Chenango-County-New-York.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT I have detached Josiah, Elijah, and Johanna who were added to Geni by "Abraham Lincoln," which indicates an issue in itself.  I have detached Abigail who supposedly married Jonathan Paddelford. There is no reliable evidence for he
2 CONC r and sources agree that there were 7 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Captain Philip King, son of John of Weymouth=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: 	unknown (circa 1645)
2 CONT * Death: 	Dec. 26, 1710
2 CONT * Taunton
2 CONT * Bristol County
2 CONT * Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Information supporting birth of Philip (birth c.1645) at Weymouth, Suffolk County'''
2 CONT
2 CONT "John King, who settled prior to 1640 in that part of the Weymouth, Massachusetts" from "American Biography: A New Cyclopedia, Volume 6" edited by William Richard Cutter http://books.google.com/books?id=gxEwAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22John%20K
2 CONC ing%22%20Weymouth%20children%20Philip%20%22Judith%20Whitman%22&pg=PA182#v=onepage&q=%22John%20King%22%20Weymouth%20children%20Philip%20%22Judith%20Whitman%22&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT John King, Sr., was a resident of Weymouth from 1639 to 1669. Philip, b. at Weymouth, near 1645. "History of Weymouth, MA Vol. 3 (1928) pages 349 to 352" http://www.laurenceholbrook.net/Weymouth1923/weygenk.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Mary King:
2 CONT
2 CONT         1) John, jr.,2 received grants 14 Dec. 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT         2) Samuel, marriageable, 17 Sept. 1658.
2 CONT
2 CONT         3) Mary, b. at Weymouth, 15 June, 1639; m. there 30 Nov. 1658,
2 CONT            Josiah Chapin of Braintree and Mendon; d. 30 May, 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT         4) Abigail, b. at Weymouth, 14 Mar. 1641.
2 CONT
2 CONT         5) Philip, b. at Weymouth, near 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT "History of Weymouth, MA Vol. 3 (1928) pages 349 to 352" http://www.laurenceholbrook.net/Weymouth1923/weygenk.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT Phillip, Ens.  1645
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B240.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT  * Judith Whitman King (1643 - 1711)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT * Mount Pleasant Cemetery 
2 CONT * Taunton
2 CONT * Bristol County
2 CONT * Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT * Created by: Lydia Cobb-Quequechan Ch...
2 CONT * Record added: Jun 21, 2011 
2 CONT * Find A Grave Memorial# 71727123
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=71727123  Find A Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Philip King and Judith Whitman King
2 CONT # Elizabeth born before 1680, m. Samuel Richmond
2 CONT # Hannah born 15 Apr 1681 m. Jonathan Padelford
2 CONT # Abigail born 1671
2 CONT # Esther born circa 1674 m. Stephen Williams
2 CONT # Judith born 1690 m. Mr. Alden
2 CONT # Experience born 1678 m. Nicholas White
2 CONT # Mary born 18 May 1668 m. John Leonard
2 CONT # John born 1681 m. Alice Dean
2 CONT # Elijah born 1686
2 CONT # Johannah born circa 1682 m. John Alger
2 CONT # Josiah born 1688
2 CONT # Lydia born 03 Mar 1688 m. (1) Nathaniel Rogers and (2) John Macomber
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History of the Descendants of John Whitman of Weymouth, Mass'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''by Charles Farnam  1889'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith was probably the youngest daughter of the Ancestor; she ma. prior to 1672 '''Philip King of Weymouth'''; there is a tradition that he settled first at Braintree, but in a deed dated March 1, 1672, he is referred to as being
2 CONC  '* of Weymouth; '''in 1680 he purchased land in that part of Taunton now called Raynham''' '''and removed his family to that town ; he d. Dec. 26, 1710'''''' ; his will, dated Jan. 2, 1706, probated May 7, 1711, mentions his wife
2 CONC  Judith, to whom he gives the improvements upon his property.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are two grave sights for "Phillip King".
2 CONT
2 CONT Learn about sponsoring this memorial... 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  1645 Weymouth Norfolk County Massachusetts, USA  Death:  Dec. 26, 1710 Taunton Bristol County Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Phillip King, the first American ancestor of George Washington King, of Raynham, emigrated from England in company with a brother, Cyrus, and settled at Braintree some time prior to 1680. He came to Raynham, then Taunton, bought 
2 CONC land, built a house, and became a permanent settler. The deed of sale to him of this land bears date 1680. He married Judith, daughter of Rev. William Whitman of Milton. He was a man of high character, courage, and decision, and w
2 CONC as well adapted to be a leader in the pioneer days. He was a man of sterling honesty, and won the love of the Indians by his just dealings, and, during all the troublous times of Indian warfare, was never molested by them, nor his
2 CONC , property injured. He was captain, and, probably, a deputy to Plymouth. A large number attended his funeral, which was conducted with military honors. He had seven children." History of Bristol County 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Neck O Land Cemetery  Taunton Bristol County Massachusetts,  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Philip King:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip King (2), John (1) of Weymouth, Mass. b. near 1645 at Weymouth, Mass. Lived at Braintree and Taunton in 1680. d. Dec. 26, 1710 at Taunton (Raynham). His will made in 1706 
2 CONT m. ante 1671 JUDITH WHITMAN (WHITEMAN) (2) daughter of JOHN WHI'IMAN (1) 1603-1692, from England to Dorchester, Mass.1635; freeman; 1639; removed to Weymouth about 1641; Ensign Military Co., 1645; appointed by Gen. Court to "sne s
2 CONC mall causes", and his wife RurH REED. Philip and Judith sell land, in Weymouth, March 1st 1672-73; (Suffolk Deeds 8: 210-11) He was a member of a committee at Heymouth No-v. 27, 1682. He soon removed ·to Taunton. (Hist. of Weymout
2 CONC h v. 3, pp. 352-53). He is called the brother of THOMAS KING of Scituate, Mass. who came from Cold Norton, County Essex, England (E. E. Pierce Papers, Ne'" Bedford, Mass. )
2 CONT Children: Seven; Mary, Elizabeth, Experience, Hannah, Lydia, Judith, John. Although several were probably born in Weymouth their record has not been found, however, .in a bound copy of the Taunton, Mass. Evening Ne,-ls of July 20,
2 CONC  1899 found in the Ne\OTberry Library, Chicago, Ill. the names of these children are given. There is also a copy of his will dated 1706 in which they are named.  1..Mary King· (3) b..May 18, 1668; d. Feb. 6, 1769 m. JOHN LEONARD o
2 CONC fTaunton  2. Elizabeth King (3) m. Dec. 16, 1696 JOHN (HOHN) HALL of Taunton; 3 children  3. Experience K.ing (3) m. June 2, 1703 NICHOLAS WHITE of Taunton; · 9 children 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Hannah King (3) b. 1671 at Taunton; d. 1725  m. ante 1706 JONATHAN PADELFORD Jr. (3) b. 1679 son of JONATHAN PADELFORD (2) b. 1656, of Braintree and Taunton. and his wife HANAH THAYER, daughter of THOMAS THAYER of Thornbury, Co
2 CONC unty Gloucester, England and of Boston and Braintree, Mass. For the records of Padelford family and their wiives, MARGERY WHEELER, MARY BLANDFORD, daughter of JOHN BIANDFORD of Sutton, Mansfield, County Wilts, England and of Sudbu
2 CONC ry, Mass. see ("The Abridged Compendium of American Genealogy - First Families of America" by F. A. Virkus &Co. V. III page 195)  Children: Ten - one of which was JUDITH PADELFORD (4) who m. DAVID ALDEN (4), JOHN ALDEN (3), JOSEPH
2 CONC  (2), JOHN (1) tbe 7th signer of the Mayflower Compact.  5. Lydia King (3) 1st. m. Jan. 9, 1709-10, NATHANIEL WILLIAMS JR. 2nd m. JOHN MACOMBER  6. Judith King (3) 1st m. Jan. 1712-13 EBENEZER WILLIAMS of Taunton married 2nd Col. 
2 CONC EBENEZER ROBINSON 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. John King (3) b. about 1681  CYRUS KING is called a brother to PHILIP KING in "Genealogy of the Family of Kings" who lived in Raynham, Mass. from 1680 to 1685 by E. Sanford. Published in Taunton,  Mass. 1866. No further record 
2 CONC of CYRUS has been found.
2 CONT
