2 CONT == Biography == Thomas, son of James and Jane Leonard, was baptised at Kinver, Staffordshire, England on August 7, 1641.<ref>"England Births and Christenings, 1538-1975", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903
2 CONC /1:1:J94T-XFC : 19 March 2020), Thomas Leonard, 1641.</ref>
2 CONT Thomas came to New England with his father, mother, and uncle Henry "when a small boy."<ref name=Deane>Deane, William Reed. Genealogical Memoir of the Leonard Family. Boston, MA: Self-Published for the New England Historic-Genealo
2 CONC gical Register, 1851. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalmemo00dean/page/6/mode/2up?q=autograph Page 7.]</ref> He married Mary Watson of Plymouth in August of 1662.<ref>Vital Records of Taunton Massachusetts to the Year 1850
2 CONC  Volume II-Marriages. Boston, MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_M299.shtml Page 299.]</ref><ref>The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New Englan
2 CONC d 1620-1633, Volumes I-III. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New EnglandHistoric Genealogical Society, 2010), (Originally Published as: New England Historic Genealogical Society. Robert Charles Anderson, The Great Migratio
2 CONC n Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III, 3 vols., 1995). ''By Subscription. '' [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB393/i/12107/1946/1415522091 Page 1946.]</ref> They had eleven known children who were born in
2 CONC  Taunton.<ref name=Deane/> Thomas worked for his father at the forge and was manager of the Taunton Iron Works for thirty years. He held commissions, including Major in the Bristol Company Regiment, was a probate Judge, town clerk
2 CONC , deacon of the Church.<ref>Koster, Fannie Leonard. Annals of the Leonard Family. Brooklyn, NY: Self-Published, 1911. [https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/item/375118-annals-of-the-leonard-family?viewer=1&offset=0#p
2 CONC age=72&viewer=picture&o=info&n=0&q= Page 39 ]</ref> Thomas' military career was especially storied, spanning 48 years. He was elected Ensign of the first Military Company in 1665. He also served as Captain and Major of the First R
2 CONC egiment of the County of Bristol.<ref>Emery, Samuel Hopkins. History of Taunton, Massachusetts From its Settlement to the Present Time. Syracuse, NY: D. Mason & Co., Publishers, 1893. [https://books.google.com/books?id=iqsvAQAAMAA
2 CONC J&pg=PA372&dq=Emery+%22History+of+Taunton%22+%22August+3,+1611%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjAqI_PpvPrAhXEG80KHb66BYcQ6AEwAHoECAAQAg#v=onepage&q=Emery%20%22History%20of%20Taunton%22%20%22August%203%2C%201611%22
2 CONC &f=false Page 372.]</ref>  Thomas died at Taunton on November 24, 1713.<ref>Vital Records of Taunton Massachusetts to the Year 1850 Volume III-Deaths. Boston, MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1929. [https://ma-vitalr
2 CONC ecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_D129.shtml Page 129.]</ref> He is buried in the Neck O Land Cemetery, Taunton, Bristol County , MA 
2 CONT === Children ===# Mary b 3 Aug 1663<ref>Vital Records of Taunton Massachusetts to the Year 1850 Volume I Births. Boston, MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/T
2 CONC aunton_B256.shtml Page 256.]</ref># Thomas b 22 Jan 1665;<ref>Taunton, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B259.shtml  Page 259.]</ref> m Joanna Pitchard# John b 18 May 1668;<ref>Taunton, 1928. [ht
2 CONC tps://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B254.shtml Page 254.]</ref>m Mary King# George b 18 Apr 1671;<ref>Taunton, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B252.shtml Page 252.]</ref
2 CONC > m AnnaTisdale# Samuel b 1 Feb 1673;<ref name=Vital>Taunton, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B257.shtml Page 258.]</ref> m Katherine Deane# Elkanah Leonard b 15 May 1677<ref name=Taunton>Taunt
2 CONC on, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B251.shtml Page 251.]</ref># James b 17 Dec 1679;<ref>Taunton, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B253.shtml Page 253.]</re
2 CONC f> d 1682# Daughter; stillborn 10 Apr 1681<ref>Taunton, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B259.shtml Page 259.]</ref>
2 CONT # Seth b 28 Apr 1682;<ref name=Vital/> d Nov 1682# Phebe b 3 Mar 1684;<ref>Taunton, 1928. [https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_B252.shtml Page 252.]</ref> d 1685
2 CONT # Elizabeth b 15 Jul 1686;<ref name=Taunton/> m Jonathan Williams
