2 CONT [https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Апостол,_Даниил_Павлович Russian Wikipedia] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Danylo Pavlovich Apostol''' (Ukrainian: Данило Апостол; Russian: Данила Апостол; Romanian: Dănilă Apostol) (1654–1734), was a Hetman of Zaporizhian Host from 1727 to 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT The founder of the Russian noble house of the Apostles, after the suppression of continuity in the male line, who received permission to bear a double surname - Muravyov-Apostol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Danila the Apostle's father Pavel Efremovich (died in 1678[5]). Pavel Efremovich was originally from Moldova, he moved to the Cossacks of the Zaporozhye Army and during the Khmelnitsky uprising in 1653 married Cossack Maria Lesnit
2 CONC skaya, daughter of Mirgorod Colonel Grigory Lesnitsky. 
