1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Joane Brooke
2 CONT * Christening 11 May 1555, St. Leonard's Eastcheap; London
2 CONT * Death:  October 10, 1634
2 CONT *Burial:   St Leonard Churchyard, Shoreditch, Greater London, England Note: No stones remain. The area was heavily damaged during WWI
2 CONT * Parents: John Brooke and Elizabeth Whatman 
2 CONT * She was from Salford, Essex
2 CONT * She was a member of the leatherseller company of London.
2 CONT * She is mentioned in the wills of both her parents, and her husband's will of 1608/1609.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.footefamily.org/joan_brooke.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Foote of Shalford
2 CONT
2 CONT A Yoeman in old England was a Freeholder, next under the rank of Gentleman, and in the early times one who owned a small landed estate. Robert of Shalford was such a man. He owned property in Shalford and Royston. He was the son o
2 CONC f John Foote of Royston and the father of Nathaniel Foote the Settler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Joan Brooke June 18, 1576 in St Leonard's Eastcheap, London, Eng, daughter of John Brooke and Elizabeth Watman. Joan was born June 18, 1559 in London, England, and died October 10, 1634 in St Leonard's Parish, London, E
2 CONC ngland. She was a member of the leatherseller company of London. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the brother of John Foote of London, and the father of Nathaniel Foote "The Settler." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Joan's Children
2 CONT
2 CONT No.	Name	Parent	Birth	Death	Wife
2 CONT * (4)	JR. Robert Foote	(2)	1577	1646	Elizabeth Child
2 CONT * Elizabeth Foote	(2)	1579	1658	Thomas Jennings
2 CONT * (5)	James Foote	(2)	1580	---	Unknown
2 CONT * (6)	Mary Foote	(2)	1585	---	John Hewes
2 CONT * Francis Foote	(2)	1587	1624	Unknown
2 CONT * (7)	Joshua Foote	(2)	1591	1655	Unknown
2 CONT * (8)	Joseph Foote	(2)	1588	1639	Anne
2 CONT * (9)	Daniel Foote	(2)	1590	1648	Unknown
2 CONT * (10)	Nathaniel Foote	(2)	1592	1644	Elizabeth Deming
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * For more tree, http://fam.eastmill.com/f296.htm#f4981 --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Brooke Foote Memorial
2 CONT
2 CONT . Birth: 	Jun. 18, 1560 Greater London, England Death: 	Oct. 10, 1634 Greater London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Brooke Birth Date: 11 May 155 5 Birth Place:   St Leonards, Eastcheap, Londonmap Christening:   11 May 1555 in London, England, at St. Leonard Eastcheap church. Death:  October 10, 1634 Burial:   Burial: St Leonard Churchyard
2 CONC , Shoreditch, Greater London, England Note: No stones remain. The area was heavily damaged during WWII Children:  Nine Children Marrage:   Robert Foote of Shalford on June 18, 1576 Generation:   Second Generation In England Father
2 CONC : John Brooke  Mother: Elizabeth Whatman Marrage: 18 JUN 1576, St. Leonard Eastcheap ,London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Brooke married Robert Foote a Yeoman in old England and was a Freeholder, next under the rank of Gentleman, and in the early times a person who owned a small estate with attached lands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert of Shalford was such a man. He owned property in both towns of Shalford and Royston. He was born the son of John Foote of Royston sometime before 1558 AD. He died about 1608. He was the brother of John Foote of London, and 
2 CONC the father of Nathaniel Foote "The Settler."
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Joans Children
2 CONT
2 CONT No.	Ancestor's Name	Parent	Birth	Death	Wife (4)	JR. Robert Foote	(2)	1577	1646	Elizabeth Child ----	Elizabeth Foote	(2)	1579	1658	Thomas Jennings (5)	James Foote	(2)	1580	---	Unknown (6)	Mary Foote	(2)	1585	---	John Hewes ----	Fra
2 CONC ncis Foote	(2)	1587	1624	Unknown (7)	Joshua Foote	(2)	1591	1655	Unknown (8)	Joseph Foote	(2)	1588	1639	Anne (9)	Daniel Foote	(2)	1590	1648	Unknown (10)	Nathaniel Foote	(2)	1592	1644	Elizabeth Deming
2 CONT
