1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Robert Foote  
2 CONT * Gender:	Male   
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1553  Royston, Hertfordshire, England (United Kingdom)   
2 CONT * Death:	before February 16, 1608   St. Leonard's, East Cheap, London, England  
2 CONT * Place of Burial:	St Andrew Churchyard, Shalford, Essex, England 	 
2 CONT * Son of John Foote, of Royston and Helen Warren 
2 CONT * Husband of Joane (Brooke) Foote 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.footefamily.org/robert_shalford.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT Yoeman in old England was a Freeholder, next under the rank of Gentleman, and in the early times one who owned a small landed estate. Robert of Shalford was such a man. He owned property in Shalford and Royston. He was the son of 
2 CONC John Foote of London and the father of Nathaniel Foote the Settler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Joan Brooke June 18, 1576 in St Leonard's Eastcheap, London, Eng, daughter of John Brooke and Elizabeth Wetman. She was born June 18, 1559 in London, England, and died October 10, 1634 in St Leonard's Parish, London, En
2 CONC gland. She was a member of the leatherseller company of London. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the brother of John Foote of London, and the father of Nathaniel Foote "The Settler." 
2 CONT
2 CONT No. Ancestor's Name  Parent  Birth Death Wife 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Joan's Children 
2 CONT
2 CONT # (4) JR. Robert Foote  (2) 1577 1646 Elizabeth Child  
2 CONT # Elizabeth Foote  (2)  1579 1658 Thomas Jennings  
2 CONT # (5) James Foote (2)  1580 - Unknown  
2 CONT # (6) Mary Foote  (2)  1585 - John Hewes  
2 CONT # Francis Foote - (2) 1587 1624 Unknown  
2 CONT # (7)  Joshua Foote (2) 1591 1655 Unknown  
2 CONT # (8) Joseph Foote  (2)  1588 1639 Anne  
2 CONT # (9)  Daniel Foote  (2)  1590 1648 Unknown  
2 CONT # (10) Nathaniel Foote  (2)  1592 1644 Elizabeth Deming 
2 CONT
2 CONT  -------------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of his marriage, Robert Foote was Citizen and Fishmonger of St. Mary Boettals in Thames Street, London; later he was of Wethersfield, Essex; still later of Shalford, Essex. According to TAG 54, St. Mary Boetalls in Tha
2 CONC mes Street is not easy to locate. According to "A Plan of London in the Latter Part of the Middle Age," there is no St. Mary's on Thames Street. There was a St. Botolph's (often misspelled Bowtall, etc.) at Billingsgate on Thames 
2 CONC Street a few blocks from St. Leonard's. There was also a St. Mary's Bothaw on Cannon Street, four or five blocks from St. Leonard's. The author suggests the christenings of Nathaniel Foote and his siblings might be found in the Lo
2 CONC ndon area rather than in Shalford or Wethersfield in Essex. Robert's will was made at Shalford, dated 27 January 1608/1609 and probated 15 February 1608/1609 (PCC 21 Dorset = Waters 1276 f.). It mentions wife Joan, a lease in Roys
2 CONC ton; the poor of the parish; the poor in Wethersfield. Joan was to have the yearly rent out of tenements held of Sir Robert Chester, knt., in the town of Royston; sons Robert, James, Daniel, Nathaniel, Francis, Josua, Joseph; daug
2 CONC hter Elizabeth Foote; daughter Mary Hewes and son-in-law John Hewes of Royston. Robert, James and Joseph were apparently above age 24. Robert got the mansion house with stock of hop poles. Bequest to Mr. Richard Rogers, preacher o
2 CONC f God his Word [the famous preacher 1550-1618].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Robert Foote of Shalford Source: Obituary Record Search,  ObituaryLocator.com/Official 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Foote of Shalford, Essex, yeoman, 27 January 1608, proved 15 Feb 1608. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To the poor in the parish twenty shillings. to the poor in Wethersfield 20s. To my well beloved wife Joan, during her natural life, all such yearly rent as to me is reserved out of my lease of certain tenements which I hold for di
2 CONC vers years
2 CONT
2 CONT yet enduring by the grant of Sir Robert Chester knight and lying and being in the town of Royston, the yearly rent whereof to me reserved is at this present eight pounds. I give her also one annuity of four pounds to be paid durin
2 CONC g her natural life by my son Robert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To my son James 5oF.  To son Daniel 40L at four and twenty.  The same each to sons, Nathaniel, Francis, and Josua at like ages .  To daughter Elizabeth Foote 40L at day of marriage or at age of thirty.  To son Joseph my lease and 
2 CONC term of years in a certain hopground called Plomley w hich I hold by lease from Mr. Josyas Clarke and his wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other gifts to him. Certain household stuff to wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Ormes my maid servant.  To --Tibbet, wi fe of William Tibbett, 5s in recompence of her pains she hath taken with me. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Mr. Richard Rogers preacher of God his word 20s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The wife of George Elsing. Thomas Cott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To my son Robert my free tenement or mansion house wherein I now inhabit, with the land and the stock of hop poles upon the hop ground, he to pay the legacies & c. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The residue of my goods &c. to all my children.
2 CONT
2 CONT If it happen my daughter Mary Heewes to be departed then her part to be paid to her children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT For the execution of this will I do ordain, nominate and appoint my well beloved son Robert Foote to be my sole executor and I do desire my well beloved brother John Foote of London grocer and my son in law John Hewe s of Royston 
2 CONC to be supervisors and assistants to my executors. Dorset, 21
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worshipful_Company_of_Fishmongers
2 CONT * https://fishmongers.org.uk/
