2 CONC makes the case for Isaac being son of Ann/Hannah.* Donald Lines Jacobus, Families of Ancient New Haven, (9 vols., 1922-32), 1(1922):162-63; 6(1926):1459-61. It is this work that suggested that John Potter was he who married Elizab
