2 CONT This profile and bio were edited and reformatted by T Stanton December 2018 as part of the PGM Project. The profile is heavily indebted to the original work by Randy Seaver who suggests the following for additional information:
2 CONT
2 CONT The classical work by Melatiah Everett Dwight, "The Kirbys of New England," was published by Trow Printing, New York, in 1898.
2 CONT
2 CONT The above work has been significantly improved by further research in the work by Bertha W. Clark, "Richard Kirby of Sandwich, Dartmouth and Oyster Bay," 1955 (on FHL Microfilm 0,962,260, Item 15). This manuscript has much detail 
2 CONC on the English ancestry, the New England and Long Island families of Richard Kirby.
2 CONT
2 CONT The English ancestry and biography of Richard Kirby was also provided in the book "Ancestral Lines, Third Edition" compiled by Carl Boyer 3rd, published by the compiler in Santa Clarita, California in 1998. Boyer discusses earlier
2 CONC  research on Richard Kirby's English ancestry, and accepts the Kirby family work by Bertha W. Clark which is included in the book "The Ancestry of J.P. Guilford" by Dr. Joan S. Guilford, published in 1990
