2 CONT Profile last modified 18 Sep 2023 | Created 30 Jan 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Kirby migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Kirby was born about 1615 in England, daughter of Humphrey Kirby (1592–>1624) and Marjorie White (~1596–~1659).
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane married Richard Kirby (born about 1603 in Rowington, Warwickshire, England; son of John Kirby and Martha (Ward) Kirby). Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Kirby
2 CONT Richard Kirby (~1633–1720)
2 CONT Jane Kirby (~1636–<1707)
2 CONT Sarah Kirby (~1638–<1707)
2 CONT Ruhamah Kirby (~1640–>1710)
2 CONT Recompense Kirby (~1643–1720)
2 CONT Increase Kirby (1650–<1650)
2 CONT Jane died on March 23, 1650 in Sandwich, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay, aged about 34.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Kirby (abt. 1615 - 1650)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Jane [uncertain] Kirby [uncertain]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1615 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Humphrey Kirby and Marjorie (White) Kirby
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Richard Kirby [half], Joseph Kirby, Michael Kirby and John Kirby
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Richard Kirby — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Richard Kirby Jr., Jane (Kirby) Launders, Sarah (Kirby) Allen, Ruhamah (Kirby) Smith, Recompense Kirby, Abigail Kirby and Increase Kirby
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 23 Mar 1650 at about age 35 in Sandwich, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
