2 CONT     from Benton Harbor, and my father's name was John Tripp and my mother's name
2 CONT
2 CONT     was Isabel Moses and before she married my father when she was a maid and they
2 CONT
2 CONT     had about twelve children and much kindred we had and when I grew in years I
2 CONT
2 CONT     was put an apprentice to a shapt (ships?) carpenter whose name was John Baaty
2 CONT
2 CONT     (Beety, Beedy?) of [Horys]bury three miles of from Alsand in Lincolnshire
2 CONT
2 CONT     aforesaid where i served years and sometime after wrought with him and after that
2 CONT
2 CONT     I bound myself to owe Frances East for 4 pounds a year for 4 years who sold me
2 CONT
2 CONT     and I had served him and his assign for about a year and a half. He sold me
2 CONT
2 CONT     to Robert Jafra (Jeffery?) then living in Boston and Boston church members
2 CONT
2 CONT     persecuted some to the offending of others. My master came to Rhode Island with
2 CONT
2 CONT     the said persecuted people and I with him and his wife being sickly and they
2 CONT
