2 CONT Acus was son of Benoni Tripp and Elizabeth Mosher who married on 21 Nov 1728 at Little Compton, Newport, RI. Benoni was probably born ca 1706, son of Job Tripp and a first wife who must have married prior to 1706. This wife appare
2 CONC ntly died and Job married second Elizabeth Sweet, daughter of James Sweet and Jane Browning. Job was the son of Peleg Tripp and Anne Sisson; Peleg the son of John Tripp and Mary Paine.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Job and his first wife are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Job Jr. b 1701
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Isaac, b 1704, m Sarah Dow
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mehitable, bc 1705
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Benoni, b 1706, m Elizabeth Mosher
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Ann, bc 1707, m Robert John Moon 1729 Kingston
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Mary, bc 1709, m John Dawley 1730
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Phebe, bc 1710, m William Rice 1730
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. William, bc 1712, m Mary Wilcox and Mary Waite
2 CONT
