2 CONC 3/1634) to Frances East for four years. After about one and one half years 	of service (1635/1636), East sold the contract to Robert Jafra of Boston. Jafra fled Boston, with John Tripp in tow, to Rhode Island to avoid religious pe
2 CONC rsecution. Thereafter, Jafra sold the contract to Randall Holden of 	Portsmouth, RI. After some time, John Tripp paid off (probably 1637/1638) the remaining time on the contract.
2 CONT
