2 CONC 635/1636 when 	he immigrated to Boston on the same ship as William Hall (Abiel Tripp, son of John Tripp, married Deliverance Hall, daughter of William Hall). This likely sequence agrees with the immigration date of 1635 cited by D
2 CONC r. Carolyn Syron 	Valentine in "Trip Wills, Deeds and Ways", 1932. The Passenger and 	Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s (page 296) has the immigration place of 	RI in 1638, this not being a conflict with immigration date of 163
