1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not a known child of https://www.geni.com/people/Edmund-Freeman-II/6000000008790028940?through=6000000002459880687
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOT Mary Freeman.  Most likely Mary Atkinson.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/r/o/j/Heather-W-Rojo/GENE25-0082.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Freeman{sic. likely Atkinson} (F) b. 1620, d. 01 Sep 1692 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Freeman{sic. likely Atkinson} was born in 1620; died circa __ ___ 1691 per Bigilow. She married Richard Sisson before 1644; Portsmouth RI / Dartmouth; 1640 per 499. Mary died on 1 September 1692. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary (unknown surname) and Richard Sisson: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # George Sisson (1644 - 07 Sep 1718)  
2 CONT # Anne Sisson+ (1647 - 13 Jan 1714/15)  
2 CONT # Elizabeth Sisson  
2 CONT # John Sisson  
2 CONT # James Sisson  
2 CONT # Mary Sisson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://boards.ancestry.com/localities.northam.usa.states.massachusetts.counties.bristol/874.906.1020.1214/mb.ashx
2 CONT
2 CONT Bristol Co., Mass.   In response to your query concerning Richard Sisson(1) and his wife Mary, maiden name unknown. I am descended from their son George Sisson(2), and have been researching them for many years. I also belong to th
2 CONC e NEHGS,in Boston, from which I receive great records of New England. I have also corresponded with many other Sisson researchers throughout the years. None of them have ever found any proof that Mary's name was Freeman, that I kn
2 CONC ow of. I searched Freeman records and could find no connections. Many of us now believe Mary's name may have been Atkinson, as there are records in England, that seem to coincide with our Richard and Mary. I believe the Freeman er
2 CONC ror was made many years ago, and has been continued, regardless of proof. If you have any proof, I would like very much to know of it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
