2 CONT =RHODE ISLAND RECORDS & PROVIDENCE PLANTATIONS IN NEW ENGLAND.=
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol I.  by John Russell Bartlett. [974.5 N29r-SLC FHC] Printed by order of the Legislature. 1636-1666. Page 91 - 1st day of the 8th month  1640. A Catalog of such [Persons], who, by the Generall consent of the Company were admitte
2 CONC d to be Inhabytants of the Island now called Aqueedneck, having submitted 1638, themselves to the Government that is or shall be established, according to the word of God therein.  Mr. Edward Wilcocks.
2 CONT * 4.  Volume III.  Page 2260.  The name Edward Wilcox was in a list of inhabitants admitted to the island of Aquidneck, in 1638.  He was of Portsmouth and Kingstown, was early at Narragansett, and it seems had a connection with Ro
2 CONC ger Williams in establishing trading houses for the advantages of trade.  ￼
2 CONT * 5.  Famille Faucher Giroux Gauthier [faucher@trekquebec.com] gives Daniel Wilcox b ca 1565 d 25 Nov 1605 and Isabell b ca 1568 as his parents.￼
2 CONT * 6. Parents-John Wilcox and his father was William md C. Born - St Edmunds, Bury, co Suffolk, England [Great Britain]
2 CONT * 8 Documented events in his life were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>*  1. CR Baptism; 12 Feb 1603/04; South Elkington, Lincoln, Eng 4. Edward the son  of Danyell Wylcock was Baptised the xiith of february
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* 2.VR Death of Spouse; Bef 27 Jun 1630; Croft, Lincoln, ENG 1. 1630 - Marye the wyfe of Edward Wilcoxe was buried the xxvijte Day of June
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* 3. VR - Death of Child; Bef 27 Sep 1630; Croft, Lincoln, ENG 1. 1630. Daniell Wilcoxe a [blotted & illegible] sonne of Edward.  Wilcoxe was buried the same  day of September
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>> * 4. VR - Birth of Child; 4 Mar 1632/33; Croft, Lincoln, ENG 1. 1632/3.  Daniell the sonne of Edward Wilcoxe was christened the fourthe Day of March
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* 5. VR - Birth of Child; Bef 26 Dec 1634; Croft, Lincoln, ENG 1. 1634.  Stephen ye son of Edward Willcocke & Susanna his wife bapt  December : 26th
2 CONT >> >>>>>>>>* 6. Emigrant Ancestor; After 1630.  Edward married Susanna Thompson 1, daughter of Amos Thompson and Carynthapuch Jackson, on 12 May 1631 in Orby, Lincoln, Eng . (Susanna Thompson was baptized on 6 Sep 1607 in Orby, Li
2 CONC ncoln, Eng .) Documented events in her life were:  1. CR - Baptism; 6 Sep 1607; Orby, Lincoln, Eng . Documented events in their marriage were:  1. VR - Marriage; 12 May 1631; Orby, Lincoln, England.  SOURCES: 1.  Susanna Thompson,
2 CONC  the daughter of Amos Thompson, baptized September 6, 1607.  Edward Wilcocke & Susan Tomson [married] May 12, 1631. RIGR, Vol. 2, pages 91-100. NEHGR, Apr. 1993, pages 188-191.
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>*  7.  Edward Wilcox - born 12 February 1604 in South Elkington, co Lincoln, England.  Died ca 1660 in Orby, co Lincoln, England.  
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* 8.  Edward Wilcox #2468 (1.John1) b. 12 Feb 1604, South Elkington, Lincolnshire, England, m. 12 May 1631, in Orby, Lancashire, England, Susanna Thompson #12356, b. 6 Sep 1607, Orby, Lincolnshire, Eng., (daughter of Amo
2 CONC s Thompson #12357 and Carynthaphuch Jackson #12358). Edward died 1680, Portsmouth, Newport, RI. Edward was at Island of Aquidneck, Rhode Island in 1638. He was at Newport by 20 May, 1638.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3. i Stephen Wilcox #2469 b. 6 Feb 1633. Stephen, baptized December 26, 1634
2 CONT * 4. ii Daniel Wilcox #2466 b. ABT 1634. Daniel, christened March 4, 1632/3
2 CONT * 5. Mary Wilcox #6327 b. Abt 1635.10,  12 MAY 1631
2 CONT
2 CONT
