2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward died sometime after May 20, 1638, when he was listed as an inhabitant of Portsmouth, Rhode Island.[2] He was certainly deceased by April 13, 1660, when Daniel sold land that had belonged "to my father, Edward Wilcox".[1] Ed
2 CONC ward Wilcox, immigrant ancestor, was one of the free inhabitants of the island Aquidneck, now Rhode Island, in 1638, and joined in founding the compact of government in May 28 of that year. About the same time he had a trading hou
2 CONC se in Narragansett in company with Roger Williams. Sometime after they took into their business Richard Smith Sr., formerly from Gloucestershire, England, later of Taunton, Massachusetts. Edward Wilcox died probably at Narraganset
2 CONC t before 1648, and in 1653, the above-mentioned Smith appears to have acted as guardian for eight children, supposed to have been those of Wilcox. Children: Stephen, mentioned below; Daniel, married November 28, 1661 Elizabeth, da
2 CONC ughter of John and Sarah (Warren) Cook. Doubtless others.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 Fiske, Jane Fletcher. "Edward Wilcox of Lincolnshire and Rhode Island." The New England Historical & Genealogical Register 147 (1993): pp. 188-91. Digital image at americanancestors.org (subscription required).
2 CONT *  Moriarty, G. Andrews "One Branch of the Rhode Island Wilcox Family" The American Genealogist. New Haven, CT: D. L. Jacobus, 1937-. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2009 - .) Re
2 CONC ference Volume 19 (1942_, pages 23-25
