1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Sarah Warren
2 CONT *Born 1614 in Leiden, South Holland, Netherlands
2 CONT *Died 15 Jul 1696 in Dartmouth, Bristol, Massachusetts Colony
2 CONT *Daughter of Richard Warren and Elizabeth (Walker) Warren
2 CONT *Sister of Mary (Warren) Bartlett, Anna (Warren) Little, Elizabeth (Warren) Church, Abigail (Warren) Snow, Nathaniel Warren and	Joseph Warren Sr
2 CONT *Wife of John Cooke — married 28 Mar 1634 in Plymouth, New England 
2 CONT *Mother of Sarah (Cooke) Hathaway, Elizabeth (Cooke) Wilcox, Hester (Cooke) Taber, Mary (Cooke) Taber and Mercy (Cooke) West
2 CONT
2 CONT MAYFLOWER DESCENDANT  - her father was Pilgrim Richard Warren -tcd
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Warren-65
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Warren  was born about 1614 in Leiden, South-Holland, Netherlands[1]. Sarah at about 10 years of age arrived, in Plymouth, on the ship "Anne." Sarah Warren married John Cooke on March 28, 1634 in Plymouth. She was the mother
2 CONC  of 5 daughters; Sarah, Elizabeth, Hester, Mary and Mercy. Sarah died after 15 July 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1623 she immigrated on the ship "Anne." The Ann(e) and the Little James arrived together in July (10), 1623 - "The Planters". "The vessels parted company at sea; the Ann arrived the latter part of June, and the Little James som
2 CONC e week or ten days later; part of the number were the wives and children of persons already in the Colony." - "Hotten's Lists"[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Husband's Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Bond of Executrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Know all men by these presents that we Sarah Cooke of Dartmouth in the County of Bristoll in the Province of the Masachusett Bay in New England widow & Relect of John Cooke late of said Dartmouth Decd and Thomas Taber & Jonathan D
2 CONC elono Both of said Dartmouth Yeomen Do stand & are firmely bound and oliged unto John Saffin Esqr Judge of Probat of wills &ca within sd County, in the Sum of five Hundred Ninety four pounds To be payd unto the sd John Saffin or h
2 CONC is Successor in sd office To the which payment well and truely to be Made we Bind Or selves & Either of us by himselfjoyntly & Severally for & in the whole Our & Every & Either of our heires Executors & Administrs firmely by these
2 CONC  presents sealed with our seales Dated in Dartmouth the fifteenth Day of July 1696 in the Eighth Year of his Majesties Reign
2 CONT
2 CONT The Condition of this present obligation is such that whereas the above Bound Sarah Cooke is made Executrix of the Last
2 CONT
2 CONT 36 Yarmouth, Mass., Vital Records
2 CONT
2 CONT will & Testament of John Cook of Dartmouth aforesd Deceasd Bearing Date the Ninth Day of Novemb, 1694 & hath Never Legally proved the same, Iff therefore the sd Executrix shall with all Conveinient Speed bring into the Registrs Of
2 CONC fice for the County of Bristoll afforesd A true & perfect Inventory of the Estate of the Estate of the said Decd And shall well & truely Admñiistr upon & Duely Dispose of all & Singular the Goods Chattels, Credits & Estate left by
2 CONC  the said Decd according to the Tennor & true meaneing of his sd will. & as the Law directs And also shall Render a true & plaine account of her Administcon and Doings therein to the said office at or before the Sixteenth Day of A
2 CONC prill 1697 without fltaud or farther Delay then this Obligation to be voyde & of None Effect or Els to stand abide and Remaine in fill force strength & Vertue
2 CONT
2 CONT the mark of Sarah (S) Cook
2 CONT Signed sealed & Delivered in the presence of Thomas Delano the mark of+ :Hannah Savery Thomas Taber Jonathan Delano
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Mayflower Descendant Legacy CD-ROM"
2 CONT
2 CONT === Family ===
2 CONT Sarah Warren married John Cooke on March 28, 1634 in Plymouth.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cooke and his wife, Sarah Warren, had 5 daughters, and no sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah (b. abt. 1635, d. 1713). She married on November 20/1652, Arthur Hathaway, born 1631, died 1712 at Marshfield, Mass. 6 children,
2 CONT # Elizabeth (b. abt. 1635, d. 6 December 1715).  She married on  November 28/1661, Daniel Wilcox, who died July 2/1702, son of Edward  Wilcox, and they had ten children. She was a direct ancestor of  Winston Churchill, Prime Minis
2 CONC ter of England.
2 CONT # Hester (Esther) (b. 16 August 1650, d. 1672).  She married in 1667,  Thomas Taber, born February 1645, died November 11/1730, son of  Philip and Lydia (Masters) Taber, see subject 336. She was a direct  ancestor of Franklin D. R
2 CONC oosevelt.
2 CONT # Mary (b. abt 1652, d. between 26 April 1708 and 25 January 1714/15): She married in 1667-8, Philip Taber, born 1644, died 1693, brother of  her sister Hester's husband.
2 CONT # Mercy (b. 25 July 1654, d. 21 November 1733).  She married   in 1682, Stephen West, born 1654, died 1748, son of Bartholomew and   Catherine (Almy) West.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://mayflowerhistory.com/cooke-john
2 CONT *[Kellogg, Lucy Mary, Edna W. Townsend, and Robert S. Wakefield. Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims Who Landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620. Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Des
2 CONC cendants, 1975.]
2 CONT *Robert S. Wakefield, compiler, Mayflower Families through five-generations: Family of Richard Warren, Judith H. Swan, Revisor, third edition (Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendents, 2004), p. 5.
2 CONT * Richard & Elizabeth Warren, Pilgrim Hall Museum.
2 CONT *Robert S. Wakefield, Mayflower Families in Progress: Richard Warren for Four Generations (Plymouth: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1991).
2 CONT *Ruth Berg Walsh, "The Search for Pilgrim Richard Warren's Parentage," Mayflower Quarterly, 51:109-112.
2 CONT *Eugene Aubrey Stratton, Plymouth Colony, Its History and Its People, 1620-1691 (Salt Lake City: Ancestor Publishers, 1986).
2 CONT *Nathaniel Morton, New England's Memorial (Cambridge, 1669).
2 CONT *William Bradford, Of Plymouth Plantation, ed. Samuel Morison (New York: Random House, 1952).
2 CONT *Mayflower Web Pages, by Caleb Johnson.mayflowerhistory.com
2 CONT *Richard & Elizabeth Warren, Pilgrim Hall 
2 CONT *the Mayflower Society and family records.
