2 CONT iii.     BARTHOLOMEW WEST,1,2 b. in England,2 d. bef 1684 in Monmouth Co, NJ,2 buried in Shrewsbury, Monmouth Co, NJ,2 resided 1651 in Portsmouth, Newport Co, RI.2  He married ca 1653,2 Catherine Almy (daughter of William Almy and
2 CONC  Audry ___).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From the WorldConnect Database: "The Freeman, Howe, Parke, Stockwell, Thatcher, Martin etc", by Peter Howe Freeman:
2 CONT
2 CONT "As written in the "Genealogical and Personal Memorial of Mercer County,New Jersey" Vol. I
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartholomew and Katherine, with most of their family, came to MonmouthCounty, New Jersey, about the year 1666, and were among the founders ofthe new settlements that took the name of Shrewsbury and other well knownnames. Bartholom
2 CONC ew was a member of the first Assembly of East New Jersey,which met December 14, 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried on his land in Shrewbury township in a halfacre not farfrom a branch of the Shrewsbury River, and several of the family werealso buried there, and it is highly probable that at least twogenerationsof the Wests were a
2 CONC lso buried there. Near this burial plot wasthe burial plotof Robert West, Sr., another of the Wests who came fromRhode Island. In deedsexecuted in 1697 and 1703, these burial plots were"reserved forever,"but all traces of them are
2 CONC  now lost.
2 CONT
2 CONT These early Wests of East Jersey were probably of the faith andPersuasion of the Puritans. After the death of Barthlolmew hiswidowKatherine married Nicholas Brown, of Shrewsbury, the same who gave thelot at Shrewsbury in 1706 on w
2 CONC hich the Episcopal church there was firstbuilt, and on which the present edifice stands. "
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
