1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: John arrived aboard the "True Love" in 1635 landing at New London Conn. With his brother Zacharia (b 1595 England). John (1) went on to Weymouth, Mass and Zacharia (1) stayed in Conn. According to Walt Whitman ( ), Amer
2 CONC ican Poet and Ancestor of Zacharia (1), both were sons of Abijah Whitman (b England).
2 CONT                           "John Whitman of Weymouth" was the title of a book published in 1889 by Charles H.
2 CONT                          Farnham of Yale University. The research necessary for the listing of the 15,000
2 CONT                         descendants of John (1) was apparently a project of the Genealogical Department of
2 CONT                         this University. In the days of limited transportation (few railways, paved roads,
2 CONT                         telephones or telegraph services) the services of many workers with horse and buggy
2 CONT                         or on horseback would have been required. They had to cover the whole Eastern
2 CONT                         United States and Nova Scotia. The completion of such a listing was quite an
2 CONT                         achievement. There cannot be many other similar family records of this magnitude.
2 CONT                         The choice of the Whitman family was probably due to the fact that one of Charles
2 CONT                         Farnham's ancestors was a Whitman, any other old family would probably have
2 CONT                          answered the purpose.
2 CONT    John (1) was one of the earliest settlers of the town of Weymouth, in the State of    Massachusetts. He is the Ancestor of nearly all of the name of Whitman, and at least as many of other names. In December 1638, it appears by 
2 CONC Winthrop's Journal, he was made free, viz: admitted to the rights and privileges of a citizen.
