2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gungazo&id=I03437
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [1]ELIZABETH GOODELL (Goodale) born about 1638 in Salem, Massachusetts (Bowen, 1646[2]). She married (1) JOHN SMITH about 1658. Their first child was born about 1660[3]. John died in 1672 (Torrey[4]).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, born Salem, Massachusetts (North Fields):
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Smith born probably about 1658, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT John Smith, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT Sarah (Smith) Clark, b. 1660, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT Mary (Smith) Haskell, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT ELIZABETH, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT Elizabeth (Smith) Sturtevant b. aft. 1662, baptized 8 Aug., 1672.
2 CONT See the record for her husband John Smith regarding the court scandal with her sister-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodell deeded a portion of his Great Cove farm and the house on it to his son-in-law, John Smith in 1658. This seems to indicate that Elizabeth must have been married by 1658, since it is likely that this land was bequeath
2 CONC ed upon their marriage. From this it would seem that Elizabeth was probably born about 1638 and was the daughter of Robert and his first wife, Katherine. This is contrary to that which has been written in some previously published
2 CONC  genealogies which have said that Elizabeth was the daughter of Robert's second marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married (2) WILLIAM BENNETT on 6 Mar 1673/4 (Torrey, 1675[4])[5]. They had one child, Grace Bennett, who died young. William probably died not long after, and before 1680. In 1680, Elizabeth was living with her father an
2 CONC d son, John Smith Jr. (probably born ca1660). See Bowen #10.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died some time after Dec 1692, when her son Abraham Smith agreed with his brothers and sisters to take care of his mother in return for her land.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Elizabeth's husband John of Salem Village probably lived with her father and helped with the farm. Her father bequeath to her and her son John his house & orchard and "all the meddowes that I now possess".
2 CONT Robert Goodell deeded a portion of his Great Cove farm and the house on it to his son-in-law, John Smith in 1658. This seems to indicate that Elizabeth must have been married by 1658, since it is likely that this land was bequeath
2 CONC ed upon their marriage. From this it would seem that Elizabeth was probably born about 1638 and was the daughter of Robert and his first wife, Katherine. This is contrary to that which has been written in some previously published
2 CONC  genealogies which have said that Elizabeth was the daughter of Robert's second marriage.
2 CONT According to North America Family Histories 1500-2000 on 6 Dec 1692 Abraham Smith agreed with his brothers and sisters to take care of his mother Elizabeth Bennett during the remainder of her life in consideration of the land whic
2 CONC h she then possessed (Essex Deeds 9:67)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Goodale-13
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Elizabeth (Goodale) Bennett (1638 - aft. 1692)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Bennett formerly Goodale aka Smith, Goodell
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 11 Oct 1638 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Robert Goodale and Katherine (Unknown) Goodale
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Mary (Goodale) Pease, Abraham Goodale, Isaac Goodale, Nehemiah (Goodale) Goodell, Sarah (Goodale) Batchelder, Zachariah Goodale, Jacob Goodell and Hannah (Goodale) Kilham
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Smith — married 1657 in Essex, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Bennett — married 1674 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Mary Goodale (Smith) Haskell, John Smith, Sarah (Smith) Clark, Elizabeth (Smith) Sturtevant, Abraham Smith and Grace Bennett
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 1692 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colon
2 CONT
