1 NAME William /Swift/
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Swift
2 _MARNM Swift
2 NICK William Swift II
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 25 APR 1627
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bermondsey
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 DEC 1705
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sandwich
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE 18 JAN 1706
2 ADDR
3 CITY Barnstable
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU William Swift migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640).
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Swift-62
2 CONT
2 CONT William Swift, b. 25 Apr 1627 St. Mary Magdalen, Bermondsey [TAG 77:166], son of William Swift (1575 - 1644) and Joan Unknown (1576 - 1663).[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT William was at Watertown, Massachusetts in 1634 and later at Sandwich, where he served as Deputy to the Plymouth General Court in 1673, 1674, 1677 and 1678.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married by 1651 Ruth____ [MD 14:166; Sand VR 1:15]; assumed to be mother of his children (named in his 1705 will). Some say she was a Tobey, Dillingham, Morse or Arnold without source. Published 21st century researchers Robert 
2 CONC Charles Anderson and Jane Fletcher Fiske both admit no knowledge of her surname.[3] An unsourced marriage date of 18 Nov 1650 in Sandwich, Massachusetts, has been suggested.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 7 Jan. 1705/6 in Sandwich, Barnstable Co, Massachusetts according to his inventory. His will, dated 15 Dec. 1705, proved 29 Jan 1705/6, names wife Ruth, daughter Hannah Tobie, Temperance Bourn, Hester Gibbs and Dina Perry,
2 CONC  sons Josiah and Jirah, the sons of his son William deceased, and son-in-law Timothy Bourn (Barnstable Probate, 2:217).[4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT #Hannah b 11 Mar 1651[6] prob. 1651/2); m. (1) Ambrose Fish; m. (2) Thomas Tobey.
2 CONT #Ruth (1652),
2 CONT #William, b 28 Aug 1654; d. before his father; m. Elizabeth ____, parentage unknown; she was not the daughter of John Thomson as often stated.
2 CONT #Ephraim, b 7 Jun 1656; m. Sarah Perry, dau of Ezra.
2 CONT #Mary or Maria, b 7 Apr 1659; d 1 Mar 1682; m 6 Feb 1677 Shubel Smith.
2 CONT #Samuel, b 10 Aug 1662; m. Mary ___.
2 CONT #Jireh, b 1665; m 26 Nov 1697 Abigail Gibbs
2 CONT #Temperance, b 1666; m. Timothy Bourne[7]
2 CONT #Esther or Hester, b 1668; m about 1689-90 John Gibbs Jr
2 CONT #Josiah, b 1670
2 CONT #Dinah, b abt 1672; m. Benjamin Perry
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT More info is needed, but it looks like this is the guy that made the trip from England to the Colonies. He's referred to as William the 2nd, though it looks like he is more like the 4th or 5th in a line of William Swift or Swyft. 
2 CONC William IV (1619 --1705) married Ruth Allen Tobey in 1649. Some say she was a Morse or Arnold, so we are only sure of the first name. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had eleven offspring, Hannah, Ruth, William III, Ephraim, Mary, Samuel, Jireh, Josiah, Temperance, Ester, and Dinah. Dinah married a Benjamin Perry. William II served many years in the Massachusetts General Court. Our line of
2 CONC  Swifts descends through Samuel 10 August 1662 B. 25 May 1730)..
2 CONT
2 CONT Interestingly, his younger brother Jireh was born in Suffolk County, England. Older brother Ephraim was born 6 June 1656. Samuel had a son Ephraim, another of our distant grandfathers. Jireh and Samuel both married Gibbs girls, Ab
2 CONC igail and Mary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT We are connected to William I and William II through Samuel. William II represented Sandwich in the General Court (legislature) four times, was surveyor of local highways, served as constable, and was a selectman for 15 years. He 
2 CONC married a second wife, Mary Lynde Butler, born 1658.
