1 NOTE William married a lady by the name of Ruth Tobey in 1645.
1 NOTE .. of Sandwich.
2 CONT .. of Sandwich.
1 NOTE Death date from Torrey, New England Marriages Prior to 1700. Town meeting of Sandwich, Massachusetts., 10 Mar 1676 (1677?): "A town meeting warned by Benjamin Hammond by virtue of a warrant from the Governor for the choice of offi
2 CONC cers to serve the present year. And the town hath made the choice of William Swift, Sr., and Steven Skiffe, Deputies; Henry Dillingham, Constable; John Bourne and Elisha Bourne, Grand Jurymen; William Swift, Steven Skiffe, Thomas 
2 CONC Tupper, Selectmen; Michael Blackwell, Daniel Wing, Surveyors." From Cape Cod Library of Local History and Genealogy, Vol. II, p. 1644. Crocker has 7 Jan 1705/06 for death. A William Swift, 21, to be transported to Virginia on the 
2 CONC Primrose, 27 Jul 1635. [NEHGR, iv, 189] On 1643 list of men able to bear arms in Sandwich [NEHGR, iv, 258] Burke�s Landed Gentry, 2932. Says he died in 1705; will proved 29 Jan 1706. [BINGHAM.GED]
