1 NOTE Torrey, New England Marriages Prior to 1700, lists William's wife as "Ruth Parsons" not "Ruth Ellingham." Could Ellingham be from a second marriage? Extrapolation from Torry shows that Dianah has a brother, William (1654-1701), wh
2 CONC o may be a half-brother. "Ellingham" might also be a variant of "Dillingham." Landers and Crocker also have "Parsons." NEHGR, iii, 193, notes a William Ellingham, sworn as freeman at Accomentieus or Gorgeana, 22 Nov 1652. [BINGHAM
2 CONC .GED]
1 NOTE Also have name as Ruth TOBEY: born about 1628 in Sandwich, Barnstable, MA; died in 1706 in Sandwich, Barnstable, MA. [Michelle Marx]
