2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Someone had placed as a baptismal location "Bermondsey Abbey". One other online source (LDS, so I hesitate to use it as any authority) identified the baptismal place as St. Mary Magdalene Church in Bermondsey (apparently the 13th 
2 CONC century church that stood on the site of the present St. Mary Magdelene Church, which was torn down and rebuilt 1680-1690). This would make more sense since abbeys didn't normally carry out baptisms - as I understand it, usually b
2 CONC aptisms were relegated to parish churches. Would welcome clearer documentation of the baptismal site.
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT b. BEF 15 MAR 1613/14;  christening:15 MAR 1613/14
2 CONT
2 CONT emigration: July 1623 arrived at Plymouth on the Ann
