2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Baptized 15 Mar 1614 in  St Mary Magdalene, Bermondsey, Surrey, England. Marriage and Baptism records show last name spelled Hicks NOT Hickes.<ref>Church of England Parish Registers, 1538-1812. London, England:London Metropolitan 
2 CONC Archives.</ref><ref>St Mary Magdalene Bermondsey,Southwark, Surrey England Parish Register by subscription at:https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/1624/31280_199007-00084?pid=2885883
2 CONT </ref> Emigrated with mother Margaret and siblings (Samuel, Ephraim, Lydia) in arrived June 1622 following her father by a year.  <ref>Frost, Josephine C. The Frost Genealogy : Descendants of William Frost of Oyster Bay, New York 
2 CONC : showing connections (1912) [https://archive.org/details/frostgenealogyde00fros/page/343 p. 343 at Archive.org] Seen as North American Family Histories - 6th Generation Hicks Family - by subscription at: [https://www.ancestry.com
2 CONC /interactive/61157/46155_b290412-00456?pid=3312857 Ancestry]</ref> Married c. 1635 George Watson<ref name="GMB">Anderson, Robert Charles,[http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/great-migration-begins-immigrants-to-ne-1620-1633
2 CONC -vols-i-iii/image/?volumeId=12107&pageName=1944&rId=235198127 "George Watson," Featured Name] (Vol I-III, Page 1944)''The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III.'' (Online database accessed Apri
2 CONC l 16, 2015: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2010)</ref> She died 22 May 1663 in Plymouth, MA<ref>Shurtleff, Nathaniel B. Records of the Colony of New Plymouth of New England. Miscellaneous Records
2 CONC 1633-1689. Boston, MA: Legislature of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, 1857.  [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofcolonyo0708newp#page/n35/mode/2up/search/%22Phebe+Watson%22+1663  Page 23.]</ref>
2 CONT === Children ===
2 CONT :Children of George and Phebe (Hicks) Watson:<ref name="GMB"/> 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Watson-790|John Watson# Watson-35|Phoebe Watson, m. Jonathan Shaw<ref>Morris, Tyler Seymour. ''Ephraim and Pamela (Converse) Morris: Their Ancestors and Descendants.'' 1894. [https://books.google.com/books?id=bRs5AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA1
2 CONC 39 Page 139]</ref>
