1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Andrews-81
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Pitts formerly Andrews aka Hodges
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1631 in Taunton, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Henry Andrews Sr. and Mary (Pool) Andrews
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Henry Andrews Jr., Abigail Andrews and Sarah (Andrews) Talbot
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Hodges — married 1648 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Peter Pitts — married 2 Apr 1654 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of John Hodges, Henry Hodges, Samuel Pitts, Mary (Pitts) Hathaway, Sarah Pitts, Peter Pitts, Alice (Pitts) Wilbore and Ebenezer Pitts
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 1700 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 23 Oct 2019 | Created 30 Aug 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Andrews was born about 1631 probably in England. She is the daughter of Henry Andrews and Mary Pool.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married William Hodges around 1648/1649 in Taunton.[1] They had two children, John and Henry.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hodges died April 2, 1654, in Taunton. He seems to have held considerable property, which Mary settled on her two sons (less 30 pounds and her clothes for herself) in her will proved on March 15, 1655.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married secondly Peter Pitts about 1655. They had six children.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Pitts died June 9, 1692, and Mary was his executor at which time she was described as "a very antient and infirm woman."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Andrews Hodges) Pitts was an inn holder in Taunton in 1700. She must have died some time after that but no record has been found.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
