2 CONT {{Puritan Great Migration}}
2 CONT == Biography ==Ann was baptized 5 Jul 1621 North Benfleet, Essex, England<ref>Davis, Walter Goodwin, BA, LLB of Portland, ME.   Ancestry of John Lake, Husband of Margaret (Reade) Lake. ''The New England Historical and Genealogical
2 CONC  Register'', v. 84 (1930), pp. 304-317.  (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001).  [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB202/i/11699/316/236582702 link at AmericanAncestors ($)]</re
2 CONC f> 
2 CONT She was the daughter of John and Margaret (Reade) Lake.
2 CONT John Gallup came to this country with his mother, two brothers and sister Joan, in the ship Griffin, arriving at Boston on the 4th day of Sept., 1633. He married Hannah Lake, daughter of John and Margaret Lake,and sister of Elizab
2 CONC eth Read, who married John Winthrop, Jr., Governor of Connecticut. She also came to this country with her mother, in the ship Abigail, arriving Oct. 6, 1635, after a passage of ten weeks.<ref name=HoS> Richard Anson Wheeler. Histo
2 CONC ry of the Town of Stonington,County of New London, Connecticut, From Its First Settlement in 1649 to 1900. New London, CT: Press of the Day Publishing Co., Jan. 1900. [https://archive.org/stream/historytownston00wheegoog#page/n400
2 CONC /mode/2up Page: 382]</ref> She married John Gallup in Boston, MA in 1643 -Children Elizabeth, Hannah, John, Esther, Benadam, William, Samuel, & Christobel (female), Elizabeth, Mary, Margaret<ref name=HoS/> Hannah died after her hu
2 CONC sband, who died in the Great Swamp Fight 19 Dec 1675. Distribution of his estate was made partially to his widow.<ref>Genealogical History of the Gallup Family of the United States Author: John D. Gallup Publication: Hartford Prin
2 CONC ting Co. Hartford CT. 1893[https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhist00gall#page/n55/mode/2up p. 22]</ref> The widow Gallop was involved in a lengthy court case against her neighbor in Stonington, Capt. George Denison. This case 
2 CONC was still ongoing in 1685. She died sometime after that. <ref>Connecticut: Minutes of the Court of Assistants, 1669-1711. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2013.) Originally publis
2 CONC hed as: Colony of Connecticut, Minutes of the Court of Assistants, 1669-1711, by Helen Schatvet Ullmann, CG, FASG. Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2009.</ref> Hannah is buried at White Hall Graveyard, Mystic, Ne
2 CONC w London County, Connecticut.<ref>[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8932358/elizabeth-hannah-gallup Findagrave # 8932358] has images of newer memorial stone. There is no date on the stone. The FindAGrave page states that she di
2 CONC ed 19 December 1675, but this is a mistake.</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From: ''Genealogical Record of the Hodges Family'', Pg. 75:''':'''3''' - Henry Hodges (2) [Wm. (1)], b. 1652, Taunton, Mass.; d. 1717 Sept. 30, Taunton, aged 65; m. 1674 Dec. 17, Taunton, Ester Gallop, dau. of John & '''Hannah 
2 CONC (Lake) Gallop''', b. 1653 July 21, Taunton. :11 children born in Taunton: - ::'''9.''' i. Mary (4) Hodges, b. 1675/6 Feb. 3. ::'''10.''' ii. Esther (4) Hodges, b. 1677/8 Feb. 17. ::'''11.''' iii. William (4) Hodges, b. 1679/80 Mar
2 CONC ch 18, ::'''12.''' iv. Charity (4) Hodges, b. 1682 April 5. ::'''13.''' v. John (4) Hodges, b. 1684. ::'''14.''' vi. Henry (4) Hodges, b. 1685 or 1686. ::'''15.''' vii. Joseph (4) Hodges, b. 1688 or 1689. ::'''16.''' viii. Benjami
2 CONC n (4) Hodges, b. about 1691. ::'''17.''' ix. Ephraim (4) Hodges, b. about 1693. ::'''18.''' x. Elizabeth (4) Hodges. ::xi. Abigail (4) Hodges. :Hannah (Lake) Gallop, mother of Ester (Gallop) Hodges, was daughter of [[Lake-38  | Jo
2 CONC hn]] & [[Reade-15 | Margaret (Reade) Lake]]. John Lake was a merchant in Dublin. After his death, his widow, with her daughters Hannah and Martha, and her sister [[Reade-50 | Elizabeth]], the new wife of [[Winthrop-14 | Gov. John 
2 CONC Winthrop Jr.]], accompanied the Governor on his voyage to New England in 1635, Margaret lived for a time at Boston in the family of [[Winthrop-12 | Gov. John Winthrop senior]]. Her brother, Thomas Reade, came to Salem, Mass., and 
2 CONC settled there, but returned to England and became Colonel in Cromwell's army. AfterCromwell's death he assisted Gen. Monk in the restoration of Charles II and was placed in command of Sterling Castle. Margaret Reade's mother, Eliz
2 CONC abeth, married for her 2nd husband the famous Hugh Peter, chaplain of Oliver Cromwell, whose career in New England and Old England, ended tragically, has been the occasion of much comment and controversy. :[Continues with biograph
2 CONC ical information for Henry Hodges, and biography of Esther (Gallup) Hodges' father, John Gallop.] ''This profile is a collaborative work-in-progress. Can you contributeinformation or sources?'' <!-- This comment, and everything el
2 CONC se, canbe edited or removed. -->
2 CONT
