2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Bridport, Dorset]]
2 CONT == Biography ==John was the youngest son of John Gallop and Christabell Bruschett, baptized in Bridport, Dorset, on 11 July 1630, recorded as the son of John Gollop. His given name is unusual, as there was an older living sonnamed
2 CONC  John.  He is presumed to have died young, since he is not mentioned in his father's will (dated 20 December 1649), in which John Gallop calls Samuel and Nathaniel his "two youngest Sonns".<ref name=TAG68>Parsons, Gerald James. "J
2 CONC ohn Gallop/Gollop of Bridport, Dorsetshire, England, and Boston, Massachusetts", ''The American Genealogist'' 68:12 (1993) [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB283/i/12963/12/0 Link atAmericanAncestors ($)]</ref><ref>Father's prof
2 CONC ile https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gallop-7</ref>
2 CONT [[Gallop-7|John Gallop]], the father, had sailed for New England almost four months before this son's baptism, accompanied by his older son [[Gallop-261|John]] (baptized 1621). Christobel, wife and mother of the migrants remained 
2 CONC in England, which we know from a letter by John Winthrop. It has been suggested that she named this last son John, thinking she might never see her husband or eldest son again.<ref name=TAG68 />
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references />*The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2010), (Originally Published as: New England Histor
2 CONC ic Genealogical Society. Robert Charles Anderson, The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III, 3 vols., 1995). https://www.americanancestors.org/DB393/i/12107/727/0
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/projects/Great-Migration-Passengers-of-the-Griffin-1633/18457#:~:text=This%201633%20journey%20carried%20religious,Cotton%2C%20during%20the%201633%20voyage ]. 
2 CONT ***********
