1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth seen as February 24, 1626  Barnstable, Plymouth Colony, Colonial America without supporting evidence.  Her father Robert Lee arrived in America “by 1636.” Mary Lee married in 1651 to John Howland Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Mary Lee===
2 CONT * Birth: about 1628, England or the Plymouth Colony 
2 CONT * Death: AFT 6 MAY 1693 / Bef 6 May 1697 in Barnstable, MA
2 CONT * Father: Robert Lee 
2 CONT * Mother: Mary Atwood
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # 26 OCT 1651 in Plymouth, MA to John Howland b: 24 APR 1627 in Plymouth, MA.  He was the son of John Howland & Elizabeth Tilley, passengers of the Mayflower in 1620 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #  Mary Howland b: ABT 1652 in Plymouth, MA.  Married John Allyn. 
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Howland b: 17 MAY 1655 in Barnstable, MA.  Married John Bursley.
2 CONT #  Isaac Howland b: 25 NOV 1659 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Ann Tayler.
2 CONT #  Hannah Howland b: 15 MAY 1661 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Jonathan Crocker.  
2 CONT #  Mercy Howland b: 21 JAN 1662/63 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Joseph Hamblin.  
2 CONT #  Lydia Howland b: 9 JAN 1664/65 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Jeremiah Thomas.  
2 CONT #  Experience Howland b: 28 JUL 1668 in Barnstable, MA.  Married James Bearse.  
2 CONT #  Anne Howland b: 9 SEP 1670 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Joseph Crocker.  
2 CONT #  Shubael Howland b: 30 SEP 1672 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Mercy Blossom.
2 CONT #  John Howland b: 31 DEC 1674 in Barnstable, MA.  Married Mary Crocker.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lee-302
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Lee married John Howland on October 26, 1651, in Plymouth, Plymouth, Massachusetts[4][5][1] An annotation by Robert Bowman in his compilation of Barnstable Vital Records identified the parties to this marriage as Mary Lee, so
2 CONC n of Robert, and John Howland, elder child of the Pilgrim.[6][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 10 children: Mary, Elizabeth, Isaac, Hannah, Mercy, Lydia, Experience, Anne, Shubael, and John. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died after May 22, 1693 (date John and Mary delivered deed to Justice of Peace William Bradford), in Plymouth, Plymouth, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed Records
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lieut. John Howland, Mary Howland, both of Barnstable''', Jacob Cook, Frances Cook, both of Plymouth to Joseph Finney, of Plymouth, May 6, 1693. Acknowledged May 22, 1693 and May 6, 1697. Recorded May 14, 1705, Plymouth County.
2 CONC  … Mary Lee, probably Mary Atwood before her marriage, died in Barnstable after 6 May 1693 the date she and her husband signed a deed, and probably before 6 May 1697 the date her husband acknowledged the deed alone.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Birth date and location 
2 CONT ''12 September 2023'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gen’s profile notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Birth seen as February 24, 1626 Barnstable, Plymouth Colony, Colonial America without supporting evidence. Her father Robert Lee arrived in America about 1636. Mary Lee married in 1651 to John Howland Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT I don’t think there’s a birth record at all.  If she married 1651, figure she was born no later than 1635, and more likely, around 1630.  So that makes her born in England.  
2 CONT
2 CONT But let’s seen what the citations say.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lee-302
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Lee[1][2][3] was born in 1626, in Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # Torrey [marriage record - doesn’t cite birth]
2 CONT #  Sons of the American Revolution [submitted pedigree - disregard]  
2 CONT # Roser, Susan E., Mayflower Births and Deaths: From the Files of George Ernest Bowman at the Massachusetts Society of Mayflower Descendants. Vol 2 page 159. (Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1992.) Accessed o
2 CONC n Ancestry.com at https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3718/images/mayflowerbdii-002191.159 [No birth date cited] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Let’s look at her father at https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lee-43 to see if we can nail down when he emigrated and married.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration
2 CONT
2 CONT >The immigration date and location of this family is not known, Anderson in the "Great Migration Directory" said only "'''by 1636'''":
2 CONT
2 CONT Lee, Robert: Unknown; 1636; Plymouth [PCR 1:48, 12:29; MD 5:153-59, 11:32, 200-6; Emerson-Benson 338-39]. Key
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Lee married Mary Atwood[3] at Plymouth, Massachusetts. [Based on … ?] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conclusion: if the first records for her parents in America is “by 1636”, it seems more likely she was ''born in England by 1630.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Will of John Atwood d. before Feb 1644'''
2 CONT Names “my brother and sister Lee and their two children Ann & Mary”
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000198157658821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source:  England Historical and Genealogical Register Vol 4. p. 173 < [https://play.google.com/books/reader?id=NcIMAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover&source=gbs_atb_hover&pg=GBS.PA173 GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Torrey said this about the union in "New England Marriages to 1700": LEE, Robert (related to John ATWOOD who m Ann) & Mary [ATWOOD] (-1681); by 1635; Plymouth[2] In 1650, Robert and Mary are mentioned in his sister Ann Attwood's
2 CONC  will.[4]
