2 CONT ===Mary Bodfish 
2 CONT *Born 29 Jul 1643 in Barnstable, Massachusetts 
2 CONT *Daughter of Robert (Botfish) Bodfish and Bridget 
2 CONT *Sister of John Bodfish, Sarah (Bodfish) Blossom, Elizabeth Bodfish,  Robert Bodfish and	Joseph Bodfish
2 CONT *Wife of John Crocker — married 1659 (to Dec 1662) 
2 CONT *Mother of Elizabeth Crocker and	Jonathan Crocker
2 CONT *Died Dec 1662 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bodfish-20
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bodfish, daughter of Robert and Bridget Bodfish of Sandwich, married John Crocker, son of Deacon William and Alice Crocker, in Nov. 1659. (p. 68; p 212) [1] (p. 192) [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Mary (Bodfish) Crocker in Dec. 1662 ( p. 150)[3], John married second April 25, 1663, Mary Bursley daughter of John Bursley. (p. 211) [1](p. 389) [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT #Elizabeth born Oct. 7, 1660 (p. 150)[3] (p. 389) [4]; died Jan. 15, 1716; married Deacon Richard Child in 1678. (p. 212) [1]
2 CONT #Jonathan born July 15, 1662 (p. 150)[3]; married Hannah Howland, daughter of John Howland, on May 20, 1686. (p. 389) [4] He died on Aug. 24, 1746, buried at West Barnstable. (p. 211)[1]
2 CONT
