1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-183567
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''Bridget (Unknown) Hinckley (abt. 1615 - aft. 1662)
2 CONT
2 CONT Bridget Hinckley formerly [surname unknown] aka Botfish, Bodfish, 
2 CONT [Maiden name not known]: "Lugg" (unproven), Bloom ('''unproven''')
2 CONT [Find A Grave shows "Sugg" without providing a source.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1615 in Kent, England [uncertain] [if Robert Bodfish's birth's county isn't known, it's unwise to guesstimate the county of birth for Bridget.– Ken Shelley 14 May 2024.] 
2 CONT Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Robert (Botfish) Bodfish — married 1638 in Sandwich, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT Wife of Samuel Hinckley Sr — married 15 Dec 1657 in Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of John Bodfish, Sarah (Bodfish) Blossom, Mary Bodfish, Elizabeth Bodfish, Robert Bodfish and Joseph Bodfish [ '''<—''' It's worth noting that Anderson's Great Migration only finds support for three children: Sarah, Mary, a
2 CONC nd Joseph.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 1662 in Plymouth, Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Bridget (Unknown) Hinckley migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT Bridget Bodfish was born around 1616[1] in Kent, England.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900 Author: Yates Publishing Publication: Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2004. American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI) Author: Godfrey Memor
2 CONC ial Library, comp. Publication: Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 1999. Ancestry Family Trees ↑ http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=sse&db=agbi&h=1348365&ti=0&indiv=try&gss=pt ↑ http://trees.ancestry.com
2 CONC /rd?f=sse&db=agbi&h=1348365&ti=0&indiv=try&gss=pt
2 CONT
2 CONT Acknowledgments
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you to Grant Knudsen, Rick Mahler, John Putnam, Gregory Nelson, Abby Brown, Earl Bice, Amanda Thomas, and to all who contributed to this profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert Bodfish - was born in 1612/was born Bef. 1610 in England, lived in Barstable, MA and died on 19 Nov 1651 in Sandwich, Barnstable ,Massachusetts .
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Bridget about 1639 in Barnstable, MA.
2 CONT Bridget - After Robert died in 1651, she married Samuel Hinkley in 1657, the father of Governor Thomas Hinkley.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestor of this family wrote his name "Robert Botfish", yet on the records it is written Botfish, Botflish, Bodfish, Badfish, Bootfish, and, Boatfish. He was early at Lynn,made freeman May 6, 1635 at Lynn, Mass., and of Sandw
2 CONC ich in 1637, of which town he was one of the original proprietors. The Indian title to the lands in Sandwich was purchased by William Bradford and his partners for the Old Plymouth Company in 1637, for 16lbs, 19 shillings, payable
2 CONC  in commodities, and 24 January 1647, they assigned their rights to Edmund Freeman, and on the 26 of February following, he assigned the same to George Allen, John vincent, William Newland, Robert Botfish. Anthony Wright and Richa
2 CONC rd Bourne, a committee of the proprietors of the town of Sandwich. In 1640, the meadow lands were divided, giving to each in proportion to his quality and condition, Robert Bodfish had five acres assigned to him, a little less tha
2 CONC n an average amount.
2 CONT
2 CONT January 1, 1638 Robert Bodfish desired to become a freeman of the Plymouth Colony. In 1641, he was a surveyor of Highways, in 1644 he served on the Grand Jury and also was licensed to "draw wine in Sandwich". The family all moved 
2 CONC to Barnstable, Mass in 1657. 
2 CONT Children: 1) John BODFISH  Abt 1636 - ____ 
2 CONT 2) Mary BODFISH  1643 - Dec 1662  m.  29 Nov 1659, Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts John Crocker BIRTH:   1 May 1637, Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts  
2 CONT CHRISTENING:   11 Jun 1637, Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts  DEATH:   May 1711, Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts BURIAL:   1711, Barnstable, Barnstable, Mass  Father: William CROCKER  Mother: Alice 3) Sarah Bodfish was born
2 CONC  in 1638 in Sandwich, MA and died on 3 Oct 1704 in Barnstable, MA . 4) Sarah married Peter Blossom on 21 Jun 1663 in Barnstable, Mass.. Peter was born in 1648 in Barnstable, Mass.. He was the son of Thomas Blossom. He died in 1706
2 CONC  in Barnstable, Mass. 5) Robert Bodfish  Abt 1647 - ____
2 CONT  6) Elizabeth BODFISH  1647 - ____
2 CONT  7) Child BODFISH  27 Mar 1648 - 27 Mar 1649
2 CONT  8) Child BODFISH  3 Apr 1649 - 2 Dec 1744 9)  Joseph Bodfish was born on 3 Apr 1651 in Sandwich, Mass married Elizabeth Besse/ Bessey in 1674  
2 CONT
2 CONT RECORD:
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha (James E.) McCourt, Descendants of Rev. John Smith,  married Susanna Hinckley, 13 Jun 1643, Additions and Corrections to The American, Pg. 1. "
2 CONT >>Bridget and Robert were of Saugus Plantation in 1635 and in Sandwich 1637. Robert d. 19 Nov. 165? (SVR pg. 22); bef 1657.  Children by Bodfish were: Robert Jr., John, Mary, Sarah, dau., and Joseph. Bridget and probably the four 
2 CONC youngest children moved to Barnstable, Ma. 1657 but following Smauel's death in 1662, returned to Sandwich where she is listed with a residence in 1667 property survey. Her death is not recorded in Sandwich."
2 CONT
2 CONT C. F. Swift, Revised by, Genealogical Notes of Barnstable, Massachusetts Families (1979 Genealogical Publishing Co. Baltimore, Maryland), Vol. 1 pg. 68-74. Being a reprint of the Otis Amos Papers Orginally published in The Barnsta
2 CONC ble Patriot, Barnstable, Mass. Vol. 1 - 1989 Vol. 2 1890 F.B. & F. P. Goss Publishers & Printers. "
2 CONT >>Bodfish...The ancestor of this family wrote his name Botfish...Jan'y 1 1638-9 Robert Bodfish desired to becoma a freeman of Plymouth colony...He died 1651, leaving a wife Bridget who became Dec 15, 1657 the second wife of Samuel
2 CONC  Hinckey...He had...Joseph...Mary...Sarah...Peter...Robert."  
2 CONT
