1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Botfish-1
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''Robert (Botfish) Bodfish (abt. 1612 - 1651)
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Bodfish formerly Botfish
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1612 in Bromfield, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Bridget (Unknown) Hinckley — 
2 CONT
2 CONT married 1638 in Sandwich, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of John Bodfish, Sarah (Bodfish) Blossom, Mary Bodfish, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Bodfish, Robert Bodfish and	Joseph Bodfish
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 19 Nov 1651 in Sandwich, Barnstable, Massachusetts, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile managers: Amanda Thomas  [send private message], 
2 CONT
2 CONT Shirley Becker [send private message], and Earl Bice  [send private message]
2 CONT
2 CONT Botfish-1 created 10 Dec 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT Categories: Puritan Great Migration.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (Botfish) Bodfish migrated to New England 
2 CONT
2 CONT during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Botfish (as he spelled his name during his lifetime), aka Bodfish, 
2 CONT
2 CONT was born about 1614, based on estimated date of marriage, origins unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He emigrated in 1634, settling initially in Lynn, then to Sandwich, Massachusetts by 1639.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was made freeman 6 May 1635 as "Robte Bootefishe".[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1636-1644 served in a variety of capacities including jury, 
2 CONT
2 CONT surveyor of highways, petit jury and grand jury.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 7 Jan 1638/9, "Robte Badfish" of Sandwich desired his freedom[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT and took the oath of fidelity in 1639[4].
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1639 he married Bridget, whose surname is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1640: Received five acres of upland and meadow.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1643: among Sandwich men able to bear arms in Plymouth colony.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was "licensed to draw wine" in Sandwich in 1644.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT He signed his name as "Robert Botfish" 26 Feb 1647/8?[8] which also indicates he was literate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 19 November 165_[9] likely after the 3 April 1651 birth of his last child, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, and before the 15 Dec 1657 second marriage of his widow to Samuel Hinckley.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried in the Old Town Cemetery, Massachusetts.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary b abt 1639; m in Barnstable __ Nov 1659 John Crocker.[10],[11] Sarah, b abt 1643; m in Barnstable 21 Jun 1663 Peter Blossom[12] Joseph, b Sandwich 3 Apr 1651;[13] m. by 1674 Elizabeth Bessey.[14] Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Robert Charles Anderson, et al, The Great Migration, Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635, Volume 1, A-B; Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1999; pp 357-359 ↑ Massachusetts Bay Court Records 1:371 ↑ Plymouth Col
2 CONC ony Records 1:108 ↑ Plymouth Colony Records 8:184 ↑ Plymouth Colony Records 8:192 ↑ Plymouth Colony Records 8:192 ↑ Plymouth Colony Records, 2:75 ↑ Plymouth Colony Records 12:211 ↑ Sandwich Vital Records 1:22 ↑ Plymouth Colony Rec
2 CONC ords 8:43 ↑ Mayflower Descendant, 3:150 ↑ Mayflower Descendant, 3:53 ↑ Sandwich Vital Records 1:6, 16 ↑ The American Genealogist, 26:194 See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. and Canada, Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s about Robert Bodfish, Gale Research Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2009. U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900. Yates Publishing Ancestry.com Operation
2 CONC s Inc, 2004. American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI). Godfrey Memorial Library, comp. Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 1999.
2 CONT
