1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The 16th century Polish Nobility:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.almanachdegotha.org/id221.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of arms	Topór; Consort	Marianna Lubowiecka; Elżbieta Modrzejewska; Elżbieta Branicka; Zofia Krasińska; Noble family	Tarło; Father	Stanisław Tarło; Mother	Teresa Dunin Borkowska; Born	1684; Died	1750; Opole Lubelskie;
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan Tarło (1684–1750) was a Polish nobleman (szlachcic)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan became Colonel of the Crown Army and Podstoli of Crown in 1715, Lieutenant-General of the Crown Army in 1717, voivode of Lublin Voivodeship in 1719, voivode of Sandomierz Voivodeship in 1736. Marshal of the Crown Tribunal and 
2 CONC member of the Sejm. He was starost of Medyka, Sokal, Jasło and Grabowiec. Knight of the Order of the White Eagle, awarded in 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Tar%C5%82o_(1684%E2%80%931750)
