1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.footefamily.org/john_brook.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1546 John completed his apprenticeship as a leatherseller.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of John Brooke and Elizabeth Whatman  were:
2 CONT
2 CONT #William Brooke Christening 09 Oct 1556, St. Leonard's Eastcheap; London
2 CONT #Joan Brooke Christening 11 May 1555, St. Leonard's Eastcheap; London
2 CONT #Robert Brooke Christening 04 Apr 1566
2 CONT #John Brooke Christening 04 Mar 1558
2 CONT #Margaret Brooke Christening 8 MAR 1561, St. Leonard's Eastcheap; London 
2 CONT #Elizabeth Brooke
2 CONT #Susan Brooke Christening 06 Mar 1560 
2 CONT #Katherine Brooke Christening 13 Jul 1567
2 CONT #Sara Brooke 01 Oct 1570
2 CONT #Mary Brooke Christening 26 Nov 1564
2 CONT #Thomas Brooke Death: Before 1 Dec 1625
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Married name is BROOKE.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Brooke married, "8 May 1554, Elizabeth Waterman, both of St. Leonard's". Her surname is apparently incorrect in the marriage record, for in her will she names Elizabeth and William Whetman, children of her brother. Even this 
2 CONC appears to be not quite right. Her will indicates connections with Horsham, Sussex; and Blechinglee, now Bletchingley, Surrey. The Horsham connection appears to belong to the previous generation. Elizabeth would have been born bef
2 CONC ore the parish registers of Bletchingley began, but there are Whatman's there, including children the right age to be the neice and nephew mentioned above, and the burial of a Mary Broke, who corresponds perfectly with a child of 
2 CONC John and Elizabeth, and is the only occurrence of the name Brooke at Bletchingley before 1667. Elizabeth's will directed that she be buried at St. Leonard Eastcheape in London, "wherre I am a parrishioner." She gave "unto and amou
2 CONC nge the Companye of Lethersellers in London, to accompanye my Corps to the Churche at the date of my buryall Fortie shillings," "among the poore Children harboured daie of my buryall Fortie shillings." Extensive bequests of clothi
2 CONC ng and possessions were made, mentioning son-in-law Robert Foote, daughter Joane Foote and her daughter Mary Foote, daughter Margarett Foote and her daughter Elizabeth, Susan Bonner, daughter Sarah Storye and her children, brother
2 CONC s son William Whetman and his sister Elizabeth Whetmann, daughter Katheryn Flood and other.
2 CONT
