2 CONT John Foote of Royston was one of our oldest confirmed ancestors. He was born about the year 1530 in the town of Royston, Hertfordshire, England.. He owned a small manor house along with some land in the town. John was the father o
2 CONC f Robert Foote of Shalford, and the Grand Father of Nathaniel Foote the Settler. John died before. January 1558/59 in Royston, , Hertfordshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Parish records show that in the year 1548 John was married to Helen or Ellen Warren_(Waryn) the daughter of Richard Warren and Alice Jenway in Hertfordshire, England. She was born Abt. 1529 in Bassingbourn, Cambridgshire
2 CONC , Eng. Her death was recorded at St. Leonard,N/E Chapel, London,England. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The will of John Foote of Royston, tallow chandler, was probated 18 July 1558; it mentions wife Helen, son Robert, son John Foot, daughter Aves Foote, daughter Elizabeth Foote. TAG 53 says that John is brother to Robert Foote who 
2 CONC had sons Robert and John, daughters Elizabeth and Alice. This is based upon an anonymous pedigree in British Museum Additional MSS 5533, folio 99, quoted by Waters in "Genealogical Gleanings in England" p. 1285. It says Robert was
2 CONC  of Royston, Cambridgeshire, descended out of Lincolnshire, married to an unknown woman who married, second (___) Hall, sgt. trumpeter to Queen Elizabeth. TAG 54 questions this anonymous pedigree, presenting evidence that John was
2 CONC  actually the father of Robert and John. Among other things, this accounts for the fact that no probate could be found for Robert the father. John had children Robert and John, Elizabeth and a daughter called Avis or Alice/Alis (p
2 CONC robably a copyist error) -- the same children attributed to "father Robert". On 19 January 1558/1559 at St. Peter Cornhill in London there is recorded the wedding of "John Haull, trumpetor and Ellen Foote, Widowe." The coincidence
2 CONC  of children's names, spouses names, coupled with no findable will for Robert brings the authors to the conclusion John is the father, and the supposed father Robert is a confusion with John's eldest son.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT For information on the Foote family in England, see The American Genealogist 53, pp. 193-206, and 58, pp. 165-166.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation:  	tallow chandler 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Worshipful Company of Tallow Chandlers is one of the ancient livery companies of the City of London. The organisation, which engaged not only in tallow candle making but also in the trade of oils, first received a Royal Charte
2 CONC r in 1462.
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________________________________________
