2 CONT Nasalroad/Bickmore Family Home Page:Information about Robert John Foote I
2 CONT
2 CONT View Tree for Robert John Foote IRobert John Foote I (b. Bet. 1523 - 1525, d. July 18, 1558) Robert John Foote I (son of John Foote and Helen Ellen Warren)58 was born Bet. 1523 - 1525 in ROYSTON, CAMBRIDGE, ENGLAND58, and died Jul
2 CONC y 18, 1558 in Toydon, England59.He married Helen Ellen Warren on Abt. 1548 in Royston, Herfordshire, England59, daughter of Richard Warren and Alice Jenawaye.
2 CONT  Includes NotesNotes for Robert John Foote I: Robert FOOTE  oBIRTH: ABT 1525, or near,Royston,Cambridge,England  oREFERENCE: 13484  Family 1: Mrs. Robert FOOTE  oMARRIAGE: 1548/1549, Royston,Cambridge,England  1.Robert FOOTE 2.Joh
2 CONC n FOOTE 3.Elizabeth FOOTE 4.Alice FOOTE John Foote of Royston, Cambridgeshire, tallow chandler, made his undated will whih was probated 18 July 1558, in which he leaves to the church of Royston 20s; to wife Helen, all lands and te
2 CONC nements in Royston for life; and £80 to be divided among  all the children not named at this point; to servant Maud Smythe £6 13s 4d to her marriage; £3 that my brother Foote oweth to his two eldest children; to wife's brother Ric
2 CONC hard Warren the younger and to her uncle John Jenawaye of Stoone, 40s each; to  wife the rest; to son Robert a goblet, feather bed and bedding; to son John Foot a silver salt, feather bed and bedding; to Aves Foote and Elizabeth F
2 CONC oote, daughters, each three of the best spoons, bed and bedding; all the remainder to wife named  executrix; witnesses William Meede, citizen and grocer of London; John Jenaway, Nicholas Warreyn of Bassingbourn and Richard Warreyn
2 CONC  of Bassingbourn. John Foote had married Helen or Ellen Warren or Warreyn, sister to Richard Warren the younger and perhaps daughter of Nicholas Warreyn of Bassingbourn, and niece of John Jenawaye who may or may not have been brot
2 CONC her to her mother. (TAG Vol. 53 No. 4  "Nathaniel Foote's English Relatives by George E. McCracken [verbatim]) John Foote was most likely the brother of Robert Foote of Royston, Cambridgeshire, England. "Robert Foote of Shalford, 
2 CONC Essex, yeoman, 27 January 1608, proved 15 February 1608. To the poor in the parish twenty shillings. To the poor in Wethersfield twenty shillings. To my well beloved wife Joan, during her natural life, all such yearly  rent as to 
2 CONC me is reserved out of my lease of certain tenements which I hold for divers years yet enduring by the grant of Sir Robert hester knight and lying and being in the town of Royston, the yearly rent whereof to me reserved is at this 
2 CONC present  eight pounds. I give her also one annuity of four pounds to be paid during her natural life by my son Robert. To my son James fifty pounds. To son Daniel forty pounds at four and twenty. The same each to sons Nathaniel, F
2 CONC rancis and Josua at like  ages. To daughter Elizabeth Foote forty pounds at day of marriage or at age of thirty. To son Joseph my lease and term of years in a certain hopground called Plomley which I hold by lease from Mr. Josyas 
2 CONC Clarke and - his wife. Other givts to him.  Certain household stuff to wife. Elizabeth Ormes my maid servant. To ___ Tibbet, the wife of William Tibbet, five shillings in recompence of her pains she hath taken with me. To Mr. Rich
2 CONC ard Rogers preacher of God his Word twenty shillings. The wife  of George Elsing. Thomas Cott. To my son Robert my free tenement or mansion house wherein I now inhabit, with the land &c. and the stock of hop poles upon the hop gro
2 CONC und, he to pay the legacies &c. The residue of my goods &c. to all my children. If  it happen my daughter Mary Hewes to be departed then her part to be paid to her children. For the execution of this will I do ordain, nominate and
2 CONC  appoint my well beloved son Robert Foote to be my sole executor and I do desire my well beloved brother  John Foote of London grocer and my son in law John Hewes of Royston to be supervisors and assistants to my executors." Note:
2 CONC  [Genealogical Gleanings in England, Vol. 2 by Henry F. Waters A.M.]  More About Robert John Foote I and Helen Ellen Warren: Marriage 1: Abt. 1548, Royston, Herfordshire, England.59 Marriage 2: WFT Est. 1541-157260 Children of Rob
2 CONC ert John Foote I and Helen Ellen Warren are: +Richard (Robert) Foote, b. Abt. 1553, Shelford, Essex, England60, d. February 15, 1607/08, Shelford, Essex, England61.
2 CONT
