2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT Source: Google, From the files of Stephen M. Lawson A tallow chandler, his will was probated Jul. 18, 1558. Those receiving bequests included: the church at Royston, wife Helen, servant Maud Smythe, an unnamed brother, wife's brot
2 CONC her Richard Warren the younger, wife's uncle John Jenawaye, sons John and Robert, and daughters Aves <Alice> and Elizabeth. Witnesses included John Jenawaye, and Nicholas and Richard Warreyn of Bassingbourn, Cambridgeshire, which 
2 CONC is about three miles from Royston.
