2 CONT d. 06 May 1649|p22.htm#i1210|John Paine||p133.htm#i7182|Francis Spring||p133.htm#i7183|Anthony Paine||p133.htm#i7184|Martha Castell|d. 28 Jun 1603|p133.htm#i7185|||||||');"Pedigree 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony Paine was also known as Anthony Paine. He was born circa 1590 at Nowton, Linconshire, England; 1585 per World Family Tree V4Nowton is in Suffulk, not Lincolnshire as SUMNER gives! I find no Noroton, Lincolnshire, or all En
2 CONC gland, as Bigelow gives! He was the son of John Paine and Francis Spring. Anthony Paine married ? Susannah Potter, daughter of (?) Potter, before 1622; Portsmouth RI; One m. 1660 John Anthony (498). Anthony Paine was resident Admi
2 CONC tted as inhabitant on 6 December 1638 at Portsmouth, Newport, RI. He was FOUNDER on 30 April 1639 at Portsmouth, RI; He & 28 others signed compact for government of Portsmouth, RI. He was a founder on 30 April 1639 at Portsmouth, 
2 CONC Newport, RI. A contract for the marriage of Anthony Paine and an unknown person was signed on 10 November 1643; A.P. Widower, entered into an Agreement with Rose [French] Grinnell, previous to tyheir marriage. Rose was the widow o
2 CONC f Matthew Grinnell who she had married 27 Aug 1615 in Leyden, Essex, England. He married Rose French after 1643/44; Portsmouth RI. Anthony Paine married Alice Potter. Anthony Paine left a will before 6 May 1649; " I Anthony Paine,
2 CONC  in my perfect memory, do manifest my mind and last will is to give & bequest unto my daughter Alice, one cow, she or husband paying unto my daughter Mary Tripp, so much as the cow is judged to be worth more than the heiffer, and 
2 CONC to be made up equal out of the cow; and further my mind & will is to make my wife Rose Paine my whole & sole execturix to see my the former covenant & my last will performed & my debts paid, & Mr Porter & William Baulstone to see 
2 CONC my estate equally divided." Wittnesses. Wn Freeborne, Thomas Waite. He died on 6 May 1649 at Portsmouth, Newport, R.I; Month, place from Bigelow.dmt gives 27 Oct 1649, cites date of his will & widow Rose referred to as Rose Weedon
2 CONC . He was Administrator on 27 October 1649; John atripp & wife Mary give receipt to Rose Weedon, widow of Anthony Paine, for legacy from the will of the latter. He was Administrator in 1650; Anthony Paines will had given a legacy t
2 CONC o daughter Mary, for which her husband gave discharge to testator's relic by name of Rose Weeden. His estate was probated in 1650. He purchased land of PO} in 1650; "& may seem to have have had fam. from release, 1650, to share of
2 CONC  property of P. wh. d. a. 1640." After his death ? 
