1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Crosssman-of-Providence/6000000006229763010?through=6000000006970438849 & not the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Crossman-of-Taunton/6000000004094659
2 CONC 503?through=6000000006970438849 (who was not the son of John Crossman).
2 CONT * Not the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Annis-March/6000000006444369918
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Moses-104 on 6 May 2023 and then edited 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized: 20 March 1584/5 in Horkstow, Lincolnshire, England. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Nicholas Mo(y)ses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Isabel Moses on 30 July 1609 in Horkstow, Lincolnshire, England. [1]
2 CONT Children of John Tripp and Isabel Moses:
2 CONT
2 CONT All baptized at Horkstow: [1]
2 CONT # John Tripp. Bapt. 8 September 1611. Immigrant to New England. Died October 28, 1678 in Portsmouth, Rhode Island.
2 CONT # Robert Tripp. (twin) Bapt. 27 January 1613/4. Buried 10 February 1613/4.
2 CONT # Grace Tripp. (twin) Bapt. 27 January 1613/4. Buried 7 February 1613/4.
2 CONT # Francis Tripp. Bapt. 10 February 1614/5.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Tripp. Bapt. 15 December 1615. Buried 19 July 1648.
2 CONT # Dorothy Tripp. Bapt. 20 March 1618/9. Buried 19 August 1624.
2 CONT # Ann Tripp. Bapt. 7 July 1621. Buried 22 February 1626/7
2 CONT # Robert Tripp. Bapt. 8 May 1625.
2 CONT # Bridget Tripp. Bapt. 20 September 1629. Buried 14 February 1629/30
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: 4 November 1654 in Horkstow, Lincolnshire, England. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Common Errors to Avoid'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Second husband: She is sometimes found on the internet as also marrying John Crossman. This is incorrect. She was married to John Tripp as Isabel Moses and buried as Isabel Tripp.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''John Tripp, 1611 - 1678: A Glimpse into Our Founder's Life''. by Janet Tripp Andrews edited by Jan E. Tripp © November, 2016. < [https://portsmouthhistorical.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/John_Tripp_1611-1678_V11-10-16.pdf PDF]
2 CONC  >
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Tripp was baptized 8 Sep 1611/1612 at Horkstow Parish, Lincolnshire, England according to a deposition (loose folder dated 1670; New Bedford Library) concerning his personal history. He states Horkstow as his birthplace. <BR
2 CONC >
2 CONT >One of about twelve children of''' John Tripp and Isabel Moses''', John Tripp was apprenticed to John Baats of Thorsby, Lincolnshire to learn ship carpentry and served seven years and more. Thereafter, he bound himself (in 1633/1
2 CONC 634) to Frances East for four years. After about one and one half years of service (1635/1636), East sold the contract to Robert Jafra of Boston. Jafra fled Boston, with John Tripp in tow, to Rhode Island to avoid religious persec
2 CONC ution. Thereafter, Jafra sold the contract to Randall Holden of Portsmouth, RI. After some time, John Tripp paid off (probably 1637/1638) the remaining time on the contract. …
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT •Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the parish register of Horkstow, Lincolnshire, ENG (LDS FHL Film #504,248), Isabel Moyses/Moses was christened in Horkstow, Lincolnshire, ENG, 20 Mar 1584, the d/o Nicholas Moyses. She married John Tripp there in Hork
2 CONC stow on 30 Jul 1609. Her daughter Ann was chr. 7 Jul 1621 in Horkstow, and was buried in Horkstow 22 Feb 1626, i.e. age 4-1/2. Although there is no burial record for John Tripp, Isabel (Moyses) Tripp was called a widow in 1648 whe
2 CONC n her daughter Elizabeth was buried there in Horkstow. Isabel herself was bur. in Horkstow 4 Nov 1654. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Horkstow lies at the northern end of Lincolnshire, and Skirbeck lies at the southern end. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel was christened, married, and buried in Horkstow and there is no evidence that she ever went even 20 miles from her home, much less all the way to Skirbeck. Her daughter Ann was born much too late to be the husband of Edmund
2 CONC  Ingalls even if she had not died as a young child. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Below are copies of the records: 
2 CONT
2 CONT LDS FHL Film #436,033 item 3: Horkstow Parish Register Transcripts, 1561-1719: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 30 Jul 1609 -- John Tripp m. Elizabeth Moyses [Bishop's Transcript has Ezabel Moyses.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Sep 1611 -- John chr., son of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 Jan 1613/4 -- Robt. chr., son of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 Jan 1613/4 -- Grace chr., daughter of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Feb 1613/4 -- Grace bur., daughter of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Feb 1613/4 -- Robt. bur., son of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Feb 1614/5 -- Francis chr., son of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Dec 1616 -- Elizabeth chr., daughter of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Mar 1618/9 -- Dorothie chr., daughter of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Jul 1621 -- Anne chr., daughter of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 Aug 1624 -- Dorothy Tripp bur., daughter of John Tripp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 May 1625 -- Robart Trippe chr., son of John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 22 Feb 1626/7 -- Anne [Bishop's Transcript has Agnes] Trippe bur., daughter of John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Sep 1629 -- Bridgett chr., daughter of John Trippe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Feb 1629/30 -- Bridgett Trippe bur., daughter of John Trippe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 Jul 1648 -- Elizabeth bur., daughter of Isabell Tripp widow 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Nov 1654 -- Isabel Trippe a poore wid bur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John Tripp b: 27 MAY 1575 in Skirbeck, Lincolnshire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Isabel (Esable) Moses b: BEF 4 SEP 1575 in Skirbeck, Lincolnshire, England c: 4 SEP 1575
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This Isabell might be a mistaken amalgamation of two same-named women with different husbands (John Tripp and John Crossman). (Fixed, May 2023)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth surname has also been reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/surnames/moyses Moyses]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/surnames/moises Moises]
2 CONT
2 CONT Given name has also been reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Isabel
2 CONT * '''Isabelle
2 CONT * '''Ezabell
2 CONT * '''Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1580 at Skirbeck (now part of Boston), Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT * circa 1580 in Northumberland, England
2 CONT * June 25, 1580 at Horkstow, Lincolnshire (now North Lincolnshire), England
2 CONT * March 25, 1585 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * after 1597 at Skirbeck (now part of Boston), Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT * after 1610 at Skirbeck (now part of Boston), Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT * November 4, 1654 at Horkstow, Lincolnshire (now North Lincolnshire), England
2 CONT * circa 1666 at Newport, Newport County, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of burial have been (erroneously?) reported to be November 4, 1654 at Horkstow, Lincolnshire (now North Lincolnshire), England.
2 CONT
