1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Potter-582
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Potter was born in England about 1587. She was said to be the sister of Robert Potter. However, based on the year Alice was born, and the year of birth of Robert Potter and each of his siblings, she was likely his aunt, sist
2 CONC er of Robert's father George. Terms like sister were often used for an aunt, similar to brother for nephew, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the sister of Robert Potter, then of Lynn, Mass., but later of Portsmouth, R.I., where he signed the compact in 1639.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Neither Alice Potter (born about 1587) nor George Potter (born about 1584) were children of Robert Potter and Elizabeth Marshall. Robert and Elizabeth married in 1591. Their first child was baptized in 1592.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice married in England about 1610 Anthony Paine. Alice and Anthony had at least four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Alice Paine, b. Abt 1612, England, bapt. 30 Aug 1626 at Newport Pagnell, Buckingham, England, father Anthony Paine, FHL Film 88489.[2] m. Lott Strange, who died before 1688, no children; Alice d. 1690. Alice's will of 1688 left 
2 CONC legacy to her niece Elizabeth, daughter of John Tripp and her sister Mary.[3]
2 CONT # Mary Paine, b. Abt 1616 (uncertain) in England, m. (1) abt 1638, prob. in Portsmouth, R.I. John Tripp who died at Portsmouth in 1678. Mary (Paine) Tripp m. 4 Apr 1682 at Portsmouth Benjamin Engell. Mary d. 12 Feb. 1687, prob at 
2 CONC Portsmouth.[4]
2 CONT # Anne Paine, bapt. 8 Oct 1620: "Anne Payne, the daughter of Anthony Payne and Alice his wife was baptized the 8th day of Octobe 1620." (See image.)[5]
2 CONT # Anthony Paine, bapt. 24 Jul 1631 at Newport Pagnell, Buckingham, England; d. 26 Jan 1632, father Anthony Paine, FHL Film 88489.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne and Anthony did not survive. Anthony Paine named daughters Alice and Mary in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony Paine was admitted as an inhabitant of Portsmouth, Rhode Island on 6 Feb 1638:
2 CONT
2 CONT Feb 6, of the same year, 1638, ANTHONY PAINE was "received to be an inhabitant" at Portsmouth, R.I., but further particulars concerning him, or his family are wanting, except that...his wife bore the sweet name of Rose.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Anthony and 28 others (John Tripp, Robert Stainton, George Potter, Robert Potter, Wm Hutchinson, Samuel Gorton et al) signed a Compact of Loyalty to the government of Portsmouth on 30 Apr 1639.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice (Potter) Paine died probably at Portsmouth, Rhode Island before 10 Nov 1643, the day Anthony Paine signed a prenuptial with second wife Rose. As a widower, he entered into an agreement with Rose [French] Grinnell, previous t
2 CONC o their marriage.[9]
