2 CONT -------------------- JOANNA KEMBER was born about 1584, of Braxton, Devon, England, to Robert Kember and Anne. She married Peter Coffyn. She immigrated in 1642 from England to Newbury, Essex, Massachusetts, with her son Tristram a
2 CONC nd family, and two daughters Enice and Mary. She was 58 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna Kember passed away 30 May 1661, in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, at about 77 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Brixton, Devon]]
2 CONT {{Puritan Great Migration}}
2 CONT == Biography == Peter Coffin of Brixton married Joan Thember or Thumber, and died in 1627-8; she came to New England with her son, and died at Boston 30 May1661<ref>COFFIN GATHERINGS: Five Generations of Descendants of Tristram Co
2 CONC ffin of Newbury and Nantucket, By W. S. Appleton. Boston: Press of David Clapp & Son, 1896. [An outgrowth of the anniversary meeting ofthe Coffin family at Nantucket in 1881.]</ref>
2 CONT Came to New England 1642, with children Tristram, Mary, Eunice. Joan died May 1661 age 77 years (b.c. 1584).<ref name=CoffinF >"The Coffin Family." New England Historical and Genealogical Register.  24:149. (1870)</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT She came to New England with her son Tristram on the ship Hector in 1642 settling in Salisbury, Massachusetts.
2 CONT :Died 30 May 1661 in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts<ref> Old Families of Salisbury & Amesbury MA by Hoyt pg 103</ref><ref>"Pedigree Resource File," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:94XT-TNG : accesse
2 CONC d 24 October 2018), entry for Joanna Kember; file (2:2:2:MM9T-MZY), submitted 5 January 2000 by tcoleman2715129 </ref>
