1 NOTE Mayflower
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=a97f91ff-15aa-4953-9d74-5124145dabd8&tid=10221925&pid=-644207537
1 NOTE Came to America on Mayflower.  A wool comber, he was one of the few skilled workers on the ship. Signer of Mayflower Compact.
1 NOTE The Will of Francis Cooke: The last Will and Testament of ffrancis Cooke of Plymouth late Deceased: exhibited before the Court held att Plymouth aforsaid the fift day of June 1663 on the oathes of mr John Aldin and mr John howland
2 CONC ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Last Will and Testament of ffrancis Cooke made this seaventh of the tenth month 1659. I being att prsent weake and Infeirme in body yett in prfect memory throw mercy Doe comitt my soule unto god that gave it and my body to the
2 CONC  earthe; which my will is should bee Intered in a Decent and comly manner; As for such goods and lands as I stand posessed of I Doe will and bequeath as followeth;1 My will is that hester my Dear and loveing wife shall have all my
2 CONC  moveable goods and all my Cattle of all kinds; viz: neat Cattle horsekind sheep and swine to be att her Dispose 2 my will is that hester my wife shall have and Injoy my lands both upland and meddow lands which att prsent I posess
2 CONC e During her life 3 I Doe ordaine and appoint my Deare wife and my son John Cooke Joyne exequitors of this my said will Witnes John Aldin ffrancis Cooke John howland
2 CONT Inventory:  Morter and pestel, earthen pots and pans, pewterand iron pots, hammer, saw, three pairs of sheep sheers, featherbed and bolster, hoes, cushens, two hats, ten pair of stockings, old coat, gloves, twenty pounds of wool a
2 CONC nd twenty-one sheep.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis immigrated to America on the Mayflower with his son, John.  His wife, Hester, and their children Jane and Jacob arrived on the Anne in 1623.  In the Leydon archives, it is recorded that Frances entered Holland on June 30, 
2 CONC 1603.  He was a bachelor and listed his profession as a woolcomber.  He was accompanied by Phillippe De Veau and Raphael Roelandt, his friends, with Hester Mahieu, spinster, from Canterbury in England, accompanied by her sister Je
2 CONC nny Mahieu, her mother and Jenny Mahieu, her sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis was made a freeman in 1633.  He appeared frequently in Plymouth records on grand trials juries, as surveyor of highways, on various ad hoc committees and in a number of land transactions.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The ancestry of Francis Cooke is not known.  Several fake ancestries have been presented, some clearly hoaxes (one hoax can be found in "New Light on the Pilgrim Story,"  the entire chapter 6.)  For a discussion of why this is a 
2 CONC hoax, see "English Ancestry and Homes of the Pilgrim Fathers," by Charles Banks.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is conflicting evidence about the birth of Francis Cooke.  A note scribbled in Bradford's Journal says Francis Cooke died above the age of 80, meaning he was born before 1583.  However, in August 1643, he was in a list of me
2 CONC n of Plymouth between the age of 16 and 60 allowed to bear arms.  This means he was born after 1583.  Also, he was married in Leyden in 1603, so he probably would have been at least 21 at the time.  This means a birth before 1583 
2 CONC  The fact that all these records seem to conflict suggests that he was born very close to 1583.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Banks mentions a Francis Cooke baptized on 6 April 1572, in Biddenden, Kent, England, son of Thomas.  However, this person is about ten years too old for the Francis of the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cooke had been living in Holland about 8 years before the arrival of John Robinson and the rest of the Pilgrims.  His wife Hester was from Canterbury, England, so perhaps that is where he is from as well."
2 CONT
2 CONT George Ernest Bowman suggests strongly that Francis Cooke was born after August 1583.  His ground for this is that Cooke is listed in the official enrollment made by the Plymouth authorities in August, 1643, of all the men in the 
2 CONC colony between the ages of 16 and 60 who were able to bear arms.  Cook therefore must have been under 60.
