2 CONT No specific date PCR 12:5
2 CONT Cooke is granted land which "lye beyond the brook to Strawberie hill."
2 CONT 17 December 1623 PCR 11:5
2 CONT Cooke helped write "Orders agreed on at feveral times for the Generall good of the Colony and the Better government and preferration of the fame."
2 CONT 1626 No specific date Davis 1883 I:340
2 CONT Child, Mary born.
2 CONT 1627 No specific date PCR 12:9
2 CONT Cooke and 12 others are allotted "4 black Heyfers....and two shee goats in" the1627 cattle division.
2 CONT 1628 3 January 1627/8 PCR 12:14
2 CONT Helped write "about deuision of lands" that was agreed in a full court.
2 CONT 1629 January 1629 PCR 12:51
2 CONT Mention that William Bradford bought s acres of land from "Ffrancis Cooke" and sold it to Georg Watson.
2 CONT 1633 No specific date PCR 1:3
2 CONT Francis Cooke on list of "The Names of the Freeman of the Incorporation of Plymouth in New England, An: 1633."
2 CONT No specific date PCR 8:173
2 CONT On Plymouth list of freemen in 1633.
2 CONT 7 January 1632/33 PCR 1:8
2 CONT Cooke and Robert Heeks arbitrated a dispute between Samuell Tiller, the elder, and Peter Browne.
2 CONT 25 March 1633 PCR 1:10
2 CONT Taxed 18 shillings.
2 CONT 1634 27 March 1634 PCR 1:28
2 CONT Taxed 9 shillings.
2 CONT 1 October 1634 PCR 1:31
2 CONT Cooke appointed to lay out the highways.
2 CONT 1636 7 November 1636 PCR 1:46
2 CONT John Harmon acknowledged himself as an apprentice to Cooke for 7 years
2 CONT retroactive to 11 October 1636.
2 CONT 1637 7 March 1636/7 PCR 7:5
2 CONT "Frauncis Cooke" complained against Thomas Lettus, James Walker, John Browne, the younger and the elder, Thomas Teley, and Thomas Willet because they abused hiscattle which lost her calf, milk, and almost died. The jury found for 
2 CONC Cooke against the elder Browne for 3 pounds damages and 13 shillings, 6 pence charges ofthe court.
2 CONT 27 March 1637 PCR 1:52
2 CONT Cooke on "The Names of the Freeman."
2 CONT 2 May 1637 PCR 1:58
2 CONT Appointed to the committee to lay out highways.
2 CONT 7 June 1637 PCR 1:60
2 CONT Execution is granted against Mr. John Browne for the verdict recorded against him regarding Francis Cooke.
2 CONT 1638 2 January 1637/8 PCR 1:74
2 CONT Served on jury which found Edward Shaw guilty of "felonous takeing of xv from
2 CONT the person of William Corvannell."
2 CONT Served on jury which found Marke Mendlone guilty "as accessory to felony
2 CONT committed by Edward Shaw."
2 CONT 2 January 1637/8 PCR 7:7
2 CONT Served on jury which found John Davis not guilty for failing to deliver MichallTurners goods from Weymouth to Sandwich and awarded Davis 50 shillings damages and "the charges of the court."
2 CONT Served on jury which found John Holmes not guilty of trespass and awarded him 5shillings damages and "the charges of the court."
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the defendants, the executors of Mr. Thomas Prince's will against John and Elizabeth Willis over a plot of land and awarded
2 CONT 7 shillings damages and "the charges of the court."
2 CONT 2 June 1638 PCR 1:87
2 CONT Appointed to Grand Inquest.
2 CONT 8 November 1638 PCR 1:103
2 CONT Small parcel of land, previously held by Francis Cooke, was granted to Mr.
2 CONT Thomas Prence.
2 CONT 1639 4 February 1638/9 PCR 1:112
2 CONT Granted a parcel of land lying at the end of Goodman Shaw's land at Smilt River.
2 CONT 4 June 1639 PCR 12:44
2 CONT Thomas Prence's land lies next to Cooke's land.
2 CONT 3 September 1639 PCR 7:13
2 CONT Served on jury which found the defendant William Hatch guilty of trespass and awarded the plaintiff, Joseph Meriam, 5 pounds, 14 shillings, and 2 pence damagesand "the charges of the court."
2 CONT Served on jury which found the defendant John Lewis guilty of trespass and awarded the plaintiff, William Gibson, 5 pounds, 14 shillings, and 2 pence damages and "the charges of the court."
2 CONT 3 December 1639 PCR 7:14
2 CONT Served on jury which found the plaintiff, John Atwood, in a trespass case against Robert Bartlet for "three pounds three shillings six pence debt, forty shillings dam the charges of the court."
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Robert Waterman, in a trespass case against Thomas Clarke for "thirty-five shillings, five shillings dam the charges of the court."
2 CONT 1640 3 March 1639/40 PCR 7:16
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Samuell Chaundler, in a trespass case against John Jenney and awarded seventeen pounds, 4 shilling damages and other charges.
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, John Barnes, for a debt against John Holmes and awarded 8 pounds.
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, John Witcomb, 14 shillings and 6 pence against John Stow for trespass.
2 CONT 6 May 1640 PCR 1:152
2 CONT Appointed to committee to compute the number of acres of land in the meadows ofEdward Doteys.
2 CONT 2 June 1640 PCR 1:155
2 CONT Appointed to Grand Inquest
2 CONT 5 October 1640 PCR 1:163
2 CONT Francis and John Cooke granted land of not more than 200 acres, "between Leiftennant Holmes land at the North Riuer and John Rodgers land.'
2 CONT 1641 1 February 1640/1 PCR 2:7
2 CONT Appointed to the committee to layout highways.
2 CONT 1642 1 March 1641/2 PCR 2:34
2 CONT Appointed surveyor of the highways for Plymouth.
2 CONT 7 June 1642 PCR 2:40
2 CONT Appointed surveyor of the highways for Plymouth.
2 CONT 7 June 1642 PCR 7:30
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Thomas Byrd, in a trespass case against James Cudworth for 40 shilling damages and "the charges of the suite."
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, John Joyce, in a trespass case against Walter Deuell, which awarded damages "and the costs and charges of the suite."
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Samuell Hinkley, in a trespass case against Mr. Joseph Hull, which awarded charges of the defendant.
2 CONT 7 September 1642 PCR 7:31
2 CONT Served on jury which in a trespass case between the plaintiff, Samuell Hinkley,and Mr. Joseph Hull. "The action was agreed by mutuall consent."
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Richard Church, in a trespass caseagainst Matthew Fuller for debt, damages and charges of the suite.
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Mr. Willm Hanbury, in a trespass against John Shaw, which awarded charges of the defendant
2 CONT Served on jury which Willm Hiler admitted to a debt and promised to pay it within 14 days.
2 CONT 17 October 1642 PCR 2:49
2 CONT Court granted Cooke 60 acres at the "medow at the North Meddow by Joanes Riuer if it be there to be had."
2 CONT 1643 7 March 1642/3 PCR 2:53
2 CONT Appointed to the grand jury of the highways.
2 CONT 7 March 1642/3 PCR 7:33
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, Mr. Willm Hanbury against Mr. Andrew Hellot for a debt. The court found for debt, damages and cahrges of the suite.
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, John Coggen, in a trespass case against Mr. Joseph Hull. The court awarded 2 steers until the action is tried or the debt is paid.
2 CONT Served on jury which found for the plaintiff, John Tompson, in a trespass case against John Holmes, and awarded the debt, damages, and charges of the suite.
2 CONT 6 June 1643 PCR 2:56
2 CONT Appointed to the Grand Inquest.
2 CONT August 1643 PCR 8:187
2 CONT On list "of all the Males that are able to beare Armes."
2 CONT 1645 4 June 1645 PCR 2:84
2 CONT Appointed surveyor of the highways for Plymouth.
2 CONT 1648 1 August 1648 PCR 2:132
2 CONT On a coroner's jury "to make inquiry of the death of the child of Allis Bishop,the wife of Richard Bishop." Jury found child of 4 years with her throat and windpipe slashed and a knife lying next to her. Allis confessed to the jur
2 CONC y that "shee murdered the child with the said knife."
2 CONT 1649 11 July 1649 PCR 12:175
2 CONT Jacob Cooke bought land from Mr. Thomas Prence for 21 pounds and 10 shillings which adjoined the lands of Mr. Jon Combes and Francis Cooke.
2 CONT 1650 9 April 1650 PCR 12:185-6
2 CONT "Ffrancis Cooke" gave an upland medow of 100 acres, which he was granted on 5 October 1640, "lying att the North Riuer" to his son Jacob Cooke "to have and to hold." Jacob then sold the land to Moris Truant for 16 pounds sterling.
2 CONT 10 June 1650 PCR 2:160
