2 CONC rs; 4.Elizabeth (c1616- 9 March 1670) married Richard Church; 5.Abigail (c1618- 3 January 1693) married Anthony Snow; 6.Nathaniel (c1625-1667) married Sarah Walker; and 7.Joseph (1627 - 4 May 1689) married Priscilla Faunce (1634- 
2 CONC 15 May 1707).[8] •> the birth of the five daughters in England are sourced from the Parish Register, Great Amwell, Hertfordshire, England. All of Richard Warren's children survived to adulthood, married and had large families. It 
2 CONC is claimed that Warren is the Mayflower passenger with most descendants, numbering over 14 million [10] including: President Ulysses S. Grant, President Franklin D. Roosevelt, former Alaska Governor Sarah Palin,[4] astronaut Alan 
2 CONC Shepard, author Laura Ingalls Wilder (Little House on the Prairie series), actor Richard Gere, Lavinia Warren, also known as Mrs. Tom Thumb, [5] educator and poet Henry Wadsworth Longfellow,[6][7] and the Wright brothers.[1]
