2 CONT said of him In Mourt's Relation Edward Winslow lists ten men on an early expedition at Cape Cod, including Richard Warren, who were from London. According to Nathaniel Morton in 1669 book, New England's Memorial:
2 CONT
2 CONT "This year [1628] died Mr. Richard Warren, who hath been mentioned before in this book, and was a useful instrument;; and during his life bore a deep share in the difficulties and troubles of the first settlement of the plantation
2 CONC  of New Plimouth."
