1 OCCU Tailor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com : accessed 08 April 2021), memorial page for Matthew West (1598–16 Jan 1677), Find a Grave Memorial no. 103605708, ; Maintained by Richard Hornsby (con
2 CONC tributor 47775749) Unknown. 
2 CONT ------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Matthew West was a Baptist tailor from Somersetshire, England who settled in Lynn, Massachusetts about 1635."
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Matthew West was a Baptist tailor who lived in Lynn, MA in 1636, became a freeman in 1637, and moved to Newport, RI in 1646.  He had five sons and a daughter: Nathaniel, Robert, Bartholomew, John, Joan, and Francis."
2 CONT
2 CONT >* "Matthew,  Francis [his son] and Francis' siblings Nathaniel, Bartholomew, Robert, John, and Joan relocated to Rhode Island. Matthew died in 1677, signing over his land and possessions to his grandson, Nathaniel West, Jr. All o
2 CONC f this is in the land records and government records of Rhode Island and New Jersey (where Bartholomew, Robert, and Joan migrated to)."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://boards.ancestryclassroom.com/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=4373&p=surnames.west
2 CONT
2 CONT >"As for Thomas West and Elizabeth Sankey being the parents of Matthew, there is no proof of this and I have only seen undocumented evidence of this on the internet."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1636- Residence: Lynn, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1637, March 9- Freeman.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1646- Residence: Newport, RI.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1655- Freeman
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT ==Sources:==
2 CONT *HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 631
2 CONT * http://boards.ancestryclassroom.com/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=4373&p=surnames.west
2 CONT * http://www.doddridgecountyroots.com/register/west.htm cites:
2 CONT * * [1]  Earl P. Crandall, Hudson, NY, citing Wheeler's "History of Stonington, CT," pp 630-31; and Austin at GDRI.
2 CONT * * [2]  William F. Donnelly, The Wests of Duck Creek, Harrison County, Virginia (now West Virginia) , Gateway Press, Baltimore MD, 1997, p. 512.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Not a member of the de la Warr family!'''
2 CONT --------------------
