2 CONT There’s a Joan Wakeman married a Matthew West
2 CONT
2 CONT "England Marriages, 1538–1973 ", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:NK47-S2Q : 13 March 2020), Mathew West, 1628.
2 CONT
2 CONT But I don’t see that we know these are the same people. "Matthew West was a Baptist tailor who lived in Lynn, MA in 1636, became a freeman in 1637, and moved to Newport, RI in 1646. He had five sons and a daughter: Nathaniel, Robe
2 CONC rt, Bartholomew, John, Joan, and Francis."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Matthew, Francis [his son] and Francis' siblings Nathaniel, Bartholomew, Robert, John, and Joan relocated to Rhode Island. Matthew died in 1677, signing over his land and possessions to his grandson, Nathaniel West, Jr. All of th
2 CONC is is in the land records and government records of Rhode Island and New Jersey (where Bartholomew, Robert, and Joan migrated to)." 1636- Residence: Lynn, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1637, March 9- Freeman.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1646- Residence: Newport, RI.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1655- Freeman
2 CONT
2 CONT http://boards.ancestryclassroom.com/thread.aspx?mv=flat&amp;m=4373&... http://www.doddridgecountyroots.com/register/west.htm cites:
2 CONT * [1] Earl P. Crandall, Hudson, NY, citing Wheeler's "History of Stonington, CT," pp 630-31; and Austin at GDRI.
2 CONT * [2] William F. Donnelly, The Wests of Duck Creek, Harrison County, Virginia (now West Virginia) , Gateway Press, Baltimore MD, 1997, p. 512. Not a member of the de la Warr family!
2 CONT
