1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Audrey Barlow
2 CONT *Birth: 1603 in Lutterworth, Leicestershire Co., England
2 CONT *Immigration: Jul 1635 From, England (Aboard the ship, "Abigail") 
2 CONT *Death: AFT 1676 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT * daughter of Stafford Barlow, Gent. (her mother's name is not known).[3]
2 CONT *Marriage 1 William Almy b: ABT 1600 in South Kilworth, Leicestershire Co., England Married: 1626
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal/Magna Carta Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT Audrey Barlowe is listed as a descendant of King Henry II of England and his mistress Ida de Tosny Countess of Norfolk[10] for eligibility to the Descendants of the Illegitimate Sons and Daughters of the Kings of Britain (aka, 'th
2 CONC e Royal Bastards Society'). She is also documented by Douglas Richardson as a descendant of a Magna Carta surety baron.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *    1. Ann / AnnisAlmy b: 26 FEB 1626/27 in South Kilworth, Leicestershire Co., England.  married John Greene.
2 CONT *    2. John Almy b: ABT 1633 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT *    3.  Job Almy b: ABT 1634 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT *    4. Catherine / Katherine  Almy b: ABT 1635 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island.  married (1) Bartholomew West, (2) Nicholas Brown.
2 CONT *    5. Christopher Almy b: 1632 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a record for the baptism of a daughter of Stafford Barlow at Narborough, Leicestershire on 2 September 1599. Her first name is not given - she is just described as "filia" (daughter).[9] This may well be for Audrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Incorrect information
2 CONT
2 CONT A fictional background for Audrey Barlowe's father, "John," states he often went by his middle name, Stafford, and that his father was named William Thomas and he was married to a Margaret Woodland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Correct information
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: Stafford Barlow, Gent.[3] Stafford is the name on Audrey's marriage license.[5] The name of Audrey's mother is not known.[3]
2 CONT *Paternal Grandparents: Stafford Barlow's parents were Thomas Barlow (or Barlowe) and Ellen (or Eleanor) Stafford.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy married by license dated 17 July 1626 Audrey Barlow ("Williamus Almie de South Kilworth," gent., "etatis 26 annorum," and "Audream Barlowe de Lutterworth ... etatis 26 annorum," with the consent of Stafford Barlowe of
2 CONC  Lutterworth, gent., father of the said Audrey. She died after 28 February 1676/7, when she was named in her husband's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had five children: Annis Greene, Catherine, Christopher, John, & Job.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter of estimated date 23 May 1650 to John Winthrop Jr., Roger Williams, in describing the activities of the crew of a French prize vessel, reported that "one of them (having lain with Mr. Amie's daughter of Portsmouth) is 
2 CONC like now to marry her. The parents and the English are troubled greatly." This cannot be daughter Annis, who had married John Greene by 1649, so, unless there is a third daughter otherwise unrecorded, this record must refer to dau
2 CONC ghter Catherine. She does not appear on the 1635 passenger list with her parents and two siblings. If she was born in New England, then, it could be no earlier than the latter half of 1635, which would make her no more than fourte
2 CONC en at the time of the incident noted above. The probable resolution is that Catherine was born in England just before or after her brother Christopher, and either was omitted from the passenger list or came at a later time. We the
2 CONC refore estimate her date of birth as about 1630, although a date around 1634 would also be consistent with the other evidence. Furthermore, if this record does apply to Catherine, then she could not have been married to Bartholome
2 CONC w West in 1650. Pending more detailed investigation of the family of Bartholomew West, we estimate that the marriage took place about 1652.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Anderson's Great Migration Study Project 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy & Audrey Barlowe
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy was the son of Christopher Almey and Unknown Clarke , was born 1601 in Dunton-Bassett or South Kilworth, County. Leicester, England. He married Audrey Barlowe 1626 in Lutterworth, Leicestershire, England. He died Febr
2 CONC uary 28, 1676 in Portsmouth, Newport County, Rhode Island. Audrey Barlowe was born abt. 1602 in Lutterworth, Leicestershire, England. She died 1676 in Portsmouth, Newport County, Rhode Island. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Immigration: from England aboard the ship, "Abigail" Jul 1635.
2 CONT Ref: http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=francescha&id=I90924
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  Dec. 22, 1603 Lutterworth Harborough District Leicestershire, England  Death:  Feb. 28, 1677 Portsmouth Newport County Rhode Island, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   William Almy (1601 - 1677)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Ann Agnes Almy Greene (1627 - 1709)*
2 CONT   Christopher Almy (1632 - 1713)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown 
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Linda Mac Record added: May 07, 2009  Find A Grave Memorial# 36841808 
2 CONT
