1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1st Emmigration 17 Jun 1635 to Sandwich
2 CONT
2 CONT # ID: I27928
2 CONT
2 CONT # Name: William Almy
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sex: M
2 CONT
2 CONT # Birth: ABT 1600 in South Kilworth, Leicestershire Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT # Death: BEF 23 APR 1677 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Christopher Almy b: ABT 1571 in South Kilworth, Leicestershire Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: ?...? Clarke b: ABT 1572 in Lutterworth, Leicestershire Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Audry Barlowe b: 1603 in Lutterworth, Leicestershire Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Married: 1626
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Has Children Ann Almy b: 26 FEB 1626/27 in South Kilworth, Leicestershire Co., England
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Has No Children John Almy b: ABT 1633 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Has Children Job Almy b: ABT 1634 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Has Children Catherine Almy b: ABT 1635 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Has Children Christopher Almy b: 1632 in Portsmouth, Newport Co., Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. WILLIAM1 ALMY, (Christopher, Thomas, John),born Dunton-Bassett, Leicester County, England, in 1601. He died Portsmouth, RI 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. Lutterworth, Leicestershire, England, by license of 1626, AUDREY BARLOW, born 1603; died after 1676. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  i ANNE2 b. Dunton-Bassett, Leicestershire, England 1627; d. 17 May 1709; m. Portsmouth, RI, about 1648, JOHN GREENE of Warwick, RI, b. Salisbury, Wilts., England, 15 Aug 1620; d. 27 Nov 1708, son of John and Joan (Tatersall) Gree
2 CONC ne. Their children: 1. Deborah Greene, b. 10 Aug 1649; 2. John Greene, b. 6 Nov 1651; 3. William Greene, b. 1 Mar 1653; 4. Peter Greene, b. 7 Feb 1655; 5. Job Greene, b. 24 Aug 1656; 6. Phillip Greene, b. 7 Oct 1658; 7. Richard Gr
2 CONC eene, b. 8 Feb 1660; 8. Anne Greene, b. 19 Mar 1663; 9. Catharine Greene, b. 15 Aug 1665; 10. Audry Greene, b. 27 Dec 1667; and 11. Samuel Greene, b. 30 Jan 1671. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 ii CHRISTOPHER, b. Dunton-Bassett, England, 1632; m. ELIZABETH CORNELL. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii JOHN, b. Sandwich, MA, about 1637; d.s.p. 1 Oct 1676; m. MARY COLE, dau of James and Mary ( ) Cole. He was a merchant. On 24 Jul 1667 he was made Lieutenant of troop of horse and in 1676 he served as Captain in King Philip's 
2 CONC War. Mary Cole was the granddaughter of James Cole, the former owner of the famous Cole's Hill in Plymouth, MA, and reputed son of Sir William Cole of England, who was able to obtain a Royal Grant of land for this Cole family in P
2 CONC lymouth Colony. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 iv JOB, b. Sandwich, MA, about 1641; m. prob. 1663, MARY UNTHANK, b. Providence, RI, about 1645; d. after 1724; dau of Christopher and Susanna Unthank of Warwick, RI. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  v CATHERINE, b. Portsmouth, 1645; m.(1) BARTHOLOMEW WEST, son of Matthew West. Bartholomew d. before 1703. She m.(2) NICHOLAS BROWN. Children: (West): Bartholomew, William, John, and Stephen b. 1654. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy came to America first between 1628 and 1631. He very likely worked for his passage as he is not included in any passenger list available at this date. Further, his family was not with him. He was in Lynn, MA in 1631 w
2 CONC here he was fined for taking and using a canoe without permission. Before July 1634, he went back to England. In 1635 he returned to America in the ship `Abigail' with his wife Audrey and his two children; Anne, age 8, and Christo
2 CONC pher, age 3. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On his return to America he lived in Lynn. In the Spring 1637, he and nine others founded Sandwich, on Cape Cod, in the Plymouth Colony. On 22 June 1642 he sold his Sandwich house and lands and was soon in Portsmouth, RI where he 
2 CONC received a grant of land 14 Nov 1644. He became a Freeman in 1655, a Juryman in 1656, a Commissioner in 1656-57-63, and Foreman of the Jury in 1668. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His will, dated 28 Feb 1676, proved 23 Apr 1677, names sons Christopher and Job as Executors. He requested his body be buried beside his son John. He bequethed property to sons Christopher and Job, daughters Anna and Catherine, an
2 CONC d £20 to grandchild Bartholomew West at twenty-one years of age. 
2 CONT
2 CONT source:
2 CONT
2 CONT almy.us/news/almyindex.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT William b 1601
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher b 1632, son of William & Audrey
2 CONT
2 CONT William b 1655 son, of Christopher & Elizabeth Cornell
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel b 1701, son of William & Debra
2 CONT
2 CONT Job b 1736, son of Samuel m 1st Susanna, 2nd Ann
2 CONT
2 CONT Otis b 1771,son of Job & Ann
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt.Andrew b 1795, son of Otis & Lucinda
2 CONT
2 CONT Job b 1819 son of Capt. Andrew, m Mary Allyn Abell, he d 9/6/1897
2 CONT
2 CONT Sanford b 4/14/1825 d 11/3/1903 son of Andrew & Clarissa, and brother of Job, m Ellen Augusta Carrique, 2 children Ellen, Fredrick
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Clarissa (Almy) Almy wife of Capt Andrew and mother of Job and Sanford was a decendant of the original William Almy. Of the children of William there is record of four, Annis, Christopher,John,and Job, and Mrs. Almy is decend
2 CONC ed from Job, while as stated he husband sprang from the line of Christopher.
2 CONT
2 CONT (II) Job Almy, son of William, married Mary Unthank,and live in Portsmouth,Warwick,and Providence RI respectively.He was a deputy in Warwick from 1670-72 and assistant in 1673,74,75. He died in 1684. His children were: William,Chr
2 CONC istopher,William(2) Susanna,Audry,Debra,Cathrine,John,Mary and Job
2 CONT
2 CONT (III) Job Almy(2) son of Job, b.3/3/1681 Portsmouth m 12/6/1705 Bridget dau of Peleg & Mary(Coddington) Sanford and resided in Tiverton. He d 1/25/1767, children Job b 3/4/1707:Peleg 10/25/1709: Mary 6/20/1711:Eliphal 8/3/1713 Bri
2 CONC dget 5/16/1716Ann 1/28/1718:John 4/18/1720: Job5/16/1722:Debra 3/21/1724
2 CONT
2 CONT (IV) John Almy, son of Job& Bridget m Hannah
2 CONT
2 CONT children ofTiverton, Sanford b 8/28/1759:Pelegb 1/8/1761:Bridget 9/21/1762: John 4/16/1764: and Cook 9/24/1765.Themother of these died 1765
2 CONT
2 CONT (V) Sanford Almy,son John & Hannah b 8/28/1759 Tiverton RI m 9/27/1781 Lydia dau of Pardon & Mary Gray.Their children of Little Compton town record, accordind to Arnold, were: George b 7/7/1782: John b 7/17/1783: Hannah b 3/20/178
2 CONC 5:Fredrick b 11/20/1786:Sanford b 9/20/1788: Humphrey b 8? 27/1790: Pardon b 6/18/1792: Mary b 6/16/1794: Angelina 10/26/1796: Clarissa 8/24/1799:Louisa 9/12/1801: Lydia 3/7/1804:John C. 11/19/1807: and Fanny F 3/14/1810
2 CONT
2 CONT (VI) Clarissa Almy, born 8/24/1799, married Capt Andrew
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Elam6(Cook5,John4, etc.) Almy (b. in Tiverton 1800), a nephew of the Pardon5 Almy you mention, was a great-great-great grandfather of Marilyn Monroe (see Gary Boyd Roberts, "Notable Kin," vol. 1, p. 134.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pardon5 Almy of Little Compton had a son, Pardon Almy, Jr. who was a Lt. in the 19th Massachusetts and was killed in battle at Second Manasses, 30 Aug. 1862.
2 CONT
2 CONT William1 Almy was the ancestor of three Presidents, namely Harding, Nixon and Carter. (See G.B. Roberts, "Ancestors of American Presidents.")
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the tree to Nixon starting with Christopher & Elizabeth's dau. Elizabeth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth & Lewis Morris
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Morris & Mary Porter
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Morris &
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Burdg
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Burdg &
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Burdg Jr. &
2 CONT
2 CONT M. Mathews
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Burdg &
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane M.Hemingway
2 CONT
2 CONT Almira Park Burdg &
2 CONT
2 CONT Franklin Milhous
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Milhous &
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Anthony Nixon
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Milhous Nixon
2 CONT
2 CONT I also have Carter's tree & tried to enter it in another column but it didn't work. He descends from Richard & Mary (Porter) Morris' son Job & wife Mary Audry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Correction to 4/12/01 Almy msg.: Job Morris & Mary Ansley--not Audry.
2 CONT
2 CONT I also have a link from Christopher Almy & Elizabeth Cornell to Pres. Jimmy Carter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Almy - Lewis Morris
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Morris - Mary Porter
2 CONT
2 CONT Job Morris - Mary Ansley
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Morris - Abel Ansley
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Ansley - Wiley Carter
2 CONT
2 CONT Littleberry Walker Carter - Mary Ann Diligent
2 CONT
2 CONT William Archibald Carter - Nina Pratt
2 CONT
2 CONT James Earl Carter - Bessie Lillian Gordy
2 CONT
2 CONT James Earl Carter, Jr. b. 1924
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy
2 CONT
2 CONT Name - William Almy  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth - 1601 Dunton-Bassett or South Kilworth, County. Leicester, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death - February 28, 1676 Portsmouth, Newport County, Rhode Island 
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation - Gentleman 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7686. William Almy (30)(170) was born in 1601 in South Kilworth, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leicestershire, England. He died on Feb 28 1677/78 in Portsmouth, Rhode 
2 CONT
2 CONT Island. William Almy came to New England in 1635, with his family on the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail. There are references to an earlier William Almy of Cambridge, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Massachusetts, but it is unlikely that these are the same man. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Way was ordered to serve him until he had cleared a debt amounting 
2 CONT
2 CONT to 111 pounds, no small sum at that time and place. William Almy was of 
2 CONT
2 CONT gentry origins, as indicated by the fact that he is always referred to as 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mister in the records. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to Sandwich, Massachusetts, in April 1637 and to Portsmouth, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhode Island, in 1641. He held a number of minor offices in Rhode Island 
2 CONT
2 CONT and appears to have been prosperous. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the first Quakers in America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy and Audrey Barlow were the 7th great grandparents of both 
2 CONT
2 CONT President Richard Nixon and of President Jimmy Carter. He was married to 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7686. William Almy (30)(170) was born in 1601 in South Kilworth, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leicestershire, England. He died on Feb 28 1677/78 in Portsmouth, Rhode 
2 CONT
2 CONT Island. William Almy came to New England in 1635, with his family on the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail. There are references to an earlier William Almy of Cambridge, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Massachusetts, but it is unlikely that these are the same man. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Way was ordered to serve him until he had cleared a debt amounting 
2 CONT
2 CONT to 111 pounds, no small sum at that time and place. William Almy was of 
2 CONT
2 CONT gentry origins, as indicated by the fact that he is always referred to as 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mister in the records. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to Sandwich, Massachusetts, in April 1637 and to Portsmouth, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhode Island, in 1641. He held a number of minor offices in Rhode Island 
2 CONT
2 CONT and appears to have been prosperous. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the first Quakers in America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Almy and Audrey Barlow were the 7th great grandparents of both 
2 CONT
2 CONT President Richard Nixon and of President Jimmy Carter. He was married to 
2 CONT
2 CONT Audrey Barlow before 1627 in England.
2 CONT
