2 CONT William Army, Ancestral Records and Portraits, Colonial Dames
2 CONT
2 CONT Willia Almy, the American ancestor of all who bear the name, was born in Belinden Parish, Kent, Eng., 1601.  He came to New England with John Winthrop and his associates, but made two journeys back to England before he brought ove
2 CONC r his wife Audrey and their son Chrostopher and daughter Annis, in 1635.  He lived in Sandwich, 1637, but sold his property there to Edmund Freeman in 1642.  He had a grant of land at Portsmouth, RI, in 1644; was a Juryman, 1656; 
2 CONC Commissioner, 1656, 1657, 1663; and Foreman of Jury, 1668.  He was a member of the Society of Friends, and died in Portsmouth, February 28, 1677, his wife having died earlier.  Their daughter Anne or Annis, married John Greene, jr
2 CONC .
2 CONT
