2 CONT Title: New England Historic Genealogical Register (NEHGR), Boston, MA, Page: 71-321.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  William Almy came to New England first by himself sometime before 1631 when he was recorded at Lynn, Massachusetts. He returned to England around 1634 and came back to Massachusetts with his wife Audrey and their children o
2 CONC n the Abigail in 1635. In 1637 the Almys were one of the first ten families to settle in the town of Sandwich, Massachusetts, where they remained only four years.
2 CONT In 1642 they moved to Portsmouth, Rhode Island, where Audrey is to believed to have died in 1676. New England Historical and Genealogical Register, October 1917, Volume 71, Number 284, page 310.
2 CONT Childrens documentation: Genealogies of New Jersey Families From The Genealogical Magazine of New Jersey, Volume II.
2 CONT Geneological Dictionary of R.I. p. 236: 14 Jun 1631 - Fined 11s for taking Mrs. Glover's cow without consent; 1 Jul 1634 - Fined 10s for not appearing in court.
2 CONT 1635 - Having been home to England. Came the 2nd time to N.E. on the "Abigail." Age 34 yrs; wife Audrey 32, daughter Anne 8, Son Christopher 3.  22 Jun 1644 - Sold Sandwich land to Edward Freeman.  14 Nov 1644 - Had a grant of lan
2 CONC d at Wading River in Portsmouth.  Feb 1676 - Will proved by sons Christopher and Job. His body to be buried beside his son John.
