2 CONT === Disputed Origins ===
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Lettice 1604-1681 (Lettice-7) was Ann/Anne (1606-1687).Not a Mayflower passenger but related to the Shurtliff (Bradford) family. Some sources say LNAB Savoy, some say Unknown.* The most definitive and recent source 
2 CONC is the 1986 Plymouth Colony, Its History & People, 1620-1691, By Eugene Aubrey Stratton, p. 317-318,which mentions only Anne, no maiden name.
2 CONT See http://www.wikitree.com/g2g/46590/pgm-thomas-lettice-wife-anne-savoy-or-anne-unknown for question about LNAB. 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===1687: Members dyed: Anne Lettice, widow, July 2/3: in her eighty firstyeare, or thereabouts. <ref>Plymouth Church Records 1620-1859. CD-ROM. Boston, Mass.: New England Historic Genealogical Society; Colonial Society o
2 CONC f Massachusetts, c2003. (Online database. NewEnglandAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2008.)</ref> 
2 CONT
