1 NOTE [v15t3582.ftw]
2 CONT
2 CONT The date and place of John Jenney's birth is not known. His marriageis recorded in Leyden, Holland. It reads John Jenney single man, brewersman from Norwitch in England, now dwelling in Rotterdam, accompanied byRoger Wilson his ac
2 CONC quaintance; with Sarah Carey, single woman fromMonksoon in England, accompained by Joanna Lyons, her acquaintance.
2 CONT After their marriage the Jenneys made their home in Leyden, where theybecame members of the famous Separatist congragation of which the pastorwas Reverand John Robinson.
2 CONT Three children were born to the Jenneys while they lived in LeydenAbagail, Samuel and one that died in infancy and was buried in St.Peter's yard June 16, 1618.
2 CONT In the spring of 1623 two ships, Ann and Little James,set sail fromLand's End in England bound for Plymouth. The Jenneys were in the LittleJames, arriving in Plymouth in August, after three months and two days.Sarah was born aboar
2 CONC d ship a month before arrival at Plymouth; she isPresident George Bush's ancestor.
2 CONT After arriving in Plymouth John Jenney became very succesful in theshipping business and he also owned a Grist Mill. The Mill has beenrestored and now houses a gift shop and restaurant.
2 CONT More information can be found in "Pioneers of Massachusetts" by CharlesHenry Pope page 258. Also Atwode Annals.
