2 CONT ----
2 CONT There is no record of what became of WILLIAM Deane’s wife, but it is obvious that she died before he made his will.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "William - d. about 1634, South Chard, Somerset. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Joane - b. before 1597; bur. Dec. 14, 1621, Chard, Somerset.
2 CONT # William - d. 1678, South Chard. Named eldest son in his father's will.
2 CONT # Thomas - d. 1672. Married Jun. 10, 1629, Chard, Somerset Mary WARRY, daughter of John WARRY and Mary DEAN.
2 CONT # John - b. about 1597; d. 1660, Taunton, Bristol Co., MA. Will dated Apr. 25, 1660. To America in 1637 aboard the 'Speedwell' with brother Walter. Married Alice. Children of John and Alice DEANE: John married Sarah EDSON; Thomas 
2 CONC married Catherine STEPHENS (daughter of Thomas STEVENS, Jr., and granddaughter of Thomas STEVENS and Mary WALLE); Israel did not marry; Isaac married Hannah LEONARD; Nathaniel did not marry; and Elizabeth married Josiah EDSON.
2 CONT # Margerie - d. about 1635, Dorchester, MA. First wife of Elder John STRONG.
2 CONT # Isaacke - Married Oct. 12, 1636, Thornecombe, Devon Margerie SMITH.
2 CONT # Susan - Mentioned in 1654 will of Anne HURT.
2 CONT # Eleanor - Living in 1634.
2 CONT # Walter - bap. May 13, 1612, St. Mary, Chard, Somerset; d. 1659, Taunton, MA. To America in 1637 aboard the 'Speedwell' with brother John. Married in 1637 at Taunton, MA Eleanor COGAN, STEP daughter of William COGAN, granddaughte
2 CONC r of Barnard COGAN, and great granddaughter of Robert COGAN. William COGAN may have married second the widow of John STRONG of Chard, Somerset. The Apr. 24, 1654 will (proved Jun. 23, 1655) of William COGAN, a tanner of South Char
2 CONC d, names two "daughters" named Eleanor: one being Eleanor COGAN, then unmarried, and the other being Eleanor DEANE, wife of Walter DEANE in New England. Children of Walter and Eleanor DEANE: Mary married Shadrack WILBORE (son John
2 CONC  married Alice PITTS, daughter of Peter PITTS and Mary ANDREWS); Lydia married Bartholomew TIPPING; James married Sarah TISDALE; Ezra married Bethia EDSON; Benjamin married Sarah WILLIAMS; and Joseph married Mary TIPPING.
2 CONT # Elizabeth - Living in 1634. Called youngest daughter in her father's will
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT There has been extensive research done on the family of William Deane of Chard, Somerset, England and all published research shows that the identity of his wife is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, some sites perpetuate the myth that she was Margaret and even give her a maiden name. So where did this name come from? It came from a completely different Deane family. There is no relationship to this family (see above 
2 CONC sources). But if you are interested in the other Deane family please see: [https://books.google.com/books?id=TCsEAAAAIAAJ&amp;pg=PA187&amp;lpg Collectanea Topographica Et Genealogica, Volume 3 p 190 edited by Frederic Madden, Bulk
2 CONC eley Bandinel, John Gough Nichols] Someone saw that and copied it and then someone copied them and – well you know how the Internet can be… But to be clear this is an entirely unrelated Deane family. In fact in none of the publish
2 CONC ed genealogies does an author even suggest a Christian name much less a maiden name for her. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT Some of these require a subscription.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Deane, The New England Historical and Genealogical Register (Boston, MA: NEHGS, Oct 1897) Will of William Deane of Soutchard, Somerset, England, 1634 Volume 51, p 432-4 [http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-engla
2 CONC nd-historical-a... link] See also the Will of William Cogan p 434
2 CONT
2 CONT John B Threlfall, The New England Historical and Genealogical Register (Boston, MA: NEHGS, 1985) Additions to the Deane Ancestry in England Vol 139 p 324-25 [http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-a... l
2 CONC ink]
2 CONT
2 CONT David Kendall Martin, The American Genealogist: The First Wife of Shadrach Wilbore and Children of Walter Deane of Taunton MA (New Haven, Conn.: D.L. Jacobus, 1983) Vol 59 224-27 [http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/america
2 CONC n-genealogist-the... link]
2 CONT
2 CONT Deane Family, New England Historical & Genealogical Register (Boston, MA: NEHGS, October 1849) Vol 3 p 375-387. See John Deane p 383, His children p 384. Thomas Deane and his children p 386 [http://www.americanancestors.org/databa
2 CONC ses/new-england-historical-a... link]
2 CONT
2 CONT Selim Walker McArthur, McArthur-Barnes Ancestral Lines. (Portland, Maine: Anthoensen Press, 1964), Donald Lines Jacobus, ed. See Ancestor Tables 87-89
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayflower Descendants 17:158-9
2 CONT
2 CONT Author Denorvan Genealogy of the Dean family descended from Ezra Dean, of Plainfield, Conn. and Cranston, R. I., preceded by a reprint of the article on James and Walter Dean, of Taunton, Mass., and early generations of their desc
2 CONC endants, found in volume 3, New England historical and genealogical register, 1849 (Scranton, PA: F H Gerlock & Co., 1903) [https://archive.org/details/genealogyofdeanf00dean link]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Savage, A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England Showing Three Generations of Those Who Came Before May, 1692 (Boston, Massachusetts: Little, Brown and company, 1880), vol 2, p 64:1261 [http://www.usgen
2 CONC net.org/usa/topic/newengland/savage/ read online]
2 CONT
2 CONT Search for the Passengers of the Mary & John 1630, Volume 1 through present (Toledo, Ohio, 1985+) 26;22-25, 27:19,87-99
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
