1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''one of the first 58 landholders in Rehoboth'''
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the 1836 History of Rehoboth (Leonard Bliss, Jr., pages 24 and 25)  the original purchase of Rehoboth was drawn by sections "...that by which lands, now granted by the Court of Plymouth to the town, is to be divided a
2 CONC ccording to person and estate, as is expressed in this following list:"  [Isaac Martin is on the list.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Isaac Martin===
2 CONT * b	1591 England	
2 CONT * son of Richard Martin & Katherine Lyde
2 CONT * married Margaret Ford 1618	
2 CONT * d 1643 Rehoboth, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac’s wife Margaret Ford was born in 1599 in Ottery St Mary, Devon, England.   Margaret died in Plymouth, Plymouth, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Isaac and Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT * i. Mary Margaret Martin b. 1619 in Pontypool, Trevethan, Monmouthshire, Wales; d. 1684 in Taunton, Bristol, Mass.; m. 1640 Taunton, Mass to James Henry Leonard (1621 – 1691)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://minerdescent.com/2011/11/14/richard-martin-sr/
