2 CONC  the Haskell family spread to other villages in Dorset, Somerset, Wiltshire, and Hampshire, and then to other countries: USA in 1635, Canada, Australia, and New Zealand in 1850, and South Africa in 1898.  Ref: "Origins of the Hask
2 CONC ell Family: Earliest Parish Recorded Dates of Haskell Family Residence in Towns and Counties of Great Britain", compiled by N. H. Haskell and W. A. Haskell, in "Haskell Journal: Newsletter of the Haskell Family Association, v3, #3
2 CONC , 1986.
