1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Goodale-of-Dennington-Salisbury/6000000002066971049?through=6000000007604352487
2 CONT * Not the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Goodell/6000000083945664309?through=6000000006444050808 & https://www.geni.com/people/Joan-Goodell/6000000083946227116?through=6000000006444050808.  Their son was https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Robert-Goodale-II/6000000206104932945
2 CONT * See Geni discussions: [https://www.geni.com/discussions/184256?msg=1233825 27 July 2018] & [https://www.geni.com/discussions/279683?msg=1703581 28 May 2024] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT ''Updated 28 May 2024''
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert [https://www.geni.com/surnames/goodell Goodell] was born 1604 in England and died after 12 October 1682 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  His parents are not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The name is often given as '''Goodale'''.  It has also been given as [http://www.geni.com/surnames/goodele Goodele].
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodale (1604-1682), progenitor of the Goodell/Goodale family in America, came from England with his wife and three children on the ship "Elizabeth" in 1634 and settled in Salem, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Elizabeth" left Ipswich, England on April 30, 1634 and landed at Boston in July. At that time, Robert Goodell was 30, his wife Katherine was 28, their daughter Mary 4 years old, their son Abraham was 2 and their baby, Isaac w
2 CONC as 6 months old. The first record of the Goodells in America indicated that they settled just north of Salem at Great Cove in the North Fields.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodell seems to have devoted his life to the development of his large grant for the benefit of his sons and daughters. As they married, he gave them a generous acreage as a wedding gift, thus creating a family settlement a
2 CONC bout his own homestead. Although his clear firm handwriting would seem to indicate a good education, he took no part in local or broader governmental affairs and his name seldom appears in the records in any active capacity except
2 CONC  as plaintiff or defendant in suits based on the ownership of his stock or land.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT #  1629 in England to Katherine  (1606-1666).  She was NOT the daughter of  Henry Kilham b: 10 AUG 1558  & Alice Goodell b: ABT 1560.  10 children.
2 CONT # 30 August 1669 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts to Margaret Lazenby (1614-1683).  No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Catherine :
2 CONT #  Mary b: 1630 in Dennington, Suffolk, England.  Married John Pease.
2 CONT #Abraham b: 1632 in Dennington, Suffolk, England.  Married Hannah Rhodes.
2 CONT #  Isaac  b: NOV 1633 in Dennington, Suffolk, England.  Married Patience Cook. 
2 CONT # Nehemiah b: 30 MAY 1636 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married Hannah Haven.
2 CONT # Sarah  b: 1638 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  married John Batchelder.
2 CONT # Zachariah  b: 31 MAY 1640 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married Elizabeth Beauchamp.
2 CONT # Jacob  b: 9 JAN 1642/43.  "Jacob Goodale d. in 1676, after being severely beaten by Giles Corey". Died without issue.
2 CONT # Charity  b: 1644 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts. Married Joh Abbe.
2 CONT # Hannah  b: 6 AUG 1645 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married Lot Kilham.
2 CONT # Elizabeth  b: ABT 1649 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married 1) John Smith.  2) Henry Bennett.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT See https://www.geni.com/discussions/184256?msg=1233825 & https://www.geni.com/discussions/279683?msg=1703581
2 CONT
2 CONT The origins and kinship of Robert Goodale, of Salem are not certain ['''sic: disproved'''.] Parents seen as https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Goodell/6000000083945664309?through=6000000006444050808 & https://www.geni.com/people/J
2 CONC oan-Goodell/6000000083946227116?through=6000000006444050808.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodale, in Anderson, Robert Charles; George F. Sanborn; and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. The Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635. (Boston, Massachusetts: NEHGS, 1999-2011) Vol 3 pp 101-108. < [https://www.americ
2 CONC anancestors.org/databases/great-migration-immigrants-to-new-england-1634-1635-volume-iii-g-h/image?pageName=107&volumeId=7118&filterQuery=category:Great%20Migration%20Study%20Project AmericanAncestors] >
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodale of Dennington shown here was erroneously proposed to be the father of Robert Goodale of Salem, MA by George E Williams in A genealogy of the descendants of Robert Goodale/Goodell of Salem, Mass West Hartford, Conn. 
2 CONC (West Hartford, CT: 1984). This Robert did have a son named Robert bp on 16 Aug 1601, however, he died young and a second son named Robert was bp 17 Mar 1611/2. '''The second son is too old to be the immigrant. Therefore this Robe
2 CONC rt is not the father of Robert of Salem, MA.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.wiggo.com/personal/Genealogy/Goodale_Book/goodale_book.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT *At any rate, to be found recorded in the Parish Records of Dennington, Suffolk County, England, are the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Marriages: 1590 12 June Robert Goodale and Joan Artys
2 CONT *Baptisms: 1601 15 Aug. Robert, son of Robert and Joan Goodale
2 CONT
2 CONT *Other children of this couple whose baptisms are recorded also are Mary, 1591; Margaret, 1593; William, 1596; Anne, 1599; Edward, 1603; Elizabeth, 1607; and Thomas, 1610.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Thomas ‘the Elder’ Goodale1 and his wife Elizabeth were probably parents of Robert2 who married Joan Artys and was father of our Robert3, Immigrant Ancestor. Robert2 was "a small landed proprietor and cultivator, employing his ca
2 CONC pital and labor in various modes which grew out of the occupation of lands."
2 CONT
2 CONT *On March 1, 1612, arms were granted to Thomas Goodall of Earle-Stoneham, as follows: Arms: Gules, an eagle displayed Argent, beaked and membered Or, on a canton of the last a Chaplet Gramine Vert. Crest: On a wreath an eagle disp
2 CONC layed Argent beaked and membered Or and gorged with a chaplet Gramine Vert.' The Boston Transcript No. 9830 states that Robert brought to America the arms granted Thomas Goodall of Earle-Stoneham.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT His Parents were not Robert Goodell b: 1568 in Cosgrove, Northamptonshire, England  & Joan Artys b: ABT 1570 in Dennington, Suffolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Although his birth year was given as 1604 in his oath of allegiance when sailing for America, one of Robert's descendants has verified the church baptisimal record as 1601. [sic: not this man] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Speculation 
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Elizabeth Goodell, the grandparents of Robert were probably members of the [http://www.geni.com/surnames/godelle Godelle] or [https://www.geni.com/surnames/goodelle Goodelle] family, French Huguenots who emigrated to L
2 CONC ondon in the 1530's.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Anderson, Robert Charles. ''Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635'', Volume III, G–H. (Boston: NEHGS, 2003): pages 101-108. AmericanAncestors.org < [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/great-migration-imm
2 CONC igrants-to-new-england-1634-1635-volume-iii-g-h/image?pageName=101 link] > Page 107 ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206104918872 document attached])
2 CONT # ''Genealogy of the Descendants of Robert Goodale / Goodell of Salem Mass'' by Williams, Geo E. - 1984 https://archive.org/details/genealogyofdesce00will/page/n7/mode/2up ('''disproved origins''')
2 CONT # ''Pioneers of Massachusetts'' by Pope, Charles Henry -1900
2 CONT # LDS Ancestral file (Goodale)
2 CONT # ''History of Salem MA'' by Perly
2 CONT # Wason Research
2 CONT # Vital Records of Salem MA
2 CONT # ''Batchelder, Batcheller Genealogy'' by Pierce Frederick Clifton - 1898
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=zsQWAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA164&ots=7DcMvgMWzB&dq=John%20goodale%201679&pg=PA164#v=onepage&q=John%20goodale%201679&f=false Daughters of the American Revolution Magazine,] Volume 20.  Page 164.  113. Good
2 CONC ale-thurston: "Zachariah was a son of '''Robert Goodale''', who embarked at Ipswich, England, with his wife Katherine in April, 1634, he in his 31st, and she in her 29th year. They brought with them three children, Mary, 4 years: 
2 CONC Abram, 2 years, and Isaac, 6 months.—(Hist. Marlborough, Mass.. 1657-1861.) 
2 CONT #http://www.wiggo.com/personal/Genealogy/Goodale_Book/goodale_book.ht
2 CONT # https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dotsicle&id=I32627
2 CONT # http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=clcaldwell&id=I01013
2 CONT #http://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/richard-goodale_14488148
2 CONT #Hotten, John Camden. ''The Original Lists of Persons of Quality...'' (London, 1874): page 280 and page 282. < [https://archive.org/details/originallistsofp00hottuoft/page/294/mode/2up Archive.Org] >  Robert Goodall (age 30) his w
2 CONC ife Katherine (age 28)  and three children sailed from the port of Ipswich, Suffolk County, England on the ship "Elizabeth" in 1634. 
2 CONT # The ancestry of Lydia Harmon, 1755-1836 by Walter Goodwin Davis (Boston, 1924)
