1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Edmund Vassell Perry=
2 CONT * BIRTH 27 Jan 1587, Bideford, Devonshire, England  
2 CONT * DEATH 1659 (aged 71–72) Sandwich, Barnstable County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * MARRIAGE Sarah Crowell in 1613 in Bridford, Devonshire, England [19],[20],[34]  
2 CONT * BURIAL Old Quaker Meeting House Cemetery at Spring Hill, Sandwich, Barnstable County, MA, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  205131762  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Edmond Perry and Sarah Perry were the first to come to Sandwich, Massachusetts, United States, from Devonshire, England, sometime between 1624 and 1627.  A Quaker, he was in frequent trouble with the authorities on account of his 
2 CONC religious beliefs.  He married Sarah Crowell, daughter of John Crowell and Elishua [Unknown], in Oct. 10, 1614 in Bridford, Devonshire, England [19],[20],[34] (Sarah Crowell was born about 1592 in County Devonshire, England,[19],[
2 CONC 20],[34] died before 7 Jun 1659 in Sandwich, Barnstable, MA [19],[20] and was buried in 1659 in Sandwich, Barnstable, MA [34] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Alternate Biography==
2 CONT Edmond Perry was born on 27 Jan 1587/88 in Devonshire, England. He was the son of John PERRY and [__?__]. His mother was probably not Judith VASSELL (1567 – 1650). He married Sarah BETTS in 1613 in Bridford, Devonshire, England. E
2 CONC dmund reportedly emigrated to Plymouth Colony (Sandwich) in 1637 and died shortly thereafter. Another source says Edmond Perry and his wife Sarah cam to America in 1639 on the ship “Lion.” However Irving says Edward died in 1614 b
2 CONC efore the rest of his family emigrated to America. This theory says that Sarah Perry, the widow of Edmund Perry, emigrated to America with her children, but no husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT Edmund Perry is not listed in Savage's Genealogical Dictionary, Anderson's Great Migration Directory, Farmer's Genealogical Register, or Holme's Directory of the Ancestral Heads of New England Families.  In short, without primary 
2 CONC source documentation, the facts for this family are at present impossible to ascertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a considerable amount of conflicting information about Edmund Perry and his wife Sarah. Most of the information comes from family histories that differ in their accounts, though most agree he was born about 1588 in Devon,
2 CONC  England. Some say Edmund emigrated to Plymouth Colony in 1637 or 1639 and died shortly thereafter in Sandwich. Others say he died 07 Jun 1659 in Sandwich. Still others say he died in England in 1614 before the rest of the family 
2 CONC emigrated to America. Edmund's wife Sarah's maiden name is also in dispute. Some say Betts, some say Crowell.
2 CONT
2 CONT The file Perry.txt gives a number of generations of Edmund Perry’s descendants. The names of his children were taken from that file. It is reported that Edmund was an immigrant in 1637. In this case, all of his children were immig
2 CONC rants with him. [1]  Death date from Irving is 1614, which is not likely. Irving places birth date (incorrectly?) at 27 Jan 1599 and the place of death (incorrectly!) as Sandwich, Massachusetts. 1614 is probably the date of marria
2 CONC ge. Lander has marriage in 1612: "It is reported that Edmund was an immigrant in 1637." 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Chronology==
2 CONT Christening Date: 27 Jan 1588 Warminster, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT *Alt. Christening, 13 Apr 1596, County Sussex, England. [469] 
2 CONT *Alt. Birth, 27 Jan 1598/99, County Devonshire, England. [33] 
2 CONT *Alt. Death, 1614, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA. [33],[245] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Sarah Elizabeth "Betts" Crowell? Perry 1592–1659
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT John Perry 1612–1642
2 CONT Arthur Vassell Perry 1615–1652
2 CONT Margaret Perry Freeman 1623–1688
2 CONT Anthony Perry 1624–1683
2 CONT Rev Ezra Perry 1625–1689
2 CONT Ezra Perry 1625–1689
2 CONT Edward Perry 1630–1695
2 CONT Hannah Perry Dillingham 1632–1673
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Descendants==  
2 CONT GG Grandfather of Gen. Nathanael Greene, Rev. War
2 CONT
