2 CONC nce is cited by Benjamin F. Wilbour as part of a note of his published in 'English Origins of New England Families', NEH&GR (Second Series, Vol.1). In his note, Wilbour says this marriage record 'may pertain' to the Thomas BURGESS
2 CONC  who had land granted to him 3 April 1637 at Duxbury, died 23 Feb. 1684/5 at Sandwich, MA and whose wife, Dorothy, died there 27 FEb 1686/7. Wilbour also cites as a source Winifred Lovering Holman's 'Burgess Lineage, 1957-1958', a
2 CONC  typescript in the NEH&GR Library."
