2 CONT From http://pcez.com/~bigshoe/du/Pery/burges.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Most online genealogies of this family go back to Truro, Cornwall; but they are incorrect:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"...Current wisdom is that (4770) Thomas Burgess was the son of Thomas Burgess Jr. of Truro, Cornwall, and his wife Elizabeth Pye. He was the son of Thomas Burgess and Honour Sydenham (usually spelled Sidnam in America) and the g
2 CONC randson of Ellis Burgess and Catherine Corniche. All of this comes from the Heralds Visitation of Cornwall in 1620 and various Burgess, Sydenham and other wills. If so his father was the mayor of Truro and either his father, or gr
2 CONC andfather was a member of Parliament for Truro in the first and last Parliaments of James I (Puritan parliaments). There is a serious, but not necessarily fatal flaw in this. The records of the Church of St. Mary Magdalen in Truro
2 CONC  (where George Phippen was rector and the Burgesses worshiped) all survive. They do list the birth of a Thomas Burgess at about the correct time to Thomas Burgess Jr. and Elizabeth Pye. The problem is that they also list the death
2 CONC  of a Thomas Burgess as an infant, and in the will of Thomas Burgess Jr. he mentions a son Thomas as a minor (too young to be our Thomas).
2 CONT
2 CONT "The only hope for this line is that the death notice at St. Mary's does not call the father of the infant "Thomas Burgess Jr." as he is called in all the other parts of the record, families do use a name twice and our Thomas may 
2 CONC have already married, or left the country by this time. Joe Burgess argues that the Truro family was literate (the elder Thomas signs his will) and Thomas Burgess of Sandwich signs his name with the letter "T" as his mark, and tha
2 CONC t makes this connection unlikely....
2 CONT
2 CONT --Dean Burgess, 29 August 2000 c/o http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=glencoe&id=I6470
2 CONT
2 CONT >"...in the will of the latter Thomas [husb. of Eliz. Pye, of Truro], written 22 April 1626, his son http://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Burgess/6000000039497695853?through=6000000006444727443  was listed last of six sons who had no
2 CONC t yet "accomplished the age of one and twenty," suggesting that he was the youngest, born probably not much before 1613 and quite likely several years later. This conclusion was supported by the 1620 Visitation of Truro, listing n
2 CONC o Thomas among the children of Thomas and Elizabeth (Pye) Burgess."
2 CONT
2 CONT -- http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~thesays/joan/pafn14.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT He is my 8th great grandfather. -- courtesy of William L. DeCoursey 
