1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Goodman-Mayflower-Passenger/6000000009326086201 or of https://www.geni.com/people/Goodman-of-Edlesborough/6000000052385109882
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Dorothy===
2 CONT * b. poss. b. 1603 Earls Barton, Northampton, England
2 CONT * d. 27 Feb. 1686/87 i. Old Town Cem., Sandwich, Barnstable Co., MA
2 CONT * Parents: unknown 
2 CONT * Married:.Thomas Burgess
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT * i. Ruth Burgess [not mentioned in (4770) Thomas's will or codicil.] b. ABT [1627] Sandwich, Barnstable, MA d. 22 June 1693 Yarmouth, Barnstable, MA Family: Richard "Rock" (not Tailor) Taylor 1643 Yarmouth, MA b. 1619 Truro, Corn
2 CONC wall, England (now though to have been https://www.geni.com/people/Ruth-Taylor/6000000008539384315?through=6000000021720043338 )
2 CONT * ii. Thomas Burgess b. ABT 1627 England d. 26 Feb 1717 Sandwich, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT * iii. John Burgess b. 10 Feb. 1627/28 Turo, Cornwall, England
2 CONT * iv. (2385) Elizabeth Burgess/ Burge
2 CONT * v. Jacob Burgess b. 1631/36 Sandwich, Barnstable, MA d. 17 Mar. 1718/19 Sandwich, Barnstable, MA m. Mary Nye (1642-1706) 1 June 1660/70 Sandwich, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT * vi. Joseph Burgess b. 1638 Sandwich, Barnstable Co., MA d. Aug. 1695 Sandwich, Barnstable Co., MA
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~thesays/joan/histories/burgess.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Thomas Burgess 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:  Parish of Chester-le-Street, Tanfield, England 1628 to Dorothy   (Waynes? - this is a question)  according to "The Burgess History Tree" by Paul F. Burgess, she is Dorothy Waynes or Pippen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Dorothy (---) 
2 CONT
2 CONT  POSSIBLE SURNAME OF DOROTHY, WIFE OF THOMAS BURGESS: 
2 CONT
2 CONT      A Thomas Burgess and a Dorothy Waynes were married in Tanfield, York, 
2 CONT
2 CONT           England, in 1628, according to a record from "Paver's Marriage Licenses" as listed in the Yorkshire Archaeological Journal, Vol. 20, Pg. 74, 1909. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Winifred Lovering Holman's "Burgess Lineage, 1957-1958," a typescript in the New England Historic-Genealogical Society library, gives Dorothy Phippen as being the wife of this Thomas Burgess.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=glencoe&id=I6455
2 CONT
2 CONT POSTING TO BURGESS ARCHIVES by AlRose509_AT_aol.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Following e-mail from Dean Burgess  Here is where the Thomas Burgess debate now stands.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Thomas Burgess did marry Dorothy Waynes, but Paul Burgess, who will probably also reply to you, hired a British genealogist to trace this marriage record and the couple had no children. We know Dorothy Burgess was not a Waynes. 
2 CONC While I was in Cornwall I traced all of the children of the Rev. George Phippen (all of the records still exist) and found he had no daughter named Dorothy. The origin of this name as her maiden name comes from the fact that Thoma
2 CONC s Burgess of Truro (widely believed to be Thomas of Sandwich MA's father) calls George Phippen his "brother-in-law" in his will. Records show he was his brother-in-law, but that was because George Phippen married, as his second wi
2 CONC fe, Thomas Burgess's wife's sister.Thomas's wife was Elizabeth Pye. We know Dorothy Burgess was not a Phippen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The parents listed below are not accurate.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=38446914
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1603
2 CONT Lancashire, England Death: 	Feb. 27, 1687 Sandwich Barnstable County Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT d/o John Goodman & Joan Pye
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   John Goodman (1587 - 1621)
2 CONT   Joan Elizabeth Pye Goodman (1582 - 1626)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Thomas Burgess (1601 - 1685)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Thomas Burgess (1627 - 1717)*
2 CONT   Joseph Burgess (1628 - 1695)*
2 CONT   John Burgess (1628 - 1701)*
2 CONT   Elizabeth Burgess Perry (1629 - 1717)*
2 CONT   Jacob Burgess (1632 - 1719)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Old Town Cemetery Sandwich Barnstable County Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
