1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name at Birth: Joane Unknown b.1599 in Bocking, Essex, England. Christening: 25 Mar 1599 - England. Death: 26 NOV 1663 - Sandwich, Barnstable, Massachusetts, United States  Gender: Female. Married to William Swyft 
2 CONC by 1620 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note 1: There is no documented source for a maiden name of SISSON. See Jane Fletcher Fiske's "William Swift of London and Sandwich, Mass." in The American Genealogist, vol 77 (2002):161 for the most recent research done. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note 2: Joane is possibly a second wife, and not mother of William's children, per Frank Allaben, 'Journal of American Genealogy' 2:20. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fined along with Robert Harper and his wife, Joseph Allen, John Newland and his wife, William Allen, William Gifford, Matthew Allen, the wife of Henry Dillingham, William Newland and his wife, John Soule, Rodolphus Elmes, Peter Ga
2 CONC unt, Dorothy Butler, Obadiah Butler, John Jenkins, Richard Kerby Sr., Richard Kerby Jr., John Smith of Plymouth and his wife Deborah, Lydia Hickes of Plymouth, and Henry Howland for "being att Quakers meetings." Fined 4 pounds eac
2 CONC h. Oct 1660.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Swift by his 2nd wife Joan:
2 CONT
2 CONT #William Swift, bp St. Mary Magdalen, Bermondsey 25 Apr 1627 [TAG 77:166]; m by 1651 Ruth____ [MD 14:166; Sand VR 1:15]; assumed to be mother of his children (named in his 1705 will)
2 CONT # Esther Swift, bp St. Mary Magdalen, Bermondsey, 28 May 1629 [TAG 77:166]; m1 by 1646 Ralph Allen, mason; probably m2 Sandwich 14 Feb 1664/5? Henry Bull of Rhode Island.[Sand VR 2:1248; TAG 77:170-172]
2 CONT #Sarah Swift, bp St. Mary Magdalen, Bermondsey, 7 Aug 16331 [TAG 77:166]; bur there 8 Sep 1631 [TAG 77:166]
2 CONT --------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan was the widow of Roger Dumbleby when she married William Swift in 1626. Joan's birth name is still unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [http://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000028654412963 "Great Migration Begins, Vol 6, pg 269"]
2 CONT
2 CONT ****************************************************************** When Ralph Jr. https://www.geni.com/people/Ralph-Allen-Jr-of-Sandwich/6000000012669399266 died, all of his land was passed down to his son Jedediah Allen https://w
2 CONC ww.geni.com/people/Jedediah-Allen/6000000003075681102. The will of Joan Swift https://www.geni.com/people/Joan-Swyft/6000000001853055196 , grandmother of Jedediah and Experience, shows that Ralph's wife https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Esther-Swift-Bull/6000000003077358443 only had two surviving children in 1663: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Joan Swift dated 12: 8mo: 1662, inventoried 25: 10mo: 1663, includes: to grandchild Experience Allen https://www.geni.com/people/Experience-Allen/6000000001853755972 chest of drawers & bible; to my 2 grandchildren Hannah S
2 CONC wift https://www.geni.com/people/Hannah-Tobey/6000000003938033054 & Experience Allen all linen and pewter; to Jedediah Allen & Experience Allen 1/3 of estate House & garden; and debt from Francis Allen [Plymouth Colony Wills, FHL 
2 CONC film 0567794, v. 2, part 2, p. 16. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The only other mention of Experience is the family Bible of Jedediah [NEHGR, v. 25, p. 146]. His Bible lists the deaths of his father and mother, and Experience, but the months and years of their deaths are lost. Jedediah's first 
2 CONC child was Experience https://www.geni.com/people/Experience-Allen-Field/6000000003075678825, b. 30 Aug 1669, which suggests that Experience daughter of Ralph had died by 1669.  In summary, all of the records suggest that Ralph Jr.
2 CONC  (stonemason) did not have a earlier wife. 
