2 DATE 24 SEP 1672
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ipswich, Essex
3 STAE Massachusetts
1 OCCU FIRST EUROPEAN WOMAN TO COME TO THE MASS. BAY COLONY  IN 1635 ON THE ABIGAIL
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret READE - b. Jul 11, 1598, North Benfleet, Essex; d. Sep. 1672, Ipswich, Essex Co., MA. Her will of Aug. 30, 1672 was proved Sep. 24, 1672. She left her husband in England and immigrated to New England befor
2 CONC e 1635 with her daughters Ann and Martha, and resided for some years with her brother-in-law Gov. John WINTHROP, Jr. Her later years were spent at Ipswich, living with her daughter Martha (LAKE) HARRIS and with her brother-in-law 
2 CONC Deputy Gov. Samuel SYMONDS. In a letter of Jan. 18, 1661/2 she wrote to John WINTHROP, Jr., Margaret includes comments "concerning my husbands death, & how hee edned his dayes." Daughter of Edmund READE and Elizabeth COOKE.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Children of John and Margaret Lake include:
2 CONT # John - bap. Jul. 6, 1617, Wickford, Essex; d. probably about Dec. 1657, Wickford, Essex.
2 CONT # Thomas - bap. Jan. 18, 1617/8, Wickford, Essex.
2 CONT # Richard - bap. May 21, 1620, Wickford, Essex; d. there May 22, 1620.
2 CONT # Hannah - bap. Jul. 3, 1621, North Benfleet, Essex, England; d. after 1675, Stonington, New London Co., CT. Married Capt. John GALLUP. 
2 CONT # Elizabeth - bap. Aug. 31, 1623, Wickford, Essex; bur. there Aug. 31, 1623. 
2 CONT # Martha - bap. Jul 20, 1624, North Benfleet, Essex, England; d. Apr. 5, 1700; Ipswich, Essex Co., MA. She was married on Nov 15, 1647 in Ipswich, Essex Co., MA to Thomas HARRIS (b. Apr. 25, 1618, Gloucestershire, England d. Aug 2
2 CONC , 1687, Ipswich, Essex Co., MA), son of Thomas HARRIS and Elizabeth HILLS. Daughter of Martha and Thomas HARRIS: Elizabeth married her first cousin John GALLUP (son of Capt. John GALLUP and Hannah LAKE). 
2 CONT # Samuel - bap. Mar. 29, 1629, North Benfleet, Essex; bur. there Mar. 19, 1629/30. 
2 CONT # Elizabeth - bap. Feb. 17, 1630/1, North Benfleet, Essex. Probably died as infant. 
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *''''''Margaret Reade
2 CONT *''''''F, #75223, b. 11 July 1598
2 CONT *Father      Edmund Reade b. 23 May 1563, d. 1 Dec 1623
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Cooke b. 2 Jul 1568, d. 1637
2 CONT *''''''     Margaret Reade was born on 11 July 1598 at North Benfleet, Essex, England. She married John Lake, son of John Lake and Elizabeth Sandell, circa 1616 at North Benfleet, Essex, England. Her estate was probated on 24 Sept
2 CONC ember 1672 at Ipswich, Essex, MA.
2 CONT *''''''Family      John Lake b. 26 Sep 1590, d. 18 Jan 1662
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Hannah Lake+ b. 3 Jul 1621, d. 9 Dec 1675
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2503.htm#i75223
2 CONT *_______________________________ 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Immigration on ship Abigail with family on 1635-10-06
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: North Benfleet, Essex]] [[Category: Ipswich, Massachusetts]]
2 CONT
2 CONT Puritan Great Migration 
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was a daughter of Edmund Reade and Elizabeth (Cooke) Reade ofWickford and North Benfleet, Essex, England. She was born on 11 July 1598 and baptized on 16 July 1598 at North Benfleet, Essex.<ref name=Davis315>Davis, Ancest
2 CONC ry of John Lake, [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/image/?pageName=315&volumeId=11699&rId=23526188 page 315].</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to John Lake in about 1616. <ref name=Davis315 />
2 CONT Children of John Lake and Margaret (Reade) Lake were:<ref>Davis, pages316-317.</ref>
2 CONT # John, baptized on 6 July 1617 at Wickford, Essex
2 CONT # Thomas, baptized on 18 January 1618/9 at Wickford, Essex# Richard, baptized on 21 May 1620 and buried on 22 May 1620, at Wickford, Essex
2 CONT # Ann (later called Hannah), baptized on 3 July 1621 at North Benfleet, Essex; emigrated to New England with her mother and married John Gallop
2 CONT #Elizabeth, baptized on 5 June 1623 and buried on 31 August 1623 at North Benfleet, Essex
2 CONT #Martha, baptized on 20 July 1624 at North Benfleet, Essex; emigratedto New England with her mother and married Thomas Harris.
2 CONT # Samuel, baptized on 29 March 1629 and buried on 19 March 1629/30 at North Benfleet, Essex
2 CONT #Elizabeth, baptized on 17 February 1630/1 at North Benfleet, Essex;no further record. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (Reade) Lake left England without her husband some time between 1631 and 1635, emigrating to New England with her sisters, including Elizabeth (Read) Winthrop, wife of Gov. John Winthrop, and her two daughters, Ann (Hanna
2 CONC h) and Martha. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret lived in Ipswich, Massachusetts, and died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gen. of the Lake Family, by Adams 1915, and Davis, Ancestry of John Lake, pages 315-316.<
2 CONT *Wheeler's ''History of Stonington, Connecticut'', states that she arrived in Boston onthe ship ''Abigail'' on 6 October 1635.<Wheeler, p. 382>
2 CONT *''The Great Migration Directory'' states Margaret Lake's date of arrival in New England as 1638.<Anderson, Robert Charles. ''The Great Migration Directory,'' New England History Genealogical Society, 2015.>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===
2 CONT She died at Ipswich, Massachusetts, between 30 August 1672, when she made her will and 24 Sept 1672, when the will was proved.<ref name=Davis315 />
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT * Davis, Walter Goodwin, BA, LLB of Portland, ME.   Ancestry of John Lake, Husband of Margaret (Reade) Lake. ''The New England Historical and Genealogical Register'', v. 84 (1930), [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB202/i/11699/
2 CONC 304/23526071 pp. 304-317].  (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001).
2 CONT * Davis, Walter. ''[[Space:The Ancestry of Bethia Harris, 1748-1833|The Ancestry of Bethia Harris, 1748-1833]]'' (The Southworth Press, Portland, Maine, 1934) 
2 CONT *Wheeler, Richard Anson. ''[http://books.google.com/books?id=tvILAAAAYAAJ History of the Town of Stonington, County of New London, Connecticut: From Its First Settlement in 1649 to 1900]''. Stonington, Connecticut: Press of the Da
2 CONC y Publishing Company, 1900.
2 CONT *FindAGrave|102111690
2 CONT *  John Winthrop [brother-in-law to Martha]  Early New England Families Study Project: Accounts of New England Families from 1641 to 1700 < [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/early-new-england-families-1641-1700/image?vo
2 CONC lumeId=13918&pageName=2&rId=250756662&refreshed=true AmericanAncestors] > Martha Reade, who married Samuel Symonds, whose sister Elizabeth was a wife to Gov. John Winthrop, Jr. of CT.  Stepfather Hugh Peters came in the Abigail in
2 CONC  1635 with his stepdaughters Elizabeth Winthrop and Margaret Lake.
