2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial stone located at Whitehall Burying Ground #21, Mystic, CT. reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain John Gallup, 2nd.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Born in Dorset, England, 1615. Arrived in Boston September 4, 1635. Removed from Boston to Taunton , 1640 to New London 1651. In 1654 to his residence in Whitehall, built upon a tract of land on the Mystic River, granted him reco
2 CONC gnition of the service rendered by himself and his father in the Pequot War. Slain December 19, 1675 in the Narragansett Swamp Fight. Buried near the scene of the Battle."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source(s): Gallup Genealogy, History of Stonington, CT.
2 CONT
