1 NOTE [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 14, Ed. 1, Tree #1317, Date of Import: Jul 16, 2005]
2 CONT
2 CONT A 1620 Mayflower passenger with her parents, Elizabeth Tilley married
2 CONT fellow passenger John Howland.  Widowed in 1672, she died in 1687 at the
2 CONT home of her daughter, Lydia Browne, in Swansea.
1 NOTE Mayflower Passenger
1 NOTE John Carver takes in Elizabeth
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=6a191673-d7e4-4484-8961-e08cfbc44cbd&tid=2367764&pid=-497236978
1 NOTE Elizabeth Tilley
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=314672b4-9cb1-4c04-ad08-2510ce95265c&tid=2367764&pid=-497236978
1 NOTE Mayflower passenger
1 NOTE Elizabeth Tilley the Early Years
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=99db37dd-bd20-428a-9553-eec3d7fdd747&tid=2367764&pid=-497236978
1 NOTE Individual:
2 CONT
2 CONT According to notes on web-site 
2 CONT http://www.irons-assoc.com/~sue/SUEWEBGEN.wbg/ - 
2 CONT Elizabeth came to America on the Mayflower 21/12/1621 with her parents 
2 CONT and siblings
2 CONT
2 CONT From WebPage http://members.aol.com/calebj/passenger.html
2 CONT
2 CONT In ye Name of God Amen I Elizabeth Howland of Swanzey in ye County of 
2 CONT Bristoll in ye Collony of Plymouth in New Engld being Seventy nine yeares 
2 CONT of Age but of good & perfect memory thanks be to Allmighty God & calling 
2 CONT to Remembrance ye uncertain Estate of this transitory Life & that all 
2 CONT fflesh must Yeild unto Death when it shall please God to call Doe make 
2 CONT constitute & ordaine & Declare This my last Will & Testament, in manner & 
2 CONT forme following Revoking and Anulling by these prsents all & every 
2 CONT Testamt & Testamts Will & Wills heretofore by me made & declared either 
2 CONT by Word or Writing And this to be taken only for my last Will & Testament 
2 CONT & none other. And first being penitent & sorry from ye bottom of my heart 
2 CONT for all my sinns past most humbly desiring forgivenesse for ye same I 
2 CONT give & Committ my soule unto Allmighty God my Savior & redeemer in whome 
2 CONT & by ye meritts of Jesus Christ I trust & believe assuredly to be saved & 
2 CONT to have full remission & forgivenesse of all my sins & that my Soule wt 
2 CONT my Body at the generall Day of Resurrection shall rise againe wt Joy & 
2 CONT through ye meritts of Christs Death & passion possesse & inheritt ye 
2 CONT Kingdome of heaven prepared for his Elect & Chosen & my Body to be buryed 
2 CONT in such place where it shall please my Executrs hereafter named to 
2 CONT appoint And now for ye settling my temporall Estate & such goodes 
2 CONT Chattells & Debts as it hath pleased God far above my Deserts to bestow 
2 CONT upon me I Do Dispose order & give ye same in manner & forme following 
2 CONT (That is to say) First that after my funerall Expences & Debts paid wc I 
2 CONT owe either of right or in Conscience to any manner of person or persons 
2 CONT whatsoever in Convenient tyme after my Decease by my Execrs hereafter 
2 CONT named I Give & bequeath unto my Eldest Son John Howland ye sum of five 
2 CONT pounds to be paid out of my Estate & my Booke called Mr Tindale's Workes 
2 CONT & also one pair of sheetes & one pr of pillowbeeres & one pr of 
2 CONT Bedblanketts, Item I give unto my son Joseph Howland my Stillyards & also 
2 CONT one pr of sheetes & one pr of pillobeeres Item I give unto my son Jabez 
2 CONT Howland my ffetherbed & boulster yt is in his Custody & also one Rugg & 
2 CONT two Blanketts yt belongeth to ye said Bed & also my great Iron pott & 
2 CONT potthookes Item I give unto my son Isaack Howland my Booke called Willson 
2 CONT on ye Romanes & one pr of sheetes & one paire of pillowbeeres & also my 
2 CONT great Brasse Kettle already in his possession Item I give unto my Son in 
2 CONT Law Mr James Browne my great Bible Item I give & bequeath unto my 
2 CONT Daughter Lidia Browne my best ffeatherbed & Boulster two pillowes & three 
2 CONT Blanketts & a green Rugg & my small Cupboard one pr of AndyIrons & my 
2 CONT lesser brasse Kettle & my small Bible & my booke of mr Robbinsons Workes 
2 CONT called Observations Divine & Morrall & allso my finest pr of Sheetes & my 
2 CONT holland pillowbeeres, Item I give unto my Daughter Elisabeth Dickenson 
2 CONT one pr of Sheetes & one pr of pillowbeeres & one Chest Item I give unto 
2 CONT my Daughter Hannah Bosworth one pr of sheets & one pr of pillowbeeres, 
2 CONT Item I give unto my Grand Daughter Elizabeth Bursley one paire of sheets 
2 CONT and one paire of Pillowbeeres Item I give & bequeath unto my Grandson 
2 CONT Nathaniel Howland (the son of Joseph Howland) and to the heires of his 
2 CONT owne Body lawfully begotten for ever all that my Lott of Land with ye 
2 CONT Meadow thereunto adjoyning & belonging lying in the Township of Duxbury 
2 CONT neare Jones River bridge, Item I give unto my Grandson James Browne One 
2 CONT Iron barr and on Iron Trammell now in his possession, Item I give unto my 
2 CONT Grandson Jabez Browne one Chest Item I give unto my Grand Daughter 
2 CONT Dorothy Browne my best Chest & my Warming pan Item I give unto my Grand 
2 CONT Daughter Desire Cushman four Sheep, Item I give & bequeath my wearing 
2 CONT clothes linnen and Woollen and all the rest of my Estate in mony Debts 
2 CONT linnen or of what kind or nature or sort soever it may be unto my three 
2 CONT Daughters Elisabeth Dickenson, Lidia Browne and Hannah Bosworth to be 
2 CONT equally Devided amongst them, Item I make constitute and ordaine my 
2 CONT loving Son in Law James Browne and my loving son Jabez Howland Executors 
2 CONT of this my last Will and Testament, Item it is my Will & Charge to all my 
2 CONT Children that they walke in ye Feare of ye Lord, and in Love and peace 
2 CONT towards each other and endeavour the true performance of this my last 
2 CONT Will & Testament In Witnesse whereof I the said Elizabeth Howland have 
2 CONT hereunto sett my hand & seale this seventeenth Day of December Anno Dm 
2 CONT one thousand six hundred Eighty & six. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The mark of Elisabeth E H Howland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed & Delivd 
2 CONT
2 CONT in ye prsence of us Wittnesses 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Cole 
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Vyall 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Browne 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayflower Web Pages. Caleb Johnson © 1997 
2 CONT
2 CONT =========================================================================
2 CONT =========
2 CONT Plymouth Colony: Its History and People 1620-1691
2 CONT Part Three: Biographical Sketches
2 CONT
2 CONT xxx —A daughter of John and Joan (Hurst) Tilley, Elizabeth accompanied 
2 CONT her parents on the 1620 Mayflower. She had been baptized at Henlow, 
2 CONT Bedfordshire, on 30 August 1607. At Plymouth she married John Howland, 
2 CONT and they have many descendants living today.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
