2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Elizabeth (Tilley) Howland
2 CONT
2 CONT In ye Name of God Amen I Elizabeth Howland of Swanzey in ye
2 CONT County of Bristoll in ye Collony of Plymouth in New Engld being
2 CONT Seventy nine yeares of Age but of good & perfect memory
2 CONT thanks be to Allmighty God & calling to Remembrance ye
2 CONT uncertain Estate of this transitory Life & that all fflesh must Yeild
2 CONT unto Death when it shall please God to call Doe make constitute
2 CONT & ordaine & Declare This my last Will & Testament, in manner
2 CONT & forme following Revoking and Anulling by these prsents all &
2 CONT every Testamt & Testamts Will & Wills heretofore by me made
2 CONT & declared either by Word or Writing And this to be taken only
2 CONT for my last Will & Testament & none other. And first being
2 CONT penitent & sorry from ye bottom of my heart for all my sinns past
2 CONT most humbly desiring forgivenesse for ye same I give & Committ
2 CONT my soule unto Allmighty God my Savior & redeemer in whome
2 CONT & by ye meritts of Jesus Christ I trust & believe assuredly to be
2 CONT saved & to have full remission & forgivenesse of all my sins &
2 CONT that my Soule wt my Body at the generall Day of Resurrection
2 CONT shall rise againe wt Joy & through ye meritts of Christs Death &
2 CONT passion possesse & inheritt ye Kingdome of heaven prepared for
2 CONT his Elect & Chosen & my Body to be buryed in such place
2 CONT where it shall please my Executrs hereafter named to appoint
2 CONT And now for ye settling my temporall Estate & such goodes
2 CONT Chattells & Debts as it hath pleased God far above my Deserts
2 CONT to bestow upon me I Do Dispose order & give ye same in
2 CONT manner & forme following (That is to say) First that after my
2 CONT funerall Expences & Debts paid wc I owe either of right or in
2 CONT Conscience to any manner of person or persons whatsoever in
2 CONT Convenient tyme after my Decease by my Execrs hereafter
2 CONT named I Give & bequeath unto my Eldest Son John Howland ye
2 CONT sum of five pounds to be paid out of my Estate & my Booke
2 CONT called Mr Tindale's Workes & also one pair of sheetes & one pr
2 CONT of pillowbeeres & one pr of Bedblanketts, Item I give unto my
2 CONT son Joseph Howland my Stillyards & also one pr of sheetes &
2 CONT one pr of pillobeeres Item I give unto my son Jabez Howland my
2 CONT ffetherbed & boulster yt is in his Custody & also one Rugg &
2 CONT two Blanketts yt belongeth to ye said Bed & also my great Iron
2 CONT pott & potthookes Item I give unto my son Isaack Howland my
2 CONT Booke called Willson on ye Romanes & one pr of sheetes & one
2 CONT paire of pillowbeeres & also my great Brasse Kettle already in
2 CONT his possession Item I give unto my Son in Law Mr James
2 CONT Browne my great Bible Item I give & bequeath unto my Daughter
2 CONT Lidia Browne my best ffeatherbed & Boulster two pillowes &
2 CONT three Blanketts & a green Rugg & my small Cupboard one pr of
2 CONT AndyIrons & my lesser brasse Kettle & my small Bible & my
2 CONT booke of mr Robbinsons Workes called Observations Divine &
2 CONT Morrall & allso my finest pr of Sheetes & my holland
2 CONT pillowbeeres, Item I give unto my Daughter Elisabeth Dickenson
2 CONT one pr of Sheetes & one pr of pillowbeeres & one Chest Item I
2 CONT give unto my Daughter Hannah Bosworth one pr of sheets & one
2 CONT pr of pillowbeeres, Item I give unto my Grand Daughter Elizabeth
2 CONT Bursley one paire of sheets and one paire of Pillowbeeres Item I
2 CONT give & bequeath unto my Grandson Nathaniel Howland (the son
2 CONT of Joseph Howland) and to the heires of his owne Body lawfully
2 CONT begotten for ever all that my Lott of Land with ye Meadow
2 CONT thereunto adjoyning & belonging lying in the Township of
2 CONT Duxbury neare Jones River bridge, Item I give unto my Grandson
2 CONT James Browne One Iron barr and on Iron Trammell now in his
2 CONT possession, Item I give unto my Grandson Jabez Browne one
2 CONT Chest Item I give unto my Grand Daughter Dorothy Browne my
2 CONT best Chest & my Warming pan Item I give unto my Grand
2 CONT Daughter Desire Cushman four Sheep, Item I give & bequeath
2 CONT my wearing clothes linnen and Woollen and all the rest of my
2 CONT Estate in mony Debts linnen or of what kind or nature or sort
2 CONT soever it may be unto my three Daughters Elisabeth Dickenson,
2 CONT Lidia Browne and Hannah Bosworth to be equally Devided
2 CONT amongst them, Item I make constitute and ordaine my loving Son
2 CONT in Law James Browne and my loving son Jabez Howland
2 CONT Executors of this my last Will and Testament, Item it is my Will &
2 CONT Charge to all my Children that they walke in ye Feare of ye Lord,
2 CONT and in Love and peace towards each other and endeavour the
2 CONT true performance of this my last Will & Testament In Witnesse
2 CONT whereof I the said Elizabeth Howland have hereunto sett my hand
2 CONT & seale this seventeenth Day of December Anno Dm one
2 CONT thousand six hundred Eighty & six.
2 CONT
2 CONT The mark of Elisabeth E H Howland
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed & Delivd
2 CONT
2 CONT in ye prsence of us Wittnesses
