1 NOTE John Howland was born in England about 1593 and died at Plymouth Feb23 1673
2 CONT O.S.  He was the thirteenth name on the list of forty one persons whosigned
2 CONT the memorable and celebrated document, The Mayflower Compact.
2 CONT  At the time he was 28 years of age and was a member of the JohnCarver family.
2 CONT  Some try to say he was a servant of Carver.   He John Carver sawelements in
2 CONT his character which led him to supply John Howlands wants before theyleft
2 CONT England and caused him to be considered as one of his family.
2 CONT That he, John Howland, possessed sound judgement and business capacityis
2 CONT shown by the active duties which he assumed, and the trust which wasreposed in
2 CONT him in all the early labors in establishing a settlement, he had agrand part
2 CONT to perform in the sublime work of laying the foundation of agovernment which
2 CONT has stood for nearly three centuries.
2 CONT  John Carver must have had great trust in John Howland for upon hisdeath John
2 CONT Howland inherited all his possessions and possibly that cane.
2 CONT  He was one of ten men sent out from the Mayflower of the third partyto find a
2 CONT home and that became Plymouth.
2 CONT  He was a freeman and third in number in the govenor's"cowncell"(council).
2 CONT  In 1633 he was assessor.
2 CONT  Very few of the Colony was referred to as Mr but he carried thistitle.
2 CONT  He always held some public office such as; celect-man (selectman),Jewryman
2 CONT (juryman) and deputy, until 1670 when he was about 80 years old.
