2 CONT house they lived in from 1638 until he died there in 1672.  The cellarand
2 CONT doorstone of the old house can be seen at the right of the monument.The
2 CONT society bought 4 acres of land belonging to John Howland and erectedthe
2 CONT monument of granite aboout 7 feet high, 5 feet wide and 3 feet thick.About
2 CONT twenty feet behind the monument is a flag pole of steel, fifty feethigh.
2 CONT Above the inscription is a beautiful carving of the "Mayflower" atanchor in
2 CONT Plymouth Harbor.
