2 CONT      It is written tha5t the surname of Howland was found no otherplace than
2 CONT Essex, England, mostly in Wickem and Newport areas.  In later dates,when the
2 CONT name was found in countries of Herefordshire, Surrey and Bucks,  itwas
2 CONT invariably traced back to Essex.  At the time of our John Howland,there were
2 CONT Five John Howlands living in Essex.  In two of these lines, theHowland name
2 CONT terminated in Heiresses, one of whom-- Elizabeth, bequeathed theStreatham
2 CONT Estates to her husband, The Duke Of Bedford, who then acquired theadditional
2 CONT title of Baron Howland.
2 CONT
2 CONT      John: b. 1515/1528 in reign of King Henry VIII.  His eldest son,RICHARD,
2 CONT was Doctor Of Divinity and Bishop Celesborough of Norfork, England.He married
2 CONT Agnes, d/o  John Greenway of Clay.  They had 11 sosn and 1 Daughter.Queen
2 CONT Elizabeth gave the Howlands their grant of coat of armor in 1584,which is now
2 CONT used by that family, authenticated from the Harolds College, Londonthat
2 CONT started with Bishop Howland.  This Bisghop Howland performed theobsequies of
2 CONT Mary, Queen of Scots.
