2 CONT                       DIFFERENCE OF OPINION
2 CONT
2 CONT      This Pilgrim cannot be written of without much discussion andwith the
2 CONT strong connections, the traditional history that has become part ofthe beliefs
2 CONT of every action of this land, it is very hard to give up a recognitionof the
2 CONT statements of early writiers which were received withiut a doubt untilthe
2 CONT finding of the lost journal of Governor Bradford removed GovernorCarver's
2 CONT daughter from her position as John Howland"s wife.  The "Old Bible inHartford"
2 CONT places her as more naturally as Carver's granddaughter.  JohnHowlandis
2 CONT marriage was in 1623 or 1624-- one of the earliest weddingd in thecolony.  The
2 CONT Mayflower Socity gave it as in 1621.  As he was 28 when he arrived inthe
2 CONT Mayflower, 1620, and his amrriage took place before the land divisionin 1624,
2 CONT making him, allowing for the unknown months, 32 or nearly so, thesupposition
2 CONT has arisen that he might have been a widower, and by his first wife amember of
2 CONT Governor Carver"s family.  Governor Bradford states distinctly, andhis record
2 CONT is accepted, that Governor Carver left no descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT      I feel with the descendants, and would like to prove that hemeant simply
2 CONT none bearing the name of Carver,  As early as 1638 there were Carversin the
2 CONT colony who had a grant of land in Duxbury, and Governor Bradford mayhave had
2 CONT some personal reason, perhaps prejudice, against their presuming onany
2 CONT suooosed relationship, by virtue of their name, with Governor Carver.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Tradition, that always has some foundation in truth, has clungwith
2 CONT barnacle=like tenacity to every Howland descendant; in regard to thismarriage
2 CONT nothing can shake their faith in the teachings of their childhood.
2 CONT
2 CONT      The story has been handed down from Grandmother to grandmother,and facing
2 CONT the inevitable does not lessen their own belief; they are silenced,but not
2 CONT convinced.  This claim comes constantly, even in the light of theacceptation
2 CONT of Bradford's Journal.
