2 CONT                              HIS MARRIAGE
2 CONT
2 CONT      Quietly, as he did everything, John Howland "took to wife"Elizabeth, the
2 CONT young daughter of John Tilley, "to have and to hold," and the home heprovided,
2 CONT or the love he bore her.  If her mother could be established as thedaughter of
2 CONT Gov. Carver no more would be asked of her, though she simply went onher way,
2 CONT "sorrowing, tolling, rejoicing," the births of her children recordedher daily
2 CONT life, of interest to no one but her own household.
2 CONT
2 CONT      John Howland came into his property at Island Creek Pond and alsotwo
2 CONT small islands in Greeks Harbor.  With his possessiuons followed thefeeling
2 CONT that they needed his personal supervision, so for a time he yielded to
2 CONT necessity, but the early love for Plymouth was upon him, and he leftDuxbury,
2 CONT returning to his home all the better citizen for his little outing.
