2 CONT Desire c1625, Plymouth 13 October 1683, Barnstable, MA John Gorham, c1643 
2 CONT John 24 April 1627, Plymouth after 1699 Mary Lee, 26 October 1651, 
2 CONT Plymouth 
2 CONT Hope 30 August 1629, Plymouth 8 January 1683/4, Barnstable John Chipman, 
2 CONT c1647 
2 CONT Elizabeth c1631, possibly in Maine 1691, Oyster Bay, NY (1). Ephraim 
2 CONT Hicks, 13 September 1649, Plymouth 
2 CONT (2). John Dickinson, 10 July 1651, Plymouth
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia c1633, possibly in Maine aft. 11 January 1710/11 James Brown, c1654 
2 CONT Hannah c1637, possibly in Maine unknown Jonathan Bosworth, probably on 6 
2 CONT July 1661 
2 CONT Joseph c1640, Kingston, MA January 1703/4, Plymouth Elizabeth Southworth, 
2 CONT 7 December 1664, Plymouth 
2 CONT Jabez c1644, Kingston, MA between 1708 and 1712 Bethiah Thacher, c1668 
2 CONT Ruth c1646, Kingston, MA between 1672 and 16 October 1679 Thomas Cushman, 
2 CONT 17 November 1664, Plymouth 
2 CONT Isaac 15 November 1649, Kingston, MA 9 March 1723/4, Middleboro, MA 
2 CONT Elizabeth Vaughan, c1676, probably at Marshfield, MA 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT ANCESTRAL SUMMARY: 
2 CONT The ancestry of John Howland is discussed in John Howland of the 
2 CONT Mayflower through Desire Howland for Five Generations", Vol. 1, by 
2 CONT Elizabeth Pearson White, available from the Mayflower Web Page 
2 CONT bookstore. John Howland is the son of Henry and Margaret Howland of 
2 CONT Fenstanton, Huntingdon, England. Henry died on 17 May 1635 in 
2 CONT Fenstanton, and Margaret was buried on 31 July 1629. Besides son John, 
2 CONT who came on the Mayflower, they also had Humphrey, Arthur, Henry, George, 
2 CONT and Margaret. Henry came to Plymouth sometime before 1633, and Arthur 
2 CONT came sometime before 1640. For information on Arthur Howland, see the 
2 CONT National Genealogical Society Quarterly 71:84+, and for information on 
2 CONT Henry Howland see NGSQ 75:105-116, 216-225. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Howland is an ancestor to President George Bush, and to First Lady 
2 CONT Edith (Carrow) Roosevelt (Mrs. Theodore Roosevelt). Presidents Richard 
2 CONT Nixon and Gerald Ford are descendants of John Howland's brother Henry. 
2 CONT Winston Churchill is descended from John Howland's brother Arthur. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Howland 
2 CONT Will of Elizabeth (Tilley) Howland 
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY: 
2 CONT John Howland came on the Mayflower as a servant to John Carver. He is 
2 CONT best remembered for having fallen off the Mayflower during a mighty 
2 CONT storm, as recorded by Bradford: 
2 CONT
2 CONT In sundry of these storms the winds were so fierce and the seas so high, 
2 CONT as they could not bear a knot of sail, but were forced to hull for divers 
2 CONT days together. And in one of them, as they thus lay at hull in a mighty 
2 CONT storm, a lusty young man called John Howland, coming upon some occasion 
2 CONT above the gratings was, with a seele of the ship, thrown into the sea; 
2 CONT but it pleased God that he caught hold of the topsail halyards which hung 
2 CONT overboard and ran out at length. Yet he held his hold (though he was 
2 CONT sundry fathoms under water) till he was hauled up by the same rope to the 
2 CONT brim of the water, and then with boat hook and other means got into the 
2 CONT ship again and his life saved. And though he was something ill with it, 
2 CONT yet he lived many years after and became a profitable member both in 
2 CONT church and commonwealth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Howland's wife was Elizabeth Tilley, the daughter of John Tilley and 
2 CONT Joan (Hurst) Rogers (all were Mayflower passengers). Elizabeth (Tilley) 
2 CONT Howland died on 21 December 1687, in Swansea, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
