2 CONT
2 CONT The Last Will and Testament of mr John howland of Plymouth late Deceased, 
2 CONT exhibited to the Court held att Plymouth the fift Day of March Anno Dom 
2 CONT 1672 on the oathes of mr Samuell ffuller and mr William Crow as followeth 
2 CONT
2 CONT Know all men to whom these prsents shall Come That I John howland senir 
2 CONT of the Towne of New Plymouth in the Collonie of New Plymouth in New 
2 CONT England in America, this twenty ninth Day of May one thousand six hundred 
2 CONT seaventy and two being of whole mind, and in Good and prfect memory and 
2 CONT Remembrance praised be God; being now Grown aged; haveing many 
2 CONT Infeirmities of body upon mee; and not Knowing how soon God will call mee 
2 CONT out of this world, Doe make and ordaine these prsents to be my Testament 
2 CONT Containing herein my last Will in manor and forme following; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Imp I Will and bequeath my body to the Dust and my soule to God that Gave 
2 CONT it in hopes of a Joyfull Resurrection unto Glory; and as Concerning my 
2 CONT temporall estate, I Dispose thereof as followeth; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I Doe give and bequeath unto John howland my eldest sonne besides 
2 CONT what lands I have alreddy given him, all my Right and Interest To that 
2 CONT one hundred acres of land graunted mee by the Court lying on the eastern 
2 CONT side of Tauton River; between Teticutt and Taunton bounds and all the 
2 CONT appurtenances and privilidges Therunto belonging, T belonge to him and 
2 CONT his heirs and assignes for ever; and if that Tract should faile, then to 
2 CONT have all my Right title and Interest by and in that Last Court graunt to 
2 CONT mee in any other place, To belonge to him his heires and assignes for 
2 CONT ever; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my son Jabez howland all those my upland 
2 CONT and Meadow That I now posesse at Satuckett and Paomett, and places 
2 CONT adjacent, with all the appurtenances and privilidges, belonging therunto, 
2 CONT and all my right title and Interest therin, To belonge to him his heires 
2 CONT and assignes for ever, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I Give and bequeath unto my son Jabez howland all that my one peece 
2 CONT of land that I have lying on the southsyde of the Mill brooke, in the 
2 CONT Towne of Plymouth aforsaid; be it more or lesse; and is on the Northsyde 
2 CONT of a feild that is now Gyles Rickards senir To belonge to the said Jabez 
2 CONT his heirs and assignes for ever; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto Isacke howland my youngest sonne all those 
2 CONT my uplands and meddows Devided and undivided with all the appurtenances 
2 CONT and priviliges unto them belonging, lying and being in the Towne of 
2 CONT Middlebery, and in a tract of Land Called the Majors Purchase near 
2 CONT Namassakett Ponds; which I have bought and purchased of William White of 
2 CONT Marshfeild in the Collonie of New Plymouth; which may or shall appeer by 
2 CONT any Deed or writinges Together with the aformentioned prticulares To 
2 CONT belonge to the said Isacke his heirs and assignes for ever; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my said son Isacke howland the one halfe of 
2 CONT my twelve acree lott of Meddow That I now have att Winnatucsett River 
2 CONT within the Towne of Plymouth aforsaid To belonge to him and said Isacke 
2 CONT howland his heires and assignes for ever, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I Will and bequeath unto my Deare and loveing wife Elizabeth howland 
2 CONT the use and benifitt of my now Dwelling house in Rockey nooke in the 
2 CONT Township of Plymouth aforsaid, with the outhousing lands, That is uplands 
2 CONT uplands [sic] and meddow lands and all appurtenances and privilidges 
2 CONT therunto belonging in the Towne of Plymouth and all other Lands housing 
2 CONT and meddowes that I have in the said Towne of Plymouth excepting what 
2 CONT meddow and upland I have before given To my sonnes Jabez and Isacke 
2 CONT howland During her naturall life to Injoy make use of and Improve for her 
2 CONT benifitt and Comfort; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my son Joseph howland after the Decease of 
2 CONT my loveing wife Elizabeth howland my aforsaid Dwelling house att Rockey 
2 CONT nooke together with all the outhousing uplands and Medowes appurtenances 
2 CONT and privilidges belonging therunto; and all other housing uplands and 
2 CONT meddowes appurtenances and privilidges That I have within the aforsaid 
2 CONT Towne of New Plymouth excepting what lands and meadowes I have before 
2 CONT Given To my two sonnes Jabez and Isacke; To belong to him the said Joseph 
2 CONT howland To him and his heires and assignes for ever; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Desire Gorum twenty shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath To my Daughter hope Chipman twenty shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Elizabeth Dickenson twenty 
2 CONT shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Lydia Browne twenty shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give & bequeath to my Daughter hannah Bosworth twenty shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my Daughter Ruth Cushman twenty shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give to my Grandchild Elizabeth howland The Daughter of my son 
2 CONT John howland twenty shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item my will is That these legacyes Given to my Daughters, be payed by my 
2 CONT exequitrix in such species as shee thinketh meet; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I will and bequeath unto my loveing wife Elizabeth howland, my Debts 
2 CONT and legacyes being first payed my whole estate: vis: lands houses goods 
2 CONT Chattles; or any thing else that belongeth or appertaineth unto mee, 
2 CONT undisposed of be it either in Plymouth Duxburrow or Middlbery or any 
2 CONT other place whatsoever; I Doe freely and absolutly give and bequeath it 
2 CONT all to my Deare and loveing wife Elizabeth howland whom I Doe by these 
2 CONT prsents, make ordaine and Constitute to be the sole exequitrix of this my 
2 CONT Last will and Testament to see the same truely and faithfully prformed 
2 CONT according to the tenour therof; In witness whereof I the said John 
2 CONT howland senir have heerunto sett my hand and seale the aforsaid twenty 
2 CONT ninth Day of May, one thousand six hundred seaventy and two 1672 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed and sealed in the 
2 CONT
2 CONT prsence of Samuel ffuller John Howland 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crow And a seale 
