1 NOTE [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 14, Ed. 1, Tree #1317, Date of Import: Jul 16, 2005]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Howland arrived on the Mayflower, 1620, as the indentured servant of
2 CONT John Carver.  He rose rapidly as a leader of the Colony and was one of the
2 CONT eight Plymouth Undertakers who assumed responsibility for the Colony's
2 CONT debt to the Adventurers.  In 1633, he was on the Freeman list and by then,
2 CONT if not earlier, he was a Governor's Assistant.  In 1634, he was in charge
2 CONT of the Colony trading post on the Kennebec River at present-day Augusta,
2 CONT Maine.  He received a number of land grants, was elected a Deputy for
2 CONT Plymouth, served on numerous special committees and was an important lay
2 CONT leader of the Plymouth Church.  In 1639 he received a divsion of land at
2 CONT Yarmouth, where his son John and daughter Desire settled.  Also in 1639 he
2 CONT bought a house and land at Rocky Nook (now Kingston).
1 NOTE  Christening: 16 JAN 1602/1603 Ely,Cambridge,Eng
2 CONT
