1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Lee/6000000121883898879?through=6000000001511528051
2 CONT
2 CONT See: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000121884366850&
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >To add confusion, Samuel Sturtevant’s wife, in various records, has been listed as Ann, Anna, and Hannah. Her identity and vital dates, except her 2nd marriage to John Bass, have never been proved. It has been generally "accepted
2 CONC " that Samuel married Ann Lee, daughter of Robert and Mary Lee. Robert Lee was a shoemaker at Plymouth from before January 3, 1636 until after August 6, 1662. As of October 20, 1643. he had two daughters, Ann and Mary (both mentio
2 CONC ned that date in the will of John Atwood). John Atwood called the elder Lees "my brother and sister". Daughter Mary Lee became the wife of John Howland, Jr., of Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/robert-lee_19591225
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Lee
2 CONT (1602 - 1663)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Buckinghamshire, England on 1602 to Henry Lee and Elizabeth Fletcher. Robert Lee married Mary Atwood and had 2 children. He passed away on 1663 in Plymouth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relatives of Robert Lee
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Lee
2 CONT 1578 - 1603
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Fletcher 1580 - 1602
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse(s)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Atwood 1600 - 1681
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Lee 1629 - 1693
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Lee 1622 - 1697
2 CONT ----
2 CONT American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI) about Robert Lee
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: 	Robert Lee
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Date: 	1600
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthplace: 	Eng, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume: 	102
2 CONT
2 CONT Page Number: 	265
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: 	Lee fam. Quater-millenial gathering of des. And kinsmen of John Lee of Farmington, Ct. By W.W. Lee. Meriden, 1885. (116p.):93 Directory of the anc. heads of New England fams. Comp. By Frank R. Holmes. NewYork, 1923. (2
2 CONC 74p.):147
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT What is the evidence supporting him as son of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Henry-Lee/6000000003323025253 ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Answer: There is a birth certificate in London for a Robert Lee to whom the father is Henry Lee with a Baptism Date of 25 Feb 1601-see sources. Original Document kept on Ancestry. Robert Lee's Grandfather Robert Lee was living nea
2 CONC r London at the end of his life; Source:http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/lee-robert-1533-98. There is a perfect naming convention for our Robert Lee. Grandsons are named after their Grandfathers. He
2 CONC re is a description of Sir Anthony's son, Robert Lee in the chronology of marriages noting that Henry Lee was his ilegitimate son and that he was a notable adulterer who left his wife so destitute that she had to complain to the c
2 CONC ourt for support: Also, Sir Robert had a illegitimate brother, Sir Henry Lee. (Again, using the name Henry Lee, which is used repeatedly throughout their family lineage) And then, there is cousin, Sir Henry Lee, the successor to S
2 CONC ir Henry Lee Waring. Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Lee & https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Lee_of_Ditchley (under  para. marriages and children)
2 CONT
2 CONT A Birth for a Mary Lee with a noted father Robert Lee and mother Mary Lee was found in Westminister London with a date of Sept 1st, 1635. This date is striking considering Lt. John Howland married Mary Lee in Plymouth in 1651. Thi
2 CONC s original document is in Ancestry and a summary is in the sources. This date is also striking because there are no available records of our Robert Lee with a date before 1635 in Plymouth, England. There was no way his daughter Ma
2 CONC ry was born in Plymouth before he came over.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Birth for a Anne Lee with noted father Robert Lee and mother Mary Lee was found in Westminister, London with a date of 1631. This date is striking to me because there is no birth record for Anna, Hannah Lee, daughter of our Robe
2 CONC rt Lee who married Samuel Stuartvuant and John Boss in Plymouth. (record in sources) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Its also interesting to Note that Grandma Elizabeth Fletcher died in London, England date of 1623, it's a city with many ties to our Lees. There was a manuscript that noted two Henry Lee brothers but we found one was actually Henr
2 CONC y Lee Rainsford, the grandson of Sir Robert.  With all these clues it is no wonder that many of the descendants think that Henry Lee Waring is the father. There was a Henry Lee in London, fact.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Will of John Atwood d. before Feb 1644'''
2 CONT Names “my brother and sister Lee and their two children Ann & Mary”
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000198157658821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source:  England Historical and Genealogical Register Vol 4. p. 173 < [https://play.google.com/books/reader?id=NcIMAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover&source=gbs_atb_hover&pg=GBS.PA173 GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT
