1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evidence needed to support https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Lee/6000000002447053253 as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-the-Leather-Seller-Wood/6000000006981193403?through=6000000002447053253 & https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Joan-Atwood/6000000000630284210?through=6000000002447053253.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >To add confusion, Samuel Sturtevant’s wife, in various records, has been listed as Ann, Anna, and Hannah. Her identity and vital dates, except her 2nd marriage to John Bass, have never been proved. It has been generally "accepted
2 CONC " that Samuel married Ann Lee, daughter of Robert and Mary Lee. Robert Lee was a shoemaker at Plymouth from before January 3, 1636 until after August 6, 1662. As of October 20, 1643. he had two daughters, Ann and Mary (both mentio
2 CONC ned that date in the will of John Atwood). John Atwood called the elder Lees "my brother and sister". Daughter Mary Lee became the wife of John Howland, Jr., of Barnstable, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Will of John Atwood d. before Feb 1644'''
2 CONT Names “my brother and sister Lee and their two children Ann & Mary”
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000198157658821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source:  England Historical and Genealogical Register Vol 4. p. 173 < [https://play.google.com/books/reader?id=NcIMAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover&source=gbs_atb_hover&pg=GBS.PA173 GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #“Genealogical Guide to the Early Settlers of America: With a Brief History of ...” By Henry Whittemore. Page 320. [https://books.google.com/books?id=cSrlHHj2AFcC&ppis=_c&lpg=PA320&dq=obert%20LEE%20was%20living%20in%20Plymouth%20i
2 CONC n%201636%2C&pg=PA320#v=onepage&q=obert%20LEE%20was%20living%20in%20Plymouth%20in%201636,&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT # Mistress Ann Atwood's Will. ''The Mayflower Descendant''. Boston, MA: Massachusetts Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1909. Volume XI, p. 200. Available on < [https://books.google.com/books?id=S4lHAAAAYAAJ&newbks=1&newbks_redir=
2 CONC 0&vq=Atwood&pg=PA200#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > John Atwood’s widow, will exhibited 3 December 1654  at New Plymouth.  Names brother and sister Robert and Mary Lee “and their children.”  Estate to nephew William Crow.  
2 CONT # Birth seen as 11/18/1619, Kinwarton, Warwickshire, England.
