1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputed Surname
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname is Unknown. Not Hoyt. Not Foster. No records have been found in New England, giving her a surname or relationships to persons other than her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT The source for Alice's maiden name appears to be User contributed IGI: Alice Foster, or Alice Hoyt, married 1636 to William Crocker (born 1608).
2 CONT
2 CONT There was also an Alice Hoyt Crocker who married Jacob Penoyer on March 27, 1794 in Lee MA; but that seems a little far removed for a namesake. "Deacon William Crocker and his wife Alice Hoyt" certainly appear in many family histo
2 CONC ries online, but I'm not finding a contemporary source. Powell-5629 11:42, 11 January 2015 (EST)
2 CONT
2 CONT Josephine Frost reports no record of Alice's maiden name.[1] Torrey's New England Marriages, drawn from several sources, found no maiden name in those sources.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was living in 1683 and the mother of William's children.[1], including[3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT John, born May 1, 1637[3] [4]
2 CONT Elizabeth, born Sept 22, 1639, who died May 1658[3] [4]
2 CONT Samuel, born July 3, 1642[3], who died in 1681[4]
2 CONT Job, born March 9, 1644[3] [4]
2 CONT Josiah, born 19 September, 1647[3] [4]
2 CONT Eleazar, born July 21, 1650[3] [4]
2 CONT Joseph, born 1654[3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-443297
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Alice (Unknown) Crocker (1615 - 1684)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Crocker formerly [surname unknown] aka Foster, Hoyt
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1615 in London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Crocker — married 1 May 1637 (to 4 May 1684) [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of John Crocker, Elizabeth Crocker, Samuel Crocker, Job Crocker, Josiah Crocker, Eleazer Crocker and Joseph Crocker
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 4 May 1684 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown-443297 created 15 Aug 2011 | Last modified 29 May 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice (Unknown) Crocker migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Birth Date is a rough estimate. See the text for details.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Frost, Josephine C., Ancestors of Amyntas Shaw and His Wife Lucy Tufts Williams, Showing ... (Page 32) Brooklyn, NY: [self published] 1920, Archive.org accessed April 15, 2015
2 CONT ↑ Torrey’s New England Marriages Prior to 1700. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2008.) Originally published as: New England Marriages Prior to 1700. (Boston, Mass.: New England H
2 CONC istoric Genealogical Society, 2015.) Vol 1 p. 396, which states: CROCKER, William (?1608-1692) (ae 65 in 1673 & 1/wf Alice ____ (-1683+); by 1636; Barnstable/Scituate {MD 3:150, 24:73; Crocker (1923) 58; Reg. 2:66; Swift (1953) 20
2 CONC 4; Barnstable Fam. 205; Crocker 69; Cary Anc. 79; Smith-Hale 269; Sv. 1:474; Shaw-Williams 32; Winthrop-Babcock 161; Utah Gen-Mag 20:71}
2 CONT ↑ 3.0 3.1 3.2 3.3 3.4 3.5 3.6 3.7 Massachusetts Vital Records Barnstable, Volume 3, page 150, which states [p. 401] The births of ye Children of William Crocker and Alice his Wife
2 CONT his son John born May 1st 1637
2 CONT his Daughter Elizabeth Sept 22, 1639
2 CONT his Son Samuel 3 of July 1642
2 CONT Job born March 9, 1644
2 CONT Josiah 19 September 1647
2 CONT Eleazar 21 of July 1650
2 CONT Joseph 1654
2 CONT Elizbeth Died May 1658
2 CONT ↑ 4.0 4.1 4.2 4.3 4.4 4.5 4.6 4.7 Genealogical notes of Cape Cod families by Brownson, Lydia B.; Norton, Doris V.; Held, Grace V.; Publication date 1967; Publisher Lydia B. Brownson. This open source provides information that may 
2 CONC otherwise be behind a paywall. See Vol. 14 (Crispe to Crosby), page 176 for William, his wives and children
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
