2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT **Marriage 1636, Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts599, p 205; date only,590, p 192; date only,896
2 CONT *[William Crocker] came to Barnstable Oct. 21, 1639, and his daughter Elizabeth, baptized Dec. 22, 1639, is the fourth on the list, showing that he was among the first who came.599, p 204
2 CONT *In 1643 he removed to West Barnstable; had a large landed estate,  and was perhaps the richest man in town; his sons were also wealthy.596, p 63
2 CONT *He died in the Fall of 1692. His age is not stated, but he was probably about 80 years of age.599, p 205
2 CONT
