2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From “Genealogical Notes of Barnstable Families,” Volume 1, by By Amos Otis, F. B. & F. P. Goss, Barnstable, 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT >Deacon William Crocker, a native of Lyneham, Devonshire, emigrated to New England in 1634 or 1635. Lived first Roxbury or Scituate. Removed to Barnstable in 1639, year in which the town was settled. (p. 414)[4] He was a deacon in
2 CONC  the church, and was an influential citizen and the owner of a large landed estate. (p. 1122) [5] He first settled in the easterly part of Barnstable, but in 1643, removed to the westerly part where in 1655, he owned one hundred a
2 CONC nd twenty six acres of upland and twenty two acres of meadow. (p. 1122) [5] He was often employed in the business of the town and in settling estates. He acquired a large landed estate and for many years was the richest man in the
2 CONC  town.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Estate 
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon William Crocker's Last Will and Testament was dated 6 Sept 1692, and mentions:
2 CONT
2 CONT *To Patience my loving wife.
2 CONT *Sons: John, Job, Josiah, Eliazer, Joseph
2 CONT *Grandsons: Nathaniel, son of John; Samuel, son of Job; Thomas, son of Josiah (p. 205-8).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The last will and testament of Deacon William Crocker of Barnstable, in New England.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 6th day of September Anno Dom. 1692 I, William Crocker of Barnstable, being sick and weak in body but through ye mercy of God of disposing mind and memory, and knowing ye uncertainty of this life on earth, and being desirous t
2 CONC o settle things in order, do make this my last will and testament in manner and for me following, viz:
2 CONT *first and principally, I give and committ my soul to God in Jesus Christ my Saviour and Redeemer throw whose pretious death and merrits I hope to find ye free pardon and remition of all my sinnes, and everlasting salvation, and m
2 CONC y body to ye earth from whence it was taken, to be burried in such decent manner as to my Executor hereafter named, shall seem meet and convenient, and as touching my wordly estate which god hath in mercy lent unto me, my will is 
2 CONC to bestow ye same as hereafter is expressed, and I do hereby revoke and make void all wills by me formerly made and declared and appoint this be by my last will and testament.
2 CONT *Imprimus my will is that all those debts and duties which I owe in right or conscience to any person or persons whatsoever, shall be will and truly contented and paid when convenient by my Executor.
2 CONT *Itt. I give and bequeath unto Patience my loving wift besides ye liberty to dispose of all ye estate which she brought with her or had at ye time of our intermarriage, and besides ye forty pounds I then promised to give her. inca
2 CONC se she should survive me, I give unto her my gest bedd and bedstead with all ye furniture thereto belonging.
2 CONT *Itt. I give and bequeath to my eldest son John Crocker, my now dwelling house and lands both upland and fresh meadows adjoyning and belonging thereunto now and of late under my occupation and improvement to have and to hold to hi
2 CONC m his heirs and assignes forever he or they paying to ye s'd Patience my wife twenty pounds of ye fores'd forty pounds she is to receive, and I do also hereby confirm to him my son John his heirs and assignes forever all those par
2 CONC cels of land I heretofore gave unto him and are well known to have been in his quiet possession for sundry years; I further also give and bequeath to him my son John my two oxen which he hath had in his posession some years.
2 CONT *Itt. I give and bequeath unto my son Job Crocker besides ye land I heretofore gave him and know to be in his possession, twenty acres of that fifty acres at ye ponds which I purchased of John Coggin to have and to hold to him my 
2 CONC son Job his heirs and assignes forever and that he chuse it on which side of s'd land he please.
2 CONT *Itt. I will and bequeath to my sons Josiah and Eliazer Crocker besides those lands I heretofore gave to each of them and are in their particular knowne possession, all my upland at the marsh together with all ye marsh adjoining t
2 CONC hereunto, (except such particular parcel or parcels thereof as I have heretofore given and is possest of late by any other or is in these presents hereafter mentioned) to be equally divided between them ye s's Josiah and Eliazer t
2 CONC o have and to hold to them their heirs and assignes forever: Each of them ye s'd Josiah and Eliazer paying seven pounds and ten shillings apiece to ye s'd Patience in paying of ye forty pounds above mentioned. And I further will a
2 CONC nd bequeath to my sons Josiah and Eliazer to each one cow.
2 CONT *Itt. I will and bequeath unto my son Joseph Crocker (besides ye two parcels of upland and one parcel of marsh which I heretofore gave him and is know to be in his possession ye house and land which he hired of me and now lives on
2 CONC ) that is to say, so much of my s'd land as he hath now fenced in; together with that parcel of marsh which he hath from year to year of late hired of me; to have and to hold to him ye s'd Joseph his heir and assignes forever: he 
2 CONC or they paying five pounds to ye s'd Patience to make up ye full of s'd forty pounds I promised to her as above s'd.
2 CONT *Itt. I vie and bequeath all ye rest of my lands att ye ponds to my grandsons, viz: to Nathaniel, ye son of John Crocker, Samuel, ye son of Job Crocker, and Thomas, ye son of Josiah Crocker to be equally divided between them and t
2 CONC o their and each of their heirs and assignes forever.
2 CONT *Itt. my will is and I do hereby constitute and appoint my trusty and will beloved son Job Crocker to be my sole executor to see this my last will and testament to be performed, with whom I leave all ye residue of my estate in wha
2 CONC tsoever it be, to be equally distributed amongst all my children unless I shall signifie my minde to have such part or parts thereof to be disposed to any in particular.
2 CONT *In witness whereof I have hereunto sett my hand and seal.
2 CONT *On my further consideration I signifie my mind before ye ensealing hereof and it is my will that Mr. Russell shall have my tow steers which are att Isaac Howlands and that Mr Thomas Hinckly shall have my nagro boy if he please he
2 CONC  paying fourteen pounds to my Executor for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM CROCKER ___[SEAL.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed and declared In presence of SAMUEL CHIPMAN MERCY CHIPMAN
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Chipman and Mercy Chipman whose hands are sett as witnesses to this will made oath in Court October ye 19: 1692, that they did see the above said William Crocker now deceased sign seal and declare this above written to be h
2 CONC is last will and testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH LOTHROP: cl. Examined and duly compared with ye original will and entered October ye 22, 1692. Attest: JOSEPH LOTHROP. Recorder.
2 CONT
