1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00451682&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Baron Jérôme de Gondi, de Codun, II (1550 -1600)==
2 CONT Jérôme de Gondi, de Codun, II (it. Barone Girolamo de Gondi, de Codun, II) was a great-nephew of [Antoine II (1486–1560)]
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondi_family Gondi family, En], [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondi It], [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Famille_de_Gondi Fr], [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondi_(Adelsgeschlecht)_ De], [https://
2 CONC ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%B8_(%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4)_ Ru], [https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%96_(%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0)_ Uk]
2 CONT * [https://www.britannica.com/topic/Gondi-family Gondi Family] - [https://www.britannica.com/ Encyclopædia Britannica.com]
2 CONT * [https://famvin.org/wiki/Gondi_Family Gondi Family], Vincentian Encyclopedia<br/>
2 CONT '''!!!''' '''Note''': He didn't died at 1604, he died in 1600, after his death in 1604 his son [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-de-Gondi-II/6000000178399154916 '''Jean-Baptiste de Gondi, II''']; was sold a their château in 1618. 
2 CONC '''!!!'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ... During the 1570s, the Queen offered Jérôme de Gondi ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondi_family#cite_note-4 4]) a dwelling at Saint-Cloud, the Hôtel d'Aulnay, which became the nucleus of the Château de Saint-Cloud. Henri III 
2 CONC installed himself in this house in order to conduct the siege of Paris during the [https://www.britannica.com/event/Wars-of-Religion Wars of Religion] ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Wars_of_Religion French Wars of Religion
2 CONC ]) (1562-98), and here he was assassinated by the monk Jacques Clément. After the death of Jérôme de Gondi in 1604, the château was sold in 1618 by his son [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-de-Gondi-II/6000000178399154916 '''Jean-
2 CONC Baptiste II de Gondi'''] to Jean de Bueil, comte de Sancerre, who died shortly afterwards. The château was bought back by [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois-de-Gondi-cardinal-de-Retz/6000000015738366248 '''Jean-Franço
2 CONC is de Gondi'''], archbishop of Paris. His embellishments notably included gardens by Thomas Francine.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT * ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondi_family#cite_note-4 4]): Jérôme de Gondi born in Valencia, Spain, in 1550, the son of François de Gondi; he was a Gentilhomme de la Chambre du Roi, and was sent to several diplomatic missions
2 CONC  for [https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-IX-de-Valois-roi-de-France/6000000000307280059 '''CVharles IX'''], Henri III and Henri IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.britannica.com/biography/Jerome-Gondi-II Jérôme Gondi II], French historian, [https://www.britannica.com/ Encyclopædia Britannica.com]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gondi Family''', French family of Florentine origin, whose diplomats and bankers were prominent in France from the 16th century. The family established itself in France after gaining the confidence and patronage of [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/people/Catherine-de-Medici-Queen-Consort-of-France/6000000001063166988 '''Catherine de Médicis''']. Antoine II (1486–1560) was the first Gondi to settle in France and started the most illustrious branch of the family. At
2 CONC  first a banker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyon Lyon], he was brought to Paris by [https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-de-Medici-Queen-Consort-of-France/6000000001063166988 '''Catherine de Médicis'''], who made him stewar
2 CONC d to the Duke d’Anjou, later Henry III. Jean-Baptiste (1501–1580), nephew of Antoine, was steward to Catherine herself. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A great-nephew, Jérôme II (1550–1600), Baron de Codun, helped arrange the marriage of [https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-IX-de-Valois-roi-de-France/6000000000307280059 '''Charles IX'''] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Elisabeth
2 CONC -von-Habsburg/6000000003219792459 '''Elizabeth of Austria'''] (1570). Under Henry III, he served as ambassador to Venice and Rome, and Henry IV reappointed him as ambassador to Rome. [https://www.britannica.com/topic/Gondi-family#
2 CONC ref198490 Read More]
