1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: https://books.google.com/books?id=lasG6GBNfDMC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Florian Piasecki h. Janina was captured together with Dymitr "Bayda" Wiśniowiecki h. Korybut (Дмитро Іванович Вишневе́цький). Both men were executed on the order of Sultan Suleiman since they both refused to convert to Islam. Both
2 CONC  of them were hung there on a hook: above the sea branch leading to Galata. Florian Piasecki was hanged on a hook through his thigh. Piasecki died quickly because, hanging by the thigh on the hook and turning his head downward, bl
2 CONC ood rushed rapidly to his head. Wiśniowiecki was caught by the rib and turned his eyes upward; therefore, he was alive until the third day, until the Turks shot him with a bow while he cursed their Muhammad." - Marcin Bielski (183
2 CONC 2 r.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The chronicler Okolski mistakenly assigns the Zabawa coat of arms to Florian Piasecki, which is associated with Volhynia, and confuses his name, most likely referring to him as Jan instead of Florian. This is explained in the Herb
2 CONC arz by the chronicler Kasper Niesiecki.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note sent by Tobiasz Pilarski.
