1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1st wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Augustine-Walker/6000000001526115583?through=6000000075217950993 name unknown.  mother of Ann Holland, Mary Johnson, Elizabeth Warren, Dorothy Walker.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Stringer) Walker, widow of John Jouatt, was Augustine’s second wife; she was married to John Jouatt when his children were born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary signed a will 6 23 Dec 1614 in Great Amwell, Hertsfordshire, England.Mary had a will probated 5 10 Jan 1614/1615 in Great Amwell, Hertsfordshire, England. Mary was buried at Great Amwell on 26 December 1614.[4] "Marye Walkar,
2 CONC  widdowe, late wife of Augustine Walkar of Amwell was buried the xxvith December."[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webspace.webring.com/people/eu/um_5941/aqwg116.htm#5652
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine Walker Will: Dated 19 Apr 1613, Great Amwell, Hertfordshire, no probate date [TAG 78(2):83-86 (Ap r 2003)]. Requests burial at church or churchyard of Great Amwell. Names dau. Elizabeth Warren wife of Richard Warren, her
2 CONC  three children Marey, Ann, and Sarey Warren. Thomas, John and Frauncis Holland, children of Thomas Holland & my daughter Ann, his wife. Unborn child "said Ann is now conceyved". Daughter Mary Johnson. Symon Adams, son of Symon Ad
2 CONC ams Citizen & draper of London. And Dorothy his daughter [a gold ring that was her mother's]. Wife Marey, executrix. Thomas Hassall, Vicar of "much Amwell" for services preaching at my funeral. Symon Adams the father, overseer of 
2 CONC will. Mark of Augustine Walker. Sworn by Thomas Holmested, Thomas Robert & John Larke (no date of probate).
2 CONT
2 CONT Foot Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Entered by Michael Lechner, Sep. 24, 2012.
2 CONT ↑ The Parish register and Tithing book of Thomas Hassall of Amwell. ↑ The will of Augustine Walker ↑ www.craigrich.net/TAG_Warren.pdf ↑ The Parish register and Tithing book of Thomas Hassall of Amwell. Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Augustine Walker. Thomas Hassall, Stephen G. Doree, "The Parish register and Tithing book of Thomas Hassall of Amwell", Hertfordshire Record Society, Jan 1, 1989 - Reference - 281 pages. Lechner Family History, compile
2 CONC d by Michael Lechner, with my father Ted Harold Lechner. Links
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stringer-55
