1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Vital Statistics'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Died between 1585 and 1591.  Married to Joanna Walsele.  His wife outlived him and was apparently his only wife.
2 CONT * Children mentioned in will are:  Johanna (~ Joan), Eleanor (~ Ellen, m. Mr. Balstone), and William.
2 CONT *  Walter's mother's name was Joan. He was the grandson of John Deane and Johanna Sellwood, she being the daughter of Nicholas Sellwood of Chard.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Facts, Sources, and Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Good source: http://kinnexions.com/ancestries/strong.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''WALTER DEANE''', Yeoman  - d. 1591.  Married '''Joanna Walsele''' Nov 12 1565 at Buckland, St. Mary, Somerset. She d. 1597.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1554 Rental of Streete and Leigh Manor
2 CONT * Walter Deane ['Walter crossed out and 'William' inserted] 7s. [DD/TOR 228]
2 CONT * 1564 - 1566 - Survey of Manor of Tatworth, Chard (T/PH/VCH/14):
2 CONT * WALTER DEANE by a copy dated 3 April Henry VIII (1527) holds a tenement and Cottage for his life 1566 Survey of Tatworth Manor (Devon R.O. 123 M/E31
2 CONT * Walter Deane holds by copy dated 3 Apr. 1527 one heriotable tenement and one cottage, to which pertains 17 acres of land lying in divers closes or parcels, viz. a curtilage, garden and orchard, 4 acres in South Field, 7 acres in
2 CONC  Myddlellfelde, 5 acres in North Field 2 1/2 acres in Holwaie, 3 rods in Gulwill Meade, 1/2 acre in Gore Meade. To hold to him for term of his life by grant of Thomas la Ware and Lady Elizabeth his wife under fine 33s4d, rent 13s
2 CONT * 1568 Apr. 21 -A leasse to be made to Water [sic] Deane, Johan his wiff and Elen their doughter of vij closes of pasturer [sic] and arrable called Caprons downe in the tything of Lye in the parishe of Wynsham by est[imation] xxx 
2 CONC acres and sute to the courte for xx li. paid in hand, attornayes John Pears, Thomas Toker.
2 CONT * 1580 - Survey of Manor of Tatworth, Chard (T/PH/VCH 15): WALTER DEANE holds by copy dated 16 April 7 Elizabeth (1565) a tenement and cottage for his life and the life of LETICIE, DAU. OF WILLIAM HILL. Undated later note of rever
2 CONC sion of property to Eleanor Balstone and Joan Deane, dau. of the said Joan on 10 Oct. 30 Elizabeth (1588).
2 CONT *  [1582 undated note at end of volume] Johanna Deane widow, lated wife of Walter Deane deceased holds by indenture dated 23 Apr. 1582, 7 closes of land, meadow and pasture containing by estimation 30 Acres called Caprons Downe, l
2 CONC ying in the tithing of Leigh (all trees reserved0 to hold the same for her life and after to remain to William Deane her son for term of his life by rent of 7s a year and 6s8d in the name of a heriot and suit of court twice a year
2 CONC  [DD/TOR 222]
2 CONT * 1590 - c.1609 Survey of Tatworth Manor (123 M/E 33) Johanna Deane widow holds one tenement and one cottage with appurtenances of 17 acres [etc. as listed above] to hold for her widowhood and after the premises to be granted to E
2 CONC lenor Balston and Johanna Deane, daughters of the said Johanna, for term of their lives by grant of John Petre kt. for fine of 30 pounds as appears by copy dated 10 Oct. 1593, by rent 14s.
2 CONT * 1591 Sept. 3 Street and Leigh Court Book: ...present that Walter Deane, who of the Lord held by indenture certain closes called Capon [sic] Downe, containing by estimation 30 acres, died since the last court [previous court was 
2 CONC held 9 Apr. 1591], whereupon there fell due to the lord for reliec 6s8d. And it is presented that the bailiff should admonish the wife of the said Walter that she produce the writing by which she claims to hold the said premises a
2 CONC nd show the same to the steward at the next court [ the next court was held on 7 Sept. 1591, but included no relevant entry]
2 CONT * 1597 (Devon Record Office, Ref. 123M/E31)- Survey acreage and a tenement held by Walter Deane, of South Chard in the Survey of 1580 is held by Johana Deane, wid. for her life, after which the property is to go to Eleanor Balston
2 CONC e and Johanna Deane for their lives
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Walter Deane is dated July 7, 1585, proved Jul 10, 1591, by Geoffrey Clarke Notary Public, Proctor for William Deane the son and executor. . (PCC Sainberbe 56, Wills vol 62 Somerset Record Office).
2 CONT
2 CONT To be bur. in churchyard in Chard. To poor folks 20 groates. To Eleanor Deane my daughter 30 pounds...to Joan Deane my daughter 30 pounds. Residue of my goods; to Joane my wife one moiety thereof, for her life, and aftr her death 
2 CONC to remain to William my son to whom I give all the rest of my goods, and I make him sole executor...THOMAS BONDAGE, THOMAS SMITHE and JOHN LEGG of Southcharde to be overseers, to whom I give 2s apiece. Witnessed by John Willsonn, 
2 CONC John Burghe, Thomas Smithe
2 CONT
2 CONT =--------------------=
2 CONT
2 CONT "Walter DEANE - d. 1585-1591, South Chard, Somerset, England. Walter's mother's name was Joan. He was the grandson of John DEANE and Johanna SELLWOOD, she being the daughter of Nicholas SELLWOOD of Chard. Walter was married on Nov
2 CONC . 12, 1565 at Buckland St. Mary, Somerset to Joan WALSELE (d. 1597). Walter's will, dated Jul. 7, 1585 and proved Jul. 10, 1591, names daughters Eleanor and Joan, and son William, as does the will of his widow Joan, dated Mar. 29,
2 CONC  1597 and proved May 10, 1597."
2 CONT =--------------------=
2 CONT William DEANE - d. about 1634, South Chard, Somerset. Will dated Jul. 22, 1634 names his children and his grandson John STRONG. Son of Walter DEANE and Joan WALSELE.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Joane - b. before 1597; bur. Dec. 14, 1621, Chard, Somerset.
2 CONT * 2. William - d. 1678, South Chard. Named eldest son in his father's will.
2 CONT * 3. Thomas - d. 1672. Married Jun. 10, 1629, Chard, Somerset Mary WARRY, daughter of John WARRY and Mary DEAN.
2 CONT * 4. John - b. about 1597; d. 1660, Taunton, Bristol Co., MA. Will dated Apr. 25, 1660. To America in 1637 aboard the 'Speedwell' with brother Walter. Married Alice. Children of John and Alice DEANE: John married Sarah EDSON; Thom
2 CONC as married Catherine STEPHENS (daughter of Thomas STEVENS, Jr., and granddaughter of Thomas STEVENS and Mary WALLE); Israel did not marry; Isaac married Hannah LEONARD; Nathaniel did not marry; and Elizabeth married Josiah EDSON.
2 CONT * 5. Margerie - d. about 1635, Dorchester, MA. First wife of Elder John STRONG.
2 CONT * 6. Isaacke - Married Oct. 12, 1636, Thornecombe, Devon Margerie SMITH.
2 CONT * 7. Susan - Mentioned in 1654 will of Anne HURT.
2 CONT * 8. Eleanor - Living in 1634.
2 CONT * 9. Walter - bap. May 13, 1612, St. Mary, Chard, Somerset; d. 1659, Taunton, MA. To America in 1637 aboard the 'Speedwell' with brother John. Married in 1637 at Taunton, MA Eleanor COGAN, daughter of William COGAN, granddaughter 
2 CONC of Barnard COGAN, and great granddaughter of Robert COGAN. William COGAN may have married second the widow of John STRONG of Chard, Somerset. The Apr. 24, 1654 will (proved Jun. 23, 1655) of William COGAN, a tanner of South Chard,
2 CONC  names two "daughters" named Eleanor: one being Eleanor COGAN, then unmarried, and the other being Eleanor DEANE, wife of Walter DEANE in New England. Children of Walter and Eleanor DEANE: Mary married Shadrack WILBORE (son John m
2 CONC arried Alice PITTS, daughter of Peter PITTS and Mary ANDREWS); Lydia married Bartholomew TIPPING; James married Sarah TISDALE; Ezra married Bethia EDSON; Benjamin married Sarah WILLIAMS; and Joseph married Mary TIPPING.
2 CONT * 10. Elizabeth - Living in 1634. Called youngest daughter in her father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Deane b. 1574 ENG. d. Oct 11, 1634 ENG m. Margaret Wickham. Ten children:
2 CONT =-----------------------------=
2 CONT i.William Deane b. 1600;
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.John Deane b. 1601 d. April 25, 1660 m. Alice Strong (1635-37) [See the Will of John Deane of Taunton at the following hyperlink]  http://www.mayflowerfamilies.com/wills/john_deane.htm  ch= 6    Thomas Deane m. Catherine Steven
2 CONC s d. of Thomas Stevens; Isaac Deane m. Hannah Leonard, Israel Deane, Nathaniel Deane, Elizabeth Deane  John Deane  m. Sarah Edson  7 children: John Deane b. 25 April 1677; Sarah Deane b. 13 December 1678;Ebenezer Deane b. 17 May 1
2 CONC 681; Joseph Deane b. 14 March 1683 (ch=Faxon Deane) ; Jeremiah Deane b. 24 March 1685; Elizabeth Deane b. 13 October 1689; Abigail Deane b. 12 June 1694 John and Sarah Edson Deane of Dedham  http://www.lkwdpl.org/history/5biograph
2 CONC yA-F.htm#0:27 ,http://books.google.com/books?id=hrNRAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA24&dq=will+of+Walter+Deane+Chard&lr=&as_brr=1
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.Joane Deane b. 1602 d. bef. 1634;
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.Thomas b. 1604 d. aft.1634 arrived aboard The Elizabeth and Ann; married 10 June 1629 Mary Wary (daughter of John Wary and Mary Dean) http://www.kinnexions.com/ancestries/strong.htm  http://users.tpg.com.au/mikewry/will%20extra
2 CONC cts.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT v.Susan Deane b. 1606 d.. aft.1634;
2 CONT
2 CONT vi.Isaac b. 1608 d. aft.1634; married Margerie Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT vii.Margerie Deane b. 1610 d.1635 m. John Strong (son of Richard John Strong & Eleanor Deane) Descendancy of Elder John Strong;
2 CONT
2 CONT viii.Walter (see below);
2 CONT
2 CONT ix.Ellianor Deane b. 1614 d. aft. 1634;
2 CONT
2 CONT x.Elizabeth Deane b. abt.1616 d. aft.1634. may be the Elizabeth Deane Twinning, whose son, William Twinning married Anne Doane (daughter of Deacon John Doane)  http://books.google.com/books?id=QSYAAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA6&dq=Elizabeth+Ring
2 CONC +deane#PPA11,M1 
