2 CONT Will, 22 Jul 1634
2 CONT
2 CONT I William Dean of Southchard within parish of Chard in the county of Somersett sicke of bodie but of sound and perfect memorie
2 CONT
2 CONT thanks bee given to God doe make and decalare this my last Will and
2 CONT
2 CONT Testament.......I give to the poore of Chardland twenty shillings to bee
2 CONT
2 CONT distributed by the discrecon of my Executor and of MY SONNE THOMAS DEANE
2 CONT
2 CONT ONE OF MY OVERSEERSItem: To JOHN DEANE MY SONNE I give and
2 CONT
2 CONT bequeath a chest standing in the hall, a truckle bedsted and bed
2 CONT
2 CONT furnished, wheat the halfendeale of the hay wich is in COLFIELD the
2 CONT
2 CONT remynder of the terme yet to come in BROADFIELD together with the lease
2 CONT
2 CONT thereof. The residue of the terme yet to come in HAM MEADE and the Lease
2 CONT
2 CONT thereof, yeelding and paying therefore from the Feast date of St.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michaell next after my decease to SUSAN, ELLIANOR, MARGERIE AND ELIZABETH
2 CONT
2 CONT MY DAUGHTERS foure pounds apeece yearelie during the contynuance of his
2 CONT
2 CONT now estate therein and soe rateably for any lesser terme of his estate
2 CONT
2 CONT therein at any other tyme then at the end of a full yeare happen to take
2 CONT
2 CONT end and determyne, Also I give and bequeath to him in money fortie
2 CONT
2 CONT shillings to bee paid him within three moneths after my
2 CONT
2 CONT decease. Item: To MY SONNE THOMAS (for that hee is
2 CONT
2 CONT otherwise in comptetent manner provided for) I onely give and and
2 CONT
2 CONT bequeath to him and to his wife as a remembrance of my fatherly love two
2 CONT
2 CONT silver spoons. Item: To WALTER DEAN MY SONNE I give a chest
2 CONT
2 CONT standing in the chamber over the Kitchen, a truckle bedsted and bed
2 CONT
2 CONT furnished, and a bible also I give unto him iontlie [jointly] with his
2 CONT
2 CONT BROTHER ISSACK the Lease or Leases of the grounds name WILBEERE and
2 CONT
2 CONT CANTES, and together with his said brother all profitts on the said
2 CONT
2 CONT grounds to bee received and taken during the contynuance of the terme
2 CONT
2 CONT therein yet remayneing.Item: To ISSACK DEANE MY SONNE I
2 CONT
2 CONT bequeath and give a Chest and little Fojelett or box standing in the
2 CONT
2 CONT lower chamber, a truckle bed furnished and the halfendeale of the hay in
2 CONT
2 CONT COLEFIELD, and alsoe together with HIS BROTHER WALTER DEANE I give and
2 CONT
2 CONT bequeath the grounds above menconed name WILBEER AND CANTES, by the
2 CONT
2 CONT ioyntly to be occupied during the terme therein remayneing together with
2 CONT
2 CONT the lease or leases thereof, also I give him that little woodvine
2 CONT
2 CONT withouth the utter(outer) kitchen doore, and all tymber felled and all
2 CONT
2 CONT such rafters and boords reede and billies which I have, and also in money
2 CONT
2 CONT tenne pounds to bee paid within and also in money tenne pounds to bee
2 CONT
2 CONT paid within two moneths after my decease. Item: To MY
2 CONT
2 CONT DAUGHTER SUSAN DEANE I give that bedstead which is in the inner chamber
2 CONT
2 CONT with its appurtennces, one skellet, a posnett, a great barrell, a side
2 CONT
2 CONT saddle, a coffer in the inner chamber, a third part of all my wooll, the
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAPPELL and YE WRITEINGS for holding thereof and in money seaventy three
2 CONT
2 CONT pounds six shillings an eight pence to bee paid at the endo f six
2 CONT
2 CONT months.Item To MY DAUGHTER ELEANOR DEANE I give and
2 CONT
2 CONT bequeath that Cofer which is in the chamber of the kitching, a bed stead
2 CONT
2 CONT also standing there and my best feathered furnished, a little brasse
2 CONT
2 CONT pott, one of my greater barrells, a piltion and a third part of all my
2 CONT
2 CONT wooll, and seaventie three pounds six shillings and eight pence in money
2 CONT
2 CONT to bee paid at the end of six moneths after my decease.Item:
2 CONT
2 CONT To MARGERIE STRONG MY DAUGHTER I give the least brasse pott of the three,
2 CONT
2 CONT my best cauldron and tenne pounds in money to bee paid within one yeare
2 CONT
2 CONT after my decease, and to HER SONNE and MY GRAND CHILD JOHN STRONG. I give
2 CONT
2 CONT five pounds to be paid att the end of two yeares after my decease upon
2 CONT
2 CONT sufficient discharge given to acquite my my executor
2 CONT
2 CONT thereof.Item: To MY YOUNGEST DAUGHTER ELIZABETH I give and
2 CONT
2 CONT bequeath a bedstead in the Low chamber, a featherbed furnished, a little
2 CONT
2 CONT table boord over the entire, a coffer in the inner chamber, one of the
2 CONT
2 CONT great barrells, the third part of my wooll and seaventie three pounds six
2 CONT
2 CONT shillings and eight pence in money to bee paid at the end of six moneths
2 CONT
2 CONT after my decease. And if any to whom an procon is hereby given
2 CONT
2 CONT chance to dye before his her or their porcon or pocons bee due to bee
2 CONT
2 CONT paid my will therein is that such their porcon or porcons be devyded
2 CONT
2 CONT equallie betweene MY THREE YOUNGER SONNES JOHN, WALTER AND ISAAKE and my
2 CONT
2 CONT FOWER DAUGHTERS, or betweene such of them as then bee
2 CONT
2 CONT livieing.Lastly I hereby ordeine and appoynt WILLIAM DEANE
2 CONT
2 CONT MY ELDEST SONNE to bee Executor of this my last will and testament, and
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS LEGG SONNE OF THOMAS LEGG THE ELDER and MY SONNE THOMAS DEANE
2 CONT
2 CONT Overseers hereof, and in consideracon thereof doe give to each of them
2 CONT
2 CONT two shillings. By mee William Deane. And as touching the clause in the
2 CONT
2 CONT latter end of the will that if any Legatee dye before his or her porcon
2 CONT
2 CONT become due, the testator shewed that his meaneing therein is that if any
2 CONT
2 CONT of his daughters chaunce to marry and doe happen being married to dye
2 CONT
2 CONT that such her porcon shall then bee paid to the husband of such
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter.hese being Witnesses: WILLIAM COGAN, THOMAS
2 CONT
2 CONT LEGGE, THOMAS DEANE, JOHN GIBBS No. I.Proved October 21,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1634 of S. Chard, Somerset, EnglandNEHGR 1897, Vol 51
2 CONT
2 CONT p.432
