2 CONT * William Symes born Nov 1544 in Sandwich, Kent, England; died on 27 Jul 1597 in Poundsford, Somerset, England.
2 CONT * Parents:  John Patrick Symes (1515-1563) & Jane Petty (1509-1563) Married 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Hill in 1570 Pitminster, Somerset, England. She was born 1551 in Somerset, England; died 1598 in Charde, Somerset, England.  Known children are:  
2 CONT # Margery Payne 1570 –  
2 CONT # Rev. William Symmes 1570 – 1627 
2 CONT # John Symes 1572 – 1661 
2 CONT # Henry Symes 1573 – 1599 
2 CONT # Margaret Symes 1576 – 1599 
2 CONT # James Symes 1579 –  
2 CONT # Eleanor Symes 1581 –  
2 CONT # Alice Symes 1582 –  
2 CONT # Elizabeth Symmes 1596 – 1628  
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. WILLIAM SYMES, was b. c. 1550 England. He m. (when?) (where?) ELIZABETH HILL.10 He lived at Chard,11 Somerset, Eng.12 He was granted arms in 1591.13 Owens (p. 3) says he, "was a merchant of Poundesford [Poundisford14], Somerset
2 CONC , England. He owned a mill in West Coker and lands in Taunton. According to his will he owned manors of Barwick,15 Boure,16 Stoford,17 Somerset, and [Frankham],18 Dorset, and the one he lived in in Charde. Obviously he was a man o
2 CONC f means. His coat of arms was given him in 1591. ..." He d. before 27 July 1597 19 at Pound[i]sford, 20 Somerset, Eng. His will was dated 4 June and proved 27 July 1597.21 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Symes of Poundsford (in Pitminster22), co. Somerset, merchant. Will dated 4 June and proved 27 July 1597 by Elizabeth Symes the relict. (66 Cobham.) Poor 23 of Chard & Pitminster. Rt Hon. Sir Ed. Seymour, Knt. Lord Seymour
2 CONC  of Pomeroy, Devon, by deed of 29 Nov. 31 Eliz. hath granted me an annuity of 100 marks out of the demesne of Bury Pomeroy for 99 years, if Eliz. my wife & Hen. & James my sons shall so long live. To my s. John Symes £2000 accordi
2 CONC ng to the covenants betw. me & Sir John Popham, Knt., Chief Justice, & Tho. Horner, Esq. To my s. Hen. 1000 marks. My s. Robt £500. My s. Wm. £500 at 21. My d. Eliz. 1000 marks. My dau. Margt 1000 marks at 21 or marriage. My dau. 
2 CONC Margery Pyne 1000 marks. Jasper Pyne my s.-in-l. living in Charde. My Manors of Barwick, Bowre, 24 & Stoford, co. Som., & Frankham, co. Dorset. Mill in West Coker & lands in Taunton. My manor house in Charde to Eliz. my wife for h
2 CONC er life, & she to be Ex'trix. John Pyne, Esq., Roger Hill, Gent., & my bro. in l. Hugh Hill, Gent., to be Supervisors.25
2 CONT
2 CONT He was presumably the man mentioned on p. 115 of Antigua: "1588. Armada list of subscribers. "Maye William Symes of Chard, tercio Maii, £50.'" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * The Symes family in Somerset was documented as early as 1623 in the Visitation of Somerset, and that Symes pedigree was published in 1876 in Harleian Society Publications, volume XI, 4 p. 110. The family is also documented in th
2 CONC e History of the Island of Antigua, coincidentally also on p. 110 (and continuing on page 111). Generations 1 4 of the lineage detailed in this document are shown clearly in the chart on pp. 110 111 of Antigua, although it must be
2 CONC  noted that the line connecting John Symes of Barwick and William Symes of Chard  is a dotted line, obviously implying lack of proof. 5 It is understatement to say that the reference to Gen. 5 is minimal in Antigua: it says on p. 
2 CONC 111 only "William Symes, living 1675" on the chart (but the 1675 will of his spinster sister Elizabeth, on which that "living 1675" statement is based, is abstracted in Antigua, p. 112).
2 CONT
