1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Symes (b.1540) of Somerset married Elizabeth Hill. As a wedding gift, her father, Robert Hill, gave his daughter, Elizabeth Hill, Poundsford Lodge, which is still standing. John Symes II was the eldest son 
2 CONC of William & Elizabeth, and was born on March 4, 1572 at Poundsford. John Symes II and later inherited the Poundsford estate, which has ever remained in the Symes family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children are: 
2 CONT # Margery Payne 1570 –  
2 CONT # Rev. William Symmes 1570 – 1627 
2 CONT # John Symes 1572 – 1661 
2 CONT # Henry Symes 1573 – 1599 
2 CONT # Margaret Symes 1576 – 1599 
2 CONT # James Symes 1579 –  
2 CONT # Eleanor Symes 1581 –  
2 CONT # Alice Symes 1582 –  
2 CONT # Elizabeth Symmes 1596 – 1628  
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://genforum.genealogy.com/sims/messages/6412.html
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________
2 CONT *'''Abstracts of Somersetshire wills, etc: copied from the manuscript ..., Volume 1 By Frederick Arthur Crisp, Frederick Brown
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=PElFAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA55&lpg=PA55&dq=John+Symes+1572&source=bl&ots=b3jTjiqeRr&sig=9ws6f1BrfxWuZTkhKfR79Snq3OI&hl=en&ei=PyaJTf66HZKmsQPAzu2RDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CBYQ6AEwADge#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=John%20Symes%201572&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 52.
2 CONT *'''B.110. WILLIAM SYMES, of Poundsford, Somerset, Merchant.''' Will dated June 4, 1597, proved July 27, 1597, '''by Elizabeth Symes the relict.''' [66 Cobham.] Poor of Chard & Pitminster. The R't Hon. Sir Edward Seymour, Kn't. Lo
2 CONC rd Seymour of Pomeroy, Devon by deed, Nov. 29, 31 Elizab: hath granted me an annuity of 100 marks out of the demesne of Bury Pomeroy, for 99 years, if Elisabeth my wife, & Henry & James my sons shall live so long. To '''my son''' 
2 CONC John Symes, L2000, according to certain covenants between me & Sir John Popham, K't, Chief Justice, & Thomas Horner, Esq. To Henry '''my son''', 1000 marks. To '''my son''' Robert, L500. '''My son''' William, L500, at age of 21. '
2 CONC ''My daughter''' Elizabeth, 1000 marks. '''My daughter''' Margaret, 1000 marks at age of 21 or marriage. '''My daughter Margery''' Pyne, 100 marks. Jasper Pyne, '''my son in law''', living in Charde. My Manors of Barwick, Bowre, &
2 CONC  Stoford, Somerset, & Frankham, Dorset. Mill in West Coker, & lands in Taunton. '''My manor house in Charde, to Elizabeth my wife, during her life''', Extrix. Supervisors, John Pyne, esq., Roger Hill, gent., & '''my brother''' in 
2 CONC law, Hugh Hill, gent.
2 CONT *Pg. 67
2 CONT *A. 33. B. 50. ROBERT HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Esq. Will dated Apr. 21, 1581, proved Jun 15, 1581, by Elianor(3) the relict. [26 Darcy.] Poor of Taunton, Hillbrishe & Pytminster. To my son James Hill, my estate in the Capital M
2 CONC essuage called Pownsforde alias Lodge, in Pytminster, & lands which I hold in common with Sir Henry Portmant, K't, in Pytminster. Many pieces of plate. The spice plate of silver. One piece called the Nutt. To my wife Elynor, a mes
2 CONC suage in Taunton, wherein William Awdey dwelleth, & one in Fore Street, wherein Julian Greye dwelleth, &c. To my son John Hill, an annuity of L10 from my farm called Heydon, & also an annuity of L20 to my son Hugh, & after the dea
2 CONC th of my wife Elynor, the farm of Haydon to Hugh Hill, & to James Hill if he pay L30 per ann. to Hugh Hill. To my daughter Jane, L200, & "a pott of silver called the Skynkinge pott," &c. To my daughter Margaret, L200, & my silver 
2 CONC beere jug. My goddaughter Rachel Portman, daughter of Sir Henry Portman, an old roiall of gold. To my other goddaughters 12d each. A marriage intended between my son James Hill and Ann Moryce, daughter of M'r Moryce, of Coxwell, B
2 CONC erks, esq., he to pay me L300, of which L200 to be paid to my wife, for the advancement of my daughters. My '''son in law, William Symes,(5) one silver spoon gilt, & 6/8 to their children'''. My wife, Extrix. Sir James Marrven, K'
2 CONC t, my brother in law, M'r Nicholas Wadham, my son, James Hill, M'r John Walker, of Stowey, & M'r Thomas Davidge, of Taunton, Supervisors. March 31 1593, Admon. was granted to William Wigsted, of Fontmell Gifford, Wilts, yeoman, on
2 CONC  decease of Elianor, Relict of Robert Hill.
2 CONT **         (3) Daughter of Sir James Mervyn, and second wife of the testator.
2 CONT **'''         (5) William Symes, of Chard, married Elizabeth, daughter of the testator by his first wife, Alice Clark. __________________________________
2 CONT *SYMES, John (1573-1661), of Poundisford, Pitminster, Som.; later of Frampton Cotterell, Glos.
2 CONT *b. 4 Mar. 1573, 1st s. of '''William Symes, merchant, of Chard, Som. and Elizabeth, da. of Robert Hill'''† of Taunton, Som.1 educ. Exeter Coll., Oxf. 1588, BA 1591; L. Inn 1589.2 m. settlement 29 Dec. 1595, Amy, da. of Thomas Hor
2 CONC ner† of Cloford, Som., 3s. 8da. suc. fa. 1597.3 d. 29 Oct. 1661.4 sig. Jo[hn] Symes.
2 CONT *Offices Held
2 CONT **J.p. Som. 1608-26, 1627-45;5 commr. sewers, Som. 1610, 1616, 1625; gov., Huish’s almshouses, Taunton 1616;6 sheriff, Som. 1626-7;7 commr. disafforestation, Roche forest 1627, enclosure, Sedgemoor, Som. 1628, oyer and terminer, W
2 CONC estern circ. 1629-43, knighthood compositions, Som. 1630-2;8 dep. lt., Som. c.1637-42;9 commr. assessment 1641-2, array 1642, rebels’ estates (roy.) 1643.10 Symes’s father was a successful merchant or, in the words of one of his o
2 CONC pponents of more genteel ancestry, ‘a pedlar, and a base fellow’. He acquired lands in Devon, Dorset and Somerset and was granted arms in 1591. Symes himself married the daughter of a former knight of the shire, and in his father’
2 CONC s will he was left £2,000 according to an agreement made with his bride’s father and her grandfather, lord chief justice Sir John Popham†. Symes also inherited some of his father’s business instincts, acting both as a moneylender 
2 CONC and as a charitable trustee.11 .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/symes-john-1573-1661 ________________________
