1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John and Elizabeth (Sandell) Lake
2 CONT
2 CONT John LAKE - b. 1565, Essex; bur. Dec. 10, 1612, North Benfleet, Essex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Richard LAKE and Anne WARDELL, above. He resided at Great Fanton Hall, North Benfleet, Essex, where he wrote his will on Nov. 29, 1612. John had properties at North Benfleet, Basildon, Vange and Fobing in Essex. Married in 
2 CONC 1590.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth SANDELL - bur. May 4, 1616, North Benfleet, Essex. At the time of her death she was living with daughter Elizabeth PASCHALL at Nevendon, Essex. Her will of May 1, 1616 names her three sons and four of her daughters, daug
2 CONC hter Margaret having died young. Daughter of John SANDELL (b. about 1525) and Thomasine (b. about 1525).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Elizabeth Lake:
2 CONT *1. John - bap. Sep 26, 1590, North Benfleet, Essex; d. North Benfleet, Essex.
2 CONT *   2. Elizabeth - bap. Dec. 12, 1591, North Benfleet, Essex; d. about Aug. 1651, Essex. Her will was dated Jul. 10, 1651 and proved Aug. 28, 1651. She married first Andrew PASCHALL of Nevendon, Essex, whose will of Nov. 9, 1613 w
2 CONC as proved Feb. 25, 1613/4. She married second John BREADCAKE (d. 1636) of Leigh, Essex, a mariner who died between England and Gibralter. Son of Elizabeth and Andrew PASCHALL: Andrew married Clare. Daughter of Elizabeth and John B
2 CONC READCAKE: Clare married Mr. BUNDOCK.
2 CONT *3. Sybil - bap. Feb. 11, 1592/3, North Benfleet, Essex. Married before Dec, 1612 to Andrew BENTON. They had two children.
2 CONT *4. Richard - bap. Nov. 18, 1594, North Benfleet, Essex; d. before Mar. 1651/2. Married before 1620 to Ms. PARNELL (bur. Oct. 22, 1622, North Benfleet, Essex). Children of Richard LAKE: Richard; Elizabeth; and Anne.
2 CONT *5. Thomasine - bap. Oct. 14, 1596, North Benfleet, Essex.
2 CONT *6. Margaret - bap. Mar. 12, 1597/8, North Benfleet, Essex; bur. perhaps Jul. 24, 1598, Runwell, Essex. Not living in 1612.
2 CONT *7. Thomas - bap. Oct. 21, 1600, North Benfleet, Essex; d. about Mar. 1652. His will was dated Feb. 18, 1651/2 at Nevendon, Essex, and administration of his estate was granted Apr. 8, 1652 to his overseers. He entered Peterhouse C
2 CONC ollege, Cambridge in 1618 (A.M. 1621/2), was ordained deacon at Peterborough Dec. 21, 1623, and became a priest the following day. Thomas' wife, Ms. SUMPTER, died before him. Children of Rev. Thomas LAKE: Thomas, John; and Peter.
2 CONT *8. Anne - bap. Feb. 10, 1604/5, North Benfleet, Essex. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Weblinks:
2 CONT *http://www.lynngallup.org/genfam/pafg05.htm#50
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: North Benfleet, Essex]]
2 CONT ==Biography ==John was a son of Richard Lake of North Benfleet, county Essex. He wasborn about 1565.<ref>Davis, [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/image/?pageName=312&volu
2 CONC meId=11699&rId=23546273 pages 312-313].</ref>
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Sandell.  He inherited the manors of Great Fantonand Boneviles in North Benfleet and acquired additional property fromhis wife's family.<ref name=Davis313>Davis, Walter Goodwin, BA, LLB of Portland, ME.   Ance
2 CONC stry of John Lake, Husband of Margaret (Reade) Lake. ''The New England Historical and Genealogical Register'', v. 84 (1930), pp. 304-317.  (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001) [
2 CONC https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/image/?pageName=313&volumeId=11699&rId=23507913 page 313]</ref>
2 CONT He was buried at North Benfleet on 10 December 1612.<ref name=Davis313/> His wife Elizabeth was buried at North Benfleet on 4 May 1616.<ref name=Davis313/>
2 CONT === Burial ===
2 CONT :: Date:  10 DEC 1612
2 CONT :: Place:  North Benfleet, Essex, England
2 CONT == Sources ==
