1 NOTE !Copied from:
2 CONT http://members.aol.com/calebj/passenger.html
2 CONT John Tilley
2 CONT
2 CONT BAPTIZED:  19 December 1571, Henlow, Bedford, England,
2 CONT son of Robert and Elizabeth (---) Tilley.
2 CONT
2 CONT DIED:  the first winter, between January and March, 1620/1,
2 CONT Plymouth
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIED:  Joan (Hurst) Rogers, 20 September 1596, Henlow,
2 CONT Bedford, England, widow of Thomas Rogers (no relation to
2 CONT Thomas Rogers of the Mayflower), and daughter of William and
2 CONT Rose (---) Hurst.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Note.  Joan (Hurst) Rogers had a daughter Joan Rogers by her
2 CONT first marriage, bp. 26 May 1594, Henlow, Bedford, England.
2 CONT  Joan married Edward Hawkins, probably a brother of her
2 CONT half-brother Robert's wife Mary Hawkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT  NAME
2 CONT          BAPTISM
2 CONT                        DEATH
2 CONT                                    MARRIAGE
2 CONT  Rose
2 CONT          23 October
2 CONT          1597, Henlow,
2 CONT          Bedford,
2 CONT          England
2 CONT                        died young
2 CONT                                    unmarried
2 CONT  John
2 CONT          26 August
2 CONT          1599, Henlow,
2 CONT          Bedford,
2 CONT          England
2 CONT                        unknown
2 CONT                                    unknown
2 CONT  Rose
2 CONT          28 February
2 CONT          1601/2,
2 CONT          Henlow,
2 CONT          Bedford,
2 CONT          England
2 CONT                        unknown
2 CONT                                    unknown
2 CONT  Robert
2 CONT          25 November
2 CONT          1604, Henlow,
2 CONT          Bedford,
2 CONT          England
2 CONT                        unknown
2 CONT                                    Mary Hawkins in
2 CONT                                    Bedford, England
2 CONT  Elizabeth
2 CONT          30 August
2 CONT          1607, Henlow,
2 CONT          Bedford,
2 CONT          England
2 CONT                        21 December
2 CONT                        1687,
2 CONT                        Swansea, MA
2 CONT                                    John Howland, cir
2 CONT                                    1625, Plymouth
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ANCESTRAL SUMMARY:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tilley, his wife Joan (Hurst) Rogers, and daughter Elizabeth
2 CONT came on the Mayflower. John and Joan died the first winter, but
2 CONT Elizabeth lived, married John Howland, and had eleven children.
2 CONT John's brother Edward Tilley came with wife Ann Cooper on the
2 CONT Mayflower as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tilley did not marry Prijntgen (Elizabeth) van der Velde in
2 CONT Holland.  That was easily disproved in Mayflower Descendant
2 CONT 10:66-67, and by the subsequent identification of Joan (Hurst)
2 CONT Rogers.  Also note that the article in the Mayflower Quarterly
2 CONT 49:16+ entitled "John Tilley Jr, 1599-1636" presents a theory as
2 CONT to what happened to John Tilley's son John, but the article has
2 CONT been criticized as presenting no proof but just speculations
2 CONT (Wakefield in MD 43:76; Stratton p. 362).
2 CONT
2 CONT John's wife Joan is the daughter of William Hurst and Rose (---).
2 CONT William was born c1530, and died before 1571. He lived in
2 CONT Henlow, Bedford, England. Joan Hurst was baptized in Henlow,
2 CONT Bedford, England on 13 March 1567/8. She married first
2 CONT Thomas Rogers (no known relation to Thomas Rogers of the
2 CONT Mayflower), and second John Tilley.
2 CONT
2 CONT The known ancestry of John Tilley is as follows (from The
2 CONT American Genealogist 52:198-208):
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Tilley, b. c1465, d. 1520 === Johan (---)
2 CONT         |
2 CONT Thomas Tilley, b. c1490, d. 1556 === Margaret (---)
2 CONT         |
2 CONT William Tilley, b. c1515, d. Jan. 1578/9 === Agnes (---)
2 CONT         |
2 CONT Robert Tilley, b. c1540, d. Feb. 1612/3 === Elizabeth (---)
2 CONT         |
2 CONT John Tilley, Mayflower passenger
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY:
2 CONT
2 CONT                                  John Tilley came on
2 CONT                                  the Mayflower with
2 CONT                                  his wife Joan and
2 CONT daughter Elizabeth.  John's brother Edward Tilley also came on
2 CONT the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT Caroline Lewis Kardell, "An English Line from John Tilley",
2 CONT Mayflower Quarterly, 65(August 1999):208-209.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Leigh Ward, "English Ancestry of Seven Mayflower
2 CONT Passengers: Tilley, Sampson, and Cooper," The American
2 CONT Genealogist 52:198-208.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Leigh Ward, "The Baronial Ancestry of Henry Sampson,
2 CONT Humility Cooper, and Ann (Cooper) Tilley," The Genealogist
2 CONT 6:166-186.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Leigh Ward, "Further Traces of John Tilley of the
2 CONT Mayflower," The American Genealogist 60(1984):171-173.
2 CONT
2 CONT George E. Bowman, "Jan Tellij of Leyden was Not John Tilley of
2 CONT the Mayflower," Mayflower Descendant 10:66-67.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Pearson White, John Howland of the Mayflower
2 CONT through Desire Howland for Five Generations, vol. 1
2 CONT (Camden: Picton Press, 1990).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayflower Web Pages.  Caleb Johnson © 1998
