2 CONT John Tilley, his wife Joan (Hurst) Rogers, and daughter Elizabeth came on 
2 CONT the Mayflower. John and Joan died the first winter, but Elizabeth lived, 
2 CONT married John Howland, and had eleven children. John's brother Edward 
2 CONT Tilley came with wife Ann Cooper on the Mayflower as well. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Tilley did not marry Prijntgen (Elizabeth) van der Velde in 
2 CONT Holland. That was easily disproved in Mayflower Descendant 10:66-67, and 
2 CONT by the subsequent identification of Joan (Hurst) Rogers. Also note that 
2 CONT the article in the Mayflower Quarterly 49:16+ entitled "John Tilley Jr, 
2 CONT 1599-1636" presents a theory as to what happened to John Tilley's son 
2 CONT John, but the article has been criticized as presenting no proof but just 
2 CONT speculations (Wakefield in MD 43:76; Stratton p. 362). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John's wife Joan is the daughter of William Hurst and Rose (---). William 
2 CONT was born c1530, and died before 1571. He lived in Henlow, Bedford, 
2 CONT England. Joan Hurst was baptized in Henlow, Bedford, England on 13 March 
2 CONT 1567/8. She married first Thomas Rogers (no known relation to Thomas 
2 CONT Rogers of the Mayflower), and second John Tilley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The known ancestry of John Tilley is as follows (from The American 
2 CONT Genealogist 52:198-208): 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Tilley, b. c1465, d. 1520 === Johan (---)
2 CONT |
2 CONT Thomas Tilley, b. c1490, d. 1556 === Margaret (---)
2 CONT |
2 CONT William Tilley, b. c1515, d. Jan. 1578/9 === Agnes (---)
2 CONT |
2 CONT Robert Tilley, b. c1540, d. Feb. 1612/3 === Elizabeth (---)
2 CONT |
2 CONT John Tilley, Mayflower passenger 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY: 
2 CONT John Tilley came on the Mayflower with his wife Joan and daughter 
2 CONT Elizabeth. John's brother Edward Tilley also came on the Mayflower. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: 
2 CONT Caroline Lewis Kardell, "An English Line from John Tilley", Mayflower 
2 CONT Quarterly, 65(August 1999):208-209. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Leigh Ward, "English Ancestry of Seven Mayflower Passengers: 
2 CONT Tilley, Sampson, and Cooper," The American Genealogist 52:198-208. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Leigh Ward, "The Baronial Ancestry of Henry Sampson, Humility 
2 CONT Cooper, and Ann (Cooper) Tilley," The Genealogist 6:166-186. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Leigh Ward, "Further Traces of John Tilley of the Mayflower," The 
2 CONT American Genealogist 60(1984):171-173. 
2 CONT
2 CONT George E. Bowman, "Jan Tellij of Leyden was Not John Tilley of the 
2 CONT Mayflower," Mayflower Descendant 10:66-67. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Pearson White, John Howland of the Mayflower through Desire 
2 CONT Howland for Five Generations, vol. 1 (Camden: Picton Press, 1990). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ------
2 CONT Mayflower Web Pages. Caleb Johnson © 1998 
2 CONT
2 CONT =========================================================================
2 CONT =========
2 CONT Ancestry - Stratton, Eugene Aubrey, FASG. Plymouth Colony: Its History 
2 CONT and People 1620-1691. Salt Lake City, UT: Ancestry Incorporated, 1986
2 CONT
2 CONT Plymouth Colony: Its History and People 1620-1691
2 CONT Part Three: Biographical Sketches
2 CONT Biographical Sketches
2 CONT Tilley, John
2 CONT
2 CONT xxx —A 1620 Mayflower passenger, John Tilley arrived at Plymouth with his 
2 CONT wife Joan (Hurst), his daughter Elizabeth Tilley, and his brother Edward 
2 CONT Tilley, q.v. A most valuable discovery by Robert Leigh Ward, "English 
2 CONT Ancestry of Seven Mayflower Passengers," TAG 52:198, gives the Tilley 
2 CONT origin in Henlow, Bedfordshire, and shows that John and Edward were the 
2 CONT sons of Robert and Elizabeth (_____) Tilley. John and his wife left 
2 CONT children in Bedfordshire who could conceivably have left descendants, 
2 CONT though none living today is yet known. This article, plus Ward's 
2 CONT subsequent articles, "Henry Sampson's Paternal Grandfather," TAG 56:141; 
2 CONT "Further Traces of John Tilley of the Mayflower," TAG 60;171; and "The 
2 CONT Baronial Ancestry of Henry Sampson, Humility Cooper, and Ann (Cooper) 
2 CONT Tilley," TG 6:166, show much interrelationship among the Tilleys, 
2 CONT Coopers, Sampsons, and Hursts. There were Hursts, also, living in Leiden 
2 CONT (see under James Hurst), and Bangs's Pilgrims, p. 16, shows that a John 
2 CONT Masterson, a Separatist who remained at Leiden, also came from Henlow, 
2 CONT Bedfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT
