2 TITL Sketch of the Howlands
1 NOTE Another endowment date of 28 June 1938 has been given.
1 NOTE RFN: 25512
1 NOTE     From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 2 January 1996.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 14, Ed. 1, Tree #1317, Date of Import: Jul 16, 2005]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife, Margaret, was born in England in 1575.  She was buried in
2 CONT Fenstanton, Eng, on July 31, 1629.
1 NOTE The Howlands were members of the Essex Family.  Many of theirdescendants
2 CONT emigrated to the American Colonies.  Son, John Howland, was one of the
2 CONT passengers on the first voyage of the ship "Mayflower" in 1620. The
2 CONT Howlands, of Fen Stanton, lived near the college town of Cambridge,north
2 CONT of London about 9.5 miles.
2 CONT      Their descendants include many prominent and notable Americanpeople,
2 CONT including Jennie Jerome Churchill, Gerald Ford, Richard Nixon, Johnny
2 CONT Carson, George Plimton, Edith Carow Roosevelt (wife of Theodore);Henry
2 CONT Cabot Lodge; Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, as well as you and me.
2 CONT      Their children included: 1.  Humphrey Howland     b. ca. 1600Married
2 CONT #1 Margaret Calver  ca. 1627     Had Anne, Mary, Sarah.     2nd wifewas
2 CONT Anne.     He died 1646 at St Swithin Parish, London, England. 2.Arthur
2 CONT Howland     b. ca. 1587     Became a Quaker     Married Margaret Reed.
2 CONT Came to America in 1623. He  Died 1675 Marshfield, Massachusetts 3.Henry
2 CONT Howland     b. 25 November 1604     Also became a Quaker     Came to
2 CONT America with his brother Arthur.     Married Mary Newland.     Died1671
2 CONT at Duxbury, Massachusetts 4.  John Howland, the Pilgrim a halfbrother,
2 CONT Came to America on the Mayflower in 1620     Married by 1624 toElizabeth
2 CONT Tilley of John Tilley     Had daughter, Desire Howland.     JohnHowland
2 CONT died 1672 at Plymouth, Massachusetts 5.  Margaret Howland     b.?Married
2 CONT 1623 at Fen Stanton to     Richard Phillips - a shoemaker. They had
2 CONT Thomas, Savage, Margaret, William, and Anne 6.  George Howland b. ?
2 CONT Died 1643/44 at St. Dunston, East London, England 7.  Simon Howland b.
2 CONT ca. 1604/05 at Fen Stanton 8.  William Howland     b. February 1610/11at
2 CONT Fen Stanton.
2 CONT      The Howlands were "our" earliest emigrants to the AmericanColonies.
2 CONT Our line from Henry Howland (above) who came in 1623.
2 CONT Ref.  Howland Quarterly.       Genealogical Research by Thomas ClairSmith
2 CONT of Pennsylvania       Muirhead's England/Benn 1957 (copies in unicorn
2 CONT ventures Library - Greeley, Colorado)
