1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * In most genealogies Gertruda von Ungern is erroneously listed as a daughter of Heinrich von Ungern (as most genealogies copied from the same source). She was, however a daughter of Heinrich's brother Fromhold:
2 CONT * The following correction was published in [https://pbc.gda.pl/dlibra/publication/15182/edition/11777 "Baltische Familiengeschichtliche Nachrichten" 2/1934], pages 27-28, stating that in a court case regarding the inheritance of 
2 CONC the noble estate Fistehl, descendants of all three daughters of Fromhold Fromholdssohn Ungern claimed the estate, these daughters including Gertrud, the grandmother of the Nasacken descendents (who were among the claimants in 1664
2 CONC ):  In der livl. Hofgerichtsacte 1664 N. 133 d. h. in den Prozessakten über den Erbstreit wegen dem Gut Fistehl findet sich eine Eingabe des Reinhold v. Ungern Sternberg v. 1668 IV. 11. in der er u. a. angiebt: Fromhold von Ungern
2 CONC , Fromholds Sohn, hatte nur 3 Töchter: 1. Margarethe, des sei. Obristen Zöge Mutter. 2. Gerdrut, der Nasaken Erben Grossmutter. 3. Anna, sei. Rittmeisters Patkull Schwiegermutter (verm. Heinrich Ungern) , so alle in einem Grade gl
2 CONC eiche prätension haben." Aus den Prozessakten geht ferner hervor, dass die Nachkommen aller dieser Töchter des Fromhold Fromholds Sohn Ungern Erbrechte wegen Fistehl geltend machten.
2 CONT * The last will of Heinrich von Ungern a. Fistehl (document transcript #8, dated the 28th of June 1615, published in "Aus dem Leben eines Livlaenders", [http://hdl.handle.net/10062/24081 Jahrbuch für Genealogie, Heraldik und Sphra
2 CONC gistik 1909/1910], page 153) states that of his first marriage with Katharina von Hülsen gen. von Ekeln ha had a single daughter Anna, who married Magnus von Aderkas, whereas his 2nd marriage with Margaretha von Zweiffeln was chil
2 CONC dless.
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile corrected 2020-06-15. 
