1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The 15th Century Polish Nobility:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.almanachdegotha.org/id221.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikołaj Kamieniecki h. Pilawa (1460 – 15 April 1515) was a Polish nobleman (szlachcic) and the first Great Hetman of the Crown.[a political title, historically assigned to military commanders] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikołaj was the oldest son of castellan of Sanok Henryk Kamienicki and Katarzyna Pieniążkówna. He was owner of Węglówka, Kombornia, Wola Komborska, Jabłonica, Malinówka and the Kamieniec (ger.Erenberg) castle in Odrzykoń. A truste
2 CONC d co-worker of King Jan I Olbracht and Kazimierz Jagiellończyk.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became castellan of Sandomierz, voivode of the Kraków Voivodship and was Great Hetman of the Crown from 1503 until 1515.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikołaj defeated Vlachs in the Battle of Czerniowce during the Moldavian campaign in 1509 and Turks in 1512 in the Battle of Łopuszno.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miko%C5%82aj_Kamieniecki
