1 OCCU Poet
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jan Kochanowski''' – poeta polski epoki renesansu, sekretarz królewski. Uważany za jednego z najznakomitszych twórców czasów renesansu w Europie, najwybitniejszego poetę słowiańskiego, który przyczynił się do ro
2 CONC zwoju polskiego języka literackiego. [http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Kochanowski Wikipedia PL]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jan Kochanowski''' 1530 – 22 August 1584) was a Polish Renaissance poet commonly regarded as the greatest Polish poet as well as the greatest Slavic poet prior to the 19th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:	Piotr Kochanowski and Anna, née Białaczowska.
2 CONT
2 CONT Consort:
2 CONT # Dorota, née Podlodowska
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Urszula
2 CONT # Hanna
2 CONT # Ewa
2 CONT # Poliksena
2 CONT # Halszka
2 CONT # Krystyna
2 CONT # Jan (posthumous)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Works==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kochanowski's best-known masterpiece is [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Threnody Treny (Threnodies, 1580)]. It is a series of nineteen elegies upon the death of his beloved two-and-a-half-year-old daughter Urszula (pet name Urszulka
2 CONC ). It has been translated into English as Laments) in 1920 by Dorothea Prall, and in 1995 by Stanisław Barańczak and [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seamus_Heaney Seamus Heaney].
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.ap.krakow.pl/nkja/literature/polpoet/kochtrif.htm Selection of translated poems]
2 CONT * [http://www.gutenberg.org/author/Jan_Kochanowski Works by Jan Kochanowski at Project Gutenberg]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Kochanowski Jan Kochanowski]
2 CONT * Czesław Miłosz, The History of Polish Literature, 2nd edition, Berkeley, University of California Press, 1983, pp. 60-80.
2 CONT * Jan Kochanowski, Laments, translated by Stanisław Barańczak and Seamus Heaney, New York, Farrar, Strauss and Giroux, 1995.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Первый великий поэт Польши.
