2 CONT Rafał Leszczyński (born 1526, died 1592). He was one of the leaders of the Execution Movement as well as an influential patron of Protestants, the Unity of Brethren in particular. He held a number of posts, including that of the C
2 CONC astellan of Śrem and Sejm Marshal. He was one of the strongest supporters of the Polish-Lithuanian union. He was highly regarded as a moral authority.
