1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/William-Cranfield-Jr/6000000176419482857, who had no children,  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT He was not the son of William Cranfield of Gt Barford, Bedfordshire who did have a son William but he died without children before 1570 and his sole heir was his sister Elizabeth. I have detached him from his alleged parents. See 
2 CONC The Visitation of Bedfordshire 1634 https://archive.org/details/visitationsofbed1921harv/page/n111/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Descent 
2 CONT
2 CONT Roberts, Gary Boyd. English origins of New England families: from The New England historical and genealogical register, first series. (Baltimore [Maryland]: Genealogical Pub. Co., 1984) 2:201.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Joan (Cranfield) Kirby … on Oct 20, 1640 nuncupative will in presence of Francis Kirby, Joane Bides, Ruth Brown and John Bides, which was proved by the executor in the Court of the Archdeaconry of Hitchin Dec 2, 1640. Gave 20s to
2 CONC  the poor of Watten where she was born; gave 20s to the poor of Little Munden where she lived; to grandchildren: Ruth Cowley, Richard Kirby & Joseph Whale; to cousin Elizabeth Isham; cousin Mary Newton; daughter Joan Bides; son Fr
2 CONC ancis Kirby was exor. [Eng. Orig. of NE Families 2:201]
2 CONT
