2 CONT
2 CONT     * Edward STEVENS (b. 1523, d. Oct. 22, 1587), Lord of Eastington Manor, married Joan FOWLER (b. 1529, d. Aug. 5, 1587), daughter of Richard FOWLER and Margery BENNETT.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anthony STEVENS (b. ca 1560) married Kathrine BROKE (b. 1562), daughter of Richard BROKE (b. ca 1530). They were parents of Thomas STEVENS. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Edward Stephens (1523 - 1587) was Lord of Eastington manor. He married Joan Fowler and had sixteen children. They both died the same year and are buried in Eastington Church. [https://www.aboutglos.co.uk/st-michael-and-all-angels-
2 CONC church-eastington/#:~:text=Michael%20and%20All%20Angels%E2%80%99%20Church,%20Eastington.%20St.%20Michael,and%20is%20of%20the%20Church%20of%20England%20Denomination.]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources:=
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Michael and All Angels’ Church, Eastington
2 CONT St. Michael and All Angels’ Church is in the Gloucestershire village of Eastington, near to Stonehouse and Stroud. The church building is A Grade II* Listed Building and is of the Church of England Denomination.
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Michael and All Angels’ Church The village according to www.-british-history.co.uk had a church back in 1092, although there are no records of it before 1291. In 1340 they dedicated it to St. Mary, then becomes St. Michaels in
2 CONC  the 18th-century. The building has evolved over the years including rebuilding the nave, adding the north porch and a full list of enhancements and details about the architecture is at www.britishlistedbuildings.co.uk.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1-  [https://archive.org/stream/visitationofcoun00inchit#page/151/mode/1up The Visitation of the County of Gloucester:] Taken in the Year 1623, Volume 21.  By Henry Chitting, John Philipot, William Camden.  Page 151.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2- Nichol's Hist., co. Leic. I, 586.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3 - The illustration is from Fosbrook's Abstracts of Records and MSS., co. Glouc. 405. The peaceful reign of Elizabeth was a great period in the erection of manor houses, because it marked the transition from feudal castles to h
2 CONC omes combining dignity and comfort
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4 -  The engraving represents the church as it was when the Stephens family were lords of the manor.
2 CONT
