2 CONT ===will===
2 CONT
2 CONT THE WILL OF SIR JOHN SYMES, SR. Abstracted: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "To be buried at Frampton Cotterell, County Gloucester. To my nephew Arthur Symes 100 pounds, at the end of his apprenticeship. [ the identity of Author is not known]  I am possesed for many years to come & undermined of the mansi
2 CONC on of Poundsford, my exers. Shall convey it to William Symes, the eldest son of John Symes, dead. He not to be vex or prosecute any suit against Henry & Thomas 
2 CONT
2 CONT To my nieces Elizabeth and Grace 800 pounds to be paid out of Poundsford. To my nephews John & Edward Symes, sons of my son THomas Symes. Residue to my sons Henry & Thomas Symes, evrs."  - (The words neices and nephews were used f
2 CONC or grandchildren in his will.}
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT * John drowned in a boating accident..
2 CONT * Owned Barwick Manor 
