2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight_of_the_shire Knight of the shire (Latin: milites comitatus)[1] was the formal title for a member of parliament (MP) representing a county constituency in the British House of Commons,  ... Th
2 CONC e name "knight of the shire" originally implied that the representative had to be a knight, and the writ of election referred to a belted knight until the 19th century;[1] but by the 14th century men who were not knights were comm
2 CONC only elected.[2]
