1 NAME Robert Hill, MP, of Taunton and Bagborough
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1525
2 PLAC Poundisford, Somerset, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 21 APR 1581 AND 2 JUN 1581
2 ADDR
3 CITY Charde
3 STAE Somerset
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family and Education 3rd s. of Roger Hill (d.1546) of Taunton by his w. Margery. m. (1) Alice, da. of one Clark, 1da.; (2) Eleanor, da. of John Marvyn, 3s. 2da.
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT J.p. Som. from c.1562,, q. by 1574.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1558-1603/member/hill-robert-1581 History of Parliament online]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Hill was, like his father, a Taunton merchant. Born during the first few years of Henry VIII’s reign, he inherited a house in Bagborough, some seven miles from the borough, where he was living by the beginning of Mary’s reign. Ret
2 CONC urned to Parliament once for Taunton, no mention of him has been found in its extant records. In May 1579 he was one of three magistrates ordered to prevent the Taunton clothiers from evading the statutes, and to see that weavers 
2 CONC and tuckers were not exploited. He died 28 May 1581. His will, made in April and proved on 15 June, gives details of the division of his property, which included four houses in Taunton itself, among his widow and children. The poo
2 CONC r of St. James in Taunton received £1, and there were other small charitable bequests. Hill’s two daughters, Jane and Margaret, were to have £200 each at marriage, or on their 20th birthdays. The widow was executrix, and the five 
2 CONC overseers included James Marvyn, Nicholas Wadham, and Hill’s eldest son James, aged 21.
2 CONT
2 CONT E150/936/8; Vis. Som. (Harl. Soc. xi), 51; CPR, 1553-4, p. 427; APC, xi. 125; C142/197/59; PCC 7 Alen, 26 Darcy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Volumes: 1558-1603 Author: N. M. Fuidge NotesGo To Section1386-1421
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Will==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?id=PElFAAAAYAAJ&vq=Courtenay&dq=John%20Symes%201572&pg=PA67#v=onepage&q&f=true Abstracts of Somersetshire Wills, Etc:] Copied from the Manuscript ..., Volume 1.  Page 67.
2 CONT
2 CONT >B. 50. ROBERT HILL, of Taunton, Somerset, Esq. Will dated Apr. 21, J-v 1581, proved June r5, 1581, by Elianor3 the relict. [26 Darcy.] Poor of Taunton, Hillbrishe' & Pytminster. To my son James Hill, my .estate in the Capital Mes
2 CONC suage called Pownsforde alias Lodge, in Pytminster, & lands which I hold in common with Sir Henry Portman, K', in Pytminster. Many pieces of plate. The spice plate of silver. One piece called the Nutt. To my wife Elynor, a messuag
2 CONC e in Taunton, wherein William Awdrey dwelleth, & one in Fore Street, wherein Julian Greye dwelleth, &c. To my son John Hill, an annuity of ^10 from my farm called Heydon, & also an annuity of £20 to my son Hugh, & after the death 
2 CONC of my wife Elynor, the farm of Haydon to Hugh Hill, & to James Hill if he pay ^30 per ann. to Hugh Hill. To my daughter Jane, ^200, & "a pott of silver called the Skynkinge pott," &c. To my daughter Margaret, ^200, & my silver bee
2 CONC re jug. My goddaughter Rachel Portman, daughter of Sir Henry Portman, an old roiall of gold. To my other goddaughters i2d each. A marriage intended between my son James Hill & Ann Moryce, daughter of Mr Moryce, of Coxwell, Berks, 
2 CONC esq., he to pay me ^300, of which ^200 to be paid to my wife, for the advancement of my daughters. My son in law, William Symes,5 one silver spoon gilt, & 6/8 to their children. My wife, Extrix. Sir James Marrven, K' , my brother 
2 CONC in law, Mr Nicholas Wadham, my son, James Hill, Mr John Walker, of Stowey, & Mr Thomas Davidge, of Taunton, Supervisors. March 31, 1593, Admin. was granted to William Wigsted, of Fontmell Gilford, Wilts, yeoman, on decease of Elia
2 CONC nor, Relict of Robert Hill .
