1 OCCU butcher, maltster and grazier; Alderman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT Thomas ROGERS was born 1540 in Stratford on Avon, Warwickshire, England. He died Feb 1611 in Stratford on Avon, Warwickshire, England and was buried 20 Feb 1611 in Stratford on Avon, Warwickshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: William Rogers & Matilda
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Rogers (1540–1611) was an associate of Shakespeare's father, both serving on the borough corporation's council.   John Harvard was baptised on 29 November 1607, in St Saviour's Southwark, the second son of Robert Harvard, b
2 CONC utcher, and his second wife Katherine, the daughter of '''Thomas Rogers of Stratford-upon-Avon''', a substantial butcher, maltster and grazier. It was Thomas who, after the Stratford fire of 1594 rebuilt the house which now bears 
2 CONC the name of his grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==family==
2 CONT married
2 CONT # Elizabeth Potter
2 CONT # Margaret Pace
2 CONT # Alice CALLE on 5 Nov 1581 in Stratford on Avon, Warwickshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT * from Jim Wallace, 5 December 1998: "A large number of references to Thomas Rogers and Margaret Pace can be found, but it appears there is a great deal of confusion between Thomas Rogers and Thomas Matthew Rogers <[https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/people/Thomas-Matthew-Rogers/6000000000398138625 1st profile] | [https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Rogers-Sr/6000000030169423384 2nd profile]> (son of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Bernard-Rogers-Kt/6000000000405906562) 
2 CONC who must be different individuals. must be different individuals. Marriages are also given to Alice Calle, and Elizabeth Porter. Thomas Matthew Rogers appears to have had children: Edmund, William, George, John and Thomas. It woul
2 CONC d appear that the two are related as follows (but this needs confirmation from original documentation):
2 CONT > * Thomas John Rogers - Margery Wyatt
2 CONT > * William Rogers - Matilda England
2 CONT > * Thomas Rogers - Margaret Pace
2 CONT > * John Rogers - Adrianna de Pratt
2 CONT > * Bernard Rogers
2 CONT > * Thomas Matthew Rogers
2 CONT * Hal Bradley, Bradley/Opp Ancestry, RootsWeb's WorldConnect Project, 3 February 2004.  Thrice married:
2 CONT # 27 November 1561 to Elizabeth Potter (1541 - ), child Margaret Rogers.
2 CONT # 31 January 1563 to Margaret Pace (1541 - ), eleven children: Elizabeth, Charles, Joan, Alice, Joanna, Joyce, Alice, Richard, William, Edward, Anne.
2 CONT # 5 November 1581 to Alice Calle (1553 - ), children: Thomas, '''Katherine''', Thomas, Rose, and Frances.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From an unidentified researcher:
2 CONT >The Parish Registers of Stratford upon Avon commence Anno 1558.  By the kind permission of the Vicar, the Rev. George Arbuthnot, M.A., I was enabled to devote the whole of one day, from the close of the morning service to the beg
2 CONC inning of the afternoon service, to an examination of them. I took notes of the following marriages:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1562  January 31, Thomas Rogers and Margaret Pace.
2 CONT * 1563  November 27, Henry Rogers and Elizabeth Burback.
2 CONT * 1566  July 6, Edward Huntington and Matilda Rogers.
2 CONT * 1570 October 15, John Rogers and Anne Salsbury.
2 CONT * 1579  July 20, William Rogers and Elizabeth Walker.
2 CONT * 1581  October 30, Richard Rogers and Susanna Castell.
2 CONT * 1581  November 5, Richard Rogers and Ales Calle.
2 CONT * 1592 (?3)  December 30, Antherin Russell and Joyce Rogers.
2 CONT * 1596  November 21, William Rogers and Jone Tante.
2 CONT * 1600  October 28, John Nelson to Elizabeth Rogers.
2 CONT * 1602  April 13, Lewes Rogers to Joane Rodes.
2 CONT * 1602  October 12, Francis Rogers to Elizabeth Sperpoint.
2 CONT * 1603 (4)  January 1, William Smith to Ales Rogers.
2 CONT * 1605  "Apriell 8, Robertus Harwod to Katherina Rogers."
2 CONT * 1608 (9)  February 6, Henry Stanton to Phillip Rogers.
2 CONT * 1609  July 18, Thomas Chestley to Margaret Rogers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg.181
2 CONT
2 CONT I looked through the record of the marriages down to 1637 inclusive, and found a few other Rogers marriages, which it hardly seems worth the while to print. Thomas, Henry, John, William and Richard Rogers had numerous children bap
2 CONC tized and buried. Of these I pick out the children of Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized.                                        
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret, September 26, 1562. 
2 CONT * Elizabeth, October 28, 1563.			
2 CONT * Charles, March 28, 1565.			
2 CONT * Johanna, January 24, 1566 (7).		
2 CONT * Alice, September 2, 1568.			
2 CONT * Joanna, October 14, 1571.			
2 CONT * Joyce, February 9, 1572 (3).			
2 CONT * Ales, September 11, 1574.			
2 CONT * Richard, November 10. 1575.
2 CONT * William, June 8, 1578.
2 CONT * Edward, February 18, 1579.
2 CONT * Thomas, July 22, 1582.
2 CONT * Katherin, November 25, 1584.
2 CONT * Thomas, June 11, 1587.
2 CONT * Rose, March 29, 1590.
2 CONT * Frances, March 10, 1593.
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret, December 1, 1562.
2 CONT * Johanna, February 21, 1566 (7).
2 CONT * Alice, October 3, 1568.
2 CONT * Anne, Jul 24, 1581.
2 CONT * Thomas, August 13, 1584.
2 CONT * "Infant," Janurary 15, 1591.
2 CONT * Charles Rogers. "Homo" March 30, 1609 (10).
2 CONT * Thomas Rogers, August 31, 1639.
2 CONT
2 CONT The burial of Margaret, the wife of Mr. Rogers, I did not find. He evidently married again; for I found the burial of "Alice Wyf to Mr Thomas Rogers," August 17, 1608. His own burial is thus given:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1610 (11) February 20, Thomas Rogers, one of the Aldermen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Seversmith, Herbert Furman, The Seversmith Manuscripts (Brooklyn, New York: H. Stryker-Rodda, 1968.), Notebook #6, Los Angeles Public Library, NR 929.2 S4987-1.
2 CONT * Waters, Henry F., "John Harvard and His Ancestry," NEHGR 40:4 (Oct 1886) (New England Historic, Genealogical Society.), p. 363, Los Angeles Public Library.
2 CONT * Williams, Isaac Newton, Genealogy of William Rogers: Correction and Addenda.
2 CONT * Waters, H., NEHGR 40:4, p. 363.
2 CONT * [http://oasis.lib.harvard.edu/oasis/deliver/~hua05007 Harvard family. The John Harvard family collection, 1577, 1622, and 1828-2007. HUG 1447, Harvard University Archives.]. Thomas Rogers, a cattle dealer and alderman; Katherine
2 CONC  Rogers (1584-1635) of Stratford-on-Avon, the thirteenth child, married Robert Harvard.
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=caGKnZ6GsR0C&pg=PA181&lpg=PA181&dq=Thomas+Rogers+1610&source=bl&ots=ZKdkF46cf5&sig=zVNN840XofajK51n7LBHmZLtMKY&hl=en&ei=sS-hTLKxJIjSsAOZj7Vo&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CCIQ6AEwA
2 CONC w#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20Rogers%201610&f=false Genealogical gleanings in England, Volume 2] By Henry Fitz-Gilbert Waters, New England Historic Genealogical Society  Pg.180
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=selvage1&id=I97855
2 CONT * http://www.stratford-upon-avon.co.uk/soaharv.htm
