1 NAME Thomas Gallop, of North Bowood
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1540
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bowood
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 APR 1610
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bowood
3 STAE England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Gallop of North Bowood, gentleman.  Birth date is unknown.  He died April 7, 1610.The suffixes Senior and Junior were not in use so please don't add them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Six children with Agnes Watkins (Gallup Genealogy 2009, Vol 1, xiv):
2 CONT
2 CONT # Giles Gallop died without issue.  Fellow of New College Oxford, who not conforming to the change of religion in Queen Elizabeth's tiem, resigned his post and went to Rome and became a priest.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Humphrey Gallop died without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Gallop, died July 2, 1663.  Heir of North Bowood and Strode.  He married Francesca Pawlett, daughter of George Pawlett of Melplash, Dorsetshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Gallop married Mary Crabbe.  Their son, John Gallop of Mosterne, age 33 in 1623, emigrated to America 1630 on the ship Mary & John.
2 CONT
2 CONT # George Gallop lived in Southampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Richard Gallop, Stoke Abbot, Dorsetshire; married Mary Davy, daughter of John Davy of Sampford, Devonshire (Saunford, Sandford)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas has more children, as seen in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Thomas_Gallop_%283%29
