3 CITY Henlow
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hurst was born in the mid 1530s, probably in Henlow, Bedfordshire. He was the son of Henry Hurst and Agnes (Unknown).
2 CONT
2 CONT William was married June 15, 1560 in Chipping Barnet, Hertfordshire, to Rose Marshe, daughter of John Marshe and Joan (Unknown). Their children, all born in Henlow:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rose married second John Rushe 4 Feb 1571/2 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England. She was buried 23 Jul 1601 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Rose's children are:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. John Hurst, buried 31 Oct 1565 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England. 
2 CONT *2. Henry Hurst, baptized 10 Jun 1561 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England, buried 26 Jul 1608 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England, unmarried. 
2 CONT *3. Joan Hurst, baptized 8 May 1563 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England, died young. 
2 CONT *4. Agnes Hurst, baptized 17 Aug 1565 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England, married William Albone 26 Jan 1588/9 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England. 
2 CONT *5. Joan Hurst, baptized 13 Mar 1567/8 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England, married 1) Thomas Rogers 18 June 1593 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England and 2) John Tilley 20 September 1596 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, England, passenger on th
2 CONC e Mayflower in 1621, died shortly after arrival in Plymouth, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Land & Court Records
2 CONT
2 CONT *Prerogative Court of Canterbury [need vol. & folio]
2 CONT *In the name of God amen I William Hurste of Henlowe in the Countee o f Beds being sick but in purfecte remembraunce god be thanked Unto Whos e mercie only I commyt my sowle and bodie trusting thereby to be saved, d oe make this m
2 CONC y Laste Will the thurde daye of June in the yere of our L orde God 1570 
2 CONT *First I giue Vnto '''Agnes Vnderwood''' five poundes 
2 CONT *Item to my '''godsonne William Hurst''' fortie Shillinges 
2 CONT *Item to the poore people in Henloe 11s. 
2 CONT * Item I giue to '''Rose my wief''' my Lease of the vicaredge Close in Hen low
2 CONT *Item I giue vnto '''Henry my sonne''' my Lease of Mr. Gray[shold?] in He nlowe called Sydams. 
2 CONT *And I giue all the residue of my goodes not bequeathed Vnto Rose m y wief and my children my Debts being payd and my Legacy performed Whiche Rose my Wief I doe make my hole executrice. 
2 CONT * Item I will that Rose my Wief shall haue the howse and Landes Whic h I purchased of John Awdeleye during her naturall lief only:
2 CONT * In witness Whereof I haue cawsed this my Will to be made and signe d the same: 
2 CONT *John [Marthe?] Arth[ure?] Corkett Edward At[slowe?] by me William Hurste
2 CONT *Probate granted 20 Jan 1571/2, Prerogative Court of Canterbury
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://www.boydhouse.com/michelle/gorham/williamhurst.html (dead link)
2 CONT #  Ward, Robert Leigh, "English Ancestry of Seven Mayflower Passengers: Tilley, Sampson and Cooper", The American Genealogist, Vol. 52, No. 4, Oct 1976, pgs. 198-205. < [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/american-genealo
2 CONC gist-the/image?volumeId=12344&pageName=203&rId=24157645 AmericanAncestors] >
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "William Hurst (abt.1530-1569)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hurst-27 : accessed 14 May 2024).
2 CONT ##  "Maine, Nathan Hale Cemetery Collection, ca. 1780-1980," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QVJ5-4LHR : 17 March 2018), William Hurst, 1571; citing Henlow, , Bedford, England, Cemetery,
2 CONC  Maine State Library, Augusta; FHL microfilm 1,315,426.
2 CONT ## Caleb H Johnson, "Manorial Records - New Information," The Mayflower Quarterly, Vol 76, No. 2 (June 2010), 125-134.
2 CONT ## Eugene Cole Zubrinsky, FASG: ''The Parentage of Mayflower Passenger Joan (Hurst) (Rogers) Tilley''; The Howland Quarterly, Volume 81 (December 2016), pages 11-18
2 CONT ## Neither he nor any of his children were named in Agnes (___) (Wye) Hurst's will dated 14 Nov 1570, so it is doubtful that she was his mother.
2 CONT ##Ward, Robert Leigh. ''English Ancestry of Seven Mayflower Passengers: Tilley, Sampson and Cooper'', The American Genealogist (The American Genealogist, Barrington, RI, 1976) Vol. 52, < [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB283/i/
2 CONC 12344/204/0 Page 204] > 
2 CONT ## http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~fesschequy/genealogy/Hurst.html RootsWeb: The Hurst Genealogy]
