1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There has been some confusion about who Leontij Nasackin's father is. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Baltic and Swedish sources, based on historical facts, it's shown that Leontij Nasackin's father was Fyodor Nasackin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT La Noblesse de la Russie, vol. K, Ikonnikov, NF (1960) suggests that the father is Afanassi Zloba Fedorovitch Nastchokine? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Now it has been assumed that the father is Dmitrij Klimovich Nasackin?  
2 CONT
2 CONT In which Russian sources can this claim be confirmed as a fact?  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Swedish research, Leontij Nasackin was with his eldest son in tsar Ivan IV troops, when the tsar 1558 attacked Estonia. Leontij stayed in Estonia and acquired significant land areas.
2 CONT
2 CONT If this is true that the oldest son, probably Affanasy was fighting in Estonia at the same time, then his father Leontij was born around 1520 or earlier. If this information is correct, Leontij is probably not the father to Peter 
2 CONC Nasackin 1582-1636? 
2 CONT
2 CONT At least Peter can not have the same mother as Affanasy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Nasackin was a Russian boyar, but abandoned his inheritance to great properties in Russia. The data gives suspicion of possible errors in the family history? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Clearly wrong is Maria Nasackin (married to Iwan Romanowitz) in some investigations she is considered to bee a sister to Leontij. She's more likely daughter of Leontij. It seems difficult to research the so-called Russian traitors
2 CONC ' family background. Russian research has forgotten them.  
2 CONT
2 CONT https://cyberleninka.ru/article/n/russkie-boyare-v-estlyandii-konets-xvi-nachalo-xvii-v/viewer http://daten.digitale-sammlungen.de/~db/bsb00000559/images/index.html?seite=129&fip=193.174.98.30
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.armigerousdescents.com/db/getperson.php?personID=I29883&tree=AD#sthash.YYNf6lxK.dpbs
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Nassokin_nr_740#TAB_1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://cyberleninka.ru/article/n/russkie-boyare-v-estlyandii-konets-xvi-nachalo-xvii-v
2 CONT
2 CONT Elgenstierna, Gustaf: Den Introducerade Svenska Adelns Ättartavlor 5, p. 375.
2 CONT
