1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == THOMAS MACDOWELL OF MAKERSTOUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Thomas MakDowell of Makcavistoun (1533) Tho. M'Dowall de Mackarstoun (1534) Thomas Makdowale of Makcarstoun (1539) Thome M'Dowell de Makcaristoun (1551) Thome McDowell of Makcaristoun (1551) Thome McDowell of McCair
2 CONC stoun (1556) Tho, Makdowell of McCairstoun (1565) Thomas Makdowell of Makcarston (1571)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Ancestry ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The ancestry of Thomas Macdougal of Mackerston, here treated, has not been satisfactorily identified. According to John Burke: "Thomas Macdougal, of Mackerston, who flourished before and after the middle of the sixteenth centur
2 CONC y. He is mentioned in the acts of parliament in 1545. There is every reason to believe he was the son and heir of Andrew ; at least his heir, although it must be admitted, that in no legal authority yet found is he so designed. St
2 CONC ill, however, nothing militates against the conceived relationship. He m. Janet, daughter and heir of Walter Scot, of Howpaslet, a distinguished family, from whom Lord Napier, the Scots of Thirlstane, and others of note, are desce
2 CONC nded, and had three sons and a daughter." [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera03burk/page/432/mode/1up Commoners III: p. 433]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Makdowell of Makerstoun, here treated, died in April 1571. He made his last will and testament at Makerstoun on 24 April 1571 and died  before 30 April 1571. {NRS: CC8/8/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Mcdowell of Mackerstoun died in April 1571. He made his last will and testament at Makerstoun on 24 April 1571 and died  before 30 April 1571. He nominated and appointed his sons James and Thomas to be his executors test
2 CONC amentor and intromitters with his goods and gear.. He left his part of his goods and gear (the dead's part) to his son Thomas and Richard. Confirmation was granted to the executors testamentar on 27 February 1576. [National Record
2 CONC s of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Thomas Makdowell of Makcarston, reference CC8/8/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206735699826 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206735508831 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206735371846 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 March 1532-33: Charter by Jonet Scott, daughter and heir of deceased Walter Scott of Howpaslat, spouse of Thomas MakDowell of Makcavistoun, with consent of her said spouse, to Robert Scott in Howpaslat, her uncle, of lands o
2 CONC f Meidshiels and Apiltrehall, in barony of Hassendean, sheriffdom of Roxburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD224%2f903%2f29&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=makdowell&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt
2 CONC =1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montague-Douglas-Scott Family, Dukes of Buccleuch, reference GD224/903/29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 July 1534: Charter by Elizabeth Fallow, one of the heirs of Softlaw, made in favour of Andrew Ker of Prymsydloch, Withesses: THO. M'DOWALL DE MAKCARSTOUN and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/3
2 CONC 35/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1518]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1551: Charter by which the Queen of Scots confirms possession of the lands of Lugtounlaw in the barony of Makcairstoun and sheriffdom of Roxburgh, to Thome McDowell of Makcaristoun and Jonete Scot his spouse. Thomas McDo
2 CONC well of Makcaristoun has previously resigned this land in order to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his wife. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/138/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 609]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 April 1556: Charter by which THOME McDOWELL of McCairstoun confirms that quitclaimed in favour of his cousin Alexandro McDowell of Stratharig. the lands of Stratharig and others in the barony of McCairstoun and sheriffdom of 
2 CONC Roxburgh. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 3 Fenruary 1566-67. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/438/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 1762]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 December 1565: Charter made in favour of Margarete Home, daughter of Alexander, Lord Home, and Margarete Ker. Witnessed by THO. MAKDOWELL OF McCAIRSTOUN and others. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland 
2 CONC on 13 December 1565. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/408/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 1684]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Laing Charters ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 October 1539: Charter by Sir William Richardson, vicar perpetual of the parish church of St. Cuthbert of Langtoun, with consent of James [Stewart], commendator of Kelso, and John [Philp], abbot of Lindores, administrator of 
2 CONC Kelso, granting to William Cockburn of Chowslie and Margaret Galbraith, his spouse, the lands of Gretrig, Vicar's Croft, Hauchis, Langlands and commonflat of said vicarage, in the barony of Langton, Berwickshire, except one croft 
2 CONC on the east side of the church called Hoy's Croft, now occupied by Kentigern Home, curate of the church, with pasture for one horse in the said lands : To be held in feu-farm for a yearly feu-duty (old and new) of nine merks 13s. 
2 CONC 9d. Dated at Kelso, 30th October 1539. Witnesses, Mr. Patrick Cokburne, rector of Petcokkis, Alexander Gledstanis, rector of Garwod, Richard Richardson, vicar of Sproustoun, Richaid Ker, .Tames Lawson of Hundliy, THOMAS MAKDOWALE 
2 CONC OF MAKCARSTOUN, Alexander Hoppringill, Sir William Chepman, and Sir Thomas Quhite, chaplains. Sirs Robert Lausoun, Thomas Watho, and John Rolland, notaries. Signed by the commendator, Abbot, and the following members of the conven
2 CONC t : William Kewtone, William Laiisoun, Walter Murray, Adam Chatto, Robert Lawsoun, John Paton, James Ancrum, George Gray, Jasper Wynrem, William  Wrangham, Thomas Tuiiiet, John Cosar, Thomas Newmouch, Michael Chatto, Thomas Schaw,
2 CONC  Alexander Wod, Thomas Symson, and Patrick Ogyll. Thomas Watho, notarj', signs for William Richardson. Seal of Richardson (a chevron) and that of the commendator of Kelso still attached. [1385, Box 36.[https://archive.org/details/
2 CONC calendaroflaingc00edin/page/116/mode/1up Calendar of the Laing Charts: charter number 434]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
