1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JONET SCOTT ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to John Burke, Jonet Scott, here treated, is the daughter of Walter Scott of Howpasley. She married Thomas Macdougal of Mackerston. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera03burk/page/432/mode/1up Commoners III: 
2 CONC p. 433]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 March 1532-33: Charter by Jonet Scott, daughter and heir of deceased Walter Scott of Howpaslat, spouse of Thomas MakDowell of Makcavistoun, with consent of her said spouse, to Robert Scott in Howpaslat, her uncle, of lands o
2 CONC f Meidshiels and Apiltrehall, in barony of Hassendean, sheriffdom of Roxburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD224%2f903%2f29&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=makdowell&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt
2 CONC =1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montague-Douglas-Scott Family, Dukes of Buccleuch, reference GD224/903/29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1551: Charter by which the Queen of Scots confirms possession of the lands of Lugtounlaw in the barony of Makcairstoun and sheriffdom of Roxburgh, to Thome McDowell of Makcaristoun and Jonete Scot his spouse. Thomas McDo
2 CONC well of Makcaristoun has previously resigned this land in order to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his wife. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/138/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 609]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. Gen
2 CONC eral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/zwrk/macdowall03.php Stirnet: Macdowall 03]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera03burk/page/n9/mode/1up A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, enjoying territorial possessions or high official rank; but univested wit
2 CONC h heritable honours. By John Burke, Esq. In Four Volumes. Vol. III (Henry Colburn, London, MDCCCXXXVI), 738 pp. See pp. 430-36 for an account of the family of Hay-Macdougal of Makerston]'''
