1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Of that Ilk, married twice, firstly in 1524 to Mariota Hoppringill,the daughter of William Hoppringill of Torwoodlie. The Hoppringills,also Pringles, were a notable group of Border families, and at onetime Smailholm Tower, the fin
2 CONC e ScottishHeritage house, was amongsttheir holdings. The second marriage was to Isobel, daughter of DavidHome of Wedderburn and his wife Alison Douglas, the sister ofArchibald (Bell The Cat), 5th Earl of Angus. Philip was succeede
2 CONC dfirst by his eldest son, Adam, and then by his second son, George.Philip died before 1535 and Adam died in 1551. <p></p> <p>Of that Ilk, married twice, firstly in 1524 to Mariota Hoppringill,the daughter of William Hoppringill of
2 CONC  Torwoodlie. The Hoppringills,also Pringles, were a notable group of Border families, and atonetime Smailholm Tower, the fine Scottish Heritage house, was amongsttheir holdings. The second marriage was to Isobel, daughter of David
2 CONC Home of Wedderburn and his wife Alison Douglas, the sister ofArchibald (Bell The Cat), 5th Earl of Angus. Philip was succeededfirst by his eldest son, Adam, and then by his second son, George.Philip died before 1535 and Adam died 
2 CONC in 1551.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Biography Philip Nisbet of that Ilk died before 1535, and was the eldest son of Adam Nisbet of that Ilk and Lucie Rutherfurd.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married November 1524, first to Mariota Hoppringill, daughter of William Hoppringill (Pringel) of Torwoodlie, . He married, secondly, Isobel Home, daughter of David Home of Wedderburn and his wife Alison Douglas, sister of Arch
2 CONC ibald (Bell-the-Cat), fifth earl of Angus. The second alliance no doubt explains the assistance given by the Nisbets to the Douglases in the struggles of the latter with King James V. His two eldest sons, Adam and George succeeded
2 CONC  him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held land in chief and from the earl of Huntly. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Children of Philip Nisbet of that Ilk and Mariota Hoppringill
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Nisbet of that Ilk d. 1551 succeeded by his brother George (note 1551 might be registration date and he died before that--possibly his widow?? 27 August 1540. Summons in action George Lord Hume v. Elizabeth Lawson, widow of A
2 CONC dam Nesbit of that ilk of spoliation by night from lands of Bogend, Berwickshire. NRAS859/Box 32/Folder 1) George Nisbet of that Ilk d. 1600
2 CONT
2 CONT Branch DNA YDNA R1b-P312>DF19>Z302>Z8193>R-Z43691
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes Ancestors His father Adam Nisbet of that Ilk born 1469 eldest son. He appears to have met a violent death in 1530, as on 22nd June of that year a respite is granted to Matthew Hamilton, son to Robert Hamilton in Myl
2 CONC neburn, and Duncan Dundas, brother to James Dundas in New Liston, for airt and pairt in the slaughter of Adam Nisbet of that  ilk. Adam Nisbet and his wife received on 20th May 1502 a crown charter of the lands of Auchinhay, in th
2 CONC e stewartry of Kirkcudbright. On 14th May 1523 he was served heir to his father in the lands of Nisbet, Otterburn, Over and Nether Raecleuchs, and Mordington. He was witness to a conveyance by Stephen Tailyefeir, merchant burgess 
2 CONC of Edinburgh, to George Cairns in Nuntoun and Mariote Makcullock, his spouse, of the lands of Myddilthrid de Kirkcormack in Kirkcudbrightshire, 5th December 1524. He supported the red Douglases in their struggle with king James V.
2 CONC , and on 16th April 1529 he, with his son Philip, was put to the horn for non-compearance to a charge of intercommuning with and assisting Archibald, earl of Angus, George Douglas, his brother, and Archibald Douglas, their uncle (
2 CONC Kilspindie), in their treasonable deeds. He was again denounced for assistance rendered to Archibald, earl of Angus, in raising the siege of the castle of Newark. He was married to Lucie Rutherford. Alexander Nisbet’s Heraldic Pla
2 CONC tes introduction and notes Genealogical and Heraldic by Andrew Ross, Marchmont Herald, & Francis J Grant, Carrick Pursuivant published Edinburgh MDCCCXCIL 1892 Lairds and Gentlemen: A study of the Landed Families of the Eastern An
2 CONC glo-Scottish Borders ca 1540-1603 by Maureen Manuel Meikle PH. D. University of Edinburgh Nov 1988.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandfather Philip Nisbet of that Ilk b. 1444 died 1523 and was married to Elene Rutherford
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Nisbet-639 
