1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CUTHBERT CRANSTOUN OF THIRLESTAINE MAINS===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 April 1544: Precept of clare constat granted by George, Lord Seton, Baron of Tranent in favour of Cuthbert Cranstoun as heir to his deceased father, Thomas Cranstoun and his spouse, Marion Douglas of lands in Longniddry. [ht
2 CONC tp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f11%2f24%2f1A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cuthbert+cranstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Fami
2 CONC ly, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/11/24/1A]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 September 1553: Birkenside: Precept of sasine by Mr Thomas Marioribankis of Ratho, Lord Clerk Register, and John Hammyltoun of Nelisland, as procurators of James, Master of Arran, with consent of James, Earl of Arran, the Reg
2 CONC ent, in favour of Cuthbert Cranstoun of Thyrlstane Manys and Isabel Hume, his spouse, in respect of the lands of Birkinside in the sheriffdom of Berwick, apprised from Robert Scott of Howpaslatt and Walter Scott, his son. Bailies:
2 CONC  William Henry and Thomas Castellan. [Signatures granters and consenter; three tags; seal of Hamilton, detached.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f3%2f469&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=
2 CONC n&k=cuthbert+cranstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), reference GD40/3/469]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 July 1555: Charter (Manis 30 June 1555) by Cuthbert Cranstoun of Manis in implement of contract between himself and John Cranstoun, his son, and William Douglas of Quhitinghem and Margaret Douglas, his daughter, granting said
2 CONC  John and Margaret, his spouse, the lands of Morestoun, sheriffdom of Berwick, held in feufarm of said commendator and convent. Witnesses to confirmed charter: John Cranstoun, formerly (alias) of Huntliewood, David Hopringill, Dav
2 CONC id Gray, Thomas Castellau and Alexander Castellau. Signed by commendator, sub-prior and 11 monks. Tag with fragment of seal. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f1009%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl
2 CONC =n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cuthbert+cranstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Grand Lodge of Scotland: Miscellaneous Documents, reference GD1/1009/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 March 1557: Precept of sasine by James, Commendator of St Andrews, for infeftment of Cuthbert Cranstoun of Thirlestanemains in liferent and John Cranstoun, his lawful son, heritably in the 20/- lands of West Morestoun in the
2 CONC  parish of Legertwod, in sheriffdom of Renfrew, and sealed with the common seal of the Chapter of said monastery. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f225%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n
2 CONC &k=cuthbert+cranstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Cranstoun of Thirlestainemains sasine, reference GD1/225/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1567: Tack (in Scots) by David, commendator of Driburch [Dryburgh], and convent of same to Cuthbert Cranstoun [Cranston] [of ?] Thirlstane [Thirlestane] Manis, whom failing to Thomas Cranstoun, son and apparent heir of 
2 CONC John Cranstoun, son of said Cuthbert, and his heirs male bearing the surname of Cranstoun, of half of teind sheaves of kirk of Puncatland [Pencaitland], for term of 19 years, under reservation of feu granted to Sir John Castellan 
2 CONC [Castlelaw] and Thomas Castellan of kirklands of same. (Signatures of granter and 5 members of convent. On tag, seal of convent, defaced). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f8%2f8
2 CONC 5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cuthbert+cranstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Erskine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference GD124/8/85]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '30 December 1589 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/26/mode/1up RMS: 83]'''
