2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Alive 147 (0) -1520 (executed about 50 years)
2 CONT * Title:National council and knights
2 CONT * Erik Johansson (Vasa)
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Johansson (Vasa) was born around 1470 as son of Johan Kristiernsson (Vasa) and Birgitta Gustavsdotter (Sture).
2 CONT
2 CONT He supported his uncle Sten Sture d.ä. and at the crisis of 1497 he fought on his side against the rebellious council. The same year he was dubbed a knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Cecilia Månsdotter of the Eka family, and together they had eight children, two sons; Gustav I (Vasa) and Magnus, and six daughters called Margareta (married to Joakim Brahe), Emerentia and Märta who were both ca
2 CONC ptured, together with the mother, by Kristian II in Stockholm and taken to Denmark. Two of the daughters must have died in their infancy and a daughter must have been a sister sister in Vadstena.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1501, he joined the rebellion against the King Hans (Johan II). That same year, he also became a national council, though he did not participate much in the political life, although he lived so close to the capital. In the year
2 CONC s 1504-05 he was a chieftain at Kastelholm in Åland. He was also governor of Åland between 1504-1505. One could say that he was a rather brutal man, because he looted churches and church dwellings, raped maids, knocked down people
2 CONC  he did not like, etc. And there was no point turning to justice either because it was he who had the jurisdiction. On his command, his men caused such a violent advance in Ekerö church that Bishop Mattias in Strängnäs banned him,
2 CONC  because he did not want to return what had been taken from the church there.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was among those who signed the Riksdag decision on the demolition of Stäket in Stockholm on November 23, 1517 and was also involved in judging Gustav Trolle from his office, which would later become his death. When Stockholm's 
2 CONC bloodbath was carried out on 7-9 November 1520, he was one of the doomed, even though he passed to Kristian II's side after his success. It is said that he was offered grace but that he then answered; "My companions are honest gen
2 CONC tlemen, and with them I want to die death in the name of God". So he was executed in 1520 in Stockholm's bloodbath, about 50 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#GustafIdied1560B Projects MedLands SWEDEN Project MedLands Sweden Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ERIK Johansson, son of JOHAN Kristiernsson & his second wife Birgitta Tordsdotter Bonde''' (1470-executed/murdered Stockholm 8 Nov 1520).  '''married 1492/95, CECILIA Magnusdotter,''' daughter of MAGNUS & his wife --- (-Copenha
2 CONC gen 1522/23).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erik Johansson & his wife CECILIA Magnusdotter had children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''GUSTAF Eriksson''' (Lindholmen 12 May 1496-Stockholm 29 Sep 1560).  Regent of Sweden 1521-23.  He succeeded 7 Jun 1523 as GUSTAF I King of Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Project MedLands Sweden Kings - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#_Toc481304391
