1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sigrid Eskilsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001230280088?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000085218759873 '''Daughter of Eskil Isaksson Banér and Cecilia Haraldsdotter Gren, Tab 6 - Banér nr 22''']
2 CONT * Born: 1454 in Irsta Gäddeholm, Västmanland,
2 CONT * Death:  in 1527 in Trosa, Gäddeholm, Södermanland.
2 CONT * Sigrid Eskilsdotter (Banér) (died 1527), was a Swedish noble, the mother of the Swedish regent Christina Gyllenstierna and the maternal grandmother of King Gustav Vasa of Sweden.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001230280088&photo_id=6000000139675068889&position=1 '''Sigrid Eskilsdotte family Geneology Chart''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married =
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (1) to noble councillor '''Magnus Karlsson (Eka) (d. between 1484 and 1487)''' - Sigrid Eskilsdotter, to Lindholmen in Orkesta parish, Stockholm County. Dead autumn 1527, probably at Gäddeholm (now Tureholm) in Trosa, Sö
2 CONC dermanland County is buried and buried in Trosa church. In 1520 she was imprisoned by King Christian Tyrann to Copenhagen, where she was held until the beginning of 1524. Was through her first married grandmother to King Gustaf I 
2 CONC and through her second married mother to Christina Gyllenstierna. Married 1: o 1475-01-15 with knight and councilor Magnus Karlsson, to Eka, dead 1484.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (2) to noble knight and councillor [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllenstierna_af_Lundholm_nr_3#TAB_3  '''Nils Eriksson (Gyllenstierna)'''] (d. 1495).''' She remarried in 1487, with Nils Gyllenstierna (Eriksson);
2 CONC born 1457 in Fogelvik, Tryserum, Östergötland, National Council and Chief of Police at Kastelholm and Viborg, Death 1495 in Russia, Viborg.  Nils Eriksson, (son of Erik Eriksson the older, tab 1), to Fågelvik in Tryserum's parish 
2 CONC Kalmar county. Be knight and national council 1482-08-17. Got lifelong lecture at Kastelholm County in 1485 and was sent with a help group to Riga against German words. High man on Åland 1491-03-20. White man on Viborg 1491-09-03.
2 CONC  Death there in the spring of 1495 [6]. Married 1487-10-00 with Sigrid Eskilsdotter in her 2nd married (married 1: o 1475-01-15 with knight and councilor Magnus Karlsson to Eka, dead 1484), died in autumn 1527 probably on Gäddehol
2 CONC m (now Tureholm) in Trosa landsförsaml. Södermanland County and buried in Trosa church, daughter of the knight and the national council Eskil Isaksson (Banér) and his 1st wife Cecilia Haraldsdotter (Gren). Mrs. Sigrid was imprison
2 CONC ed by the cow. Christian II 1520-11-07 and was brought in 1521 along with her daughter Christina and several other distinguished women to Copenhagen, where she was held until the beginning of 1524. Through her 1st married grandmot
2 CONC her she became King Gustaf I and through her 2nd married mother of Christina Gyllenstierna 
2 CONT =Children: with Magnus Karlsson (Eka)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Cecilia Månsdotter (1476–1523), mother of king Gustav Vasa.'''  married to Erik Johansson ( Vasa ).  Erik Johansson Vasa . Executed at Stockholm massacre 1520-11-08. Chief of Danderyd and Rydbo ship team. Knights and national
2 CONC  council. He was, as a person, rather insidious, arrogant, conflict-prone, hot-tempered and, in addition, very violent. Pleaded before the court several times for committing crimes. One of the offenses was theft in Ekerö church bu
2 CONC ilding, another was the murder of a man who illegally invaded Erik's yard. Married about 1492-95 with Cecilia Magnusdotter , daughter of the Swedish National Council Magnus Karlsson (Ekaätten) and Sigrid Eskilsdotter Banér . The w
2 CONC idow Cecilia and her daughters died in Danish captivity in 1522.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Nils Eriksson (Gyllenstierna)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Erik Nilsson to Fågelvik and Tullgarn.''' Be knight 1511-11-17. Hvidvidman at Kastelholm 1518. Halshuggen in Stockholm's bloodbath 1520-11-08. Barnlös42. Married to Brita Jönsdotter in her 1st married [married 2: o 1528 with 
2 CONC the Riksråd and the high man Måns Bryntesson (Lilliehöök), dead 1529. 3.O with the knight, the Riksråd and the king's chancellor, Ms Christoffer Andersson (Red), who brought one oak leaves in the weapon. Death in exile 1548], dead
2 CONC  around. 1580, daughter of the knight Jöns Ulfsson (Roos) to Ervalla and Ingeborg Larsdotter Tott.
2 CONT *''' Eskil Nilsson.''' Riddare 41. The carved in Stockholm's bloodbath 1520-11-08.
2 CONT * '''Christina Nilsdotter Gyllenstierna,''' born 1494, dead 1559-01-06 Hearing hole. She became, after her 1st husband's death, the leader of the patriotic party in the battle against King Christian and bravely defended Stockholm'
2 CONC s castle from May 1520 to the 15th. 5/9. Then, in derailment, Tavastehus castle and county and Kymmene gärd in Finland, but became so. 7/11 imprisoned and the following are, along with the mother and several other distinguished wo
2 CONC men, brought to Denmark, from where she was not returned to the beginning of 1524. Sweden. Got 1529 in Bellö Fjording in Södra Vedbo from here and received 1556-06-07 confirmation on his deceased husband's lamentation in Höleho Hä
2 CONC rad24 (Trosa and Vagnhärads snr. Söd.). A statue of her was erected on the outer courtyard of Stockholm Castle in 1912. Married 1: o. 1511-11-16 in Stockholm with the national director, knight and councilor Sten Sture the younger 
2 CONC (see Natt och Dag), born 1492 (?), Dead 1520. Married 2: 1527-08-11 (morning gift the following day ) Lindholmen with the knight and the national council, and the chief man of Nyköping's castle Johan Turesson (Three Roses), to Lin
2 CONC dholmen and Tullgarn, dead 1556 [SK].
2 CONT *''' Carl,''' dead child.
2 CONT * '''Nils,''' dead child
2 CONT
2 CONT Source -  [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllenstierna_af_Lundholm_nr_3#TAB_3 Gyllenstierna af Lundholm nr 3, Tab, 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source - [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001230280088album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000085218759873 Baner nr22]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrid Eskilsdotter was the daughter of Eskil Isaksson (Banér) and Cecilia Haraldsdotter (Gren). She was married twice and was by 1495 twice widowed and very wealthy. Her daughter Christina was the consort of the Swedish regent in
2 CONC  1512-1520 and the leader of the Stockholm resistance against Denmark in 1520. Sigrid was present at the coronation of king Christian II in Stockholm 4 November 1520. She was captured and imprisoned during the Stockholm Bloodbath.
2 CONC  Sigrid and her daughter Christina were the only two women sentenced to death during the Bloodbath, but in neither case was the sentence carried out. Sigrid was sentenced to be sewn into a sack and drowned at sea, but the executio
2 CONC n was interrupted when she agreed to bequeath all her assets to the monarch. Together with her daughters Christina and Cecilia, and her granddaughters as well as a large group of Swedish noblewomen, Sigrid was taken to Blåtårn in 
2 CONC Denmark in 1521. Her daughter Cecilia and two of her granddaughters died in prison, but Sigrid was allowed to return to Sweden in 1523, where her grandson was now king.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mrs. Sigrid Eskilsdotter (Banér), widow after the chief man of Viborg Nils Eriksson (Gyllenstjärna), gives 1494 (= 1496?) To the black-brotherhood monastery in Viborg, subject to the same to doomsday every week shall hold a fair 
2 CONC for her late master Viborg located empty, which hall, Per Larsson's after-wife, Ingeborg Larsdotter, had lent to unified Nils Eriksson for a man's offense. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrid Eskilsdotter was the daughter of Eskil Isaksson (Banér) and Cecilia Haraldsdotter (Gren). Sigrid was married twice and from 1495 widow. She was also wealthy. Her daughter Kristina became the national government target in 15
2 CONC 12 and led 1520 Stockholm's defense against Denmark. Sigrid was present at Kristian II's coronation inStockholm on November 4, 1520, and was imprisoned at Stockholm's bloodbath.
2 CONT
2 CONT She belonged, together with her daughter Kristina,one of the few women who was sentenced to death by the bloodbath, but this execution was never carried out; she was sentenced to be drenched by being sewn into a sack and thrown in
2 CONC to the sea, but the execution was interrupted when she agreed to let her property be confiscated by the king. She was brought to Blåtårn in Denmark in 1521 with her daughters Kristina and Cecilia and her daughter-in-law. In 1523, 
2 CONC Cecilia and two daughters died in prison.  Sigrid himself survived the captivity and eventually, in 1523, returned to Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT =RUNE BERG=
2 CONT
2 CONT Banner, Sigrid, daughter of the Swedish Parliament, Eskil Isaaksson B. to Wenngarn, first married Riksrådet Måns Carlsson to Eka, who lived 1489-1500, and the second time with National Council Nils Eriksson Gyllenstjerna.  She was
2 CONC  the mother of the cross, each of its kind is remarkable Swedish fruntimmer, namely in the first marriage to Cecilia, Gustaf Vasa’s  mother, and in others to Christina Gyllenstjerna, Sten Sture d.  On Christian Tyrann's command, S
2 CONC igrid was stopped in one sack and was thrown into the water, but was raised with the life of some Danish people denied performances and against the departure of his property.  Along her relatives, she was inaugurated in 1521 by Ch
2 CONC ristian Tyran in prison in Blue Tower in Copenhagen, but became detached after the course of the years, and however, since 1528 at Gäddeholm and buried in Trosa church.  Her brother Knut and half-brother Nils Eskilssöner B. were b
2 CONC eheaded in 1520, the former one at Lindö farm in Finland at a large stone outside the gate, and the cedar outside Raseborg in Finland.
2 CONT
