1 CONT GEN: FGRA; DESC OF JOHN BISHOP; 1000 YRS OF HUBBARD P.199; GUILFORDVITAL REC
0 @N6000000001212143212@ NOTE Notes:  From Bruce Cox - E-Mail: brucecox@pdnt.com
1 CONT John Bishop, born in England, 1604, died in Guilford, Connecticut, January 166-.  He was one of the twenty-five signers of the Covenant.
0 @N6000000001529124699@ NOTE [v7t0736.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT One with Rev. Henry Whitfield's Co who founded Guilford (originally Menunketuk), CT; signer of Guilford, CT Covenant; one of six who bought land from the Indians.
0 @N6000000006414555737@ NOTE John Bishop, immigrant ancestor, born in England, about 1600. was one of the twenty- five immigrants who came with Rev. Henry Whitfield's company from England and founded Guilford, Connecticut. His name was signed second to the Pl
1 CONC antation Covenant made on shipboard June i, 1639. Robert Kitchell signed first. The order of the name indicates the respective social and other standing of the company, judging from analogy in similar cases. He was fifth on the li
1 CONC st of trustees of the Indian purchases, and one of the four magistrates appointed to administer justice and preserve peace in the community. He brought his family of several children with him. and is said to be brother of James Bi
1 CONC shop of New Haven, a contemporary. His wife was Anne. He died February, 1661, and she died April, 1676. His estate was the largest in the colony with the exception of Mr. Whitfield's. The site of John Bishop's homestead was suitab
1 CONC ly marked at the celebration of the two hundred and fiftieth anniversary of the settlement of Guilford, Connecticut, held September 8, 9, 10, 1889. Children, probably all born in England : 1. John, mentioned below. 2. Stephen, mar
1 CONC ried May 4, 1654, Tabitha Wilkinson, of Bermuda, who died December 2i, 1692; he died at Guilford, June. 1690. 3. Bethia, married James Steele. 5. Daughter, married Hubbard.
0 @N6000000003122799526@ NOTE Arrived New Haven, Conn., on ship "St. John", September 10, 1639.  First Bishop ancestor in America.
