1 CONC 979, pp. 193-206.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #4:   Myrtle Stevens Hyde, "Ancestors of Nathaniel Foote:  Warren Line" in "The American Genealogist" (TAG) Whole Number 231, Vol. 58, No. 3, July, 1982, pp. 165-167.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #5:  Goodwin, Nathaniel. The Foote Family. Case, Tiffany and Company. Harftord. 1849. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Mr. Foote was married in England, about the year 1615, to Elizabeth Deming, sister of Mr. John Deming, who was one of the first settlers of Wethersfield, and for many years one of the Magistrates of the Colony of Connecticut, and 
1 CONC one of the Patentees named in its Charter. His children were all born in England, except perhaps the youngest. Mr. Foote died in 1644, aged about 51 years,--and was buried in the ancient burying ground in the rear of the Meeting H
1 CONC ouse, where are gathered together the the ashes of nine generations. He left behind him, surviving, a widow, two sons and five daughters. He left no will. At a Particular Court held at Hartford, November 20, 1644, the following In
1 CONC ventory of his property and Distribution of his real estate were exhibited, and an Order of Court granting administration on his estate and directing a distribution to be made, was passed. 
1 CONT
1 CONT An Inventory of the goods and Lands of Nathaniell floote of Wethersfield deceased, being 
1 CONT   truly taken and Indifferently prised by Richard Tratte Samuel Smith and Nath: Dickinson. 
1 CONT
