0 @N6000000003490616926@ NOTE Benjamin Nye came to this country and to Lynn, Mass., in the ship "Abigail", with Edmund Freeman's company in 1635.  He eventually moved to Sandwich, where, in 1654 his name appears on a list of those contributing toward building 
1 CONC a mill.  In 1655 his name is on the subscription list for building a meetinghouse; in that same year (1655) he was supervisor of highways; in 1657 he engages to pay 15 shillings yearly toward the minister's salary; was chosen cons
1 CONC table in 1661, etc.  He seems to have built amill at the little pond in town and therefore the town in 1669 voted him 12 acres of land.  He was granted permission in 1675 to build a fulling mill on the Spring River.  (Old Families
1 CONC  of SouthEastern Mass)
