1 CONT He is mentioned in the will of his father-in-law.  At the time of his marriage, Robert was a citizen and fishmonger of the Parish of St. Mary Boettals in Thames Street, London (??? Discussion of this in TAG 54: 100) Later moved to
1 CONC  Wethersfield, Essex, still later to Shalsford, Essex, where he made his will, 27 January 1608/1609.  This was a family with strong Puritan leanings!  Mr. Richard Rogers (1550-1618) - a famous preacher of the day - is mentioned in
1 CONC  Robert's will.
