0 @N6000000008307994564@ NOTE The Foote Family Association of America (FFAA)  http://www.footefamily.org/i8921.htm
1 CONT ========
1 CONT A Yoeman in old England was a Freeholder, next under the rank of Gentleman, and in the early times one who owned a small landed estate. Robert of Shalford was such a man. He owned property in Shalford and Royston. He was the son o
1 CONC f John Foote of London and the father of Nathaniel Foote the Settler. 
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Joan Brooke June 18, 1576 in St Leonard's Eastcheap, London, Middleesex, England, Eng, daughter of John Brooke and Elizabeth Wetman. She was born June 18, 1559 in London, Middlesex, England, and died October 10, 1634 in
1 CONC  St Leonard's Parish, London, Middlesex, England. She was a member of the leatherseller company of London. 
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the brother of John Foote of London, and the father of Nathaniel Foote "The Settler." 
0 @N6000000003949497809@ NOTE 16 FEB 1607/08 Buried in Shalford, Essex, England.      27 JAN 1607/08 Date of will 
1 CONT  16 FEB 1607/08 Will proved at Shalford, England 
1 CONT He is called, "my sonne in lawe Robert ffoote, Citizen and ffishemonger of London" in the will of John Brooke.    Robert was employed. His will left his mansion and adjacent lands to his son Robert; 50 pounds to his son James; and
1 CONC  40 pounds each to the rest of his children. He provided 40 shillings for the poor, and a 4 pound annuity for his wife.
