1 CONT
1 CONT ALISON M. GAVIN works in the reference division of the National Archives Building in Washington, D.C. She was the 2003 recipient of the E. Geoffrey and Elizabeth Thayer Verney Fellowship of the Nantucket Historical Association, an
1 CONC d she received an MA in history in 2004 from George Mason University in Fairfax, Virginia. She credits her parents, William F. and Katherine B. Gavin, as inspiration for this story of parent and daughter.
