1 CONT James was our first decendent of the Leonard's to come to this country. Leonards were  iron-workers in Bilston, Staffordshire, England, before their emigration prior to 1649.  They were employed by John Winthrop, Jr., first at Bra
1 CONC intree and then at Saugus, MA.  In 1652 they established the first successful ironworks in America at Taunton
1 CONT (now Raynham), MA.  NEHGR:  1851  5:403-414; 7:71-73
1 CONT      Probate 1691 James gave to his son James, some tracts of land, "the old home lot," and "his father's half share in the Taunton Iron Works," and also 4 pounds and 9 shillings more from the estate.
