1 CONT In 1637 Thomas Tupper with other Massachusetts Bay Colony men from Saugus were given permission to establish the town of Sandwich  in Plymouth Colony.   The Tupper house was located near the present mouth of the Cape Cod Canal on 
1 CONC Tupper Road.   Its location is marked by a monument erected by the Tupper descendents.
