0 @N6000000003949700306@ NOTE Robert Foote of Royston was one of our oldest confirmed ancestors, He was born about the year 1523 in the town of Royston. He owned a small manor house along with some land in the town. Robert was the father of Robert Foote of Sha
1 CONC lford, and the Grand Father of Nathaniel Foote the Settler. He had at least four sons.
1 CONT John Foote died before 18 Jul 1558 when the undated will of John Foote of Royston, Cambridgeshire, England, tallow chandler was probated (PCC 34 noodles; George McCracken, "Nathaniel Foote's English Relatives" in The American Gene
1 CONC alogist
1 CONT 1977 53: 193, hereafter McCracken; Janice Greene Valore, "More on Nathaniel Foote's Ancestors" in The American Genealogist (April 1978, 99, hereafter Valore)
1 CONT His will revealed that he had a wife named Helen, sons Robert and John, and daughters Aves or Avis (Alice) and Elizabeth. The will also alluded to the testator's brother Foote, first name not stated and his two older children. He 
1 CONC left to the church of Royston, 20s; to wife Helen, all lands and tenements in Royston for life; and L80 to be divided among all the children; to servant Maud Smythe L6/13/4 to her marriage; L3 that my brother Foot oweth to his two
1 CONC  eldest children; to wife's brother Richard Warren the younger and to her uncle John Jenawaye of Stoone, 40s each; to wife the rest; to son Robert a goblet, feather bed and bedding; to son John Foot a silver salt, feather bed and 
1 CONC bedding; to Aves Foote and Elizabeth Foote, daughters, each three of the best spoons, bed and bedding; all the remainder to wife named executrix; witness William Meede, citizen and grocer of London; John Jenaway, Nicholas Warreyn 
1 CONC of Bassingbourn and Richard Warreyn of Bassingbourn.
0 @N6000000008307994578@ NOTE The Foote Family Association of America (FFAA)  http://www.footefamily.org/i9093.htm
1 CONT ========
1 CONT John Foote of Royston was one of our oldest confirmed ancestors. He was born about the year 1530 in the town of Royston, Hertfordshire, England.. He owned a small manor house along with some land in the town. John was the father o
1 CONC f Robert Foote of Shalford, and the Grand Father of Nathaniel Foote the Settler. John died before. January 1558/59 in Royston, , Hertfordshire, England. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage: Parish records show that in the year 1548 John was married to Helen or Ellen Warren_(Waryn) the daughter of Richard Warren and Alice Jenway in Hertfordshire, England. She was born Abt. 1529 in Bassingbourn, Cambridgshire
1 CONC , Eng. Her death was recorded at St. Leonard,N/E Chapel, London,England. 
1 CONT
1 CONT John and Helen had four children 
1 CONT
1 CONT (2)  i  ROBERT FOOTE OF SHALFORD 
1 CONT Robert Foote of Shalford was the first son of John Foote of Royston. He is our second generation ancestor in England. He was born in the year 1552 and died. January 28, 1607/08, London, Middlesex, England.
1 CONT
1 CONT (3)   ii   JOHN FOOTE OF LONDON 
1 CONT John Foote of London was born about the year 1555 In Royston, Hertsfordshire, England. He married Margaret Brooke the daughter of John Brooke of London. He was nathaniel Foote's uncle. John was a citizen and Grocer of London. He d
1 CONC ied about the year 1616 and was buried at London England. John was married in the year 1581. His wife died about the year 1634 and is buried at St. Benets Grace Church in London. They had six children. 
1 CONT
1 CONT (-)   iii  AVES FOOTE. 
1 CONT
1 CONT (-)   iv  ELIZABETH FOOTE. 
1 CONT
1 CONT John's Will
1 CONT Source (PCC 34 noodles; George McCracken, "Nathaniel Foote's English Relatives" in The American Genealogist 1977 53: 193, hereafter McCracken; Janice Greene Valore, "More on Nathaniel Foote's Ancestors" in The American Genealogist
1 CONC  (April 1978, 99, hereafter Valore)
1 CONT
1 CONT John Foote died before 18 Jul 1558. When the undated will of John Foote of Royston, Cambridgeshire, England, tallow chandler, was probated His will revealed that he had a wife named Helen, sons Robert and John, and daughters Aves 
1 CONC or Avis (Alice) and Elizabeth. The will also alluded to the testator's brother Foote, first name not stated and his two older children.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT He left to the church of Royston, 20s; 
1 CONT
1 CONT To wife Helen, all lands and tenements in Royston for life; and L80 to be divided among all the children; 
1 CONT To servant Maud Smythe L6/13/4 to her marriage; 
1 CONT L3 that my brother Foot oweth to his two eldest children; 
