1 CONT ENGLISH ANCESTRY AND HOMES OF PILGRIM FATHERS
1 CONT Plymouth Colony by Eugene Stratton
1 CONT      She was a Huguenot who had lived in Canterbury and Leiden.  Her admission to the French Reformed Church in Leiden in 1603 is shown in MC 27:147.
1 CONT CALEB JOHNSON MAYFLOWER WEB PAGE
1 CONT      Francis' wife Hester Mahieu was the daughter of Jaques
1 CONT and Jenne Mahieu, French Waloon refuges that had fled to
1 CONT Canterbury, England where Hester was born about 1584.
1 CONT  When in Leyden, Holland, from 1603 until the arrival of the
1 CONT Pilgrims, Francis and Hester were members of the French
1 CONT Waloon church.  However, in 1606 Francis and his wife left
1 CONT for a trip to Norwich, and they returned in 1607 to have
1 CONT their son baptized in the Church, and in 1608 they rejoined
1 CONT communion with the Walloon Church in Leyden.  Sometime
1 CONT between 1611 and 1618, the Cookes switched and began
1 CONT communion with the Pilgrims' Separatist church in Leyden.
