1 CONT
1 CONT He was at Braintree MA in the Iron Foundry and with his brother, Henry Leonard, built the first Iron Forge in Plymouth Co, at Taunton, MA in 1652.  This Leonard family was connected with Iron Works at Lynn, Braintree, Rowley, Taun
1 CONC ton, and later at Canton, MA and were pioneers in the iron industry in America.  Source:  NEHGS Register, Leonard family, 5:414
1 CONT      He was buried 16 November 1638.
