1 CONT BIOGRAPHY
1 CONT William and Elizabeth Goodell, the grandparents of Robert were
1 CONT probably members of the Godelle or Goodelle family, French Huguenots
1 CONT who emigrated to London in the 1530's. Huguenots were Protestant
1 CONT followers of John Calvin during the 1500's and 1600's. It's members
1 CONT were persecuted in France and suffered greatly. In all, eight wars
1 CONT were fought between the Huguenots and French Catholics between 1562
1 CONT and 1598 in their struggle for survival. Although the protestants had
1 CONT the support of many French leaders and nobility, the queen mother,
1 CONT Catherine de Médicis made a compact with the Duke of Guise which
1 CONT resulted in the Massacre of Saint Bartholomew's Day on August 24,
1 CONT 1572, when thousands of Huguenots were slaughtered. During this
1 CONT period of per-secution more than two million of the Huguenots left
1 CONT France to seek a more friendly atmosphere. The Goodells were among
1 CONT that number who emigrated to England. The name appears as Goodell,
1 CONT Goodale, Goodall, or according to the late Rev. Isaac Goodell, as
1 CONT "some other of the 18 variations". We find the historian Bowen and
1 CONT other genealogists call him Goodell, while the historian Perly calls
1 CONT him Goodale.
1 CONT Although his birth year was given as 1604 in his oath of allegiance
1 CONT when sailing for America, one of Robert's descendants has verified the
1 CONT church baptisimal record as 1601. The "Elizabeth" left Ipswich,
1 CONT England on April 30, 1634 and landed at Boston in July. At that time,
1 CONT Robert Goodell was 30, his wife Katherine was 28, their daughter Mary
1 CONT 4 years old, their son Abraham was 2 and their baby, Isaac was 6
1 CONT months old. The first record of the Goodells in America indicated
1 CONT that they settled just north of Salem at Great Cove in the North
1 CONT Fields.
1 CONT The Spring, so often mentioned in the early records, in what was
1 CONT later called Liberty Hill Park, was on Robert Goodell's farm and was
1 CONT known for the first half century of Salem's history as Goodell's
1 CONT Spring. It is not recorded how he acquired this first farm. However,
1 CONT in 1636 and in 1638 he received grants of twenty acres each in that
1 CONT portion of the town which became known as Salem Village, and he
1 CONT gradually acquired by purchase similar grants made to other early
1 CONT settlers, until by 1651, he was the owner of a tract of land at Bald
1 CONT Hill comprising four hundred and eighty acres, which was con-firmed to
1 CONT him by a town grant on November 7, 1651. He probably moved to this
1 CONT new property at about that time, and as opportunity offered, disposed
1 CONT of his Great Cove farm, deeding the house and a portion of the land to
1 CONT his son-in-law, John Smith in 1658. Another lot was conveyed to
1 CONT Nicholas Manning in 1667, and a third conveyance was probably made to
1 CONT John Orne, who owned a part of the property, hitherto unconveyed in
1 CONT 1684.
1 CONT Robert Goodell seems to have devoted his life to the developement of
1 CONT his large grant for the benefit of his sons and daughters. As they
1 CONT married, he gave them a generous acreage as a wedding gift, thus
1 CONT creating a family settlement about his own homestead. Although his
1 CONT clear firm handwriting would seem to indicate a good education, he
1 CONT took no part in local or broader govern-mental affairs and his name
1 CONT seldom appears in the records in any active capacity except as
1 CONT plaintiff or defendant in suits based on the ownership of his stock or
1 CONT land.
1 CONT His will reads as follows, "I, Robert Goodell being now aged & weake
1 CONT in body, as alsoe my wife and my daughter Elizabeth Bennett, hath
1 CONT taken care of me and therefore my will & desire is & I doe will &
1 CONT bequeath unto my daughter Elizabeth Bennett & my grand child, John
1 CONT Smith, my house & the orchard & all the meadowes that I now possess
1 CONT with the pasture which is about eight acres of upland be it more or
1 CONT lesse, all which house, land & meadows my daughter Elizabeth Bennett,
1 CONT and my Grand child John Smith, shall enjoy after the lease, or terme,
1 CONT that it is now let for, is expired, they or either of them paying as
1 CONT much rent, yearly as the wife of the abovesaid Robert Goodell hath let
1 CONT it for which is to the value of twenty shillings in current pay, dated
1 CONT the twelfth of October one thousand six hundred eighty two; & after my
1 CONT daughter Elizabeth's decease, the whole lands shall be my grand
1 CONT child's John Smith. In witness I have hereunto set my hand & seal.
1 CONT Francis Scerry Robert Goodell
1 CONT John Massey his X marke & seale
1 CONT The said Francis Scerry & John Massey, whoe are entered as witnesses
1 CONT to the above written, made oath in court in Salem that in their
1 CONT presence the said Robert did signe & seale to the above written as his
1 CONT act & deed & last will & testament: In Court as Salem; 27 June 83.
1 CONT Attesr. Hilliard Verne, Clerk
1 CONT "We whose names are under written being desired by the widdow Margaret
1 CONT Goodell wife of the late deceased Robert Goodell, do appr'se the
1 CONT estate of the deceased Robert Goodell, aprizes as followeth,
1 CONT £ OE d
1 CONT the house uplands orchard & meadow 71: 00: 00
1 CONT 2 cowes 5 lbs, wearing apparell
1 CONT bedding & other lumber 3 £ 1 OE _08:___16:___00_
1 CONT 79: 16: 00
1 CONT Salem the 10 Day of March 1682/3
1 CONT Nathaniel Putnam
1 CONT Job Swinerton
