0 @N6000000003949557939@ NOTE Joan (Sisson) Swift's Will
1 CONT The 12th day of the 8th month, 1662, I Jone Swift of Sandwich, being sicke of body, but of perfect memory, do make my last Will. I do give unto Daniel Winges, his sons Samuel and John, a mare foal of a year old. I do give unto my 
1 CONC grndchild Hannah Swift, the old mare, if she be alive, if not, the next to her. Item, I give unto my grandchild Experience Allen, a chest with drawers and my Bible. Item, I give unto my two grandchildren Hannah Swift and Experienc
1 CONC e Allen, all my linen and my pewter, to be equally divided between them. Item, I give unto Mary Darbet my wearing clothes. Item, I give unto Hannah Winge the Elder my best hat and forty shillings to her daughters, to be divided am
1 CONC ongst them. Item, I give unto Jedediah Allen and Experience Allen the third part of my Estate, this house and garden being part of the third; I give unto my son William's children, each of them a mare foal; my debts being discharg
1 CONC ed, and my funeral being paid, I give the rest of my Estate to my son William, whom I make my Executor. I make John Dincent and Benjamin Hammond my overseers of this my will and give to them twenty shillings apiece. Witness, John 
1 CONC Dincent and Benjamin Hammond.
1 CONT Jedediah Allen, son of Ralph and Esther Allen, writes in the family Bible as follows: "Jone Swift, my grandmother, deceased ye 26 day --",the rest is torn off the leaf. Her will was written on October 12, 1662 and the inventory of
1 CONC  her estate was taken December 25, 1663, making her probable death date November 26, 1663. Her inventory was 105 pounds, 5 shillings.
