0 @N6000000003490633097@ NOTE
1 CONT Likely came to New England in the great "Boston Immigration" of 1630/31.  He sold his house and land in Watertown to a Thomas White of Sudbury in 1637 and moved in the Spring of 1637 as one of the first settlers of the new town of
1 CONC  Sandwich.  The farm he bought in Sandwich was the largest in the town and was still in the hands of one of his descendents (Shadrach Freeman Swift) as late as 1887.  His widow Joan survived him by 20 years.  
