0 @N6000000006668455106@ NOTE Ship: "Fortune"
1 CONT From: London, ENGLAND
1 CONT Came to America In the ship "Fortune", which followed the "Mayflower",
1 CONT arriving at Plymouth, MA November 11, 1621.
1 CONT "Hicks Family, The - In 1621 the ship Fortune arrived at Plymouth, Mass., from
1 CONT London.  She followed the Mayflower.  With this second body of Puritans came
1 CONT Robert Hicks, the ancestor of the family in america.  He settled in Duxbury,
1 CONT Mass.  Two of his sons, John and Stephen, went to Long Island.  John took a
1 CONT very active part in the affairs of the settlement, and at times filled the
1 CONT most important offices.  A town in Long Island is named for the family; also a
1 CONT street in Brooklyn.
1 CONT From "Landmarks of Monroe County, NY"  (1895)
0 @N6000000003275791682@ NOTE [HIX.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert, born 1580 he married first Elizabeth Morgan, and second Margaret Winslow. The children of the first marriage were: Thoma s and John; and of the second were Samuel, Ephraim, Lydia, Phebe , Elizabeth, and Daniel.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1621, Robert Hicks left his home in Southwark, County Surrey, England, and
1 CONT came to the Plymouth Colony in the ship "Fortune" Nov 11 1621. H e was listed as a leather dresser. He lived as a substantial cit izen of the Puritan Colony. This was the 2nd body of Puritans fo llowing the Mayflower. Source: The 
1 CONC Hicks Family, The American Ge nealogical Research Instute, Arlington VI. Note Source: Broderbu nd WFT Vol. 21 Tree # 139. His wife, Margaret, with their childr en, joined him two years later, coming in the ship "Ann" in 1622 , she
1 CONC  was the sister of the Winslow brothers who came in the :Ma yflower". Robert Hicks resided in Plymourth Colony for 26 years, sharing in the division of cattle in 1627. Source: Automated Ar chives, Salt Lake City, UT CD-Rom. Note S
1 CONC ource: Broderbund WFT V ol. 19 Tree # 1100. He was made a freeman in 1633, and died Marc h 24, 1647. Note: Another of our ancestors sailed aboard the " F ortune" in the very same year to the same destination. William S ymons also 
1 CONC sailed from England to the Plymouth in 1621. I wonder if they met aboard ship?
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert Hicks Robert was born in England and lived in Bermondsey and Southwark in County Surrey, England. Surrey is the county lo cated just southwest of London. He was a fellmonger or leather m aker. The term especially applies to
1 CONC  sheep skins. Normally Rober t would pull 300 skins a week but sometimes he could do 600 to 7 00 skins. There seems to be some question about his wife (wives) . Some list his first wife as Elizabeth Morgan who he married ab out 15
1 CONC 96. They had four children. He second married Margaret abo ut 1610 and they had five children. Some identify her as Margare t Winslow step-sister of govenor Edward Winslow. Robert came to Plymouth Colony in 1621 aboard the Fortune
1 CONC . Margaret Winslow fol lowed two years later on the Anne. Robert had his will written f or him on May 28, 1645 and died two years later on May 24, 1647. His will in part says;
1 CONT
1 CONT "In the name of God Amen I Robert hicks of Plymouth this xxviiit h day of may Anno dm 1645 being full of Infermities of body and conssidering the brevity of this mortall life but of very good a nd perfecte memory doe ordaine and m
1 CONC ake this my last will and Te stament in maner and forme foloing first I give and bequeathe my soule to Almighty god in certaine hope and assurance of a Joyfu ll Reseurection and my body to bee buried in decent maner And as concern
1 CONC ing all my wordly goods and estate my mind and will is a s foloweth first I give and bequath unto my soon Ephraim all yt my dwelling house barn and buildings with the gardins therunto b elonging sittuate in plymouth aforsaid; ... 
1 CONC my executrix heeraft er named shall have and Enjoy three Romes in the sd house during her life shee keeping her selfe unmarried viz the hall and cham ber over and seller underneath : and allso yt my soon Ephraim sh all pay her the
1 CONC  thirds of the sd lands during her life and widdo whood : and lickwise shee shall Enjoy the garden next unto the w atter side with the sd Romes as foresaid ... and fifty [acres] t o John watson there [Seawams or Secunck] allso ...
1 CONC  I doe ordayne and make Margerett my loveing wife the sole Executrix of this m y last will and Testament ..."Robert's estate came to 39 pounds and 13 shillings outside of his real estate which amounted to ov er 300 acres. His wido
1 CONC w lived on another 19 years dying between July 8, 1665 when she wrote her will and March 6, 1665/66 when i t was exhibited. Plymouth Colony, Its History & People 1620 - 16 91 by Eugene Stratton 1986 Mayflower Descendant Vol. 8, Pg
1 CONC  143 - 146. Note Source: Broderbund WFT Vol. 19 Tree # 1198. Other Sou rces WFT Vol. 23 tree # 678 Rep Men & Old Families of Rhode Isla nd V. 3 pg 1609 Sir Ellis Hicks Family - pg 77 Robert arrived in Plymouth on the Fortune in 16
1 CONC 21 Thomas and James arrived in Ply mouth on the Anne in 1623 Margaret (Winslow) Hix wife of Robert arrived in Plymouth on the Anne in 1623.
1 CONT
1 CONT ROBERT HICKS SOURCE: WFT V.I, #259, AND #1412. Lived on Bermonds ey St. Southwark, London. He was a "fellmonger" VOL-27-6842. ROB ERT HICKS 1578 Sources:"Plymouth Colony Its History and People 1 620-1691" by Eugene Aubrey Stratton
1 CONC  p. 238 "History and Genealog y of the Mayflower Planters" by Leon Clark Hills p. 70-71, 162-1 63, 168 "The Great Migration Begins Immigrants to NE 1620-1633" by Robert C. Anderson p. 927 Vol. 2 Robert Hicks arrived in Plym outh M
1 CONC a. in the "Fortune" 1621. His wife, Phebe, Samuel, Ephraim , and Lydia arrived on the "Anne" in 1623 along with Edward Bang s. Child # 9 married the daughter of John Howland and Elizabeth Tilly. Children 1-8 were all bap. at St. M
1 CONC ary Magdalen, Bermonds ey, Surry ENGLAND. All the dates listed as births were the dates they were bap. JAMES HICKS 1550 Sources: "History and Genealogy of the Mayflower Planters" by Leon Clark Hills 1981 p. 70. Sour ce: WFT. Vol. 
1 CONC 27 tree #551.
