1 CONT Will of Elizabeth (Tilley) \  Howland
1 CONT
1 CONT In ye Name of God Amen I Elizabeth Howland of Swanzey in ye County of
1 CONT Bristoll in ye Collony of Plymouth in New Engld being Seventy nine
1 CONT yeares of Age but of good & perfect memory thanks be to Allmighty God
1 CONT & calling to Remembrance ye uncertain Estate of this transitory Life &
1 CONT that all fflesh must Yeild unto Death when it shall please God to call
1 CONT Doe make constitute & ordaine & Declare This my last Will & Testament,
1 CONT in manner & forme following Revoking and Anulling by these prsents all
1 CONT & every Testamt & \ Testamts Will & Wills heretofore by me made &
1 CONT declared either by Word or Writing And this to be taken only for my
1 CONT last Will & Testament & none other. And first being penitent & sorry
1 CONT from ye
1 CONT bottom of my heart for all my sinns past most humbly desiring
1 CONT forgivenesse for ye same I give & Committ my soule unto Allmighty God
1 CONT my Savior & redeemer in whome & by ye meritts of Jesus Christ I trust
1 CONT & believe assuredly to be saved & to have full remission &
1 CONT forgivenesse of all my sins & that my Soule wt my Body at the generall
1 CONT Day of  Resurrection shall rise againe wt Joy & through ye meritts of
1 CONT Christs Death & passion possesse & inheritt ye Kingdome of heaven
1 CONT prepared for his Elect & Chosen & my Body
1 CONT to be buryed in such place where it shall please my Executrs hereafter
1 CONT named to appoint And now for ye settling my temporall Estate & such
1 CONT goodes Chattells & Debts as it hath pleased God far above my Deserts
1 CONT to bestow upon me I Do Dispose order & give ye
1 CONT same in manner & forme following (That is to say) First that after my
1 CONT funerall Expences & Debts paid wc I owe either of right or in
1 CONT Conscience to any manner of person or persons whatsoever in Convenient
1 CONT tyme after my Decease by my Execrs hereafter named I
1 CONT Give & bequeath unto my Eldest Son John Howland ye sum of five pounds
1 CONT to be paid out of my Estate & my Booke called Mr Tindale's Workes &
1 CONT also one pair of sheetes & one pr of pillowbeeres & one pr of
1 CONT Bedblanketts,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my son Joseph Howland my
1 CONT Stillyards & also one pr of sheetes & one pr of pillobeeres
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my son Jabez Howland my ffetherbed & boulster yt is
1 CONT in his Custody & also one Rugg & two Blanketts yt belongeth to ye said
1 CONT Bed & also my great Iron pott & potthookes
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my son Isaack Howland my Booke called Willson on ye
1 CONT Romanes
1 CONT & one pr of sheetes & one paire of pillowbeeres & also my great Brasse
1 CONT Kettle already in his possession Item I give unto my Son in Law Mr
1 CONT James Browne my great Bible
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give & bequeath unto my Daughter Lidia Browne my best
1 CONT ffeatherbed & Boulster two pillowes & three Blanketts & a green Rugg &
1 CONT my small Cupboard one pr of AndyIrons & my lesser brasse Kettle & my
1 CONT small Bible & my booke of mr Robbinsons Workes called Observations
1 CONT Divine & Morrall & allso my finest pr of Sheetes & my holland
1 CONT pillowbeeres,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my Daughter Elisabeth Dickenson one pr of Sheetes &
1 CONT one pr of pillowbeeres & one Chest
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my Daughter Hannah Bosworth one pr of sheets & one pr
1 CONT of pillowbeeres,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my Grand Daughter Elizabeth Bursley one paire of
1 CONT sheets and one paire of Pillowbeeres
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give & bequeath unto my Grandson Nathaniel Howland (the son of
1 CONT Joseph Howland) and to the heires of his owne Body lawfully begotten
1 CONT for ever all that my
1 CONT Lott of Land with ye Meadow thereunto adjoyning & belonging lying in
1 CONT the Township of Duxbury neare Jones River bridge,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give  unto my Grandson James Browne One Iron barr and on Iron
1 CONT Trammell now in his possession,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my Grandson  Jabez Browne one Chest
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my Grand Daughter Dorothy Browne my best Chest & my
1 CONT Warming pan
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give unto my Grand Daughter Desire Cushman four Sheep,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I give & bequeath my wearing clothes linnen and Woollen and all
1 CONT the rest of my Estate in mony Debts linnen or of what kind or nature
1 CONT or sort soever it may be unto my three Daughters Elisabeth Dickenson,
1 CONT Lidia Browne and Hannah Bosworth to be equally Devided amongst them,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item I make constitute and ordaine my loving Son in Law James Browne
1 CONT and my loving son Jabez Howland Executors of this my last Will and
1 CONT Testament,
1 CONT
1 CONT Item it is my Will & Charge to all my Children that they walke in ye
1 CONT Feare of ye Lord, and in Love and peace towards each other and
1 CONT endeavour the true performance of this my last Will & Testament In
1 CONT Witnesse whereof I the said Elizabeth Howland have hereunto sett my
1 CONT hand & seale this seventeenth Day of December Anno Dm one thousand six
1 CONT hundred Eighty & six.
