1 CONT
1 CONT Baptised 30 Aug 1607; this date agrees with death record of 21 Dec 1687, which states that at the time of death, she was 80 years of age. Elizabeth's paternal
1 CONT grandmother was named Elizabeth according to her husbands will dated, "31st sale of December, 1612; therefore she was probably named in honor of her grandmother just as her sister, Rose, was named in honor of her maternal grandmot
1 CONC her.
1 CONT Other ref:  Mayflower Increasings by Susan Roser.
1 CONT TAG, V23/4:pp 118/9; v 52:pp 198/208.
1 CONT New Haven Genealogical Magazine.
1 CONT
1 CONT PLYMOUTH COLONY  p. 362
1 CONT A daughter of John and Joan (Hurst) Tilley, Elizabeth accompanied her parents on the 1620 Mayflower.  She had been baptized at Henlow, Bedfordshire, on 30 August 1607.  At plymouth she married John Howland, and they have many desc
1 CONC endants living today.
1 CONT      Gravesite of Elizabeth Tilley:  She is buried in Little Neck
1 CONT Cemetery, Riverside, Rhode Island, in a plot owned by her son-in-laws family.
1 CONT  (Brown's plot)  She was living with her daughter in Swansea, Ma., when she
1 CONT died.  The stone has been scratched possibly by a key in several areas. It's
1 CONT not really enough to deface the stone, but unfortunate none-the-less. The
1 CONT stone is identical to the one erected on Burial Hill in Plymouth, Ma., for
1 CONT John Howland.
0 @N6000000006348426503@ NOTE Source:  Source: Caleb Johnson: MayflowerHistory.com
1 CONT
1 CONT Elizabeth Tilley was born in 1607 in Henlow, Bedfordshire, the daughter of John and Joan (Hurst)(Rogers) Tilley.  She came with her parents on the Mayflower in 1620.  Both her parents died the first winter at Plymouth, leaving her
1 CONC  orphaned at the age of 13 in the New World.  She married to Mayflower passenger John Howland around 1625 at Plymouth.
1 CONT
