0 @N6000000003076457004@ NOTE After the death of Carver, he rose rapidly as a leader in the colony.  In 1627 he was the head of one of the twelve companies which divided the livestock, and he was one of the eight Plymouth Undertakers who assumed responsibility
1 CONC  for the colony's debt to the Adventurers in return for certain monopoly trade privileges.  He was on the 1633 freeman list, and by 1633, if not earlier, was an Assistant, being reelected to this position in 1634 and 1635.  In 163
1 CONC 4 he was in charge of the colony trading outpost on the Kennebec River when Talbot and Hocking were killed.  He received a good number of land grants, was elected deputy for Plymouth, served on numerous special committees and was 
1 CONC an important lay leader of the Plymouth Church.  The Reverend John Cotton related how at his own ordination as pastor of the church in 1669 "the aged mr John Howland was appointed by the chh to Joyne in imposition of hands".  [wor
1 CONC ktree.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT After the death of Carver, he rose rapidly as a leader in the colony.  In 1627 he was the head of one of the twelve companies which divided the livestock, and he was one of the eight Plymouth Undertakers who assumed responsibility
1 CONC  for the colony's debt to the Adventurers in return for certain monopoly trade privileges.  He was on the 1633 freeman list, and by 1633, if not earlier, was an Assistant, being reelected to this position in 1634 and 1635.  In 163
1 CONC 4 he was in charge of the colony trading outpost on the Kennebec River when Talbot and Hocking were killed.  He received a good number of land grants, was elected deputy for Plymouth, served on numerous special committees and was 
1 CONC an important lay leader of the Plymouth Church.  The Reverend John Cotton related how at his own ordination as pastor of the church in 1669 "the aged mr John Howland was appointed by the chh to Joyne in imposition of hands".  [wor
1 CONC ktree.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT After the death of Carver, he rose rapidly as a leader in the colony.  In 1627 he was the head of one of the twelve companies which divided the livestock, and he was one of the eight Plymouth Undertakers who assumed responsibility
1 CONC  for the colony's debt to the Adventurers in return for certain monopoly trade privileges.  He was on the 1633 freeman list, and by 1633, if not earlier, was an Assistant, being reelected to this position in 1634 and 1635.  In 163
