0 @N6000000002263831235@ NOTE
1 CONT of Bassingbourn; will 28 Mar 1557:
1 CONT Archdeaconry of Ely
1 CONT Richarde Warren otherwysse called Waller, of Bassingborne, county Cambridge [dated 28 March 1557, proved 2 May 1557, Archdeaconry of Ely]... sycke in bodye...
1 CONT Richarde my sonne the howse whiche I nowe dwell in w't all the londe & pastuore be longynge... londe somtymes called... John Asshwells except one called Bandall... also A closse called french brydge closse... & also rowses mede...
1 CONC  and iiij acres of brodlande & ij beasts & a horse for them w'ch I had borrowed of hym & also my lease of burye yearde... sayed Rycharde my sonne both my cupbords in the hall A forme ij chayers [= chairs] & to buffet stoles & my m
1 CONC aser [large drinking bowl of hard wood, often footed and silver mounted]...
1 CONT Nycolas my sonne my mesuage at goose styll w't v Roods of lond belongyne to yt & a halfe yearde londe w't a messuage called Willimoth buttynge uppon Walton grene...
1 CONT Henrye my sonne my howse at sene[?] end...
1 CONT Alce my doughter x[pounds]... also a garnysshe of peuter of the pryce of iiijs iiijd & also my white face cowe th't latlye calved & a fether bede a materis a bolster a coverlett a payer of shets & ij pillowes w't the bers...
1 CONT Alce my wife my howse called atkynsons w'ch castell now dwelleth in w't acers londe in the ocupienge of the sayed castell dwerynge the terme of hir lyffe...
1 CONT Henry my sonne v[pounds]...
1 CONT Augerye Waren the sayed Henrs davghter xxxiijs iiijd...
1 CONT Alce my wyffe Richarde my soone & nicolas my sonne all my goods movable... [and] executors...
1 CONT Will'm Waren the sonne of Will'm Waren the elder to be supvisor.
