0 @N6000000003853665308@ NOTE William Simms (Symes) will was written 4 Jun 1597 and proved 27 Jul 1597. He left a large estate, including a manor house in Chard to his wife, plus six manors, mostly in Somerset county, a mill in West Coker and lands in Taunton.
1 CONC  His will names his wife Elizabeth, and only sons John, James and Henry and daughter Margerat Payne and son-in-law Jaspar Payne. 
1 CONT The Arms of William Simms of Chard was granted in 1591; Azure, three scallops, or; crest, a demi-hand, rampant, and erased, or. Sec arleian. 
