1 CONT THE GREAT MIGRATION BEGINS  Vol 3, p 1822
1 CONT Origin:  Leiden, Holland
1 CONT Migration:  1620 on Mayflower
1 CONT First Residence:  Plymouth
1 CONT Birth:  Baptized Henlow, Bedfordshire, 19 December 1571, son of Robert and Elizabeth _______Tilley.
1 CONT Death:  Plymouth 1620 in the first general sickness
1 CONT Marriage:  Henlow 20 September 1596 Joan (Hurst) Rogers.  She had married (1) Thomas Rogers.
1 CONT      John Tilley joined the expedition of 6 December 1620 along the coast with nine others, under the leadership of Miles Standish. (Young's Pilgrim Fathers 149) The voyage along the coast was bitterly cold and his brother Edward 
1 CONC Tilley "had like to have sounded with cold"  (Young's Pilgrim Fathers)
1 CONT      In addition to the items noted in the sketch of Edward Tilley, Robert Leigh Ward in 1985 published some additional biographical information on John Tilley (TAG 60:171-173)
1 CONT      Tag 52:198-208 "English Ancestry of Seven Mayflower Passengers"
1 CONT John Tilley joined the expedition of 6 Dec 1620 along the coast with nine others, under the leadership of Miles Standish. (Young's Pilgrim Fathers 149)
1 CONT      The known ancestry of John Tilley is as follows (from The American Genealogist
1 CONT 52:198-208):
1 CONT Henry Tilley, b. c1465, d. 1520 === Johan (---)
1 CONT         |
1 CONT Thomas Tilley, b. c1490, d. 1556 === Margaret (---)
1 CONT         |
1 CONT William Tilley, b. c1515, d. Jan. 1578/9 === Agnes (---)
1 CONT         |
1 CONT Robert Tilley, b. c1540, d. Feb. 1612/3 === Elizabeth (---)
1 CONT         |
