0 @N6000000006348426519@ NOTE John Tilley was born in 1571 in Henlow, Bedford, England, and married the widowed Joan (Hurst) Rogers on 20 September 1596 in Henlow.  He, his wife Joan, and his youngest daughter Elizabeth all came on the Mayflower to Plymouth in
1 CONC  1620.
1 CONT
1 CONT John and his wife both died the first winter at Plymouth, orphaning the 13-year old Elizabeth Tilley in the New World.  Elizabeth would later marry to Mayflower passenger John Howland.
1 CONT
1 CONT The ancestry of John Tilley is from The American Genealogist 52:198-208.
1 CONT
1 CONT The following is from:
1 CONT Robert Charles Anderson. The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England, 1620-1633, vols. 1-3. Boston, Suffolk Co., MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1995.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT JOHN TILLEY
1 CONT
1 CONT ORIGIN: Leiden, Holland
1 CONT MIGRATION: 1620 on Mayflower
1 CONT FIRST RESIDENCE: Plymouth
1 CONT BIRTH: Baptized Henlow, Bedfordshire, 19 December 1571, son of Robert and Elizabeth (_____) Tilley [TAG 52:203].
1 CONT DEATH: Plymouth 1620 in the first general sickness [Bradford 446].
1 CONT MARRIAGE: Henlow 20 September 1596 Joan (Hurst) Rogers. She had married (1) Thomas Rogers.
1 CONT CHILDREN:
1 CONT    i   ROSE, bp. Henlow 23 October 1597; no further record.
1 CONT
1 CONT    ii   JOHN, bp. Henlow 26 August 1599; no further record.
1 CONT
1 CONT    iii   ROSE, bp. Henlow 28 February 1601/2; no further record.
1 CONT
1 CONT    iv   ROBERT, bp. Henlow 25 November 1604; no further record.
1 CONT
1 CONT    v   ELIZABETH, bp. Henlow 30 August 1607; m. about 1625 JOHN HOWLAND.
1 CONT
1 CONT ASSOCIATIONS: John Tilley was the elder brother of EDWARD TILLEY, who also died in the first sickness.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT COMMENTS: "John Tilley and his wife, and Elizabeth their daughter" were passengers on the Mayflower [Bradford 442]. "John Tilley and his wife both died a little after they came ashore. And their daughter Elizabeth married with Joh
1 CONC n Howland and hath issue as is before noted" [Bradford 446].
1 CONT    John Tilley joined the expedition of 6 December 1620 along the coast with nine others, under the leadership of Miles Standish [Young's Pilgrim Fathers 149].
1 CONT BIBLIOGRAPHIC NOTE: In addition to the items noted in the sketch of EDWARD TILLEY, Robert Leigh Ward in 1985 published some additional biographical information on John Tilley [TAG 60:171-73].
